window.FWN_DIMENSIONAL_KEEPER_ALL_MY_SKILLS_ARE_AT_LEVEL_100_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_DIMENSIONAL_KEEPER_ALL_MY_SKILLS_ARE_AT_LEVEL_100_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1901,"title":"Chapter 1901: Top Four!","paragraphs":["Ervin stood quietly in the middle of the curse field and raised his black spear.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","The black sea rose behind him, and the broken gate appeared. Morgana’s curse mirrors did not shatter immediately. Instead, they began sinking. It was a strange and eerie sight. The mirrors trembled as if their curses were trying to cling to reality, while the abyss beneath Ervin dragged their foundations downward.","Morgana quickly used \"Star-Curse Labyrinth, Nameless Witch Burial,\" attempting to trap Ervin before the gate opened wider, but Ervin answered with \"Gate of the First Depth\" and pierced through the burial curse with one spear.","The battle lasted longer than many expected, because Morgana constantly shifted her curses and never allowed Ervin to swallow the entire labyrinth at once.","But once Ervin used \"Abyssal Origin Descent, Return To Depth,\" the strongest core of the Star-Curse Labyrinth sank into the black sea, and Morgana gave up before the abyssal pull could damage her foundation.","[Winner: Ervin.]","[Morgana Starveil Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","Ervin returned to his pillar in silence, while Morgana sighed softly after returning to hers.","\"Every time I fight one of you monsters, I feel as though I should have chosen a gentler path,\" she muttered.","Rakan laughed from the side. \"Like what?\"","Morgana glanced at him. \"Anything that does not involve being swallowed by black seas, cut by sword heavens, erased by void eyes, or punched by war lunatics.\"","Rakan grinned. \"That sounds boring.\"","Morgana smiled faintly. \"Of course you would think so.\"","The arena relaxed for a breath, but only for a breath. The next battle immediately pulled everyone back into tension.","[Damian Voss vs Rosaline Lunara]","Rosaline stepped onto the stage with the Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary rising behind her from the very beginning. Rose-gold palaces formed, petals filled the air, and sovereign seals descended as the entire sanctuary tried to restrict Damian’s sword before it left its sheath. She had learned from previous battles and refused to let Damian gather sword rhythm freely.","But Damian’s response was brutally clean. He opened Sword Sovereign Heaven without hesitation, not because he feared Rosaline, but because he had no reason to waste time so close to the end.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, First Edict, All Blades Refuse Submission\" shattered the first three Dawn Edicts, while \"One Sword Divides Heaven\" cut through the Royal Mandate of Purifying Light. Rosaline tried to condense everything into \"Final Dawn Edict, Sovereign Rose Spear,\" but Damian’s sword light split the spear before it could reach him.","Rosaline surrendered with a helpless smile.","[Winner: Damian Voss.]","[Rosaline Lunara Defeated.]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","The projection above the arena flashed again and again as the records of the remaining top geniuses began aligning. Max Morgan, Ervin, Revona, and Damian Voss all rose to the top. All four were still undefeated, and all four now held twenty-one victories.","The Divine Realm noticed the pattern before Angelina even spoke, and a heavy silence began spreading from one viewing platform to another. Every elder, disciple, clan leader, sect master, and hidden expert understood what it meant. The real climax had finally arrived.","Angelina Valerius floated above the central stage with her silver-white robe stirring gently around her. The laws of the Eternal Hourglass gathered behind her like golden streams, and for the first time in a long while, she did not immediately call the next random battle. Instead, she raised one hand, and the entire screen above the arena changed.","Four names appeared.","[Max Morgan]","[Ervin]","[Revona]","[Damian Voss]","Beside each name, the same record appeared.","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","The whole arena fell silent.","Angelina’s calm voice spread through the Eternal Hourglass and reached every viewing screen across the Divine Realm.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference has now entered the final stretch of the final competitive stage.\"","Her words made the atmosphere grow even heavier.","\"Among all remaining participants, only four have preserved a perfect record until this point.\"","The four names shone brighter.","\"Max Morgan.\"","\"Ervin.\"","\"Revona.\"","\"Damian Voss.\"","The moment she spoke their names, countless eyes turned toward the four pillars. Max stood calmly with his white hair drifting faintly and Dragonheart resting at his waist. Ervin stood with his black spear in hand, silent and abyss-like. Revona sat quietly, her Void Origin Eyes calm and unfathomable. Damian Voss stood with his sword sheathed, his expression as still as a blade hidden beneath snow.","Angelina continued.","\"All four of them have achieved twenty-one victories without a single defeat.\"","The screen enlarged the records once more.","[Max Morgan: 21 Victories, 0 Defeats]","[Ervin: 21 Victories, 0 Defeats]","[Revona: 21 Victories, 0 Defeats]","[Damian Voss: 21 Victories, 0 Defeats]","A storm of excitement began rising across the Divine Realm. Angelina’s voice remained calm and clear.","\"From this point onward, their remaining battles against one another will decide the final champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The arena shook with whispers.","Max against Ervin.","Max against Revona.","Max against Damian.","Ervin against Revona.","Ervin against Damian.","Revona against Damian.","Every possible pairing among them was enough to be called a peak battle.","Angelina looked at the four of them. \"All four will battle each other. Whoever remains undefeated after these final battles will become the winner of this Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The moment those words fell, the Divine Realm erupted. The Black Dragon Clan disciples shouted Max’s name with wild excitement. The Sword God Palace disciples gripped their swords with burning eyes. The hidden forces watching Ervin fell silent and tense, while countless spectators stared at Revona with deep awe. Even the defeated top geniuses on the pillars looked serious.","Rakan Thorne grinned. \"Now this is what I was waiting for.\"","Orion Starfall leaned back with a tired smile. \"The monster round.\"","Morgana Starveil chuckled softly. \"The rest of us were only sharpening stones, it seems.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked toward the four names. \"No. We were all part of the same stage. They simply reached the last door without falling.\"","Aurelian Lareth remained silent. His gaze moved briefly toward Max, and then away again.","Above the central arena, the four undefeated names continued shining. Max Morgan, Ervin, Revona, and Damian Voss. The final battles had arrived."]},{"number":1902,"title":"Chapter 1902: First Battle Between Top 4","paragraphs":["The four names remained suspended above the Eternal Hourglass like four suns that refused to fall.","[Max Morgan]","[Ervin]","[Revona]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 21]","[Total Wins: 21]","No one spoke for several breaths after Angelina Valerius finished explaining the final rule, because the weight of those words had already settled into the heart of every spectator across the Divine Realm.","All four of them had reached this point without a single defeat. All four had crushed, cut, erased, swallowed, or overwhelmed one terrifying opponent after another. Now the conference no longer needed lesser battles to shape the rankings.","The final answer would come from the four monsters fighting each other directly.","Above the central stage, Angelina slowly raised one hand.","\"The first battle among the four undefeated participants will now be selected.\"","The moment she spoke, the entire Eternal Hourglass seemed to tighten. The giant screen above the arena changed. The names of every other participant faded away, leaving only four shining names rotating around one another in a circular formation.","Golden laws flowed around the screen to ensure that the selection could not be influenced by any outside power. Not even the hidden elders watching from the ancient forces could interfere with the randomizer controlled by the Eternal Hourglass.","[Max Morgan]","[Ervin]","[Revona]","[Damian Voss]","The four names spun faster and faster. The sound of the crowd slowly faded away, and even the defeated top geniuses on the pillars stopped talking.","Rakan Thorne crossed his arms, his eyes burning with excitement. \"Here it comes.\"","Orion Starfall leaned forward slightly despite the lingering exhaustion in his body. His usual smile had returned, but there was no playfulness in his eyes this time. \"No matter which two appear first, it will be insane.\"","Morgana Starveil tilted her head, her purple eyes reflecting the rotating names above. \"Max against Damian would shake the Sword God Palace and the Black Dragon Clan at once. Max against Ervin would be a rematch with unfinished meaning. Ervin against Revona would be abyss against void. Damian against Revona would be sword judgment against origin erasure.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked at the screen quietly. \"Every combination is dangerous.\"","Aurelian Lareth remained silent, yet even he could not look away.","On one pillar, Damian Voss stood like an unsheathed sword waiting inside its scabbard. His expression did not change, yet anyone who understood swords could feel that his sword intent had grown sharper.","Sword Sovereign Heaven had already cut through too many powerful paths, but even Damian could not treat the remaining three lightly.","On another pillar, Ervin stood with his black spear in hand, his eyes deep and silent, his aura like an abyss waiting beneath calm water. The faint shadow of the broken gate seemed to linger behind him even while his Pseudo Cosmic Path was not active.","Revona sat quietly with her pale eyes fixed on the spinning names. The Void Origin Eyes did not glow violently, but the space near her gaze seemed strangely empty, as though even anticipation itself were being drawn toward nothingness.","Max Morgan stood on his pillar with Dragonheart resting at his waist. His expression remained calm, but a faint smile slowly appeared on his face.","The first name stopped.","[Revona]","The entire arena held its breath. The second name continued spinning. It passed Damian Voss, then Ervin, and then Max Morgan. Then the rotation slowed, the golden light flickered once, and the second name stopped.","[Max Morgan]","For a single instant, there was no sound. Then the Eternal Hourglass exploded.","[Final Undefeated Battle]","[Revona vs Max Morgan]","The Divine Realm erupted so violently that countless viewing formations trembled. In the Black Dragon Clan, disciples jumped to their feet and shouted Max’s name until their voices cracked. In distant halls, ancient families, hidden sects, and divine cities, countless spectators rose from their seats at the same time.","Some had wanted Max against Damian first. Some had wanted Max against Ervin. Some had wanted Revona against Damian. But the moment Revona and Max appeared together, every other thought was swallowed by excitement.","This was not merely a battle. This was the first collision among the undefeated monsters.","Max Morgan was the human genius who had stunned the Divine Realm again and again, the one who had defeated Rosaline, Rakan, Kaiden, Aurelian, Orion, and many others without losing once.","He carried Dragonheart, he had displayed the forbidden Emotion Severing Path, and his depth still seemed impossible to measure even after so many battles.","Revona was the silent genius with the Void Origin Eyes, the woman who had erased Orion’s stars, adapted against Rakan’s War God Body, resisted Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth, and remained undefeated through every terrifying challenge placed before her.","Her power was not loud, but it was terrifying because it made even the strongest attacks feel meaningless once they entered her gaze.","The entire Divine Realm began shouting.","\"Revona against Max!\"","\"The Void Origin Eyes against the Emotion Severing Path!\"","\"Can Revona erase Max’s sword?\"","\"Can Max sever the foundation of her void?\"","\"She defeated Orion, Rakan, and Kaiden, but Max has not been forced to reveal his full strength even once!\"","\"Do not underestimate her. Kaiden almost exiled her, and she still adapted. If she reads Max’s path, even he may be forced to reveal something deeper.\"","\"What if her Void Origin Realm erases Dragonheart’s attacks?\"","The Black Dragon Clan was roaring. The hidden forces watching Revona stayed silent but tense. The Sword God Palace disciples also watched closely, because Damian would eventually have to fight the winner, or perhaps both of them, depending on how the final sequence unfolded.","The same was true for the mysterious forces behind Ervin. Every piece of information from this battle would matter.","Rakan Thorne laughed loudly from his pillar. \"This is good. This is very good.\"","Orion Starfall’s eyes shone with excitement. \"I fought both of them. I still have no idea how this will go.\"","Morgana Starveil smiled faintly. \"That is what makes it interesting. Revona does not need to overpower Max. She only needs to make his attacks disappear.\"","Kaiden Voidmere shook his head slightly. \"That is easier said than done. Max’s path is not something that can be understood from the surface.\"","Ervin watched the two names quietly. Damian Voss also looked toward Max and Revona with deep focus. For the first time since his own last battle, Damian’s fingers rested lightly on the hilt of his sword. He did not move, but his attention had sharpened.","This battle would tell him something important about Max, and perhaps something equally important about Revona.","Above the arena, the screen continued shining.","[Revona vs Max Morgan]","On her pillar, Revona slowly stood. Her long hair drifted gently behind her, and her calm eyes turned toward Max. No fear appeared on her face, and no excitement appeared either. Yet the stillness around her deepened, and the faint emptiness in her gaze grew more obvious.","She knew what kind of opponent Max was. She had watched him defeat too many powerful geniuses without being pushed to the end. She had seen him use Dragonheart, the Emotion Severing Path, light power, body strength, and space mastery.","Even then, she understood one thing clearly. Max still had not revealed everything.","Max met her gaze from across the arena. For a brief moment, the two of them simply looked at each other. Then Max smiled, and that faint smile drew another wave of noise from the audience.","Revona spoke first, her voice quiet but clear enough to cross the silent gap between them. \"I wondered when I would face you.\"","Max replied calmly, \"And now you have your answer.\"","Revona’s eyes flickered slightly. \"Your sword severs things that should not be cut. It is very strange.\"","Max’s hand rested on Dragonheart’s hilt. \"The same is true for you. Your eyes erase things that should not disappear, and they do it in a very strange way as well.\"","A faint ripple passed through the air between them.","Revona said, \"Then this battle will be meaningful.\"","Max smiled a little more. \"Very.\"","Angelina Valerius looked at both of them, and even her calm eyes carried a trace of deeper attention now.","This was the first battle among the four undefeated participants. It would not merely add one win and one loss. It would break the perfect record of one monster and push the other closer to the final crown of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","The golden laws of the Eternal Hourglass thickened around the arena barrier. The central stage restored itself fully, and the air became still. The entire Divine Realm leaned toward the screens.","Angelina raised her hand and announced in a clear voice.","\"Revona.\"","\"Max Morgan.\"","\"Enter the stage.\""]},{"number":1903,"title":"Chapter 1903: Max vs Revona!","paragraphs":["Two beams of light descended, and the first battle of the undefeated four was about to begin.","The two beams landed upon the central stage, and the first battle among the four undefeated participants officially entered the eyes of the entire Divine Realm.","Max Morgan appeared on one side of the arena with Dragonheart still sheathed at his waist and his white hair drifting slightly beneath the pressure of the Eternal Hourglass. He did not immediately draw his sword.","He did not release the Emotion Severing Path. He did not let seven-colored lightning flicker around his body, and he summoned no trace of his bloodline power. He simply stood there, calm and silent, his eyes resting on Revona with a thoughtful look.","Revona appeared opposite him. Her posture was still quiet, her expression unchanged, and her pale eyes carried that same terrifying emptiness that had made so many top geniuses feel helpless.","The Void Origin Eyes were fully open now. They were not burning wildly, and they released no obvious destructive pressure.","They were simply watching everything. The space around her gaze seemed to have grown thin and unreal, as if any power that entered that range would be studied, hollowed, erased, and returned to nothing before it could finish existing.","Angelina Valerius raised one hand above the arena, and the entire Divine Realm leaned forward.","[Battle Begins.]","Yet even after the announcement appeared, Max did not move. The audience froze for a moment. They had expected the first collision to explode instantly. They had expected Revona to open the Void Origin Realm at once, or Max to draw Dragonheart and sever space with that forbidden sword path.","Instead, Max remained where he was, his gaze calm and deep, as though he were not standing at the start of one of the most important battles of the entire Cosmic Ascension Conference, but studying a difficult problem that needed to be solved correctly before the first move.","Revona also did not attack immediately. She looked at him from across the stage and spoke in her usual calm voice. \"You are not starting?\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Against others, starting first is useful. Against you, starting carelessly is foolish.\"","A slight ripple passed through the arena, and the defeated geniuses on the pillars reacted one after another.","Rakan Thorne frowned. \"He is actually thinking first.\"","Orion Starfall smiled, though his expression was also serious. \"That is the right choice. Attacking Revona without understanding her eyes is the same as throwing your technique into a grave.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked at Max quietly. \"I wonder if Max has some plan.\"","Damian Voss did not speak, but his eyes sharpened slightly. Ervin’s gaze stayed deep.","On the stage, Max’s thoughts moved quickly. He had faced Revona before. Back then, her Void Origin Eyes had already been dangerous, but they had not yet awakened fully.","Their ability to erase and nullify attacks had been frightening, yet it still held gaps. The timing had not been perfect.","The range had not been complete. The connection between her eyes, her perception, and her deeper void authority had still contained places that could be misled, bypassed, or overloaded. During that earlier clash, Max had been able to use those gaps to break past her defense.","But now things were different. Very different. Max could feel it.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes had awakened fully. The pale emptiness within them no longer felt like a sharp ability aimed only at incoming techniques. It felt like a complete law of denial. Her eyes no longer merely erased attacks after seeing them.","They traced the structure behind the attacks. They found the source, the rhythm, the path, the intent, the hidden route, and the invisible support connecting technique to user. Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth had proven that.","Even when Kaiden hid attacks through folded corridors, delayed spaces, mirror routes, and false paths, Revona had adapted. She had learned to trace the true route behind spatial techniques and erase them from their foundation.","That meant Max’s previous method would not work. If he tried to distract her vision with speed, she would read the intent behind the movement. If he tried to overwhelm her with multiple attacks, she would erase the structural roots one by one.","If he used pure sword force, the Void Origin Eyes would search for the sword rhythm and hollow it. If he released the Emotion Severing Path too directly, she might not erase the entire path, but she could still weaken the severing line before it reached her.","And if he relied on the Dimensional Sovereign Body or the Dragon Scales Transformation alone, he might win eventually through raw superiority, yet that would not truly solve the problem of her eyes.","Max narrowed his eyes slightly.","’Her eyes are not only defending now.’","He watched the faint emptiness around Revona’s pupils.","’They are learning. They are tracing. They are reading the cause behind every effect.’","A slow smile touched his lips, because that was exactly what made Revona terrifying. Orion’s stars were powerful because they burned brighter and stronger under pressure.","Rakan’s War God Body was terrifying because it grew more violent the more direct the battle became.","Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth was dangerous because it turned the battlefield into an unreadable maze.","Damian’s Sword Sovereign Heaven was frightening because it could cut through the meaningful line behind everything.","But Revona’s Void Origin Eyes were dangerous because they punished repetition and obvious structure. The longer she watched, the more she understood, and the more she understood, the more she erased.","Her strongest ability was not simple nullification. It was adaptation through absolute perception.","Max could not treat her the way he had before. If he wanted to bypass her Void Origin Eyes now, he needed something entirely different. He could not merely move faster than her sight. He had to create an attack that her eyes could not properly define until it was already too late.","He could not merely release stronger sword force. He had to sever something that was not presented as an attack at first. He could not merely overwhelm her with power. He had to make her choose what to erase, and then punish the moment that choice created a gap.","Revona watched him quietly from the other side. \"You are thinking about my eyes.\"","Max looked at her and smiled. \"Of course.\"","Revona’s expression did not change. \"You bypassed them before.\"","\"I did.\"","\"That will not work now.\"","\"I know.\"","The simple exchange made the atmosphere grow even heavier. Across the Divine Realm, countless spectators felt their scalps turn numb, because even Max had admitted it. The old tactic would not work against the fully awakened Void Origin Eyes.","At the Black Dragon Clan, several elders grew solemn.","One elder whispered, \"Senior Brother Max is being cautious.\"","Another elder nodded slowly. \"He should be. Revona is not the kind of opponent one defeats by rushing in.\"","Lady Virelia watched the screen in silence, but a faint glint passed through her eyes. She had already seen many sides of Max, yet even now she could not fully understand the depth of his thinking.","This calm before the clash might look inactive to ordinary spectators, but to those at a high enough level, it was obvious that Max was already fighting. He was not exchanging blows with Revona yet, but he was searching for the correct line of victory.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Revona raised one hand, and a faint hollow ripple spread from her palm.","\"You may think as long as you want,\" she said quietly. \"I will still look.\"","Max’s smile deepened. \"That is exactly the problem.\"","Dragonheart remained sheathed, but his fingers finally touched the hilt. The moment his hand rested there, Revona’s eyes flickered. It was not in fear. It was in focus. The pale emptiness in her pupils deepened, and the air between them grew strangely silent.","Max did not draw the sword yet. He simply stood there with his hand on Dragonheart, keeping his intent hidden beneath his calm.","He knew that the instant his sword left its sheath, Revona would begin reading the trajectory, the intent, the rhythm, and the severing foundation behind it. If he used the Emotion Severing Path in the same manner as before, she would respond faster than anyone else had.","So he needed to change the very nature of the first strike. He would have to use an attack she could not comprehend, one that even the Void Origin Eyes could not erase."]},{"number":1904,"title":"Chapter 1904: A Way","paragraphs":["Revona’s gaze remained fixed on Max’s hand. Dragonheart had not left its sheath yet, but the faint hum coming from the sword made the stillness around the arena far more oppressive than an immediate clash would have been.","The spectators had expected flames of battle, thunderous sword light, collapsing void, and world-shaking techniques. Instead, Max and Revona stood across from each other like two people facing an invisible board where the first wrong move would decide everything.","Revona finally spoke again. \"Did you find a way to bypass my ability?\"","Her voice was quiet, yet because the whole arena had fallen silent, those words spread clearly through the Eternal Hourglass.","Max looked at her. Revona’s pale eyes were deeper than before, their emptiness no longer resembling a mere ability but a law that denied the meaning of whatever entered its sight.","She was not impatient, and she was not arrogant. She was asking because she could feel that Max’s thinking had changed, and because she knew he would not remain still unless he had understood something important.","Max smiled. \"Yes.\"","The answer was simple, but the moment he said it, the atmosphere changed.","Revona’s eyes narrowed slightly, and across the Divine Realm, countless spectators felt their hearts tighten. He had found a way.","Max Morgan had stood still, studied the fully awakened Void Origin Eyes, admitted that his previous method would no longer work, and now calmly claimed that he had found a way to bypass them.","No one knew whether those words were confidence or madness.","Then Max’s aura began to rise. At first it was only a faint vibration beneath his skin, so quiet that ordinary spectators barely noticed it.","Then the ground beneath his feet trembled, and the air around his body began distorting as if a hidden furnace had awakened inside him. His white hair lifted slightly, and deep within his body, four ancient gates seemed to open one after another.","The first vein awakened.","\"Seven Divine Veins.\"","Max’s voice was calm.","\"Vein of Opening.\"","Boom!","A terrifying foundational force burst out from his body. It did not look like ordinary energy, and it did not feel like simple bloodline pressure.","It was deeper, older, and heavier, as though some sealed origin inside Max had opened its first door and let a forgotten power flow through his limbs. His aura became clearer and more stable, and the entire stage shook beneath that first wave of pressure.","The second vein followed immediately.","\"Vein of Vitality.\"","A vast life force erupted inside him. The energy around Max grew denser, thicker, and more oppressive. It was not the gentle vitality that healed wounds quietly.","It was a ferocious vitality, the kind that made the body feel indestructible and made every bone, vein, muscle, and drop of blood seem capable of enduring impossible pressure. The spectators could almost hear his body roaring.","The third vein opened.","\"Vein of Speed.\"","The air around Max blurred. For a brief instant, his figure seemed to exist in several positions at once. It was not an illusion, and it was not space folding. His body’s movement potential had simply risen beyond what ordinary perception could hold.","The light around him stretched, and the dust near his feet rose and froze in strange curved lines, as though time itself had been forced to acknowledge the sudden increase in his speed.","The fourth vein opened.","\"Vein of Strength.\"","Boom!","This time the entire arena trembled violently. A crushing physical pressure swept outward from Max like a divine mountain waking from ancient sleep. The barrier around the stage lit up, and the golden laws of the Eternal Hourglass flowed through it to contain the force.","Max had not thrown a punch, and he had not drawn his sword. He had merely opened four of the Seven Divine Veins, yet the pressure released from his body already made many participants feel their breathing grow heavy.","Rakan Thorne stood up from his pillar, his eyes widening with battle-crazed shock. Is that the full power of that technique?\"","Orion Starfall’s smile vanished for once, replaced by pure astonishment. \"He did not use this against me.\"","Kaiden Voidmere stared at Max with a solemn expression. \"Nor against me. But I think this is the true power of the Seven Divine Veins.\"","Morgana Starveil’s purple eyes flickered. \"So he still had this much hidden?\"","Damian Voss’s gaze sharpened like a drawn blade. Ervin’s eyes deepened, and for the first time the faint shadow behind him stirred slightly without being summoned.","Even Revona’s expression changed. Only slightly, but it changed.","Max stood in the middle of that terrifying storm with his body surrounded by four layers of divine-vein power. Opening, Vitality, Speed, and Strength did not act separately. They fused together inside him, each one reinforcing the others and each one making the next more overwhelming.","His foundation opened, his life force surged, his speed sharpened, and his strength became monstrous. The energy around him was no longer merely powerful. It was devastating, wild, and almost unbearable to watch directly.","The Divine Realm erupted.","\"He still had this hidden!\"","\"What kind of cultivation art is that?\"","\"Is this the first time Max Morgan is going all out?\"","\"He did not use this against Rakan!\"","\"He did not use this against Orion either!\"","Across countless viewing halls, elders rose from their seats. Some were shocked by the pressure, some were horrified by the foundation, and some stared at Max as if they were watching a monster whose true shape had finally begun to appear.","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples were almost mad with excitement. Many of them had already believed that Max had revealed most of his strength after defeating so many top geniuses, but now they realized how wrong they had been.","Even when he defeated Rakan in a pure body battle, he had not used all of this. Even when he fought Orion’s Nine Star Sovereign Body, he had not released this level of divine-vein power.","Lady Virelia’s eyes shone brightly. \"So this is what you were still keeping hidden.\"","On the stage, Revona looked at the storm of power surrounding Max and spoke quietly. \"You plan to bypass my eyes with raw speed and strength?\"","Max smiled faintly. \"No.\"","The answer made her gaze sharpen again. Max’s fingers still rested on Dragonheart’s hilt, but he did not draw it yet. \"This is only to make sure I can stand at the right place when I need to.\"","The meaning behind those words made the top geniuses narrow their eyes. He was not claiming the four divine veins were his answer. He was saying they were only preparation.","Revona understood that as well, and the emptiness in her eyes deepened. \"Then show me the rest.\"","Max looked at her for a breath. Then the sky above the arena darkened, and a rumble echoed. At first it sounded distant, like thunder rolling from beyond the world. Then seven colors began flickering in the air above Max.","Red, orange, gold, green, azure, indigo, and violet lightning appeared one after another, and each strand carried a different kind of destructive pressure. When they began twisting together, the entire Eternal Hourglass seemed to tremble.","The expressions of countless spectators changed. They had seen traces of Max’s seven-colored lightning before. They had seen him use it to erase attacks, to crush enemies, and to display an authority that felt like judgment. But this was different. This was not a faint spark, and it was not a casual release. This was the descent of the true path behind that lightning.","Max slowly raised his head.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path.\""]},{"number":1905,"title":"Chapter 1905: Lightning Plus Speed and Strength!","paragraphs":["The seven-colored thunder above him exploded outward. A vast storm world appeared behind him, filled with endless punishment lightning. The sky became a divine tribunal. Thunder pillars descended like heavenly verdicts.","At the center of the storm, a vague throne formed from seven-colored lightning, and above that throne, countless thunder symbols rotated with terrifying majesty. Every strand of lightning carried destruction.","Every rumble felt like judgment. Every flicker seemed to declare that something in the world had been found guilty and would now be punished.","\"Divine King Punishment.\"","Boom!","The Pseudo Cosmic Path fully descended. The four opened Divine Veins roared inside Max’s body at the same time, and the seven-colored lightning wrapped around him like the cloak of a thunder sovereign.","Strength, vitality, speed, foundation, destruction, judgment, and punishment gathered into one terrifying presence. The pressure around Max grew so devastating that the stage beneath him cracked again and again despite the Eternal Hourglass repairing it continuously.","The Divine Realm went completely mad.","\"Another Pseudo Cosmic Path!\"","\"He has that strange sword cosmic path, and now this seven-colored lightning path too?\"","\"What kind of monster has two Pseudo Cosmic Paths?\"","\"No, this is not normal. This cannot be normal!\"","\"Is he finally going all out?\"","The top geniuses were no longer calm. Rakan’s battle intent burned wildly, yet even he understood that this level of pressure was not something he could challenge lightly.","Orion laughed in disbelief. \"So that is what he kept hidden against me.\"","Kaiden’s eyes flickered. \"Four divine veins, Dragonheart, a strange but terrifying sword cosmic path, and now the seven-colored lightning cosmic path he used against Morgana last time. He is stacking powers before Revona can read a single stable rhythm.\"","Morgana Starveil murmured, \"But will that be enough against Revona?\"","Damian Voss stared at Max with unprecedented focus. Ervin’s hand tightened around his spear.","Revona stood opposite Max with her Void Origin Eyes fully open, her expression calm yet her aura clearly turning more serious. She had defeated every opponent so far by seeing, tracing, erasing, and hollowing the foundation of their attacks.","But Max was no longer presenting her with one clean structure to read. His body was empowered by four divine veins. His weapon still waited inside its sheath. His severing path had not yet been released.","His seven-colored lightning Pseudo Cosmic Path had descended like judgment from the heavens. Multiple sources of power overlapped around him, each one terrifying, each one different, and each one capable of becoming the true attack or merely a decoy.","Max looked at Revona through the seven-colored lightning storm. \"You can erase what you see and understand.\"","His smile became sharper. \"So I will not give you only one thing to understand.\"","Dragonheart finally began to leave its sheath. The sound of the blade sliding free spread through the arena like a cold line drawn across the soul. It was not loud, but it silenced the endless thunder for a brief instant.","The seven-colored lightning above Max kept roaring, the four Divine Veins inside his body kept blazing, and the dreadful pressure of Divine King Punishment kept descending like judgment from a sky that had already chosen its criminal.","Revona’s Void Origin Eyes brightened. She did not speak. The emptiness around her gaze grew deeper, more focused, and more dangerous than before. Her eyes locked onto Max’s hand, then Dragonheart, then the seven-colored lightning, and then the divine-vein aura moving through his body.","In that instant, her perception divided itself into several layers, each one trying to trace a different source of power.","She was not looking only at Max’s sword. She was looking at the movement of his muscles, the rhythm of his breathing, the flow of his opened veins, the descent pattern of Divine King Punishment, and the hidden line of the Emotion Severing Path that had not yet been fully released.","That was what made her terrifying.","But Max moved before she could settle on one structure.","Boom!","The ground beneath him exploded. The Vein of Speed released its full power, and Max vanished from his original position so suddenly that even the top geniuses felt their eyes tighten.","It was not spatial movement, and it was not illusion. It was raw speed, pure physical motion elevated by a divine vein until the distance between him and Revona seemed to collapse beneath his feet.","Revona’s eyes shifted instantly, and a hollow ripple spread in front of her.","\"Void Origin Eyes.\"","The space before her began to empty, trying to erase the incoming path of Max’s first strike. If he continued along that direct route, his sword momentum, physical rhythm, and even the structure of his attack would be hollowed before Dragonheart reached her.","But Max did not continue along that route. At the final instant, the Vein of Strength roared, and his foot slammed into the stage. The entire direction of his body changed with impossible violence.","Crack!","The stage beneath him shattered in a wide spiderweb, and his figure bent away from the hollow ripple without losing momentum. Using brute strength to alter the path that speed had created, Max appeared at Revona’s right side and slashed with Dragonheart.","Revona turned her gaze, and the slash began to fade. But above her, Divine King Punishment descended.","\"Punishment Lightning, First Verdict.\"","A seven-colored thunderbolt fell from the storm world behind Max, not toward her head, but toward the ground behind her, where the Void Origin Realm would normally expand to support her retreat.","Revona’s eyes flickered. For the first time, she had to choose. Should she erase the sword? Should she erase the lightning? Should she read Max’s body, or seal off her own retreat route?","Her response was almost perfect.","Her right eye locked onto Dragonheart and hollowed the surface sword light before it could fully touch her.","Her left eye traced the descending punishment lightning and weakened its destructive authority before it reached the ground. At the same time, her body shifted half a step to avoid the physical edge of Max’s blade.","But Max’s Vein of Strength erupted again. His sword, which should have been weakened by the Void Origin Eyes, suddenly gained a crushing physical force behind it. The sword light had faded, but the sword itself had not.","Dragonheart’s actual blade carried Max’s raw strength, and the strike slammed into Revona’s hastily raised palm guard.","Boom!","Revona slid backward only three steps, but she had retreated first.","The entire Divine Realm erupted.","\"He pushed her back!\"","\"Revona’s eyes erased the sword light, but Max used raw strength through the weapon!\"","\"He changed direction with his body alone!\"","\"And the lightning forced her to divide her sight!\"","On the pillars, Kaiden Voidmere’s eyes turned extremely serious. \"That is his method,\" he said quietly. \"He is not trying to bypass her eyes with one perfect trick. He is overloading the process behind them.\"","Orion Starfall leaned forward, his exhaustion forgotten for a moment. \"Speed to create pressure, strength to change direction, lightning to force decisions, and the sword to punish the gap. That is insane.\"","Rakan Thorne grinned like a madman. \"Good. This is close combat.\"","Morgana Starveil narrowed her eyes. \"It is more than close combat. He is making her eyes work against too many kinds of danger at once.\"","Damian Voss watched silently. Ervin’s gaze stayed deep, but his grip on his spear tightened slightly.","On the stage, Revona stopped sliding. Her expression remained calm, but the emptiness in her eyes was brighter than before. \"Your body is troublesome,\" she said."]},{"number":1906,"title":"Chapter 1906: Pressurizing Revona!","paragraphs":["Max smiled faintly. \"That is only one part.\"","He moved again. This time he did not charge in a straight line. The Vein of Speed carried him across the arena in a blur, while the Vein of Strength let him change direction violently without slowing down.","He moved left, then forward, then vanished to the right, then appeared above her with Dragonheart descending in both hands. Each step shattered the stage.","Each change of direction left cracks in the air. His body no longer followed ordinary combat rhythm. It moved like a thunderbolt wearing flesh.","Revona raised her hand. She finally used her Pseudo Cosmic Path.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","A hollow world unfolded behind her. The moment it appeared, Max’s seven-colored lightning field dimmed slightly near its edge.","Several punishment bolts vanished before they could descend, swallowed by the origin-level emptiness. Dragonheart’s sword aura also began to thin wherever it entered the realm’s range.","But Max had expected that. The Vein of Opening pulsed inside him, and his foundation aura expanded to stabilize his body against the hollowing pressure of the Void Origin Realm.","The Vein of Vitality followed, surging through his flesh with monstrous force and letting him withstand the drain that would have weakened most opponents instantly. Then the Vein of Speed and the Vein of Strength roared together, and Max crashed into the edge of the Void Origin Realm instead of retreating from it.","\"Divine King Punishment, Thunder Chain Judgment.\"","Seven-colored lightning chains descended from above, each one striking from a different direction. Revona’s eyes moved rapidly. Two chains vanished, three chains weakened, and one chain was redirected by the Void Origin Realm.","But Max hid behind the final chain. His body appeared through the seven-colored thunder with Dragonheart already slashing toward her waist.","Revona’s eyes shifted toward him.","\"Void Origin Eyes, Hollow Sight.\"","The slash began disappearing. But Max’s wrist changed angle. The Vein of Strength gave him enough control to force Dragonheart into a second trajectory after the first had already been erased.","The first sword line vanished beneath Revona’s eyes, but the real blade curved underneath the fading sword light and struck upward.","Revona’s body leaned back, and the blade missed her throat by a narrow margin. A thin line of blood appeared beneath her chin.","The arena went silent for a breath. Then it erupted even louder. Blood. Max had drawn blood from Revona during the first true close-range exchange.","Revona touched the wound lightly, and her eyes turned colder.","\"Void Origin Realm, Silent Collapse.\"","The hollow world behind her pulsed, and the air around Max suddenly began vanishing in layers. It was not just the attacks, and it was not just the sword aura.","The space near his limbs, the lightning around his body, and the movement path beneath his feet all began collapsing into nothingness at the same time.","Max’s expression sharpened. The Vein of Speed erupted, and he vanished from the collapsing zone before it fully closed. But Revona’s eyes followed him instantly, and a void ripple appeared where he was about to land.","Most opponents would have been forced to stop. Max did not. The Vein of Strength exploded through his legs. Instead of landing where Revona expected, he stomped midair with pure physical force and altered his descent by twisting his own momentum.","His figure slammed down behind her, and Dragonheart cut horizontally.","Revona turned halfway and raised her palm.","\"Void Origin Palm.\"","The hollow palm seal met Dragonheart.","Boom!","The clash produced no ordinary explosion. Sword force, void emptiness, divine-vein strength, and seven-colored lightning collided in one compressed point.","The surrounding ground vanished in one area and shattered in another. The barrier of the Eternal Hourglass trembled, and golden laws poured down to stabilize the stage.","Revona’s palm trembled. Max’s sword pressed forward. The Vein of Strength roared louder, and for a moment, Revona was actually being forced back in a direct collision.","That sight brought countless elders across the Divine Realm to their feet. Orion Starfall had pushed Revona into using Return To Nothing. Kaiden Voidmere had almost exiled her. Rakan Thorne had forced her to adapt against the War God Body.","But Max was doing something different. He was pressuring her from everywhere at once. He did not rely on one decisive attack, and he did not rely on one overwhelming technique. He was forcing her mind, her eyes, her body, her realm, and her perception to defend against several completely different threats at the same time.","Dragonheart pressed from close range. The Vein of Strength turned every blocked sword strike into a mountain-splitting collision. The Vein of Speed prevented her from locking down his path for more than a breath.","The Vein of Opening stabilized his foundation whenever the Void Origin Realm tried to hollow his power. The Vein of Vitality let him withstand the drain and recoil of fighting inside her field. Divine King Punishment attacked from above, from behind, from beneath, and from beyond her blind angles.","And every time Revona tried to erase one danger, Max used another to break through the gap left behind.","Max twisted Dragonheart, and a seven-colored bolt descended onto the blade.","\"Punishment Sword Strike.\"","The sword came down with thunder judgment wrapped around its edge. Revona’s Void Origin Eyes flashed, and the lightning on the blade began to vanish. But the sword beneath it still carried divine-vein strength.","She shifted her gaze to the sword, and the physical strike weakened. But the lightning above her condensed into another verdict.","\"Divine King Punishment, Second Verdict.\"","Boom!","The lightning bolt descended directly toward her shoulder. Revona opened the Void Origin Realm wider, causing the bolt to hollow out before impact, but that small expansion forced the realm’s pressure to shift outward for a fraction of a breath.","Max used that fraction. The Vein of Speed activated to its peak, and he appeared inside her defensive range. His left hand left Dragonheart’s hilt for the first time and formed a fist.","\"Vein of Strength.\"","The punch drove forward. Revona’s eyes widened slightly. She erased the first layer of force, but the second layer remained. She hollowed the second, but the third layer arrived through Max’s physical body before the technique structure could be fully read.","Boom!","The punch struck her crossed arms, and Revona was blasted backward across the stage. Her feet carved two long lines into the ground before she steadied herself near the edge of the Void Origin Realm.","A drop of blood fell from the corner of her mouth.","The Divine Realm went crazy.","\"He pushed her that far!\"","\"Max is pressuring Revona even more heavily than Orion did!\"","\"No, this is different. Orion forced her with one supreme destructive attack. Max is making her defend every second!\"","\"She cannot read everything fast enough!\"","\"His divine veins are too strong!\"","\"And the seven-colored lightning is attacking from long range while he fights close!\"","At the Black Dragon Clan, the disciples were shouting so loudly that the entire hall shook. Among the forces watching Revona, the atmosphere became suffocating. Their genius had never looked weak, and she still did not look weak. But she was being pressured, truly pressured.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Revona slowly straightened. The wound beneath her chin, the blood at the corner of her lips, the strain in her aura, and the faint trembling of her fingers all proved that Max’s strategy was working.","Her Void Origin Eyes were still terrifying, yet even they needed to choose what to erase, and Max was constantly creating choices too close together for comfort.","Revona looked at him quietly. \"You are forcing too many sources at once.\"","Max stood amid the seven-colored thunder with Dragonheart in hand and four Divine Veins roaring inside his body. \"That was the idea.\"","Revona’s eyes deepened. \"Then I will stop watching them separately.\"","The Void Origin Realm behind her became silent. Very silent. The emptiness condensed around her eyes, and for the first time in the battle, the whole arena felt the pressure of something far deeper awakening inside Revona’s gaze.","Max smiled faintly, but his grip on Dragonheart tightened."]},{"number":1907,"title":"Chapter 1907: Devouring Flames Domain!","paragraphs":["Revona’s words had barely faded when the entire arena fell silent again.","\"Then I will stop watching them separately.\"","The Void Origin Realm behind her no longer expanded outward. Instead it condensed, drawing inward as the hollow world that had spread across the battlefield began collapsing around her eyes, her palms, and the empty space between her and Max.","The pressure of that emptiness became terrifyingly pure, as if Revona had decided to stop erasing Max’s attacks one by one and instead erase the entire meaning of the battlefield before him.","Max’s eyes sharpened as he felt the change at once. This was no longer the same defensive nullification she had used earlier, nor was it merely the Void Origin Eyes tracking his sword, his lightning, his movement, and his divine-vein rhythm.","This was something much deeper. The Void Origin Realm was gathering all the power it had erased, all the hollow authority it had accumulated, and all the origin-level emptiness that made Revona so frightening into a single point.","The pale light in Revona’s eyes vanished, replaced by absolute darkness without color, weight, or sound. She raised one hand as the air before her palm began to hollow.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","The hollow point solidified before her palm, drawing the emptiness around it into a single condensed core.","\"Return To Nothing.\"","The moment those words fell, the whole stage seemed to lose its hold on existence. The seven-colored lightning around Max dimmed violently, and the cracks in the ground disappeared, not because they were repaired but because the damage, the ground, the sound, and the very concept of impact were being dragged into a silent point of origin emptiness.","The storm of Divine King Punishment trembled while Dragonheart’s hum quieted, and even Max’s four Divine Veins felt the pressure of being hollowed from the outside inward.","Across the Divine Realm, countless spectators lost their voices. They had seen Return To Nothing before.","Against Orion, it had erased the terrifying Starfall Extinction and turned collapsing star power into emptiness. Against Rakan, it had nullified the core force of his strongest War God Body strike. Against Kaiden, it had entered the Final Corridor and hollowed the Void Beyond Return from within.","Now it was being used against Max, and this time Revona was not using it defensively. She was attacking.","The point of nothingness moved toward Max, slow, almost too slow to seem dangerous. But no one laughed at that slowness, because everyone understood that speed was meaningless before it. It did not need to chase like lightning, and it did not need to cut like a sword.","Anything that entered its range would be erased from the foundation, and the more power used to resist it, the more material it would have to return to nothing.","Max stood still for one breath. Then black flames erupted from his body.","Boom!","The stage vanished beneath a wave of darkness. It was not the darkness of the abyss, and it was not the emptiness of void. It was flame, pure flame, but blacker than a moonless night and hungrier than a bottomless beast.","The flames burst from Max’s body, from beneath his feet, from the air around Dragonheart, and from the cracks in space itself, expanding outward in the next instant with terrifying violence.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","Max’s voice sounded from within the black fire.","\"Devouring Flames Domain.\"","The entire arena shook as a vast domain of black flames descended and swallowed both Max and Revona. The flames rose into walls, waves, pillars, and burning curtains so dense that even the viewing formations of the Eternal Hourglass flickered.","For the first time in the final competitive stage, the spectators outside could no longer see the full battle clearly. They could only see an enormous black-flame domain occupying the central arena, its surface constantly writhing as if countless ancient dragons and devouring beasts were moving beneath the fire.","The Divine Realm exploded in shock.","\"Another Pseudo Cosmic Path!\"","\"Black flames!\"","\"How many Pseudo Cosmic Paths does Max Morgan have?\"","\"No, this is impossible. A sword path, lightning path and now even a flames path?\"","\"The domain blocked the view!\"","\"What is happening inside?\"","Even the top geniuses on the pillars were shaken. Rakan Thorne stared at the black-flame domain with wide eyes.","\"That bastard still had another path?\"","Orion Starfall’s expression froze before he laughed in disbelief.","\"I thought he had already shown enough against me. He was hiding this too?\"","Kaiden Voidmere’s eyes narrowed as he tried to sense through the domain, but the black flames swallowed even the faint spatial perception he released.","\"This flame has devouring nature.... If I am not wrong this should be flames form the black dragon bloodline the disciples of the Black Dragon Palace carries among them.\"","Damian Voss’s hand tightened around his sword hilt while Ervin’s abyss-like gaze grew heavier.","Inside the Devouring Flames Domain, the outside world disappeared entirely. There was no audience, no pillars, and no golden arena. Only black fire remained.","Revona stood within the domain, her eyes fully open, her Return To Nothing still moving forward like the condensed will of origin emptiness. The black flames immediately surged toward it, devouring the outer layer of hollow power the moment both forces touched.","For the first time, Return To Nothing slowed.","Max stood opposite her, surrounded by black flames, seven-colored lightning, and the pressure of four opened Divine Veins. His face was calm, but his eyes were sharper than before.","The Devouring Flames Domain did not try to erase Revona’s attack. It consumed. It ate the power that Return To Nothing carried, swallowed the hollow ripples around it, and burned away the erased fragments before they could fully return to origin emptiness.","The black flames curled around the point of nothingness like countless hungry serpents, biting into the surrounding void power again and again.","Revona’s eyes narrowed.","\"Your flames devour nullification.\"","Max replied calmly, \"Not all of it.\"","He was being honest. The Devouring Flames Domain was terrifying, but Return To Nothing was also Revona’s strongest ability. The black flames could devour its outer layers, weaken its momentum, and prevent it from expanding freely, but they could not swallow the entire technique outright.","At the center of Return To Nothing, origin emptiness still remained absolute, and every time the black flames tried to consume too deeply, that emptiness erased the devouring structure before the flames could complete the act."]},{"number":1908,"title":"Chapter 1908: Null Origin Tide!","paragraphs":["Revona raised her other hand as the Void Origin Eyes shone through the black fire.","\"Then I will nullify the devouring power as well.\"","A pale hollow ripple spread from her gaze, and the black flames nearest to Return To Nothing began fading. Max’s Devouring Flames Domain roared as the flames surged again, trying to feed on the nullifying ripple.","But Revona’s Void Origin Eyes locked onto the structure of the devouring authority and erased several layers of it before it could bite back. For a moment, the battlefield inside the domain settled into a horrifying balance.","Max’s black flames devoured the outer power of Return To Nothing, while Revona’s eyes nullified the devouring process itself.","Neither side could completely overwhelm the other, but the clash was forcing both of them toward their limits. Max’s four Divine Veins roared inside him, Divine King Punishment continued rumbling above, and Dragonheart trembled in his hand.","The Devouring Flames Domain kept burning, yet Revona’s Return To Nothing still advanced inch by inch.","Max’s eyes turned colder.","’Not enough.’","The four Divine Veins had pushed his body beyond what most geniuses could imagine, and the Devouring Flames Domain had created the hidden battlefield he needed.","Divine King Punishment forced pressure from above while Dragonheart and the Emotion Severing Path still waited for the decisive moment. But against Revona’s fully awakened Void Origin Eyes and Return To Nothing, even that was not enough to guarantee victory.","He needed a gap. A real gap. Something Revona could not see in time, something that would arrive outside the rhythm of what her eyes were reading.","Max inhaled slowly. Then the 5000 Draconic Essences within him awakened, all of them at once.","Boom!","His body erupted with a roar that sounded like thousands of dragons awakening inside a single human frame.","The black flames bent around him, the Divine King Punishment trembled above him, and his veins, bones, flesh, and blood all released an ancient draconic pressure that caused even the Devouring Flames Domain to expand violently.","The first hundred essences ignited. Then five hundred. Then a thousand. Then two thousand. Then all five thousand Draconic Essences blazed at once, and Max’s physical aura changed completely. It became savage, ancient, oppressive, and impossibly heavy.","Then black dragon scales spread across his body.","\"Dragon Scales Transformation.\"","The transformation did not appear as a simple armor this time.","The scales emerged with the full support of the 5000 Draconic Essences, each one looking like a fragment of a chaotic black dragon’s hide, hard enough to resist divine weapons and dense enough to carry the weight of ancient bloodline pressure.","His hands became claw-like beneath the scale armor, his shoulders widened slightly, and his pupils sharpened as the aura around him rose beyond the level created by the four Divine Veins alone.","The Vein of Opening stabilized his foundation. The Vein of Vitality fed the transformation. The Vein of Speed sharpened his movement, and the Vein of Strength fused with the draconic essences.","But the full Dragon Scales Transformation pushed everything further, far further, and Max’s physical strength broke past its previous limit.","Revona’s expression finally became truly solemn. The Return To Nothing continued moving, but Max stepped forward through its pressure.","One step, and the black flames around his scales were erased. The lightning near his shoulder vanished, but his body did not stop.","Second step, and the Devouring Flames Domain roared, swallowing more of the outer void power.","Third step, and the 5000 Draconic Essences pushed his body forward against the hollowing force.","Revona’s eyes flashed as she raised her hand and focused Return To Nothing directly toward his chest.","Max disappeared. Not with space, and not with ordinary speed. The Vein of Speed, Dragon Scales Transformation, and 5000 Draconic Essences erupted together, and his body moved so violently that the black flames behind him exploded into a tidal wave.","Revona’s eyes followed Max, and they still found him.","Even inside the Devouring Flames Domain, even with black flames devouring perception from every direction, even with Divine King Punishment raining seven-colored thunder from above, and even with four Divine Veins roaring inside Max’s body alongside 5000 Draconic Essences pushing his Dragon Scales Transformation beyond its previous limit, those terrifying Void Origin Eyes still locked onto his movement.","But at that exact moment, the clone moved out of his dimensional space.","Hidden deep within the black flames, where the outside world could not see and where even Revona’s sight was being forced to divide itself among too many dangers at once, the clone released the Time Concept.","It did not attack Revona directly, and it did not create killing intent. It did not aim to pierce, burn, crush, or bind her. It only touched the rhythm of time inside the Devouring Flames Domain with delicate precision.","For a fraction of a breath, the black flames near Revona slowed. For another fraction, the flow around Max’s body accelerated. The difference was tiny, too tiny for ordinary geniuses to notice. But against someone like Revona, even that small delay should have been enough.","Max’s figure vanished from the path her Void Origin Eyes were reading and reappeared at her side, his scaled body moving with the combined force of the Vein of Speed, Vein of Strength, Dragon Scales Transformation, and 5000 Draconic Essences. Dragonheart rose in his hand, and the Emotion Severing Path condensed along the edge of the blade with cold and silent killing precision.","Revona’s eyes shifted. The clone tightened the Time Concept, and a brief temporal heaviness descended around her body. It was not a full stop, and it was not enough to freeze the world, but it was enough to delay her action for the smallest moment.","Max’s sword began to fall. For the first time, the strike seemed as though it would truly arrive before Revona’s Void Origin Eyes could perfectly align with the present.","Then Revona’s expression changed. Not into panic, and not into fear, but into absolute calm.","Her eyes stopped chasing Max’s sword. They stopped chasing the clone. They stopped chasing the lightning, the black flames, the draconic aura, and the divine-vein force. Instead, the Void Origin Realm inside her pupils suddenly expanded outward.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","Her voice was quiet, but it spread through the black flames like a verdict from emptiness itself.","\"Null Origin Tide.\""]},{"number":1909,"title":"Chapter 1909: Stripped Away of All His Powers!","paragraphs":["Boom!","A pale-gray wave erupted from Revona’s body in every direction. It was not like Return To Nothing. Return To Nothing was a condensed point, a terrifying origin of emptiness that gathered all nullified power into one core and returned everything before it to nothingness.","This attack was different. It was larger, wider, and far more reckless. Instead of gathering power into a single point, it released the Void Origin Realm outward as a massive domain-like tide of nullifying energy that spread in all directions at once.","The black flames were the first to touch it. They did not devour it, though they tried. The Devouring Flames Domain roared like a starving beast, sending countless black-flame currents toward the pale-gray tide.","Under ordinary circumstances, Max’s black flames would eat power, burn authority, and consume even the structure of techniques.","But the Null Origin Tide was not a normal technique. It carried the same foundation as Revona’s fully awakened Void Origin Eyes, and because it spread in every direction at once, there was no single core for the flames to swallow cleanly.","The black flames touched the tide. Then they vanished. Not burned out, and not weakened. Simply vanished.","Max’s eyes widened slightly. The seven-colored lightning of Divine King Punishment descended from above, trying to pierce the tide with heavenly judgment, but the moment the lightning entered the pale-gray wave, its destructive authority dulled, flickered, and disappeared as if it had never been released.","The black flames around Max’s body dimmed, the draconic pressure covering his scales cracked, and the roaring force of the 5000 Draconic Essences inside him suddenly dropped like a collapsing tide.","Then the four Divine Veins were struck. The Vein of Opening dimmed. The Vein of Vitality stopped surging. The Vein of Speed lost its brilliance, and the Vein of Strength fell silent.","Max felt it all vanish from his body in a single breath. His terrifying physical pressure disappeared, and the full power of the 5000 Draconic Essences was suppressed.","The Dragon Scales Transformation covering his body began fading layer by layer, the Devouring Flames Domain lost its devouring authority, and even the storm world of Divine King Punishment trembled above him before breaking apart into scattered seven-colored sparks.","For the first time in the entire Cosmic Ascension Conference, Max felt his body become empty. Not injured, and not exhausted in the normal sense.","Just empty. It felt as though someone had dried every source of power inside his body and left only the shape of a person behind.","The divine veins that had thundered a moment ago became silent, and the draconic essences that had roared like thousands of dragons became still.","The dragon scales that had made his body stronger than ever before faded from his skin, the black flames around him no longer answered his command properly, and even the seven-colored lightning above the domain collapsed into darkness.","Only Dragonheart remained in his hand, and only the Emotion Severing Path around the sword still existed. But even that was beginning to dull.","The cold severing aura on Dragonheart flickered faintly as the Null Origin Tide pressed against it, and for a moment, even Max felt the edge of his forbidden path being worn down by that dreadful wave of nullification.","The clone’s Time Concept also collapsed. Max’s pupils contracted as the temporal ripple that should have delayed Revona shattered the instant the Null Origin Tide touched it. The slowed moment vanished, and the accelerated flow around Max disappeared.","The difference in timing that he had created was erased so completely that even the memory of the advantage felt fragile.","’Even time concept was useless? Do I have to use my time Pseudo Cosmic Path?’","For the first time, genuine shock crossed Max’s eyes. He had expected Revona to resist, and he had expected her to nullify part of the time distortion after noticing the clone. He had not expected her to release a domain-scale nullifying wave that destroyed every layer of his preparation at once.","The black flames thinned, and the hidden clone was forced back into the darkness, its Time Concept fully severed from the battle rhythm.","Revona stood in the center of the pale-gray tide, blood still at the corner of her lips from using Return To Nothing earlier, her face paler than before, and her aura clearly strained.","This new attack had a cost, a heavy one. Her Void Origin Realm trembled around her, and even her eyes showed faint cracks of exhaustion.","But she was still standing, while Max stood before her with nearly all of his power-ups stripped away.","The black-flame domain still enclosed them from the outside world, but inside, its authority had been hollowed until it looked like a dying night sky.","Revona looked at him quietly.","\"Your speed is gone.\"","Max did not answer.","\"Your strength is gone.\"","The pale-gray tide continued pressing forward.","\"Your dragon transformation is gone.\"","Dragonheart trembled slightly in his hand.","\"Your flames cannot devour this.\"","The remaining Emotion Severing Path flickered faintly.","\"Even your time concept has been nullified.\"","Revona lifted her hand, and the remnants of Return To Nothing formed again beside the spreading Null Origin Tide. It was weaker than before, but with Max’s power stripped away, even a weakened Return To Nothing was terrifying enough.","\"Accept your defeat, Max Morgan.\"","The words echoed inside the fading black flames. Outside the Devouring Flames Domain, the entire Divine Realm still could not see what was happening.","They could only watch the black-fire barrier tremble violently, then dim as if something inside had erased its power from within. The spectators grew restless, and the top geniuses on the pillars narrowed their eyes, sensing that the flow of the battle had changed drastically.","Inside the domain, Max looked at Revona in silence. His body felt dry. His divine veins were silent, and the draconic essences no longer answered.","The Dragon Scales Transformation had fully faded, Divine King Punishment had collapsed, and the Devouring Flames Domain was dying. His clone’s Time Concept had failed. Only Dragonheart remained, along with the dulling Emotion Severing Path.","For any other genius, this would have been despair. But Max slowly smiled. It was not a wide smile. It was light, calm, and almost appreciative.","\"You are the strongest genius I have ever faced and the only one to push me this far.\"","Revona’s eyes flickered slightly. Max meant it. Not Damian. Not Ervin. Not Orion. Not Kaiden. Not Rakan. Not Aurelian.","At this moment, with all of his layered powers stripped away by her fully awakened Void Origin Eyes, with his Devouring Flames Domain weakened, with his time strategy broken, and with his body nearly emptied of strength, Max truly acknowledged her.","Revona was the most difficult opponent he had faced so far.","But that didn’t mean he would accept his defeat."]},{"number":1910,"title":"Chapter 1910 - 1%","paragraphs":["Max closed his eyes and entered a calm meditative state.","Then something changed inside him. At first, it was only a faint point of light in the depths of Max’s body. Then another appeared. Then another. One by one, countless specks of light began shining across his body like stars appearing in a dark sky.","It was beautiful, too beautiful for a battlefield. His body did not burn with ordinary aura, and it did not release bloodline pressure. It did not erupt with lightning, flame, dragon scales, divine veins, or sword force.","Instead, he began to shine like a night sky filled with distant stars. The light was dark, deep, and vast, and every star within it seemed to contain a separate distance, a separate direction, and a separate space folded beyond imagination.","Revona’s eyes sharpened as the Null Origin Tide touched the starlight. Nothing happened.","The pale-gray nullifying wave flowed over Max’s body, trying to erase the new power, but the starlight did not dim. It did not resist in the normal sense, and it did not clash or push back. It simply existed on a scale that Revona’s nullifying force could not define properly.","Revona’s pupils contracted, and for the first time, horror appeared in her eyes. She could not nullify it. Her Void Origin Eyes could not trace its foundation, and the Null Origin Tide could not erase its structure.","Even Return To Nothing could not immediately identify what it was supposed to return to nothingness. It felt as though the power rising from Max did not belong to the same layer of existence as everything else she had erased.","Max released a small breath. The breath sounded soft, but as it left his lips, the entire Devouring Flames Domain became still.","’Finally, I can tap into this power again even if this percentage of power was only 1% of what I previously tapped into.’","A memory passed through Max’s mind.","Orion. The hidden temporal link. The legacy of the Dimensional Keeper.","Back then, through that strange connection between himself and the last user of the Dimensional Keeper legacy, Max had briefly tapped into the legacy of the Dimensional Keeper that should have been far beyond his current self.","Since then, he had spent what felt like thousands of years in accumulated comprehension, trial, and repeated failure, trying to touch that same state again.","Most attempts had failed, and some had barely succeeded for a breath. But now, under the pressure of Revona’s Null Origin Tide, with all external powers stripped away, the deepest part of the Dimensional Keeper legacy finally answered him again.","The starlight in Max’s body deepened. It no longer looked like ordinary stars. It looked like countless dimensions shining in a dark sky. Each point of light felt like a sealed world, and each faint glow carried the weight of distance, space, time, and existence itself.","This was not the power of his Divine Veins. Not the power of his black flames. Not the power of his lightning. Not the power of his draconic essences.","This was the Dimensional Keeper legacy, a power that did not simply use space but kept dimensions, scaled far beyond the level Revona’s current nullification could fully erase.","Max raised Dragonheart. The Emotion Severing Path around the sword, which had almost gone dull, suddenly brightened with cold and terrifying clarity.","The starlight from the Dimensional Keeper legacy flowed into the blade, not as ordinary energy but as a vast dimensional authority that gave the severing edge a foundation Revona’s eyes could no longer understand.","Revona reacted instantly. The Null Origin Tide surged, and Return To Nothing condensed before her once again. She poured everything into both attacks. The pale-gray wave rushed toward Max from all directions, nullifying the remaining black flames completely, and the weakened but still terrifying Return To Nothing formed at the center of the tide.","Together they became the strongest defense and attack Revona could release in that instant.","Max stepped forward. The starlight around his body made every step look as if he was crossing different layers of space. He raised Dragonheart above his head, then slashed down.","\"Emotion Severing Sword.\"","The sword descended. There was no thunderous roar at first, only a single beautiful line of dark starlight and cold severing force. Then everything in its path split.","The Null Origin Tide was cut open. The massive domain-like wave that had erased Max’s divine veins, dragon essences, black flames, lightning, dragon scales, and time distortion was severed from its own nullifying foundation, and the pale-gray tide split apart like a curtain before Dragonheart.","Return To Nothing followed. Revona’s strongest technique, already gathered again at the center of the wave, tried to drag the sword strike back into origin emptiness. But this time, the severing force was powered by the Dimensional Keeper legacy.","The sword edge did not remain only in the present space where Revona’s eyes could trace it. It seemed to cut from several dimensions at once, passing through direction, distance, timing, and meaning before Revona could fully lock onto one layer.","The Return To Nothing trembled. Then it split, fully. The origin emptiness was cut apart from its core.","Revona’s eyes widened. For the first time, she could not understand what had happened fast enough. The sword light had already passed. The Null Origin Tide collapsed, Return To Nothing shattered, and the Devouring Flames Domain, which had nearly vanished, was blown apart by the aftermath of the strike.","The black flames opened, and the outside world finally saw the stage again. But by the time the spectators could understand what they were seeing, Max was already standing beside Revona.","Dragonheart rested against her neck. The blade did not cut her skin, but it was there. Still. Absolute.","Revona stood frozen in place. Her pale eyes were wide, the Void Origin Realm behind her was gone, and the remaining traces of Return To Nothing scattered into fading ash-like emptiness around her.","Blood slipped from the corner of her mouth, but she did not seem to notice it. Her entire attention remained on Max and on the sword touching her neck.","The whole Divine Realm fell silent. No one had seen the full battle inside the domain, but they had seen the final moment.","They had seen a dark star-like radiance split open the dying black flames, a sword line cut through the last wave of Revona’s nullification, and Max appear beside her before anyone could follow his movement.","Revona slowly turned her eyes toward him.","\"What was that power?\"","Max’s starlight slowly faded. His body looked exhausted now, truly exhausted, but his hand remained steady around Dragonheart.","\"A power I have not fully mastered yet.\"","Revona stared at him for a long moment. Then she closed her eyes, and her voice came very soft.","\"I lose.\"","Angelina Valerius’s voice descended over the silent arena.","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Revona Defeated.]","The screen above the stage updated.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 22]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 21]","For one breath, no one moved. Then the Divine Realm erupted with a roar that seemed capable of shaking every ancient land beneath the heavens."]},{"number":1911,"title":"Chapter 1911: Damian vs Ervin!","paragraphs":["The roar caused by Max Morgan’s victory over Revona did not fade quickly.","Even after the transfer light carried both of them back to their pillars, the Divine Realm remained trapped in the shock of what had just happened. Revona had been the first of the undefeated four to fall, but she had not fallen cheaply.","She had forced Max to reveal more power than anyone else in the entire Cosmic Ascension Conference, including the Devouring Flames Domain, Divine King Punishment, his four Divine Veins, the full release of 5000 Draconic Essences, the Dragon Scales Transformation, the strange time power connected to his clone, and finally that mysterious star-like legacy power that even Revona’s nullification could not fully erase.","No one could treat her defeat as weakness. If anything, the battle had proved that Revona’s strength was terrifying enough to push Max into revealing a depth that had been hidden even after all his previous victories.","But the final stretch did not stop. Angelina Valerius waited until the golden laws of the Eternal Hourglass restored the stage again.","The black flames vanished completely, the cracked ground became smooth, and the residual aura of nullification, lightning, draconic pressure, and dimensional starlight faded from the arena one by one. Only after the battlefield returned to its original state did she raise her hand again.","\"The second battle among the remaining undefeated participants will now be selected.\"","The giant screen above the arena changed once more. Only three undefeated names remained shining at the top.","[Max Morgan]","[Ervin]","[Damian Voss]","Revona’s name had not disappeared, but it had moved slightly below them now.","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 21]","The sight alone caused countless spectators to inhale deeply. One monster had fallen, and three remained.","The names spun again. Max Morgan. Ervin. Damian Voss. The light moved faster and faster, and the entire Divine Realm grew quiet once more.","After watching Max and Revona’s battle, no one thought their hearts could withstand another immediate peak collision, but the Eternal Hourglass clearly had no intention of showing mercy.","The first name stopped.","[Damian Voss]","The Sword God Palace disciples immediately straightened. The second name continued rotating. It passed Max Morgan. Then it stopped.","[Ervin]","The screen enlarged.","[Final Undefeated Battle]","[Damian Voss vs Ervin]","The entire Divine Realm erupted again. Sword Sovereign Heaven stood against Abyssal Origin Descent, the strongest genius of the Sword God Palace against the most mysterious spear genius of the conference.","One had cut through divine light, war body power, curses, dawn authority, and even Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth. The other had swallowed star power, heavenly luminance, curse authority, void-space corridors, and nearly everything that had entered the range of his abyss.","This battle carried a different kind of pressure from Max against Revona. Max and Revona’s battle had been a clash between overwhelming layered power and absolute nullification, while Damian and Ervin’s battle felt like a confrontation between two ancient paths that should never have been placed in the same world, a sword that ruled all blades against an abyss that returned all things to depth.","On his pillar, Damian Voss slowly opened his eyes. His expression remained calm, but his sword intent had already begun to rise.","Ervin also stood quietly. His black spear rested in his hand, and his gaze was as deep as a sea with no bottom. He did not speak, but the faint shadow of the broken gate behind him seemed to stir even before he moved.","Rakan Thorne crossed his arms, his grin returning.","\"This one will not be clean.\"","Orion Starfall leaned forward.","\"No. Both of them are too dangerous for that.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked at Ervin with a serious gaze.","\"If Damian’s sword cuts the gate before it opens deep enough, Damian wins.\"","Morgana Starveil said softly, \"And if the abyss swallows the sword rhythm before the final edict descends, Ervin wins. Though I am not sure how Ervin’s path works.\"","Revona sat quietly on her pillar, still pale from the previous battle, but her eyes had not lost their sharpness.","Max stood silently and watched. He had fought Ervin before and had seen the strange depth of Abyssal Origin Descent, and he had also seen Damian’s Sword Sovereign Heaven cut through concepts that most people could not even touch.","This battle was not one where either side could hold back and slowly test each other. If either Damian or Ervin tried to begin cautiously, the other would seize the rhythm and crush them immediately.","Angelina Valerius looked toward both participants.","\"Damian Voss.\"","\"Ervin.\"","\"Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended. Damian appeared on one side of the central arena, sword in hand, his robes moving softly around him. Ervin appeared opposite him, black spear lowered, his shadow stretching strangely behind him.","For a few breaths, neither moved. Then Damian spoke first.","\"You have not shown everything.\"","Ervin’s voice was calm. \"Neither have you.\"","Damian’s hand tightened around his sword. \"Then we should not waste time.\"","Ervin raised his spear slightly. \"Agreed.\"","Angelina Valerius lowered her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","The moment the words appeared, both of them released their Pseudo Cosmic Paths. There was no probing strike, no opening exchange, and no cautious movement.","Damian’s sword rose, and the sky behind him split into a vast sword world. Sword-edge mountains appeared, rivers of sword light flowed through the air, an ancient sword altar stood at the center, and high above it a silent palace appeared around an empty throne.","A single sword hung before that throne, radiating a pressure that made every weapon in the audience tremble.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven.\"","At the same time, Ervin planted his black spear into the ground. The stage beneath him darkened, and a black sea rose from nowhere, silent and endless, spreading beneath his feet until the entire arena seemed to stand above an abyssal ocean.","Ancient waves rolled without sound. In the distance, a broken gate emerged from the depths, half submerged, enormous, ancient, and covered in unreadable symbols. The moment it appeared, the light of Damian’s sword world dimmed slightly near the edges.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","Boom!","The two Pseudo Cosmic Paths collided before their masters even moved. Sword light pressed downward while abyssal depth rose upward, and the center of the arena became divided between a silver-white sword heaven and a bottomless black sea.","The stage cracked from the pressure, and the Eternal Hourglass barrier brightened instantly as golden laws poured around the battlefield.","Damian moved first.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, First Edict, All Blades Refuse Submission.\"","Countless sword lights descended from the sword heaven, not as random attacks but as edicts of submission. Every sword line carried authority that forced weapons, techniques, and killing intent to lower themselves before Damian’s blade."]},{"number":1912,"title":"Chapter 1912: An Intense Battle!","paragraphs":["Ervin raised his spear.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, First Depth Tide.\"","The black sea rose in a towering wave of abyssal water that met the falling sword lights. The sword edict cut through the first layer, then the second, then the third, but each time the sword light continued deeper, the abyss swallowed part of its sharpness.","The first wave split apart, though the sword lights that passed through it had already dimmed by half.","Ervin stepped forward.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Deep Current Thrust.\"","His spear pierced out, and a black current followed the spear tip, moving not across the surface of the stage but beneath the sword heaven’s pressure, as though it wanted to attack from the depth beneath Damian’s own footing.","Damian’s eyes shifted.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Second Edict, One Sword Divides Heaven.\"","A single sword light descended and split the incoming current apart, but Ervin had already vanished into the shadow of the black wave. He appeared to Damian’s left and thrust again.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Gate Shadow Thrust.\"","The spear carried the shadow of the broken gate. Damian turned his sword sideways.","\"White Horizon Guard.\"","Clang!","The spear struck the sword, and the impact forced both of them back half a step. Only half a step, but that was enough to make the entire arena erupt.","\"They are equal in the first collision!\"","\"Damian’s sword cut the abyssal tide, but Ervin’s depth weakened the sword edict!\"","\"This will be close!\"","Damian did not give Ervin time to expand the abyss freely. His sword moved again.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Third Edict, Blade Meets The Depth.\"","A massive sword shadow descended from above, aiming directly at the black sea beneath Ervin. It did not target Ervin’s body. It targeted the connection between Abyssal Origin Descent and the battlefield, as if Damian wanted to cut the sea itself apart before it could deepen.","Ervin’s gaze became colder.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Gate of the First Depth.\"","The broken gate opened slightly, and a deep, ancient pressure surged from beyond it. The descending sword shadow struck the sea, but the moment the Gate of the First Depth opened, the black water rose in a circular spiral and wrapped around the sword shadow like a hungry vortex.","The sword continued cutting while the abyss continued pulling, one wanting to divide and the other wanting to sink.","The clash lasted three breaths. Then both powers exploded.","Damian slid back several steps. Ervin also retreated, his spear leaving a long mark across the stage. Blood appeared at the corner of Ervin’s mouth, and a thin cut appeared across Damian’s sleeve. Both had been touched, and both had been forced.","Damian raised his sword again without changing expression.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Fourth Edict, Palace Sword Descends.\"","The palace above the sword altar brightened, and a palace-sized sword descended from the sky, carrying an oppressive sword authority that made countless swordsmen across the Divine Realm feel their hearts tremble.","This strike was not merely sharp. It felt like the judgment of the sword palace itself, as if all paths beneath it had to be split open.","Ervin looked up. The black sea beneath him became still, too still. Then the broken gate opened wider.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Return To Depth.\"","A whirlpool appeared beneath the descending palace sword. The enormous sword tried to cut through it, but the abyssal pull wrapped around it from all sides, dragging layers of sword authority downward. Sparks of silver-white sword light erupted across the sea surface while black waves rose and swallowed them again.","Damian stepped forward, strengthening the palace sword. Ervin also stepped forward, strengthening the abyssal whirlpool. For a terrifying moment, neither gave ground.","Then Damian changed the sword’s path. Instead of forcing the palace sword straight down, he tilted his blade, and the palace sword suddenly split into three sword shadows, each attacking from a different angle.","Ervin’s Return To Depth swallowed two, but the third cut through, and blood splashed from Ervin’s shoulder.","The Sword God Palace disciples roared.","But before they could celebrate, Ervin’s spear moved. He had allowed the third sword shadow to cut him in exchange for a path.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Deep Current Reversal.\"","The abyssal current that had swallowed the first two sword shadows reversed violently, carrying fragments of Damian’s own sword authority back toward him.","Damian’s eyes narrowed, and his sword flashed three times. He cut apart the reversed current, but one fragment still passed through and struck his chest. His body slid backward, and a small line of blood appeared at his lips.","The arena became even more heated.","\"They are both injured!\"","\"Ervin used Damian’s sword force against him!\"","\"Damian cut through Return To Depth, but Ervin turned the swallowed sword authority back!\"","Max watched silently, his eyes deep.","This battle was exactly as dangerous as he expected. Damian’s sword was terrifying because it could cut the critical line behind any technique, while Ervin’s abyss was terrifying because anything that entered it could be swallowed, delayed, sunk, reversed, or returned through a deeper path.","It was not a simple matter of sword against spear. It was the clash between severance and depth.","Damian stepped forward again, his aura sharpening.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Fifth Edict, Sword Heart Cannot Be Drowned.\"","The sword before the throne vibrated faintly, and Damian’s entire body became covered in sword light. For the first time, the black sea beneath him failed to drag his sword intent downward. His sword heart stabilized itself above the abyss, refusing to sink, refusing to slow, and refusing to be swallowed.","Ervin’s expression became more serious. Damian vanished, and his sword appeared before Ervin’s throat. Ervin raised his spear and blocked.","Clang!","Damian struck again. Then again. Then again. Each sword attack was clean, deadly, and aimed at the weakest transition points in Ervin’s spear path.","Ervin defended with Hollow Moon Guard, Deep Current Reversal, and Gate Shadow Thrust, but Damian’s sword heart had become too stable, and the abyss could no longer swallow the outer rhythm of the sword as easily as before.","A cut appeared across Ervin’s arm, then another near his ribs, then a third along his thigh. But Ervin did not retreat. His black spear moved more slowly now, and deeper. He stopped trying to match Damian’s speed and began letting every sword strike fall closer before answering.","It looked dangerous, almost suicidal, but each time Damian’s sword approached, Ervin’s spear rose from a deeper angle, forcing Damian to adjust at the last instant.","Damian’s sword cut Ervin’s shoulder. Ervin’s spear grazed Damian’s waist. Damian’s sword pierced through Ervin’s defense. Ervin’s abyssal current struck Damian’s chest. Both of them were now bleeding, and neither gave ground.","Then Ervin opened the broken gate again.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Second Depth Pressure.\"","The entire black sea sank, not downward but deeper, and the pressure changed at once. The sword lights around Damian became slower, as though each slash now had to pass through layers of unseen depth before reaching Ervin.","Damian’s Sword Heart Cannot Be Drowned resisted the pressure, but even that edict could not completely ignore the Second Depth.","Damian’s gaze sharpened.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Sixth Edict, Bleeding Sword Severance.\"","He slashed his own palm across the blade, and blood touched the sword. The sword heaven changed again. The blade became crimson white, and the sharpness around Damian rose to a level that made even Ervin’s abyss tremble.","This was a sword edict fueled by Damian’s blood and sword heart together, used only when ordinary sword authority could no longer cut deep enough."]},{"number":1913,"title":"Chapter 1913: The Remaining Battles!","paragraphs":["Damian attacked with a single sword, and the Second Depth Pressure split apart. A wound opened across Ervin’s chest, and he retreated several steps, blood falling onto the black sea beneath his feet.","The Sword God Palace disciples shouted with wild excitement.","But Ervin looked down at the wound, then raised his eyes. The broken gate behind him opened a little more.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","His voice was still calm.","\"Gate of the Second Depth.\"","Boom!","The gate opened, and a darkness deeper than the black sea appeared beyond it. The entire arena trembled. Damian’s Bleeding Sword Severance pressed forward, but the moment the Gate of the Second Depth opened, the abyss stopped retreating.","The black sea rose in a terrifying column behind Ervin, and a pressure far heavier than before descended onto Damian’s sword heaven.","The sword palace shook. The sword altar trembled. Even the empty throne above the sword heaven seemed to be pulled downward by the depth beyond the gate.","Ervin raised his spear.","\"Second Depth Spear.\"","The abyssal sea gathered around the spear tip.","\"Sunken World.\"","The spear thrust out, and a whole world seemed to sink behind that thrust.","Damian raised his sword with both hands.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Final Edict.\"","The single sword before the empty throne descended.","\"Throne Of The Only Sword.\"","All sword lights vanished. The mountains of sword edges faded, the rivers of sword light disappeared, and the palace dimmed. Only Damian’s sword remained. One sword, one will, and one throne.","The entire Divine Realm stopped breathing.","Damian slashed. Ervin thrust. Throne Of The Only Sword met Sunken World.","The collision did not explode immediately. For one breath, the whole arena became still. Then the stage shattered.","Golden laws surged madly around the barrier as sword authority and abyssal depth tore through the center of the battlefield. Damian’s sword cut into the sinking world, splitting layer after layer of abyssal pressure.","Ervin’s spear pushed forward, forcing the sword line deeper and deeper into darkness. Every inch of the clash felt like a decision between two possible endings. If Damian’s sword cut one layer further, Ervin would fall, and if Ervin’s abyss sank the sword one breath longer, Damian would lose.","Both of them poured everything into the clash. Damian’s hand bled along the sword hilt, and Ervin’s chest wound tore open further. The broken gate behind Ervin groaned, and the empty throne behind Damian trembled. Neither retreated.","Crack!","The sword line cut through Sunken World, and the abyssal spear shadow split apart.","The Sword God Palace erupted in joy.","But Ervin did not stop. His eyes became deeper than ever before.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","The broken gate behind him opened to its widest point yet.","\"Second Depth Spear.\"","His voice was quiet, but it carried through the entire arena.","\"Abyss Returns All Roads.\"","The shattered Sunken World did not disappear. It returned, not as the same attack but as countless fragments of abyssal route gathering behind Damian’s sword line.","The paths Damian had already cut became roads leading back toward him, each one carrying a remnant of Ervin’s depth. Damian’s Final Edict had cut through the direct attack, but Ervin had hidden his last move inside the broken routes left behind by the clash itself.","Damian’s eyes changed. He realized it a fraction too late. He turned his sword, and the Throne Of The Only Sword cut backward, severing most of the returning abyssal roads.","But not all. One road remained, a narrow black path no wider than a spear tip that slipped through the edge of the sword’s final arc and appeared before Damian’s chest.","Ervin appeared at the end of that road. His spear stopped against Damian’s heart. At the same time, Damian’s sword stopped at Ervin’s throat. Both weapons reached their targets, but Ervin’s spear was one breath closer. One tiny margin. One impossible fraction.","The entire arena froze. Blood dripped from Damian’s lips, and blood also fell from Ervin’s throat where Damian’s sword edge had barely touched the skin. Neither moved.","For several breaths, the whole Divine Realm remained silent. Then Damian looked down at the spear touching his chest. His expression remained calm. After a long moment, he lowered his sword.","\"I lost.\"","The words were quiet, but they shook the entire Divine Realm.","Angelina Valerius announced the result immediately.","[Winner: Ervin.]","[Damian Voss Defeated.]","The screen above the arena updated.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 22]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Damian Voss]","[Total Battles Fought: 22]","[Total Wins: 21]","For a breath, the Sword God Palace was completely silent. Then even there, many disciples slowly clenched their fists, not in shame but in pain and respect. Damian had not been crushed, and he had not been overwhelmed.","He had pushed Ervin to the very brink, forced him to open the Gate of the Second Depth wider than before, and nearly ended the battle with Throne Of The Only Sword.","The difference between victory and defeat had been so small that countless spectators were still unsure whether they had seen it clearly.","At the hidden forces watching Ervin, the silence was even heavier. Ervin had won, but his victory had come by the smallest possible margin.","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, Damian sheathed his sword slowly. Ervin lowered his spear. For the first time, a faint trace of exhaustion appeared on Ervin’s face.","Damian looked at him and said, \"You won.\"","Ervin replied calmly, \"Your final sword attack was also very strong.\"","Damian nodded once. \"I know but it wasn’t strong enough.\"","Ervin gave a slight nod.","The transfer light descended and returned both of them to their pillars.","The second undefeated record had been broken.","Damian Voss had fallen, and only two participants still stood undefeated, Max Morgan and Ervin.","However, the moment the Divine Realm erupted into discussion about the final champion being decided between those two, Angelina Valerius raised her hand once again.","Her calm gesture immediately pressed down upon the chaotic noise spreading through the Eternal Hourglass, and the great screen above the arena shifted from the battle result to the complete ranking rules of the final competitive stage.","\"The winner of the Cosmic Ascension Conference will not be decided by one undefeated pairing alone,\" Angelina said, her voice clear and steady. \"This stage is still based on total victories.\"","The crowd quieted. The defeated geniuses on the pillars also looked toward her.","Angelina continued, \"Max Morgan and Ervin remain undefeated, but several important battles among the top four have not yet taken place. Those battles will still affect the final number of victories, the ranking order beneath the champion, and the possibility of equal records.\"","The four names appeared once again.","[Max Morgan]","[Ervin]","[Revona]","[Damian Voss]","Then the remaining matchups appeared beneath them.","[Ervin vs Revona]","[Max Morgan vs Damian Voss]","[Damian Voss vs Revona]","[Max Morgan vs Ervin]","The moment those four matchups appeared, the entire Divine Realm became heated again.","Angelina looked over the arena and said, \"Ervin must still face Revona. Max Morgan must still face Damian Voss. Damian Voss and Revona must also battle each other. After those battles, Max Morgan and Ervin will have their final confrontation.\"","The great screen flashed with golden light.","\"After all remaining battles are completed, the participant with the highest total number of wins will become the champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\""]},{"number":1914,"title":"Chapter 1914: Ervin vs Revona!","paragraphs":["The explanation caused the atmosphere to become even heavier. Damian’s loss did not make him irrelevant, and Revona’s loss did not remove her from the stage’s importance.","Ervin still needed to prove whether his abyss could swallow Revona’s nullification, and Max still had to face Damian’s Sword Sovereign Heaven before reaching Ervin.","This also meant that the final battle between Max and Ervin would become even more terrifying, since every prior result would sharpen the pressure surrounding it.","Rakan Thorne grinned from his pillar.","\"Good. They still have to fight everyone properly.\"","Orion Starfall laughed softly.","\"That is fair. A round-robin should not let anyone escape a monster just because another monster fell first.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked at the projected matchups.","\"Ervin against Revona will be difficult. Damian against Max may be even worse.\"","Morgana Starveil smiled faintly.","\"And Damian against Revona will decide which of the fallen undefeated monsters stands higher.\"","Damian Voss stood silently on his pillar, his expression calm despite his recent defeat. His sword had lost to Ervin by the smallest margin, but his battle intent had not weakened, and when his gaze moved toward Max, the sword intent around him became colder and more refined.","Revona sat with her eyes half-closed, still recovering from her terrifying battle against Max. She had lost, but no one doubted her strength. If anything, everyone now looked at her with even deeper fear, because they had seen how far she had pushed Max before falling.","Ervin stood quietly with his black spear in hand. Max also stood calmly, Dragonheart resting at his waist.","The two undefeated participants had not yet faced each other, but the path toward their final battle was now clear. Before Max and Ervin could decide the crown, the remaining top-four battles had to burn through the stage.","The Cosmic Ascension Conference had not ended. It had entered its most dangerous stretch.","Angelina Valerius allowed the explanation to settle across the Eternal Hourglass.","The four remaining top matchups shone above the arena, each one heavy enough to decide not only records but pride, reputation, and the final shape of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Even after Max Morgan defeated Revona and Ervin defeated Damian, nothing had become simple. If anything, the path to the championship had become even more intense, because every remaining battle among the top four now carried the weight of the entire Divine Realm’s attention.","The giant screen shifted again.","[Remaining Top Four Battles]","[Ervin vs Revona]","[Max Morgan vs Damian Voss]","[Damian Voss vs Revona]","[Max Morgan vs Ervin]","The names remained there for several breaths. Then Angelina raised her hand.","\"The next battle will now be selected.\"","The golden light around the screen spun once, then twice, before the first matchup brightened.","[Ervin vs Revona]","The moment those two names shone, the entire arena fell into a deep silence. Then the Divine Realm erupted.","Abyssal Origin Descent stood against Void Origin Realm, the broken gate against the Void Origin Eyes, an abyss that swallowed everything into unfathomable depth against a pair of eyes that erased, nullified, hollowed, and returned power to nothing.","This was not a battle of simple force. This was a battle between two terrifying paths that both denied the enemy in completely different ways. Ervin’s abyss did not merely block attacks.","It sank them, swallowed them, redirected them, and dragged their meaning into the depth behind the broken gate.","Revona’s void did not merely defend. It traced the source of power, erased its structure, nullified its authority, and returned it to nothingness before it could complete its purpose.","Across the Divine Realm, countless spectators began speaking at once.","\"Ervin defeated Damian by the smallest margin.\"","\"But Revona pushed Max further than anyone.\"","\"Can the abyss swallow Void Origin Realm?\"","\"Can the Void Origin Eyes erase the broken gate?\"","\"Return To Nothing against Gate of the Second Depth. This might be even stranger than Damian and Ervin’s battle.\"","On the pillars, the defeated geniuses also became serious.","Rakan Thorne crossed his arms and grinned.","\"This one will be annoying to watch, but terrifying.\"","Orion Starfall smiled faintly, though there was rare seriousness in his eyes.","\"Revona already fought Max, so she is not in perfect condition. But Ervin just fought Damian to the limit too. Neither one is fresh.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked toward Ervin’s black spear, then toward Revona’s pale eyes.","\"That makes it more dangerous. When people like them are exhausted, they stop wasting power and go straight for decisive moves.\"","Morgana Starveil’s purple eyes reflected the names above.","\"Depth against nothingness. I wonder which one can deny the other more completely.\"","Damian Voss stood quietly on his pillar, his gaze fixed on Ervin. He had just lost to that abyss by a margin so thin that even the spectators had almost failed to recognize it, but there was no resentment in his eyes.","Only focus, only respect, and only the cold awareness that the man who had beaten his sword now had to face an opponent whose ability could erase even the foundation of attacks.","Max Morgan also watched silently. He had faced Revona and knew better than anyone here how terrifying her fully awakened Void Origin Eyes were.","He had been forced to reveal layers of power he had kept hidden for the entire conference, and even then, Revona’s Null Origin Tide had almost stripped him bare before the Dimensional Keeper legacy answered him.","But he had also faced Ervin before, and he knew that Abyssal Origin Descent was not an ordinary Pseudo Cosmic Path. It did not behave like darkness, and it did not behave like water. It was depth, return, and an ancient gate to something far more profound.","This battle would not be easy for either side.","On one pillar, Ervin slowly stood. His expression remained calm, but his face was paler than before. The battle against Damian had clearly cost him.","The Gate of the Second Depth had opened wider than ever, and even though the Eternal Hourglass was healing him, the exhaustion of pushing his abyss that far could not disappear instantly.","On another pillar, Revona also opened her eyes. She was still pale from her battle against Max, her aura thinner, and the faint emptiness in her gaze no longer looked as effortless as before.","Yet when her Void Origin Eyes fully opened, the surrounding space still seemed to quiet down, as if even the laws of the Eternal Hourglass had to acknowledge the danger in her sight.","Angelina Valerius looked toward both of them.","\"Ervin.\"","\"Revona.\"","\"Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended.","Ervin appeared on one side of the central arena with his black spear in hand, his long shadow spreading beneath him like a silent sea. Revona appeared opposite him, calm and pale, her Void Origin Eyes fixed directly on the man who had defeated Damian Voss.","For a brief moment, neither of them spoke. Then Ervin lifted his spear slightly.","\"Your eyes are very troublesome. I don’t know how Max was able to bypass them\"","Revona replied quietly, \"Your abyss gates are also troublesome too and so I think it will be a good battle.\"","Ervin’s gaze deepened. \"Then we should not delay.\"","Revona’s eyes shone with faint emptiness. \"No. We should not.\"","Above them, the giant screen flashed.","[Top Four Battle]","[Ervin vs Revona]","The Eternal Hourglass barrier brightened. The entire Divine Realm leaned closer.","Angelina Valerius raised her hand.","The next battle was about to begin."]},{"number":1915,"title":"Chapter 1915: An Epic Clash!","paragraphs":["Angelina Valerius lowered her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","The moment the words appeared, Ervin and Revona moved at the same time. There was no testing and no polite first exchange.","Both of them had already fought enough battles to understand that holding back in this final stretch was meaningless.","Ervin had just defeated Damian Voss by the smallest possible margin, but that victory had come at a terrifying price. His aura was still unstable, and the shadow of the Gate of the Second Depth behind him had not fully settled.","Revona had already been defeated by Max Morgan after forcing him to reveal layers of strength that shook the Divine Realm, but she had also paid a heavy cost. Her Void Origin Eyes were still sharp, yet the faint paleness of her face proved that her battle with Max had not been easy.","Even so, neither of them hesitated.","Ervin planted his black spear into the stage.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","The black sea rose, and the broken gate emerged from the abyss, ancient, silent, and terrifying, its unreadable symbols flickering with a darkness that seemed older than the arena itself. The moment the gate appeared, the air around Ervin sank.","The stage no longer felt like solid ground. It felt like a surface floating above endless depth, and anything that stepped too close to him risked being dragged below.","Revona’s eyes opened fully.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","The world behind her became hollow, without color, sound, or warmth. Only origin-level emptiness spread silently behind her like a pale-gray world that denied all things.","The Void Origin Eyes shone within that emptiness, calmly watching the black sea, the broken gate, the spear in Ervin’s hand, and even the faint abyssal currents moving beneath the stage.","The two Pseudo Cosmic Paths collided before their masters physically exchanged a single blow. Abyss rose upward while void pressed downward.","The black sea tried to swallow the hollow realm into its depths, while the Void Origin Realm tried to erase the structure that allowed the abyss to exist on the battlefield. The center of the arena twisted between sinking darkness and pale emptiness, and the Eternal Hourglass barrier brightened instantly as golden laws poured around the stage.","Ervin raised his spear.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, First Depth Tide.\"","The black sea erupted forward in a great wave.","Revona lifted one hand.","\"Void Origin Eyes.\"","The first layer of the tide vanished. The second layer hollowed. The third layer lost its direction and collapsed into pale-gray emptiness. But the wave was too deep to disappear completely. Beneath the erased surface, a hidden current continued moving, bending around the Void Origin Eyes’ field of sight and rushing toward Revona’s feet from below.","Revona’s eyes shifted.","\"Void Origin Realm, Hollowing Wave.\"","The hidden current was erased the moment it touched the edge of her realm, but Ervin had already moved. His spear emerged from the shadow of the current.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Deep Current Thrust.\"","Revona turned her palm.","\"Void Origin Palm.\"","Spear and palm collided. There was no loud explosion at first. The abyssal spear force tried to sink into her palm, while the hollow palm seal tried to erase the spear force from its root. The two powers trembled against each other, then burst apart in a ring of black water and pale-gray emptiness.","Ervin slid back half a step. Revona also retreated half a step.","The Divine Realm erupted immediately.","\"They are equal at the start!\"","\"Revona erased part of the First Depth Tide, but Ervin hid a second current beneath it!\"","\"His abyss is not simple to nullify!\"","\"And her Void Origin Realm is not simple to swallow!\"","Ervin did not slow down. He knew that if he allowed Revona’s eyes to calmly study his abyss, the battle would become more difficult with every breath.","He had seen what happened to Kaiden, and he had seen how Revona adapted to the Grand Void Labyrinth. He had also seen how even Max had needed to create multiple layers of power and hidden timing just to bypass her perception.","So Ervin attacked more fiercely than ever.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Gate of the First Depth.\"","The broken gate opened slightly, and a deeper pressure descended upon the stage. The black sea beneath Ervin became heavier, darker, and more ancient. He stepped forward, and the abyss moved with him.","His spear thrust out again and again, each strike carrying hidden currents, delayed depths, and sinking force that tried to drag Revona’s Void Origin Realm into a lower layer before her eyes could erase it.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Hollow Descent Thrust.\"","\"Abyss Spear Art, Gate Shadow Thrust.\"","\"Abyss Spear Art, Deep Current Reversal.\"","Revona’s eyes moved calmly. One thrust vanished, and the shadow of the gate was hollowed. The reversed current was erased halfway, but the remaining half curved around her and struck her shoulder.","Blood appeared, and the arena stirred. Ervin had wounded her.","Revona looked at the blood on her shoulder, then back at Ervin. Her expression did not change, but the emptiness in her eyes deepened.","\"Trace To Nothing.\"","The next abyssal current Ervin released did not merely disappear. Revona’s eyes followed it backward, tracing the route through the black sea until they found the deeper current that carried it. That hidden current collapsed, then another, then another. Several of Ervin’s concealed abyssal paths vanished inside the black sea itself.","Ervin’s gaze sharpened, and he immediately changed his rhythm. Instead of sending currents toward her, he let the black sea sink beneath the stage. For a breath, nothing attacked Revona. Then the ground below her disappeared.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Return To Depth.\"","A whirlpool opened beneath Revona’s feet, dragging her downward with frightening force. This was not a direct attack to be erased from the front. It was a pull from below, a sinking authority that tried to claim her position and return it to the abyss.","Revona’s Void Origin Realm expanded beneath her. The whirlpool hollowed, but it did not vanish fully. The depth continued pulling. Revona’s body sank half a step, then one full step.","Her eyes shone brighter as she erased the first layer of the whirlpool, then the second, then the third. But the Return To Depth technique kept rising from lower layers of the black sea, and for a brief moment, the entire Divine Realm saw Revona being dragged downward.","Ervin stepped forward and thrust his spear.","\"Gate Shadow Thrust.\"","The spear tip arrived before her chest.","Revona’s eyes narrowed.","\"Void Origin Realm, Silent Eye Field.\"","The emptiness around her gaze spread outward in a wide arc. The Gate Shadow Thrust dulled instantly, its killing intent erased before its spear force could fully arrive. At the same time, the Return To Depth whirlpool beneath her feet lost its deepest foundation and collapsed into nothingness.","Revona stepped out and struck forward with her palm.","\"Void Origin Palm, Hollow Return.\"","Ervin raised his spear to block, but the palm seal did not attack the spear. It struck the abyssal support around his body instead. The black sea beneath him thinned, and the Gate of the First Depth trembled. Ervin was pushed back several steps, his expression turning more solemn.","Rakan Thorne watched with a tight grin.","\"They are already hurting each other.\"","Orion Starfall’s eyes were bright.","\"Ervin is attacking from depth. Revona is erasing from origin. Every clash is cutting away something fundamental.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked grim.","\"If this continues, whoever loses control of their Pseudo Cosmic Path first will lose.\"","Damian Voss watched Ervin quietly. He had just fought that abyss himself, so he knew how terrifying the Gate of the Second Depth was. Yet even he could see that Revona was forcing Ervin to spend more power than he wanted, since every route erased by her eyes made the black sea less stable.","Max stood silently, his gaze fixed on Revona. He knew what she still had not used, and he knew that if Ervin could not get past it, the battle would end exactly as she intended.","On the stage, Ervin took a slow breath. The black sea around him darkened again.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","The broken gate opened wider.","\"Gate of the Second Depth.\"","Boom!","The entire stage sank under invisible pressure, and Revona’s Void Origin Realm trembled. The second depth was not merely stronger than the first. It changed the nature of the abyss. The black sea no longer only swallowed attacks.","It made everything feel lower than itself, so sword light could sink, star power could sink, and spatial routes could sink. Even void emptiness seemed to gain weight under its pressure."]},{"number":1916,"title":"Chapter 1916: Too Strong!","paragraphs":["Ervin raised his spear.","\"Second Depth Spear.\"","The black sea climbed onto the spear like a world sinking into one point.","\"Sunken World.\"","The spear thrust forward.","Revona’s eyes flashed.","\"Void Origin Realm, Return To Nothing.\"","A condensed point of emptiness formed before her palm.","Sunken World crashed into Return To Nothing, and the stage vanished under the collision. The black sea tried to sink the point of nothingness into the Second Depth, while Return To Nothing tried to erase the world carried by the spear.","For several breaths, neither side moved. The entire arena seemed locked between two forms of denial. One returned everything to depth. The other returned everything to nothing.","Ervin’s arms trembled, and Revona’s face turned paler. Both were being pushed. The Gate of the Second Depth groaned behind Ervin, and the Void Origin Realm flickered behind Revona.","The pressure between them became so terrifying that golden laws from the Eternal Hourglass had to descend again and again to stabilize the barrier.","Then Ervin suddenly coughed blood, but his eyes did not waver. He stepped forward into the collision, and the black spear in his hand cracked faintly beneath the pressure.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","His voice became deeper.","\"Forbidden Depth Art.\"","The moment those words appeared, the expressions of several hidden experts across the Divine Realm changed. Behind Ervin, the broken gate opened beyond the safe limit, and the symbols on it bled black light.","His flesh tore open along his arms, shoulders, and chest, as if his own body could not withstand the depth he was trying to call out. Bones groaned, and blood flowed down his hands and dripped onto the spear. Even his aura became unstable, as though the abyss he controlled was beginning to pull him down as well.","Revona’s eyes sharpened.","\"You will break your body.\"","Ervin replied quietly, \"It doesn’t matter.\"","The broken gate roared.","\"Second Depth Forbidden Spear.\"","The abyss gathered behind him like a collapsed world.","\"Gate Beyond Drowning.\"","Ervin thrust, and this time, even Return To Nothing was pushed back. The point of origin emptiness trembled violently as the forbidden spear pressed into it.","The abyssal force behind Ervin’s strike was no longer merely trying to sink an attack. It was trying to drown the law of nullification itself beneath a depth that should have been beyond his current limit.","Revona’s feet slid backward, one step, then another. Blood spilled from her lips.","The Divine Realm went wild.","\"He is pushing Return To Nothing back!\"","\"Ervin is using a forbidden technique!\"","\"His body is cracking!\"","\"He is trying to defeat Revona before she can use that final nullifying wave!\"","Inside the stage, Revona’s expression finally became strained. Her Void Origin Eyes shone so brightly that faint cracks of pale light appeared around her pupils.","She poured more power into Return To Nothing, but Ervin continued pushing forward, his body breaking under the force of his own forbidden depth.","His spear pressed closer, and the black sea rose behind him like an apocalypse. Revona’s Return To Nothing began to distort. For a moment, it truly looked as if Ervin might break through.","Max narrowed his eyes. Damian’s gaze sharpened. Orion stopped breathing. Rakan’s fists clenched.","Then Revona raised her other hand. Her voice was quiet.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","The hollow world behind her opened fully.","\"Null Origin Tide.\"","A pale-gray wave erupted from Revona in every direction.","It was the same move she had used against Max, the same final domain-like nullifying attack that had stripped away the power of his Divine Veins, his 5000 Draconic Essences, his Dragon Scales Transformation, Divine King Punishment, the Devouring Flames Domain, and even the timing advantage created by his clone.","Now it descended upon Ervin.","The black sea was struck first, and the Second Depth trembled. The abyssal waves lost their shape and began vanishing layer by layer. The hidden currents were erased, and the swallowed power inside the sea was nullified.","The path connecting Ervin to the Gate of the Second Depth dimmed violently.","Ervin’s forbidden spear still pressed forward, but the Null Origin Tide spread around it. The abyssal force coating the spear vanished, and the Second Depth pressure disappeared from its tip.","The black light bleeding from the gate was erased, and the forbidden art collapsed around Ervin’s body.","His eyes widened slightly. His body had already been pushed to the brink, and now the Null Origin Tide stripped away the very powers sustaining his final attack. The black sea beneath his feet dried into emptiness.","The Gate of the Second Depth flickered like an illusion about to vanish. The abyssal aura covering his body disappeared, and the spear in his hand lost its terrifying depth.","For one breath, Ervin stood there with almost nothing left, just like Max had before him. His power was gone. His abyss was silent. His gate had dimmed, and his forbidden technique had been nullified.","His body, already cracked from forcing the Gate Beyond Drowning, trembled violently as blood poured from dozens of wounds.","Revona stood opposite him, also pale, wounded, and breathing unsteadily. Null Origin Tide had clearly cost her greatly, especially after using Return To Nothing against the forbidden spear. Her Void Origin Eyes were strained, and blood stained her lips, but the pale-gray tide still surrounded her.","Ervin tried to raise his spear. His arm shook, and the spear rose only halfway. The Gate of the Second Depth flickered behind him, but it could not open again. The Null Origin Tide had stripped too much away.","Unlike Max, Ervin did not have the Dimensional Keeper legacy. He did not have a higher-scale power that Revona’s nullification could not define. He had only his abyss, and his abyss had been nullified.","Revona looked at him quietly.","\"You gave everything.\"","Ervin did not answer. He forced one foot forward, and his body almost collapsed from that step alone.","The crowd fell silent. Even Revona’s eyes flickered slightly. Ervin was still trying to move.","He gathered the last trace of abyssal force inside his body. It was not enough to open the gate, not enough to summon the sea, and not enough to form a true technique. It was only a faint black current around the spear tip, a remnant of a remnant, but he still pointed it toward Revona.","\"Abyss Spear Art.\"","His voice was hoarse.","\"Hollow Descent.\"","He thrust. The spear moved slowly compared to before, but it carried all that he had left.","Revona raised her hand. The pale-gray tide moved, and the last black current vanished. Her palm stopped before his chest.","\"Void Origin Palm.\"","The hollow force struck, and Ervin’s body was thrown backward. He crashed into the shattered stage, rolled once, and came to a stop near the edge of the arena. His spear fell beside him, and the broken gate behind him finally disappeared completely.","For a few breaths, no one spoke. Ervin tried to move, and his fingers twitched toward the spear, but his body did not rise.","Angelina Valerius looked down at him and spoke calmly.","\"Ervin is unable to continue.\"","The result appeared above the arena.","[Winner: Revona.]","[Ervin Defeated.]","The Divine Realm remained silent for one long breath. Then it erupted.","Revona had won. She had lost to Max, but she had defeated Ervin.","Ervin had given everything. He had opened Abyssal Origin Descent from the beginning, forced the Gate of the Second Depth, and used Return To Depth and Sunken World before finally turning to a forbidden depth technique that almost shattered his own body.","He had pushed Revona so hard that she had been forced to use Return To Nothing and then the same Null Origin Tide she had used against Max.","But he could not get past it. Once Null Origin Tide stripped his abyss away, he had nothing left that could reverse the battle.","The screen updated.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Revona]","[Total Battles Fought: 23]","[Total Wins: 22]","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 23]","[Total Wins: 22]","On the pillars, Damian Voss watched in silence. He had lost to Ervin, and Ervin had now lost to Revona, who had herself lost to Max.","The top four had begun cutting into one another, and the final rankings were becoming more complicated with every battle.","Rakan Thorne released a long breath.","\"That woman is terrifying.\"","Orion Starfall smiled bitterly.","\"Yes. Max was the only one who could still pull out something after that tide erased everything.\"","Kaiden Voidmere nodded slowly.","\"Ervin had the strength to nearly break Return To Nothing. But Null Origin Tide ended him.\"","Morgana Starveil looked at Revona with a deep gaze.","\"She was pushed to the edge again.\"","Max watched Revona quietly. He understood the cost better than anyone.","Revona stood in the arena, pale, bleeding, and clearly exhausted. Her Void Origin Eyes no longer looked effortless, and the Null Origin Tide around her slowly faded as her body trembled once before steadying again.","She had won, but just like against Max, she had been forced to use everything.","The transfer light descended and carried Ervin back to his pillar, where the Eternal Hourglass immediately began repairing his broken body. Revona also returned to her pillar and sat down without a word.","The battle had ended, and Ervin had fallen. The final stretch of the Cosmic Ascension Conference had become even more unpredictable."]},{"number":1917,"title":"Chapter 1917: Damian vs Max!","paragraphs":["The shock of Revona’s victory over Ervin had not even fully settled when the giant screen above the Eternal Hourglass shifted once again.","The new records shone clearly for all to see.","[Max Morgan] [Total Battles Fought: 22] [Total Wins: 22]","[Ervin] [Total Battles Fought: 23] [Total Wins: 22]","[Revona] [Total Battles Fought: 23] [Total Wins: 22]","[Damian Voss] [Total Battles Fought: 22] [Total Wins: 21]","The moment the updated records appeared, countless people across the Divine Realm immediately understood how heavy the next battle would be.","Max, Ervin, and Revona now stood tied at twenty-two victories, while Damian had fallen one step behind with twenty-one. That meant the next result would affect everything.","If Max won, he would rise to twenty-three victories and place one foot ahead of all the others before his final battle with Ervin. If Damian won, he would rise to twenty-two victories again and drag the entire top ranking back into chaos.","Angelina Valerius stood calmly above the stage and waited for the murmurs to settle. Then she raised her hand.","\"The next battle will now begin.\"","The light above the arena spun once more, and under the focused gazes of everyone present, two names slowly brightened until they stood alone above all others.","[Max Morgan vs Damian Voss]","For a moment, the entire arena seemed to forget how to breathe. Then the Divine Realm erupted once more.","The Black Dragon Clan disciples all stood up at once before the huge live screen floating above the clan grounds. Some of them clenched their fists, some widened their eyes, and some simply stared without blinking, because everyone understood what this meant.","Max was finally going to face the strongest swordsman of the Sword God Palace in a true official battle of the final stage.","Lady Virelia looked at the screen with a solemn gaze, but beneath that solemnity there was a clear trace of expectation.","\"Max,\" she murmured softly, \"do your best.\"","The seven family heads standing nearby also watched with serious expressions.","Even Mathew Grimes, who had long since stopped underestimating Max, narrowed his eyes and said, \"This battle will be dangerous. Damian Voss is not a man who loses twice in spirit, even if he already lost once in record.\"","On the other side of the Divine Realm, the Sword God Palace disciples had already become extremely excited. Their strongest genius had lost to Ervin by the smallest margin possible, and many of them had been left with frustration burning in their chests.","But now that Damian had been matched against Max, the same Max who held Dragonheart and had embarrassed the Sword God Palace more than once, their emotions surged again.","\"It is finally happening!\"","\"Senior Brother Damian must win this!\"","\"Max Morgan may be strong, but in a pure sword battle, how can he compare to Senior Brother Damian?\"","\"He carries the Sword of the Sovereign, but that does not make him the strongest swordsman!\"","Even among the hidden forces, many old monsters silently straightened in their seats. This battle was not merely about victory count. It was also about the dignity of the sword path itself.","Damian Voss represented the refined and tyrannical edge of the Sword God Palace, while Max Morgan carried Dragonheart, the Emotion Severing Path, and a sword talent that had already shocked the entire conference time and again.","On the pillars inside the Eternal Hourglass, the remaining geniuses all turned their eyes toward Max and Damian.","Orion Starfall smiled widely. \"Good. I have been waiting for this one.\"","Rakan Thorne laughed. \"If these two really go all out with swords, the stage might split.\"","Kaiden Voidmere watched quietly. \"It depends on what kind of battle they choose to fight.\"","Revona, still pale from her fight against Ervin, slowly lifted her eyes and looked toward Max. There was no doubt in her gaze, since she knew better than most here that Max’s sword was not ordinary anymore.","Ervin also raised his head and looked toward the arena. Even though he had just lost, his eyes were still deep and focused, and he too wanted to see what kind of sword path Max would reveal against Damian.","Angelina’s voice rang out clearly.","\"Max Morgan.\"","\"Damian Voss.\"","\"Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended. Max appeared on one side of the arena, calm as ever, Dragonheart resting at his hand. Damian appeared on the other side, his posture straight, his sword already in hand, and the sword intent around him calm but terrifyingly condensed.","He no longer looked like a man bothered by his previous defeat. If anything, he looked even sharper now, as if the loss to Ervin had only refined his edge further.","The two of them faced each other across the stage. For a few breaths, neither spoke. Then Damian looked at Max and said calmly, \"We have already crossed swords before, but that was not an official battle.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"That is true.\"","Damian’s gaze shifted briefly to Dragonheart, then returned to Max’s face. \"You and I are both swordsmen. If we fight normally, the battle may drag on longer than it should, and both of us still have more battles ahead.\"","Max looked at him with mild curiosity. \"So what do you propose?\"","Damian lifted his sword slightly, and the sword intent around him sharpened.","\"One sword attack each,\" he said. \"No repeated exchanges. No prolonged battle. We each use one true sword attack, and with that single clash, we decide the victor.\"","The moment those words were spoken, the arena fell silent again. One sword attack. Just one.","The Sword God Palace disciples were stunned for a moment, but then many of them became even more excited. To them, this was the most fitting way for a swordsman of Damian’s level to fight another swordsman he acknowledged. It would not be a contest of exhaustion, attrition, or secondary abilities. It would be a direct collision of sword paths.","At the Black Dragon Clan, many disciples also stared with widened eyes.","\"Only one attack?\"","\"Is Damian that confident?\"","\"No. This means he truly acknowledges Max.\"","Lady Virelia’s eyes sharpened as she looked at Max on the screen. She understood Damian’s intention very well. This was not arrogance alone. It was also pride, a swordsman’s pride. If he could not defeat Max through the sharpest essence of his sword in one strike, then he would have no need to drag the battle any further."]},{"number":1918,"title":"Chapter 1918: One Sword Attack!","paragraphs":["On the stage, Max looked at Damian for a few silent breaths. Then he smiled.","\"Good.\"","He slowly drew Dragonheart from its sheath, and a cold, clear hum spread across the arena.","\"If a single sword attack is enough for you,\" Max said calmly, \"then a single sword attack is enough for me as well.\"","Damian’s eyes became even sharper. \"So you agree?\"","Max nodded once. \"I agree.\"","That simple answer immediately made the entire Divine Realm hold its breath again.","Angelina Valerius looked at both of them for a moment before speaking. \"The terms are accepted. This battle will be decided by a single sword clash.\"","Her words caused the stage beneath them to begin glowing brighter. The laws of the Eternal Hourglass strengthened the barrier around the central arena, as if even it understood that one attack from Damian Voss and one attack from Max Morgan would not be ordinary sword moves.","Damian took a step back and raised his sword before him. Max also stepped back and held Dragonheart in both hands. The air between them changed at once. No one spoke, and no one moved carelessly.","Every spectator, every genius, every elder, and every clan across the Divine Realm fixed their gaze on the stage, because everyone understood one thing. The next moment would decide everything between these two swordsmen.","The entire Eternal Hourglass became silent after Max and Damian agreed to decide the battle with one sword attack. This was not a silence born from confusion. It was the silence of anticipation.","Everyone understood that a normal battle between these two would have been earth-shaking. Damian Voss had Sword Sovereign Heaven, a terrifying Pseudo Cosmic Path that had already cut through Aurelian’s divine luminance, Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth, Rakan’s War God Body, and many other supreme techniques.","Max Morgan had Dragonheart, the Emotion Severing Path, and a depth of sword comprehension that had only grown more frightening with each battle. If they fought normally, the clash could have lasted a long time, with both sides revealing layer after layer of strength.","But they had chosen one attack. One sword. One collision. One result.","On the stage, Damian Voss slowly closed his eyes. The sword in his hand lowered slightly, and the air around him became completely still. For a few breaths, there was no movement from him at all, yet the entire arena began to feel a sharp pressure spreading outward.","It was not wild, loud, or explosive like lightning or the abyss. It was the kind of pressure that made every sword in the Divine Realm tremble inside its sheath, because Damian’s entire being seemed to be gathering into one pure edge.","Above and behind him, Sword Sovereign Heaven began to appear. Sword-edge mountains rose into existence, and rivers of sword light flowed across the sky.","An ancient sword altar stood at the center of that world, while far above it the sword palace appeared with its empty throne.","The single sword hanging before the throne descended slowly, and as it did, all the countless sword lights throughout the Sword Sovereign Heaven bowed toward it.","This was not the First Edict, nor the Second, nor the Third, Fourth, Fifth, or Sixth. Damian did not intend to hold anything back. Against Max Morgan, anything less than the strongest attack would be meaningless.","His sword heaven began to collapse inward. The mountains of swords broke apart and turned into streams of sharp light, and the rivers of sword energy rose into the sky and flowed into the descending sword before the throne.","The sword altar cracked, and the palace trembled. The empty throne shone with a cold and noble brilliance. All of Damian’s sword authority, sword heart, sword intent, sword laws, blood, will, and battle experience gathered into the weapon in his hand.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven.\"","Damian opened his eyes.","\"Final Edict.\"","The single sword before the throne fused into his blade.","\"Throne Of The Only Sword.\"","The moment those words fell, the entire sword world behind him disappeared. No sword mountains, no sword rivers, no sword palace, and no altar or throne remained. Only Damian remained, and only his sword remained.","Because only one sword remained, everything else in the arena seemed to lose the right to be called sharp.","Across the Divine Realm, every swordsman felt their heart tremble, and the Sword God Palace fell into complete silence. This was Damian Voss pushing his strongest sword attack to the absolute limit.","The attack he had used against Ervin had already been terrifying, but now, after experiencing defeat and refining his sword heart through that loss, and after facing Max Morgan directly, Damian’s final edict had become even purer than before.","His sword was no longer merely cutting force, law, rhythm, space, or authority. It was declaring that beneath this one sword, all other paths would be judged.","Max stood opposite him, and Dragonheart hummed softly in his hand. The moment Damian’s strongest attack reached its peak, Max’s eyes became serious as well. He had already seen how terrifying Throne Of The Only Sword was.","If Damian had used this attack against most other geniuses, the battle would have ended instantly. Even Revona’s Void Origin Eyes would need to treat this sword with caution, because Damian had compressed his entire Pseudo Cosmic Path into one clean and absolute strike.","Max exhaled slowly. He did not activate Divine King Punishment. He did not release the Devouring Flames Domain. He did not use the four Divine Veins, and he did not summon the power of the Dimensional Keeper legacy again. This was a sword battle, so he would answer with the sword.","Dragonheart rose before him, and a cold, silent aura spread from the blade.","\"Emotion Severing Path.\"","The moment those words left Max’s mouth, the warmth of the arena vanished. Damian’s sword was pure, proud, sovereign, and absolute. Max’s sword was quiet, cold, forbidden, and terrifying.","The Emotion Severing Path did not merely carry sharpness. It carried severance. It severed feeling, intent, connection, rhythm, authority, and the invisible things that allowed power to remain whole.","The air around Dragonheart became deathly calm, as if every emotion in the battlefield had been cut away before the sword was even swung.","But this time, Max did not stop there. He closed his eyes for a brief moment, and then the sword technique inherited from the Sword Saint flowed through his body.","\"Saint Origin Sword Art.\"","The moment the name appeared, Dragonheart’s aura changed again, and the cold severing power of the Emotion Severing Path gained structure. Before this, Max’s Emotion Severing Path had been frightening because of how forbidden and unpredictable it was.","It could sever things that should not be severed, and even top geniuses struggled to understand where the true danger lay.","But now, when Max fused it with the Saint Origin Sword Art, that forbidden severing path gained a sacred sword framework that seemed to arrange every strand of severance into perfect order.","Emotion Severing Path was the edge, and Saint Origin Sword Art was the form. One was forbidden severance, and the other was the Sword Saint’s order.","When the two merged, the power gathered around Dragonheart became so sharp, so calm, and so complete that even Damian’s eyes changed.","For the first time, a trace of deep admiration appeared in his gaze."]},{"number":1919,"title":"Chapter 1919: The Deadly Confrontation!","paragraphs":["\"That sword art...,\" Damian said softly.","Max looked at him. \"It belongs to a senior whose sword path deserves utmost respect.\"","Damian nodded once. \"Then I will answer it with everything I have.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Good.\"","The two of them moved at the same time. Damian stepped forward, and the entire arena seemed to vanish before his sword.","\"Throne Of The Only Sword.\"","His blade came down. At that moment, every spectator felt as though there was only one sword left in the world. It carried Damian’s full belief, full pride, full defeat, full refinement, and full will.","The sword did not need a storm behind it anymore, because it was the storm. It did not need the sword heaven to support it anymore, because it was the sword heaven condensed into one strike. It cut straight toward Max with the dignity of a sovereign blade that refused to bow before anything.","Max also stepped forward, and Dragonheart descended in his hands.","\"Saint Origin Sword Art.\"","His eyes became calm.","\"Emotion Severing Sword.\"","The blade moved. There was no thunder, no flame, no dragon roar, and no dimensional starlight. Only one sword line remained, a cold, orderly, perfect sword line that carried the full power of the Emotion Severing Path through the structure of the Sword Saint’s technique.","It did not rush to overpower Damian’s sword, and it did not try to crush the Throne Of The Only Sword through greater energy. It moved as though it had already found the invisible thread connecting Damian’s final edict to his sword heart, his sword heaven, his throne, and the singular declaration that only his sword should remain.","The two swords met.","Clang.","The sound was impossibly clear. For one breath, nothing exploded. Damian’s sword pressed forward, and Max’s sword held. Then the stage split beneath them.","Boom!","A ring of sword force erupted outward and slammed into the Eternal Hourglass barrier. Golden laws surged wildly around the arena, layer after layer activating to contain the collision.","The air above the stage was cut into countless invisible fragments, and the ground beneath both swordsmen shattered into deep cracks that stretched from one end of the battlefield to the other.","Damian’s Throne Of The Only Sword pushed with absolute authority. It tried to judge Max’s blade, and it tried to force every other sword path beneath its throne. It tried to cut through the Saint Origin Sword Art and declare Dragonheart inferior to the one sword before it.","But Max’s Emotion Severing Sword did not compete for the throne. It severed the connection that made the throne absolute.","The cold line around Dragonheart slid along Damian’s sword authority, not against the surface of his blade but through the invisible structure behind it.","Saint Origin Sword Art guided the severing power with terrifying precision, preventing the Emotion Severing Path from scattering wildly. Every bit of the forbidden path was placed exactly where it needed to be.","It severed the pride from the pressure. It severed the edict from the throne. It severed the sword heaven’s final support from the single blade, and it severed the meaning of \"only sword\" from Damian’s attack.","Damian’s pupils contracted, and his sword began to tremble.","\"No,\" someone from the Sword God Palace whispered.","The Throne Of The Only Sword still pressed forward, but its absolute pressure began to crack. The sword itself had not weakened. Damian’s will had not weakened, and his technique had not been flawed.","But Max’s attack was not destroying it from the outside. It was cutting apart the invisible arrangement that allowed all of Damian’s power to exist as one perfect sword.","Crack!","A faint sound echoed through the arena. A line appeared in Damian’s sword light, then a second, then a third.","Damian gritted his teeth and poured everything he had into the final edict. His sword heart burned, and his blood flowed along the blade. The faint image of the empty throne appeared behind him again, trying to stabilize the final attack. But Max’s sword moved one inch deeper.","The Emotion Severing Sword cut through the last connection. The empty throne split, and the final edict broke. The Throne Of The Only Sword shattered.","A blinding storm of broken sword light exploded around them, and for several breaths, no one could see the center of the battlefield. The Eternal Hourglass barrier groaned under the impact, and golden laws descended like chains to suppress the remaining sword force.","Across the Divine Realm, countless swordsmen stared without blinking, their hearts pounding as though they had just watched the highest pride of the sword path collide with something forbidden and divine.","When the light finally faded, Max stood behind Damian, Dragonheart lowered at his side. Damian remained standing in his original position, his sword held forward, but the blade light around it had disappeared.","A thin line of blood appeared at the corner of his mouth, and his sword hand trembled once.","For a moment, Damian said nothing. He simply looked at his sword. The sword itself had not broken, but his strongest attack had.","After a few breaths, Damian closed his eyes.","\"You cut through my attack. You win.\"","Max turned slightly and looked at him. \"It wasn’t easy.\"","Damian opened his eyes again. There was no anger in them, only exhaustion and respect. He looked at Dragonheart, then at Max, and a faint smile appeared on his face for the first time.","\"Good sword.\"","Max smiled lightly. \"Yours too.\"","Damian exhaled. Then he lowered his sword.","\"I lose.\"","Angelina Valerius’s voice descended over the arena.","[Winner: Max Morgan.] [Damian Voss Defeated.]","The screen above the Eternal Hourglass updated.","[Battle Record Updated.] [Max Morgan] [Total Battles Fought: 23] [Total Wins: 23]","[Battle Record Updated.] [Damian Voss] [Total Battles Fought: 23] [Total Wins: 21]","For one long breath, the entire Divine Realm remained silent. Then the eruption came.","The Black Dragon Clan exploded into thunderous cheers. The Sword God Palace stayed silent at first, but soon many disciples clenched their fists with complicated expressions. Damian had lost again, yet there was no shame in this defeat.","He had pushed his strongest attack to its limit. He had refined the Throne Of The Only Sword after losing to Ervin, and he had poured everything into one sword clash, only to still be defeated by Max’s Emotion Severing Sword fused with the Saint Origin Sword Art.","That did not make him weak. It only proved that Max’s sword path had reached a terrifying level.","On the pillars, Orion Starfall released a long breath. \"One attack. They really decided it with one attack.\"","Rakan Thorne shook his head, his expression rare and serious. \"If that sword had hit me, I would not even know what was cut.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked at Max with deep eyes. \"He did not overpower Damian’s sword. He found its source and severed it.\"","Revona remained silent, but her gaze toward Max became more focused than before.","Ervin watched Damian for a moment, then Max. His abyss-like eyes darkened.","Max had defeated Revona. Max had defeated Damian. And now, only one final unavoidable battle remained between the top undefeated contender before Max and Ervin battle was the battle between Damian and Revona."]},{"number":1920,"title":"Chapter 1920: Damian vs Revona!","paragraphs":["The victory screen from Max Morgan’s battle against Damian Voss slowly faded from the sky above the Eternal Hourglass.","The arena remained heavy with the lingering aura of that single sword clash. Even though the stage had already begun restoring itself under the golden laws of the Eternal Hourglass, countless spectators across the Divine Realm were still trapped in the memory of what they had just seen.","Damian had used the strongest sword attack of Sword Sovereign Heaven, pushing Throne Of The Only Sword to its absolute limit, while Max had answered with the Emotion Severing Path fused with the Saint Order Sword Art and severed the invisible connection that made Damian’s final edict absolute.","Damian had lost, but no one could call that defeat humiliating. He had stood as one of the greatest swordsmen of the younger generation and had lost only after using the very peak of his sword path against an even stranger and more terrifying sword.","Angelina Valerius waited until the golden laws repaired the central stage completely before she raised her hand again.","\"The second last battle of the Cosmic Ascension Conference will now begin.\"","The moment those words spread across the Eternal Hourglass, the Divine Realm immediately became tense again. There were only two battles left now. Damian Voss against Revona, then, at last, Max Morgan against Ervin. The champion would be decided after those final results.","The great screen above the arena shifted, and two names appeared.","[Damian Voss] [Revona]","For a moment, the audience fell into a strange silence. Then the entire Divine Realm erupted again.","Sword Sovereign Heaven stood against Void Origin Realm.","The sword that had almost defeated Ervin and had just pushed Max into revealing the Saint Order Sword Art now faced the woman whose Void Origin Eyes had erased Orion’s stars, hollowed Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth, stripped Ervin’s abyss bare, and forced Max to reveal the Dimensional Keeper legacy before she finally fell.","This battle no longer involved undefeated records.","Both had lost.","But that did not reduce the weight of the match at all. If anything, it made it more important in a different way, because this battle would decide who stood higher among the two fallen monsters of the top four.","It would also show whether Damian’s sword, which had nearly reached the peak of singular sword authority, could cut through the terrible Null Origin Tide that had stripped even Ervin of all ability to resist.","On his pillar, Damian slowly stood. His face was still pale from his battle with Max, and the Eternal Hourglass had not fully erased the spiritual exhaustion left behind by forcing Throne Of The Only Sword to its limit.","Even so, his posture remained straight, and his eyes carried no frustration, no hesitation, and no fear. A swordsman could lose, but a true swordsman did not let defeat make his blade dull.","Revona also opened her eyes. Her battle with Ervin had clearly consumed her as well. Her Void Origin Eyes looked calmer now, but beneath that calmness was a deep exhaustion.","She had used Return To Nothing, Null Origin Tide, and several deeper applications of Void Origin Realm in consecutive battles against Max and Ervin. Even someone like her could not continue using such powers without paying a price.","Angelina Valerius looked toward both of them.","\"Damian Voss.\"","\"Revona.\"","\"Enter the stage.\"","Two beams of light descended. Damian appeared on one side of the arena with his sword in hand. Revona appeared opposite him, her pale eyes already open and watching.","For a few breaths, neither of them moved. Damian looked at her calmly and said, \"I saw your battle with Max and Ervin, and honestly I don’t know if I could defeat you.\"","Revona replied quietly, \"Your attack against Max was powerful too but I want to see.\"","Damian’s sword intent rose slowly. \"Then we both understand there is no point in delaying.\"","Revona’s eyes deepened. \"Yes.\"","Angelina raised her hand.","[Battle Begins.]","The moment the battle started, both of them used their strongest power without hesitation.","Damian’s sword rose.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven.\"","A vast sword world appeared behind him. Sword-edge mountains pierced upward, rivers of sword light flowed across the sky, and the ancient sword altar stood at the center of that world.","Above it, the palace and the empty throne appeared once again, with the single sword hanging before the throne. Even after his previous defeats, even after exhausting himself against Max, the Sword Sovereign Heaven still descended with terrifying majesty.","Revona’s eyes shone.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","The world behind her became hollow, without sky, ground, sound, or warmth. Only pale-gray emptiness spread behind her, quiet and absolute.","The Void Origin Eyes looked through Damian’s sword world, not merely at the sword lights but at the structure behind them, the edict behind the sword path, the connection between Damian and his Pseudo Cosmic Path, and the foundation that allowed his sword heaven to pressure the battlefield.","The two Pseudo Cosmic Paths clashed immediately. Sword light descended, and void emptiness rose.","The first impact split the stage into silver-white sword scars and pale-gray hollow cracks. Golden laws of the Eternal Hourglass poured down at once, strengthening the barrier because this was not a normal collision.","Damian’s sword did not merely cut, and Revona’s void did not merely defend. Each side was trying to deny the other at the most fundamental level.","Damian attacked first.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, First Edict, All Blades Refuse Submission.\"","Countless sword lights descended from above, each one carrying the command of sword sovereignty. They did not scatter loosely across the battlefield. They converged from every angle, each blade-like light aiming for the gaps in Revona’s Void Origin Realm.","Revona lifted one hand.","\"Void Origin Eyes.\"","Half of the sword lights vanished before they touched her, and the other half dimmed, losing their killing intent and falling apart in pale-gray ripples. Yet Damian had already expected that. He stepped forward and raised his sword again.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Second Edict, One Sword Divides Heaven.\"","A single enormous sword line descended from above, splitting through the hollow ripples that had swallowed the first edict. It reached Revona faster than the previous attacks, and because it was condensed into one line, her Void Origin Eyes had to focus more sharply to erase it."]},{"number":1921,"title":"Chapter 1921: Same as Max and Ervin!","paragraphs":["Revona’s gaze locked onto the sword line, and it began to vanish. But Damian followed instantly.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Third Edict, Blade Meets The Void.\"","His sword moved through the opening created by the second edict, and a different sword light pierced from beneath the first one. Revona’s eyes shifted, erasing the second sword line halfway, but the remaining sword force cut across her sleeve and drew a thin line of blood from her arm.","The arena stirred. Damian had wounded her early.","The Sword God Palace disciples erupted.","\"Senior Brother Damian!\"","\"He is not giving her time to read everything!\"","\"He is using strongest attacks one after another!\"","Damian did not stop. He knew very well that Revona became more dangerous the longer she watched. If he gave her time to trace the foundation of Sword Sovereign Heaven, then his later attacks would lose their meaning one by one.","So he did what only a swordsman like him could do. He kept attacking with his strongest moves without hesitation.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Fourth Edict, Palace Sword Descends.\"","The palace above the sword altar brightened, and an enormous sword shadow fell from the sky like the judgment of the Sword God Palace itself.","Revona’s Void Origin Realm expanded to meet it, hollowing the outer sword force, but Damian stepped into the pressure and slashed again before the fourth edict fully ended.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Fifth Edict, Sword Heart Cannot Be Judged.\"","His sword heart stabilized. The pale-gray emptiness that tried to dull his sword intent failed to erase it completely. Damian’s blade cut through the hollowing field around Revona and forced her to retreat one step, then a second, then a third.","The Divine Realm went wild.","\"He is pushing Revona back!\"","\"Damian is using edicts continuously!\"","\"He knows he cannot let her adapt!\"","Revona’s eyes remained calm, but her expression had become more serious. Damian appeared before her through a river of sword light.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven, Sixth Edict, Bleeding Sword Severance.\"","Blood flowed along his sword, and the crimson-white sword light erupted with far more danger than before. It cut through one layer of the Void Origin Realm, then another, forcing Revona to raise both hands to block.","Her Void Origin Eyes shone brightly, tracing the blood sword’s authority, but Damian’s attack was too fierce and too close. The sword line passed through the edge of her defense, and blood appeared at the corner of Revona’s lips.","Damian’s sword did not pause. The empty throne behind him trembled, and his strongest sword intent began gathering again. Revona’s Void Origin Realm cracked around the edges. The spectators across the Divine Realm felt their breathing stop.","For a moment, it truly looked like Damian might push her into a corner before she could use her deepest method.","Damian raised his sword with both hands. The sword heaven behind him began to collapse inward. The mountains dissolved, the rivers vanished, the palace dimmed, and the altar cracked. The single sword before the throne descended again.","\"Sword Sovereign Heaven.\"","Damian’s voice was calm but exhausted.","\"Final Edict.\"","All his remaining sword authority gathered into one blade.","\"Throne Of The Only Sword.\"","The entire battlefield seemed to acknowledge only one sword again. That terrifying attack descended toward Revona.","Revona looked at the incoming sword. Her eyes shone with absolute emptiness.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","A point of nothingness formed before her palm.","\"Return To Nothing.\"","The two strongest attacks collided. For a breath, the arena lost all sound. The Throne Of The Only Sword tried to cut through the point of origin emptiness, while Return To Nothing tried to erase the absolute sword authority from its foundation.","The sword pressed downward, and the point of nothingness trembled. Revona slid backward, her feet carving deep marks into the stage. Damian’s sword hand bled, and his face became paler, but he continued pressing his final edict forward.","One inch. Then another. The point of Return To Nothing began to crack.","The Sword God Palace disciples shouted madly.","\"He is breaking it!\"","\"Senior Brother Damian is breaking Return To Nothing!\"","Revona’s eyes sharpened, and blood slipped down her chin. For the first time, Damian’s sword had pushed her strongest condensed technique close to collapse without relying on hidden tricks, time distortion, dimensional legacy, or layered domains. It was pure sword, pure will, and pure attack.","But Revona still had one more move. The move that had stripped Max bare. The move that had ended Ervin’s forbidden depth technique.","She slowly raised her other hand. Her voice was quiet.","\"Void Origin Realm.\"","The hollow world behind her opened fully.","\"Null Origin Tide.\"","Boom!","A massive pale-gray wave erupted from Revona’s body in every direction, and the Null Origin Tide swallowed the arena. Damian’s sword world was struck first.","The remaining mountains of Sword Sovereign Heaven vanished, the rivers of sword light disappeared, the cracked altar was erased, and the dim sword palace faded. The empty throne trembled violently before losing its shape.","Then the tide reached Damian himself. The sword authority around him dulled, and the Final Edict began losing its foundation.","The blood sword force vanished from his blade, and the sword heart that had resisted judgment was stripped of its external support. The Throne Of The Only Sword, which had been pressing Return To Nothing toward collapse, suddenly lost its absolute pressure.","Damian’s eyes changed. For the first time, he personally felt what Max and Ervin had faced. It was not like being blocked, and it was not like being overpowered. It was like everything that made his power meaningful had been removed.","His sword heaven disappeared, his sword edict disappeared, and his sword aura disappeared. Even the sharpness of the strike in his hand seemed to dry up under the pale-gray tide. Only his physical grip on the sword remained.","The Throne Of The Only Sword shattered.","Revona’s Return To Nothing also collapsed from the strain, but Null Origin Tide continued sweeping outward. Damian stood in the middle of it, his robes torn, his face pale, and his sword lowered slightly as the last traces of Sword Sovereign Heaven disappeared from around him.","He tried to raise his sword again. His wrist moved, but no sword light answered. The Null Origin Tide had stripped it all away.","Across the Divine Realm, the Sword God Palace fell into stunned silence."]},{"number":1922,"title":"Chapter 1922: The final battle!","paragraphs":["Damian looked at his sword quietly. Then he looked at Revona. She stood opposite him, pale and bleeding, clearly pushed to the edge by his repeated strongest attacks. Her Void Origin Eyes were exhausted, and her breathing was unsteady.","She had not won easily. Damian had forced her into a corner and nearly broken Return To Nothing with the pure strength of his sword.","But the Null Origin Tide had decided the result.","Damian slowly exhaled. \"So this is what they felt.\"","Revona replied quietly, \"You almost broke Return To Nothing.\"","\"But I could not get past the tide.\"","\"No.\"","Damian closed his eyes for a brief moment. Then he lowered his sword.","\"I admit defeat.\"","Angelina Valerius announced the result immediately.","[Winner: Revona.]","[Damian Voss Defeated.]","The screen above the arena changed.","[Battle Record Updated.] [Revona] [Total Battles Fought: 24] [Total Wins: 23]","[Battle Record Updated.] [Damian Voss] [Total Battles Fought: 24] [Total Wins: 21]","The Divine Realm erupted again, but the reaction was complicated. Revona had won, and Damian had lost.","Yet no one could overlook what had happened. Damian had pushed Revona hard enough that she had been forced to use Return To Nothing and then Null Origin Tide, the same attack that had stripped Max of almost all his powers and defeated Ervin outright.","He had almost cornered her with sword attack after sword attack, and for a moment, the entire Divine Realm had believed his Throne Of The Only Sword might actually break through.","But Revona’s final tide remained too terrifying.","On the pillars, Orion Starfall released a long breath. \"That attack is simply unreasonable.\"","Rakan Thorne frowned. \"It strips everything. How are you supposed to fight when your power is gone?\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked toward Max. \"Only Max had something beyond its reach.\"","Morgana Starveil’s gaze remained on Revona. \"And yet Damian almost forced her down before she used it.\"","Ervin watched silently. He understood Damian’s defeat better than most, because he had experienced the same thing. There was no shame in losing to Null Origin Tide. The terrifying thing was that Damian had nearly reached Revona before the tide swallowed his sword.","Max Morgan stood quietly on his pillar. His gaze rested on Revona for a moment, then shifted to Damian. Both of them were monsters, and both had reached the end of their strength. Now only one battle remained.","The final battle of the Cosmic Ascension Conference. Max Morgan against Ervin.","The second last battle of the Cosmic Ascension Conference ended with Revona standing victorious over Damian Voss.","Her victory did not come easily. Damian had pushed her to the brink with Sword Sovereign Heaven, forcing her to use Return To Nothing and then Null Origin Tide before he finally admitted defeat.","The Sword God Palace was silent, not because its strongest genius had been humiliated, but because he had shown the full dignity of a swordsman even in defeat.","Revona returned to her pillar pale and exhausted, while Damian stood quietly on his own pillar, his sword lowered at his side and his eyes calm despite another loss.","The records above the arena changed once more.","[Max Morgan] [Total Battles Fought: 23] [Total Wins: 23]","[Revona] [Total Battles Fought: 24] [Total Wins: 23]","[Ervin] [Total Battles Fought: 23] [Total Wins: 22]","[Damian Voss] [Total Battles Fought: 24] [Total Wins: 21]","Only one battle remained. The moment the Divine Realm realized that, the entire atmosphere changed.","The chaotic discussions surrounding Revona’s Null Origin Tide, Damian’s final sword, and Ervin’s earlier defeat slowly faded into one heavy, boiling silence. Countless eyes turned toward the two remaining pillars.","On one side stood Max Morgan, the white-haired genius of the Black Dragon Clan, the man who had defeated Revona, Damian, Orion, Kaiden, Rakan, Aurelian, Rosaline, and every other opponent placed before him.","On the other side stood Ervin, the abyssal spear wielder who had defeated Damian by the smallest margin and had only fallen to Revona after she used the same terrifying Null Origin Tide that had almost stripped Max bare.","One was still undefeated. The other had lost once, but no one dared to treat him as lesser.","Angelina Valerius stood above the restored central arena, her silver-white robe moving gently even though no wind existed in the Eternal Hourglass. Her pale golden hair shone beneath the golden laws surrounding the stage, and when she raised her hand, the entire Divine Realm quieted at once.","\"The final battle of the Cosmic Ascension Conference will now begin.\"","Her voice spread through every viewing formation, every ancient hall, every clan square, every sect pavilion, every hidden space, and every battlefield projection across the Divine Realm.","The screen above the arena flashed.","[Final Battle] [Max Morgan vs Ervin]","The moment those two names appeared together, the Divine Realm erupted with a roar that seemed capable of shaking the heavens.","The Black Dragon Clan exploded first. Countless disciples stood from their seats, shouting Max’s name with faces flushed from excitement. Elders who had been trying to maintain dignity for the entire conference finally failed to hide the trembling in their eyes.","Lady Virelia watched the screen with a proud and solemn expression, while Mathew Grimes and the other family heads stared as though they were witnessing the birth of something that might reshape the entire Divine Realm’s younger generation.","\"He reached the final battle undefeated!\"","\"Max Morgan is one victory away from the championship!\"","\"If he defeats Ervin, he will stand above every genius in this conference!\"","Across the Sword God Palace, the Nine Star Court, the Grand Void Sanctum, the War God Palace, the Stellar Templar, the elven factions, the hidden clans, and countless ancient forces, no one looked away.","Even those who had once mocked Max for his background, his origins, or his connection to the Black Dragon Clan now watched him with heavy expressions. A genius who could reach this point could no longer be dismissed by anyone.","At the same time, countless gazes also gathered on Ervin. He was not the undefeated one now, and he was not the statistical favorite.","But after his battle against Damian, after his forbidden technique against Revona, and after the terrifying depth of Abyssal Origin Descent had been revealed again and again, no one believed he had no chance.","If there was anyone remaining who could still force Max into danger, it was Ervin.","On the pillars, the top geniuses became silent. Revona opened her pale eyes and looked toward Max first, then toward Ervin. She had fought both of them and understood the danger of each more clearly than anyone else.","Damian Voss stood with his arms lowered, his sword sheathed, but his gaze was sharp and focused. Orion Starfall leaned forward with a bright smile, unable to hide the excitement in his eyes. Rakan Thorne grinned with battle hunger, while Kaiden Voidmere’s gaze became deep and still.","Angelina looked toward the two remaining contenders.","\"Max Morgan.\"","\"Ervin.\"","\"Enter the stage.\""]},{"number":1923,"title":"Chapter 1923: Ervin’s Thoughts!","paragraphs":["Two beams of golden light descended. Max appeared on one side of the central arena with Dragonheart at his waist, his white hair falling calmly over his shoulders and his expression unreadable.","Ervin appeared opposite him with his black spear in hand. His body had been mostly repaired by the Eternal Hourglass, but the exhaustion in his aura had not fully disappeared.","After fighting Damian to the brink and then breaking himself against Revona’s Null Origin Tide, even someone like Ervin could not return to perfect condition so quickly. Yet his eyes were still deep, steady, and abyss-like, as if the broken gate behind him had only sunk deeper after every defeat and victory.","For a few breaths, neither spoke. The Divine Realm watched in complete silence.","Then Ervin looked at Max and smiled wryly. \"It seems the final battle has become strange.\"","Max raised an eyebrow slightly. \"Strange?\"","Ervin glanced at the screen above them, where the records still shone clearly. \"You have twenty-three victories and no defeats. I have twenty-two victories and one defeat. Even if I defeat you here, both of us will have one defeat, and both of us will stand at twenty-three victories.\"","The spectators quieted even further as they realized what he meant.","Ervin shook his head lightly. \"In other words, even if I win, I will not truly become champion outright. The conference will end in a draw between us.\"","The words spread across the arena and immediately caused waves of discussion throughout the Divine Realm. Many people had been so caught up in the excitement of the final battle that they had not fully calculated the result.","Max had defeated Revona and Damian, while Ervin had defeated Damian but lost to Revona. If Ervin defeated Max now, his record would become twenty-three wins and one defeat, and Max’s record would also become twenty-three wins and one defeat.","In that case, unless Angelina or the Eternal Hourglass introduced another tiebreaker, the top of the conference would indeed become a draw.","In fact, even Revona had only one loss here, and that came against Max. So if Max were to lose against Ervin here, it would become a three-way tie between him, Ervin, and Revona.","But if Max won, then there would be no argument. He would finish with twenty-four victories and no defeats. Absolute champion.","The pressure of the final battle became even heavier.","Max looked at Ervin and smiled faintly. \"Then you should make sure I win.\"","Ervin’s wry smile deepened. \"If only you can force me to.\"","He paused for a moment, then his gaze became more curious. \"Before that, I do have one question.\"","Max looked at him calmly. \"Ask.\"","Ervin’s eyes narrowed slightly, but there was no hostility in them, only genuine interest. \"How did you defeat Revona after she stripped away your powers?\"","The entire arena became quieter. Even Revona’s gaze sharpened slightly from her pillar.","That question had been sitting in the hearts of countless spectators since Max’s battle against Revona. They had seen Revona use Null Origin Tide, and they had seen how it stripped Max of his powers before doing the same to Ervin and Damian.","Ervin had fallen once his abyss was erased, and Damian had been forced to admit defeat once his sword heaven was stripped away. Yet Max had somehow risen from that exact state and cut through Revona’s final defense.","What power had he used? What was that star-like radiance? What kind of legacy could remain beyond Revona’s nullification?","Max smiled. \"It is a secret.\"","Ervin stared at him for a breath. Then he laughed softly. It was not loud, but it was the first time many people had seen Ervin smile so openly.","\"I expected that answer.\"","He then lifted his black spear slowly, and the air around him began to sink.","\"Regardless of anything, let us have a good battle.\"","Max’s hand moved to Dragonheart’s hilt.","\"Agreed.\"","The atmosphere between them changed instantly. The light conversation faded, and the final battle truly began to take shape.","Ervin’s abyssal aura deepened, and beneath his feet, the faint shadow of a black sea began to spread. It was quieter than before, but more condensed. The broken gate did not appear yet, but its presence could already be felt somewhere deep below the battlefield, waiting to rise from the darkness.","Max’s sword aura also began to awaken. Dragonheart hummed faintly, and a cold, silent edge spread from him, brushing against the air like a blade that had not yet been drawn but had already severed the tension around it.","Angelina Valerius looked at them both, and for a rare moment, even she seemed to pause.","It was not hesitation, and it was not uncertainty. It was more like acknowledgement.","Even someone of her status, someone carrying the dignity of the hidden Valerius clan and acting under the recognition of the Eternal Hourglass itself, could feel the weight of this final battle.","Max Morgan had reached this point without a single defeat, cutting down every opponent placed before him, while Ervin stood opposite him with one defeat on his record but an abyssal spear path deep enough to terrify every genius who had faced it.","Their records were different, but their presence on the stage made it impossible for anyone to treat this as a simple final match.","The laws of the Eternal Hourglass brightened around the arena. Golden threads spread across the barrier like countless ancient seals preparing to contain a disaster. The restored stage beneath Max and Ervin became silent, yet that silence carried a pressure heavier than any roar.","On one side, Dragonheart gave a faint hum from Max’s hand, as though the sword itself understood that the last obstacle before the championship had appeared.","On the other side, Ervin’s black spear rested quietly in his grip, while the shadow beneath his feet deepened like a sea waiting for the first crack in the world.","Angelina’s gaze moved once across the stage, then across the pillars where Revona, Damian, Orion, Kaiden, Rakan, Morgana, and the other geniuses watched without blinking.","After that, her eyes lifted toward the countless viewing formations connected to the Divine Realm.","Then her hand descended.","[Final Battle Begins.]","The moment those words appeared, no one cheered. The entire Divine Realm held its breath.","Max Morgan against Ervin. The undefeated white-haired swordsman against the abyssal spear wielder. One carried Dragonheart, the Emotion Severing Path, and layers of power that had broken through even Revona’s final nullification.","The other carried Abyssal Origin Descent, the broken gate, and a spear path that had defeated Damian Voss by the smallest possible margin before forcing Revona to reveal everything. This was no longer only a clash between sword and spear.","It was the final collision between two monsters who had walked through the strongest geniuses of the conference and still remained standing at the end.","One battle would decide everything. If Max won, the Cosmic Ascension Conference would end with an absolute champion, a perfect record, and a name that no force in the Divine Realm could ignore again.","If Ervin won, Max’s undefeated record would be broken, Ervin would stand equal to him in total victories, and the conference would end in a draw between two terrifying existences who had both reached the summit from different paths.","The pressure was so heavy that even the top geniuses on the pillars forgot to breathe for a moment.","The final battle had begun."]},{"number":1924,"title":"Chapter 1924: Using Full Strength!","paragraphs":["The moment the final battle began, neither Max nor Ervin moved recklessly.","They stood on opposite sides of the arena, watching each other through the heavy silence that had fallen over the Eternal Hourglass.","After all the battles they had seen and fought, both of them understood one simple truth. There was no longer any need for shallow testing.","Ervin had watched Max defeat Revona, Damian, Orion, Kaiden, Aurelian, and Rakan, along with every other opponent placed before him.","Max had watched Ervin defeat Damian by the smallest margin and push Revona to the point where she had been forced to use Return To Nothing and Null Origin Tide.","Neither of them was an unknown opponent, and neither was weak enough to be handled with half-hearted attacks.","The first movement came from Max. His hand tightened around Dragonheart. Then the four Divine Veins opened inside his body.","\"Vein of Origin.\"","\"Vein of Vitality.\"","\"Vein of Speed.\"","\"Vein of Strength.\"","Boom!","A terrifying pressure erupted from Max’s body and shook the entire stage.","The Vein of Origin opened the deepest foundation of his power and made his aura suddenly feel vast, stable, and ancient, as if every technique he released would be supported by an origin that refused to collapse.","The Vein of Vitality filled his body with monstrous life force, causing his blood, bones, muscles, and spirit to surge with relentless endurance. The Vein of Speed sharpened his movement until his body seemed prepared to vanish at any instant, while the Vein of Strength poured a crushing physical force into his limbs that made the ground beneath his feet crack outward in a wide circle.","The audience had seen these four Divine Veins before, but even now, when they appeared together again, the shock they caused did not lessen. Max had already proved against Revona that these veins were not ordinary bodily enhancements.","When they worked together, his physical body became a weapon that could pressure even a fully awakened Void Origin Eyes user.","Now, with Dragonheart in his hand and Ervin standing before him, those same four Divine Veins made Max’s presence feel like a storm contained inside a human body.","But Max did not stop there.","Seven-colored lightning appeared above him. At first, it was only a faint crackle. Then the sky above the arena split open with a violent roar.","A throne of seven-colored lightning appeared in the storm, and behind it, a vast thunder tribunal formed like an ancient judgment hall descending from the heavens.","The lightning did not feel like ordinary destructive power. It carried verdict, punishment, authority, and divine wrath. Every arc of lightning seemed to be waiting for Max’s will, as if the entire storm existed to punish whatever opponent stood before him.","\"Pseudo Cosmic Path.\"","\"Divine King Punishment.\"","The seven-colored lightning roared. Then Dragonheart released a colder sound. The warmth around Max disappeared, and a silent, forbidden aura spread along the blade.","The invisible things in the air seemed to tremble before it, since killing intent, battle rhythm, technique connection, authority, and certainty all became fragile beneath that sword aura.","\"Emotion Severing Path.\"","The moment Max released both Pseudo Cosmic Paths, the atmosphere in the arena changed completely. On one side, Divine King Punishment hung above him like a heavenly verdict ready to descend.","On the other, Emotion Severing Path rested on Dragonheart like a forbidden edge capable of cutting the invisible support behind any technique. Between them stood Max’s body, strengthened by the four Divine Veins. The combination was terrifying.","Ervin watched it all calmly, but the abyss in his eyes grew deeper.","\"So you are starting seriously.\"","Max looked at him and said, \"You are not someone I can afford to test slowly.\"","Ervin smiled faintly.","\"Good.\"","He planted the end of his black spear into the stage, and the ground beneath him darkened.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","The black sea rose, spreading outward from beneath Ervin’s feet and covering half the arena in an instant. The water was not water in the ordinary sense.","It was depth given form, darkness given weight, and silence given motion. Every wave carried the feeling of something sinking forever, and every ripple seemed connected to a place so deep that light, sound, and direction could not return from it.","Then the broken gate emerged. It rose from the black sea, enormous and ancient, half-submerged behind Ervin, covered in unreadable symbols that flickered like dying stars beneath the abyss.","The moment it appeared, the arena seemed to tilt downward toward Ervin, as if the world itself had found a lower point and wanted to fall into it.","\"Gate of the First Depth.\"","The gate opened, and a heavy abyssal pressure surged across the stage.","Ervin lifted his spear. \"I will not hold back.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"That is better.\"","Ervin moved first.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Hollow Descent Thrust.\"","His spear pierced forward, and the black sea behind him followed the tip like a sinking world. The attack did not travel in a straight line.","It dropped through depth, vanished from the surface of the battlefield, and reappeared directly before Max’s chest with a pressure that could drag his body and sword into the abyss at the same time.","Max stepped forward. The Vein of Speed flashed, and Dragonheart moved.","\"Emotion Severing Sword.\"","His blade cut across the path of the spear.","Clang!","The first collision erupted with terrifying force. The abyssal thrust tried to pull Dragonheart downward, but the Emotion Severing Path cut through the connection between the spear force and the depth behind it.","At the same time, Max’s Vein of Strength erupted through his arm, and the sheer physical power behind his sword forced Ervin’s spear to bend slightly to the side.","Ervin’s eyes narrowed. Max did not stop. Seven-colored lightning descended from above.","\"Divine King Punishment, Thunder Verdict.\"","A pillar of seven-colored lightning slammed toward Ervin’s head.","Ervin spun his spear immediately.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Hollow Moon Guard.\"","A crescent-shaped abyssal shield rose before him, swallowing the first layer of lightning. But Divine King Punishment did not act like ordinary thunder.","The moment its first layer was swallowed, the second layer detonated inside the abyssal guard, causing seven-colored arcs to burst through the darkness.","Ervin slid back. Max appeared before him at the same instant. The Vein of Speed made his movement almost impossible to follow, and the Vein of Strength carried Dragonheart down with brutal force.","Clang!","Spear and sword collided again, and this time Ervin was forced back three steps.","The Divine Realm erupted.","\"Max has the advantage!\"","\"Ervin’s abyss swallowed part of the lightning, but Max’s sword severed the depth connection!\"","\"He is attacking with body, lightning, and sword path at the same time!\"","\"That combination is too much!\""]},{"number":1925,"title":"Chapter 1925: Sever The Descent!","paragraphs":["Ervin’s expression remained calm, but his arm had clearly trembled from the last collision. Max’s physical strength was different from Damian’s sword pressure and Revona’s nullification. Damian’s attacks were sharp and absolute, and Revona’s attacks erased and hollowed.","Max, however, brought too many different kinds of danger at once. His body struck like a dragon, his lightning punished from above, and his sword severed the hidden structure behind Ervin’s abyss. Every time Ervin blocked one layer, another layer followed immediately.","Ervin stepped deeper into the black sea.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, First Depth Tide.\"","The sea rose in a massive wave and charged toward Max from the front, while two hidden currents curved behind him from both sides.","Max did not retreat. The Vein of Origin stabilized his foundation, the Vein of Vitality surged through his body, and the Vein of Strength roared in his arm. Then he slashed.","\"Emotion Severing Path, Severing Current.\"","Dragonheart cut through the front wave, and the visible black sea split apart. But the two hidden currents still arrived from behind. Before they could strike his back, the thunder tribunal above him roared again.","\"Divine King Punishment, Sevenfold Trial.\"","Seven bolts of lightning descended at once. Three struck the hidden current on the left, and three struck the hidden current on the right. The final bolt struck directly toward Ervin.","Ervin raised his spear and thrust upward.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Deep Current Reversal.\"","The black sea twisted around his spear and absorbed the final lightning bolt before reversing part of its force back toward Max.","But Max had already vanished from his original position. The Vein of Speed carried him through the gap between two crashing waves, and in the next instant, he appeared at Ervin’s right side.","His fist moved before his sword.","Boom!","The punch landed against Ervin’s spear shaft. It was only a punch, but it carried the Vein of Strength. The spear shaft slammed into Ervin’s chest, and the impact drove him backward across the stage.","The black sea beneath him erupted to slow his retreat, but Max’s seven-colored lightning crashed down again, striking the sea and forcing the abyssal water to scatter.","Ervin coughed softly, and a trace of blood appeared at the corner of his mouth.","Across the pillars, the geniuses became even more serious.","Damian Voss looked at the stage and said quietly, \"He is not giving Ervin time to deepen the gate.\"","Kaiden Voidmere nodded. \"That is the correct choice. If the abyss is allowed to settle, every attack becomes harder to finish.\"","Revona watched Max with pale, sharp eyes. \"He is attacking the rhythm, not only Ervin.\"","Rakan Thorne grinned. \"And his body is absurd.\"","On the stage, Ervin wiped the blood from his lips with the back of his hand.","\"You are faster than before.\"","Max held Dragonheart calmly. \"You have seen my fights. I cannot surprise you with something ordinary.\"","Ervin’s smile deepened slightly. \"Then I will go deeper.\"","The Gate of the First Depth trembled, then it opened wider.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","The pressure of the black sea increased.","\"Gate of the Second Depth.\"","Boom!","The stage sank under a far heavier force. The black sea turned denser, and the darkness beyond the broken gate became so deep that even the light of Divine King Punishment dimmed slightly near its edge.","This was the same gate that had pushed Damian to the brink and allowed Ervin to unleash attacks powerful enough to threaten the strongest geniuses of the conference.","Max’s eyes sharpened. The battle had truly started now.","Ervin raised his spear with both hands.","\"Second Depth Spear.\"","The black sea gathered around the spear tip, forming a sinking world of darkness.","\"Sunken World.\"","He thrust forward, and a terrifying force surged toward Max. It did not merely attack his body. It tried to make his entire position sink. The ground, air, sword aura, lightning path, and even the space around him seemed to descend toward the Second Depth.","If this attack struck cleanly, Max’s momentum would collapse, and Ervin would drag the rhythm of the battle into his own abyssal world.","Max stepped forward again. The Vein of Origin shone within him, the Vein of Vitality roared, the Vein of Speed accelerated his body, and the Vein of Strength gathered into Dragonheart. Above him, Divine King Punishment descended, and around his sword, the Emotion Severing Path condensed.","\"Divine King Punishment, Heavenly Verdict Descent.\"","Seven-colored lightning crashed into the front of Sunken World. At the same time, Max swung Dragonheart.","\"Emotion Severing Sword.\"","The sword line cut into the sinking world. The abyssal force pressed forward with frightening power. Divine King Punishment destroyed layer after layer of the outer depth, while Emotion Severing Path cut into the connection between the spear and the Second Depth behind it.","Max’s body still felt the sinking pressure, but the four Divine Veins held him in place.","The Vein of Vitality prevented the pressure from crushing his internal flow. The Vein of Origin prevented the abyss from disturbing his foundation, and the Vein of Strength allowed him to keep pushing forward with terrifying physical force.","For several breaths, Sunken World and Max’s combined attack clashed violently. Then Max took one step. The stage cracked. He took another, and Ervin’s spear trembled. A third step, and Sunken World split.","Ervin’s eyes changed. Max broke through the front of the attack and arrived before him, Dragonheart descending with lightning wrapped around its edge.","Ervin raised his spear.","Clang!","The impact forced Ervin’s knees to bend slightly. The black sea behind him surged to support him, but Max’s Emotion Severing Path cut the support halfway, and Divine King Punishment struck the sea from above, weakening it further.","Max leaned forward slightly. His voice was calm.","\"You cannot block me like this.\"","Ervin’s gaze deepened. \"I know.\"","The broken gate behind him groaned. He twisted his spear and released a sudden inward pull.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent, Return To Depth.\"","A whirlpool opened beneath Max’s feet, and the abyss tried to drag him downward. Max’s body sank slightly for the first time, but he did not panic. His Vein of Strength erupted again, and he stomped the ground with terrifying force.","The stage cracked outward. At the same time, Dragonheart stabbed downward.","\"Emotion Severing Path, Sever The Descent.\""]},{"number":1926,"title":"Chapter 1926: This is my strongest attack!","paragraphs":["The sword pierced into the edge of the whirlpool, and the invisible connection pulling Max toward the Second Depth was cut. The whirlpool collapsed.","Ervin used that brief moment to retreat, but Max followed immediately with the Vein of Speed. His movement was too fast, too direct, and too violent.","In close combat, Ervin’s spear was profound, and his technique carried incredible depth, but Max’s body had become too overwhelming with the four Divine Veins activated.","Every sword strike carried the strength of a body refiner. Every step crossed distance like lightning. Every collision threatened to tear Ervin’s guard apart.","\"Abyss Spear Art, Gate Shadow Thrust.\"","Ervin’s spear stabbed from the shadow of the broken gate.","Max turned Dragonheart sideways and blocked.","Clang!","\"Divine King Punishment, Judgment Chain.\"","Seven-colored lightning wrapped around the spear shaft. Ervin released abyssal depth to swallow it, but the Emotion Severing Path on Dragonheart flashed again and cut at the rhythm of his release.","The chain of lightning tightened for a fraction of a breath, and that was enough for Max to step in and slam his shoulder into Ervin’s chest.","Boom!","Ervin was blasted backward, and blood spilled from his mouth. The Gate of the Second Depth shook behind him.","The Divine Realm was boiling now.","\"Max is suppressing him!\"","\"Ervin opened the Second Depth, but Max still has the upper hand!\"","\"His body is too strong, and those two Pseudo Cosmic Paths are attacking different weaknesses!\"","\"Divine King Punishment breaks the outer abyss, while Emotion Severing Path cuts the hidden connections!\"","\"How is Ervin supposed to defend against all that while also dealing with Max’s physical strength?\"","Ervin landed near the edge of the arena, one knee bending slightly before he forced himself back up. The black spear in his hand trembled. His eyes remained calm, but his breathing had grown heavier.","Max stood at the center of the battlefield, Dragonheart in hand, seven-colored lightning roaring above him, Emotion Severing Path spreading from his sword, and the four Divine Veins blazing through his body like divine channels of ancient power.","At that moment, even the top geniuses had to admit one thing. In direct clashes, Max had the upper hand. Ervin’s abyss was deep, his spear was terrifying, and his Pseudo Cosmic Path was worthy of standing near the top of the entire conference.","But Max’s physical strength, supported by the four Divine Veins and reinforced by the simultaneous pressure of Divine King Punishment and Emotion Severing Path, was too much for him to handle in straightforward exchanges.","Ervin slowly exhaled. Then he smiled faintly despite the blood on his lips.","\"As expected, I cannot beat you head-on.\"","Max looked at him calmly. \"You knew that already.\"","\"I did.\"","The broken gate behind Ervin became darker, and the black sea beneath him sank again. His smile faded, and his eyes became abyssal.","\"That is why I will have to use something else.\"","The moment Ervin said those words, the black sea beneath him stopped moving. It did not calm. It became dead still. The entire Abyssal Origin Descent behind him changed in a way that made even the top geniuses on the pillars feel their expressions tighten.","The Gate of the Second Depth, which had already opened earlier, trembled as though something behind it was pushing against its ancient frame.","The unreadable symbols carved across the broken gate began bleeding black light, and every drop that fell into the sea below caused the stage to sink with a dull, oppressive rumble.","Max watched quietly.","Ervin lifted his spear with both hands. His fingers were already bleeding. The previous forbidden art he had used against Revona had nearly broken his body, but this one was different. The aura coming from him did not merely strain his flesh. It began destroying him from within the moment he summoned it.","Cracks appeared across his arms first, thin and dark, as if abyssal pressure had carved itself beneath his skin. Then those cracks spread to his shoulders, chest, neck, and face. Blood flowed from them, but it did not fall normally.","The blood sank into the air, swallowed by the abyss before it could touch the ground.","The Divine Realm became silent. Everyone could see what was happening. Ervin was burning his body as the price for one final spear.","Revona’s pale eyes narrowed from her pillar. She had forced Ervin into a similar state before, but even she could tell that this technique was beyond what he had used against her.","Damian Voss silently gripped the hilt of his sword, his gaze becoming solemn.","Orion Starfall’s smile disappeared for the first time in a long while, while Rakan Thorne’s battle-crazed expression became heavy. Kaiden Voidmere stared at the broken gate with deep eyes, as if he could feel the space around the arena becoming unable to escape the pull of the abyss.","Angelina Valerius looked down at the battlefield, her eyes calm but sharper than before. The golden laws of the Eternal Hourglass began brightening even before Ervin attacked.","Ervin coughed blood. His knees bent slightly, but he did not fall. Instead, he smiled. It was not a wry smile this time. It was a clear one.","\"Max Morgan,\" he said, his voice hoarse but steady, \"this attack will destroy my body if the Eternal Hourglass does not repair me afterward.\"","Max looked at him silently.","Ervin raised his spear higher. \"But if I do not use it here, then there is no meaning in standing in this final battle.\"","The broken gate behind him opened again, not wider but deeper. A third layer did not appear as a visible gate but as a dark absence beyond the second gate, a depth so heavy that even the black sea seemed afraid to fall into it.","The moment that depth appeared, Ervin’s body cracked further. His bones groaned, and his blood vessels burst beneath his skin. The abyssal pressure around him became so dense that the arena floor beneath his feet began to cave downward, even though the Eternal Hourglass laws were continuously repairing it.","\"Abyssal Origin Descent.\"","Ervin’s spear shook.","\"Forbidden Final Depth Art.\"","The black sea rose behind him, then collapsed into the spear. The broken gate bent inward, and the darkness beyond it poured into the spear tip like the last shadow of a dying world.","\"Body-Burying Abyss Spear.\"","The moment the name fell, Ervin’s aura disappeared from the surface of the battlefield. Then it returned from below. Not from below the stage, but from below existence. The spear in his hand no longer looked like a weapon. It looked like a black line connected to a place where all worlds sank after their end.","The attack had not yet been released, but everyone could feel that if it landed, it would not simply pierce flesh or destroy defense. It would bury the body, the power, the movement, the will, and the battlefield itself under a depth that Ervin’s current body was never meant to carry.","His skin split further. Blood poured from him, and even his black spear began to crack. Yet his eyes remained fixed on Max.","\"This is my strongest attack.\""]},{"number":1927,"title":"Chapter 1927: The Winner!","paragraphs":["Max’s expression did not change. He did not mock him, and he did not praise him loudly. He only tightened his grip around Dragonheart.","Then the 5000 Dragon Essences inside his body awakened. All at once.","Boom!","A roar that sounded like thousands of dragons rising from an ancient battlefield exploded from Max’s body. The four Divine Veins were already burning inside him, but the moment the full power of the 5000 Dragon Essences surged through his flesh, blood, and bones, the pressure around him changed completely.","His body no longer felt like that of a swordsman strengthened by divine veins alone. It felt like a human-shaped dragon monarch standing beneath a storm of seven-colored heavenly punishment.","Black dragon scales spread across his skin.","\"Dragon Scales Transformation.\"","The scales emerged layer by layer, each one dense, sharp, and filled with chaotic draconic pressure. His shoulders widened slightly, his pupils sharpened, and the air around his body cracked under the sudden rise of raw physical force.","The Vein of Origin stabilized the violent power.","The Vein of Vitality kept his body from being torn apart by the surge.","The Vein of Speed sharpened every muscle and nerve, and the Vein of Strength fused with the 5000 Dragon Essences, pushing his physical power to a level beyond what he had shown earlier in the battle.","Above him, Divine King Punishment roared, and the seven-colored lightning throne brightened until it looked like a divine court judging the final spear of the abyss.","Dragonheart began to hum. The Emotion Severing Path spread over the blade again, colder than ever before. Then Max added the sword technique that had defeated Damian’s strongest sword.","\"Saint Origin Sword Art.\"","The moment the name appeared, Dragonheart’s aura became terrifyingly complete. The Emotion Severing Path alone was a forbidden edge, a path that could cut emotion, connection, intent, rhythm, certainty, authority, and even the invisible foundation behind techniques.","But with the Saint Origin Sword Art guiding it, that forbidden edge gained origin, structure, and perfect sword order. The severing force no longer spread outward like a cold mist.","It gathered into a single pure line along Dragonheart’s blade, refined until every fragment of power knew exactly what it had to cut.","Max’s right hand held Dragonheart, and his left hand rested near the hilt. His dragon-scaled body sank slightly as the seven-colored lightning gathered above the blade, and the Emotion Severing Path condensed inside the sword edge while the Saint Origin Sword Art gave form to it all.","Across the Divine Realm, countless experts stood up.","\"This pressure.\"","\"The Eternal Hourglass is reacting.\"","\"Both attacks are beyond what the stage expected from the younger generation.\"","The golden laws around the arena became blinding, and for the first time, the Eternal Hourglass trembled faintly. It was not a violent shake. It was small, almost unnoticeable to ordinary spectators, but every true expert sensed it.","The Eternal Hourglass, the supreme venue that had casually contained the battles of the greatest geniuses of this era, had trembled because of the attacks gathering on the stage.","Ervin saw it. Max saw it. Neither stopped.","Ervin stepped forward first. His body almost broke from the movement, but the spear in his hand descended with him.","\"Body-Burying Abyss Spear.\"","The spear thrust out, and the world before Ervin sank. The stage, air, space, lightning, sword aura, and even the golden laws around the impact point seemed to bend downward toward a final depth. The black line of the spear carried the weight of a buried world, rushing toward Max with a power that could have ended nearly any other genius in the conference.","Max stepped forward at the same time. His dragon scales flashed, and the 5000 Dragon Essences roared. Divine King Punishment descended into Dragonheart, and his sword came down.","\"Saint Origin Sword Art.\"","His eyes were calm.","\"Emotion Severing Sword.\"","The slash appeared. It was not large at first. It was a single sword line, cold, bright, and terrifyingly quiet, wrapped in seven-colored lightning and carried by the raw physical force of Max’s dragon-scaled body. But the moment it moved, everything in its path began to separate.","The sinking pressure in front of Ervin was cut. The abyssal line connected to the final depth was cut. The buried-world force wrapped around the spear was cut, and the connection between Ervin’s broken gate and the forbidden spear was cut.","The sword did not merely collide with the Body-Burying Abyss Spear. It severed the things that allowed that spear to become the strongest attack of Ervin’s life. The Saint Origin Sword Art guided Max’s Emotion Severing Path with ruthless precision, while the seven-colored lightning punished each severed layer before the abyss could reform it.","The full physical power of the 5000 Dragon Essences and Dragon Scales Transformation drove the blade forward like an unstoppable dragon descending with divine judgment.","The Body-Burying Abyss Spear trembled. Ervin’s pupils contracted. For a brief moment, his strongest attack pushed back. The abyss roared from beyond the broken gate, and the black line of the spear tried to drag Max’s sword slash into the final depth.","But Max’s slash only became brighter. The Eternal Hourglass trembled again, and golden laws burst around the arena like chains trying to hold the battlefield together.","Then the forbidden spear split.","Crack!","The sound was not loud, but it echoed across the entire Divine Realm. The black line of abyssal depth was cut apart from the center.","The Body-Burying Abyss Spear collapsed layer by layer, its buried-world pressure severed, its final-depth connection broken, and its forbidden authority shattered beneath the combined power of Max’s dragon-strengthened body, Divine King Punishment, Emotion Severing Path, and Saint Origin Sword Art.","Ervin’s black spear broke in his hands. The broken gate behind him cracked, and the black sea dropped as if its source had been severed.","Max’s sword slash continued forward. It did not stop after cutting the attack. It passed through the remains of the abyss, through the shattered shadow of the gate, through the last defense Ervin raised with his broken spear shaft, and stopped only when Dragonheart’s edge reached the side of Ervin’s neck.","The arena became silent. Ervin stood frozen, blood pouring from the cracks across his body. His forbidden art had nearly destroyed him.","His strongest attack had been severed. His spear had broken. And Max stood before him in full Dragon Scales Transformation, seven-colored lightning fading around Dragonheart, his white hair moving gently behind him and his eyes calm.","For several breaths, neither spoke. Then Ervin looked at the broken spear in his hands. After a moment, he gave a soft laugh.","\"So even this attack of mine got severed.\"","Max lowered Dragonheart slightly, but the blade remained close enough to end the battle if Ervin tried to continue.","\"It was a good attack.\"","Ervin smiled faintly, blood staining his lips. \"It was my best.\"","\"I know.\"","Ervin’s knees finally weakened. Before he could collapse, the golden laws of the Eternal Hourglass wrapped around his body to keep his injuries from worsening further. He looked at Max one last time, still smiling faintly despite his ruined state.","\"Then I lose.\"","Angelina Valerius raised her hand. Her voice spread across the silent arena.","[Winner: Max Morgan.]","[Ervin Defeated.]","For one breath, the entire Divine Realm remained completely still. Then the final result screen began to shine."]},{"number":1928,"title":"Chapter 1928: Winner of Cosmic Ascension Conference!","paragraphs":["For one breath, the final result screen above the Eternal Hourglass shone like the brightest star in the starry sky.","The whole Divine Realm seemed frozen under that golden light, as if everyone needed a moment to take in what had just happened.","Ervin’s strongest forbidden spear, the Body-Burying Abyss Spear, had come out with enough force to shake the Eternal Hourglass itself. Still, Max Morgan had faced it without fear.","He had unleashed the full power of his 5000 Dragon Essences, entered the Dragon Scales Transformation, strengthened his body with the four Divine Veins, gathered Divine King Punishment into his blade, guided the Emotion Severing Path through the Saint Origin Sword Art, and cut down the strongest attack Ervin had ever thrown.","The black sea was gone. The broken gate had faded. Ervin’s spear had snapped. And Max Morgan was still standing.","Angelina Valerius looked down at the arena, her pale golden eyes taking in the state of the battlefield. Golden light from the Eternal Hourglass wrapped around Ervin, healing the damage from his forbidden technique and keeping his body from breaking down further.","Across from him, Max stood with Dragonheart lowered at his side. His dragon scales were fading, and small sparks of seven-colored lightning drifted around him like the last pieces of a storm.","Then the result screen changed.","[Battle Record Updated.]","[Max Morgan]","[Total Battles Fought: 24]","[Total Wins: 24]","[Total Defeats: 0]","Beneath it, new words appeared.","[Perfect Victory Record Achieved.]","Then a second record showed up.","[Ervin]","[Total Battles Fought: 24]","[Total Wins: 22]","[Total Defeats: 2]","The whole Eternal Hourglass went quiet. No one spoke. No one cheered. It felt like no one was even breathing.","Then Angelina Valerius raised her hand. The golden light around the Eternal Hourglass grew brighter, and the huge screen above the arena stretched out until it filled almost the entire sky over the stage.","Ancient symbols circled around it slowly, like divine seals marking down an event people would remember for years to come.","Angelina’s voice rang out.","\"The final battle has ended.\"","Her tone was calm, but there was a weight behind it that made every word land harder.","\"With twenty-four wins, zero losses, and a perfect record in the final stage, Max Morgan is the winner of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The golden screen lit up.","[Cosmic Ascension Conference Champion]","[Max Morgan]","For one moment, those words hung over the arena like something out of the heavens. Then the whole Divine Realm exploded. The noise was bigger than anything that had come before it.","Every viewing formation linked to the Eternal Hourglass shook under the flood of voices. Countless cities, forces, clans, palaces, floating islands, ancient halls, trading hubs, academies, and hidden corners of the world shook with millions of people shouting Max’s name at once.","Max Morgan. The name spread like wildfire.","In the Black Dragon Clan, the entire place lost it. Disciples shouted until their voices went hoarse. Elders who had kept their composure for centuries stood up with shaking hands.","Some laughed out loud. Some slammed their fists on tables hard enough to break them. Some just stared at the screen with wet eyes, still not quite believing that someone from their own clan had reached the top of the Cosmic Ascension Conference with a perfect record.","\"Champion!\"","\"Max Morgan is the champion!\"","\"Twenty-four wins and not a single loss!\"","\"The Black Dragon Clan has raised the strongest genius of this whole conference!\"","Lady Virelia stood in front of the huge projection with her hands clasped behind her back. Her face stayed calm, but the small curve at the corner of her mouth said everything she didn’t put into words.","She was the one who had chosen Max. She had brought him into the Black Dragon Clan and watched him grow from an unknown talent into someone who could now stand above Damian Voss, Revona, Ervin, Orion, Kaiden, Rakan, Aurelian, and every other top genius of this generation.","Mathew Grimes stared at the screen for a long moment before letting out a deep breath.","\"From now on, no one in the Divine Realm will dare call him just a lucky junior.\"","Another family head nodded slowly. \"That’s right. From now on, every force out there will have to put his name at the very top of their watch list for the younger generation.\"","In the Sword God Palace, the mood was mixed. Damian Voss had now lost twice in the final stretch, but none of the swordsmen there could deny what they’d just seen.","Max hadn’t won because Damian was weak. He’d won because his sword was sharp enough to cut through the final edict of Sword Sovereign Heaven itself.","Many disciples stared at the champion screen without saying a word, their pride stung, but quietly shaken by the sheer beauty of the sword clash they’d just watched.","In the Nine Star Court, Orion Starfall’s supporters cheered and sighed all at once. Orion had lost to Max, but that fight had forced Max to bring out the Emotion Severing Path in full.","The Nine Star Court’s elders knew well enough that Orion’s loss hadn’t dulled his shine. It had just placed him in the same era as someone even more terrifying.","In the Grand Void Sanctum, Kaiden Voidmere’s elders watched the screen with heavy, unreadable faces. Max had beaten Kaiden with a clear edge in the Void Genesis Art and the Dimensional Sovereign Body.","Now that Max was champion, their thoughts grew even more complicated, since they understood the link between Max and their own supreme inheritance path was not a simple one.","In the War God Palace, Rakan Thorne’s supporters laughed loudly despite his loss. To them, losing to the champion wasn’t shameful. It just proved Rakan had fought someone truly worth fighting.","In the elven lands, the reaction hit harder. Aurelian Lareth sat in silence in front of the projection, his face pale, his fists clenched so tight his nails dug into his palms.","Every time Max’s name flashed on the screen, it felt like another slap to his pride. The stolen Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline inside him pulsed faintly, and Max’s calm voice echoed in his memory again.","\"Take care of my bloodline until then. It won’t be long before I come for it.\"","Aurelian’s face twisted, but he said nothing. There was nothing he could say.","Far from him, among the scattered survivors of the old third elven faction, Nancy, Caroline, Jessica, and others watched the same projection with pounding hearts.","Some covered their mouths. Some cried quietly. Some just stared at the white-haired young man under the champion screen, struggling to connect him to the child whose life had once been torn apart by betrayal.","Caroline’s eyes filled with tears. \"He really did it.\"","Nancy nodded, her voice shaking. \"Her Majesty’s son is the champion.\"","Inside the Eternal Hourglass, the other top fighters were watching Max too.","Revona sat quietly, pale and worn out, but there was no bitterness in her eyes. She had lost only after pushing Max hard enough to reveal a power that even her Null Origin Tide couldn’t erase. To her, that loss made sense.","Damian Voss stood with his sword sheathed, calm, a trace of respect still lingering in his eyes.","Ervin, still wrapped in healing golden light, looked at Max and smiled faintly despite his battered state.","\"You really became champion.\"","Max looked back at him. \"You made that final fight hard.\"","Ervin laughed softly. \"Not hard enough.\"","Max didn’t answer right away. Then he smiled.","\"You kept standing until your spear broke.\"","Ervin’s smile stayed faint. \"It was the least I could do.\""]},{"number":1929,"title":"Chapter 1929: End of the Conference!","paragraphs":["Angelina Valerius lowered herself slightly, and the golden light around the arena gathered above Max.","A glowing mark slowly took shape in the sky, marking him as champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference. It didn’t sink into him right away. It just hovered there, shining like a crown waiting for the formal ceremony.","The whole Divine Realm watched that scene. Countless people understood this moment meant more than just the end of a conference. It marked the rise of a name.","Max Morgan had entered the Cosmic Ascension Conference as a surprising talent from the Black Dragon Clan. He was leaving it as the strongest genius of his era. At least, that’s what most of the Divine Realm believed.","But far away from the great clans and palaces buzzing over the new champion, there was a quiet, out-of-the-way planet with dim skies, broken mountains, and a small city protected by old formations.","Inside a simple, well-guarded hall on that planet, a few people were watching the same broadcast. The picture wasn’t as clear as the ones the big forces had. It flickered now and then from the distance and interference, but the words above the arena still came through.","[Cosmic Ascension Conference Champion]","[Max Morgan]","Among the people in that hall stood a beautiful woman with a calm smile.","Freya, Max’s older sister. Her eyes stayed fixed on the screen, and when she saw Max standing under the golden champion banner, her expression softened in a way few people around her had ever seen. There was pride in her eyes, but no surprise.","There was warmth in her smile, but no disbelief.","Beside her stood Lucien. He stared at the projection for a long while without saying anything. His usual easy manner had given way to something more serious, and his eyes stayed locked on Max’s figure, as if he were trying to measure something the screen couldn’t fully show.","After a long pause, Lucien let out a slow breath.","\"He’s really become the strongest genius in the Divine Realm.\"","The others in the room turned toward him. Lucien didn’t look away from the screen.","\"I always knew Max was special, but this is different. Beating Revona, Damian, Ervin, and everyone else with a perfect record isn’t something you can put down to talent alone.\" His eyes grew more serious. \"If I fought him right now, at the same level, I’m not sure I could beat him.\"","Those words made the whole room go quiet. Everyone there knew how much pride and strength Lucien carried, so hearing him say something like that meant a lot.","Freya just smiled. Her eyes stayed on Max. She wasn’t shocked, and she wasn’t doubtful. She simply watched the white-haired figure under the champion screen and thought to herself.","’Of course you did it, Max.’","Her smile grew a little warmer.","’I wouldn’t expect anything less from my little brother.’","===","The final result screen kept shining above the Eternal Hourglass for a long time.","[Cosmic Ascension Conference Champion]","[Max Morgan]","[Final Record: 24 Wins, 0 Defeats]","[Perfect Victory]","Max Morgan had won. The white-haired genius of the Black Dragon Clan had gone through the entire final stage without losing a single match.","He’d beaten the strongest young fighters of this generation one after another.","He’d beaten Rosaline’s Dawn Sovereign Sanctuary, Rakan’s War God Body, Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth, Aurelian’s Heavenly Luminance Divine Dominion, Orion’s Nine Star Sovereign Body, Revona’s Void Origin Realm, Damian Voss’s Sword Sovereign Heaven, and Ervin’s Abyssal Origin Descent.","Every name he’d faced was strong enough to shake an ancient force on its own, yet all of them had eventually fallen to his sword, his body, his bloodline, his Pseudo Cosmic Paths, and the deep well of strength hidden behind his calm face.","Angelina Valerius stood above the restored arena and looked down at Max. Golden light from the Eternal Hourglass gathered around her like streams of ancient power, and for the first time since the final stage began, the giant hourglass above the arena stopped turning.","The sand inside it went still, and the whole world inside the venue seemed to bow toward the end of the conference.","Angelina raised both hands slightly.","\"The Cosmic Ascension Conference has come to its end.\"","Her voice was calm, but it carried further than ever before.","\"The final stage is complete. Every battle has been recorded. Every ranking has been confirmed. By the authority of the Eternal Hourglass, watched over by the Primordials, and witnessed by the whole Divine Realm, I officially declare the Cosmic Ascension Conference over.\"","The golden screen lit up again.","[Cosmic Ascension Conference Officially Concluded.]","[Champion: Max Morgan.]","The moment those words appeared, the whole Eternal Hourglass roared one last time. This wasn’t just a roar of shock anymore. It was a roar of closure, the sound of an era recognizing its newest monster.","The defeated fighters on the pillars looked at Max, each with a different look on their face.","Orion Starfall smiled brightly, his eyes still full of excitement from a fight worth remembering. Rakan Thorne laughed loudly and punched his own palm, clearly already hungry for another shot someday.","Kaiden Voidmere stayed quiet, but the respect in his eyes was plain to see.","Damian Voss stood tall with his sword at his waist, calm and dignified even in defeat.","Revona’s pale eyes stayed fixed on Max, as if she were still trying to work out the star-like power that had gotten past her Null Origin Tide.","Ervin, mostly healed now by the Eternal Hourglass, looked at Max with a small smile, the broken pieces of his spear already restored beside him by the venue’s power.","Angelina’s gaze passed over all of them before settling back on Max.","\"The award ceremony and everything else after the conference will be handled according to the rules of the Eternal Hourglass and the agreements between the participating forces. For now, everyone will be sent back to their own forces.\"","Golden light lit up beneath every fighter. One by one, beams of light came down, and the pillars began to empty. Some fighters vanished quietly.","Some looked at Max one last time before disappearing. Some clenched their fists, already thinking ahead to the day they’d get to fight him again.","Max stood in the middle of the arena as the light gathered under his feet. Dragonheart rested quietly at his side, and the last traces of seven-colored lightning faded from the air around him.","His dragon scales were gone, his divine veins had closed, and the terrifying power from the final battle had settled back into his body.","Even without any visible power around him now, he seemed heavier somehow, as if the title of champion had added an invisible weight to his presence.","Angelina Valerius looked at him one last time.","\"Congratulations, Max Morgan.\"","Max gave a small nod. \"Thank you.\"","Then the golden light swallowed him whole."]},{"number":1930,"title":"Chapter 1930: Celebrations!","paragraphs":["The Eternal Hourglass disappeared from his vision. For an instant, there was only silence and flowing golden light. Then the world changed.","Max appeared back in the Black Dragon Clan. The moment his feet touched the ground, a thunderous roar hit him from every direction.","\"Max!\"","\"Champion!\"","\"Max Morgan!\"","\"The champion has returned!\"","It felt like the entire Black Dragon Clan had gathered to welcome him. The main square was packed with disciples, elders, branch members, family guards, servants, retainers, and powerful figures from every faction in the clan.","Huge banners had already gone up across the sky, black and gold dragon flags flapped in the wind, and countless celebration formations sent streams of light into the heavens. Dragon-shaped fireworks burst above the clan grounds, spelling out Max’s name again and again in blazing golden letters.","[Max Morgan]","[Cosmic Ascension Conference Champion]","The cheering grew even louder the moment everyone saw him standing there. Many young disciples shouted until their voices cracked. Some looked at him like they were seeing the future of the Black Dragon Clan itself.","Even elders who normally kept a strict, dignified air were smiling openly, their eyes full of pride and disbelief. The Black Dragon Clan had sent Max to the Cosmic Ascension Conference as a top-tier genius, but he had come back as the undisputed champion with a perfect record.","That changed everything. This win didn’t belong to Max alone anymore. In the eyes of the clan, it belonged to the whole Black Dragon Clan too.","Lady Virelia stood at the front of the crowd. Her expression stayed calm, but the pride in her eyes was impossible to hide. She looked at Max for a few breaths before a faint smile crossed her face.","\"You did well.\"","Those three words were simple, but to the people who knew her, they carried a lot of weight.","Max smiled faintly. \"I only did what I had to do.\"","Mathew Grimes laughed loudly from the side. \"Only did what you had to do? Brat, you beat every monster in that conference and came back with twenty-four wins and zero losses. Do you know how many old clans probably can’t sleep right now because of you?\"","Several family heads laughed along, while some elders nodded with serious looks.","One elder said, \"From today on, the name Max Morgan won’t just be treated as a rising genius. It’ll be treated as the name of a future overlord.\"","Another elder added, \"No force out there will dare look down on the Black Dragon Clan’s younger generation again.\"","The disciples roared once more.","\"Future overlord!\"","\"Champion Max!\"","\"Black Dragon Clan’s pride!\"","Max looked out at the sea of excited faces and felt something strange in his chest. He’d faced storms of lightning, abyssal gates, void nullification, sword thrones, war bodies, and divine light, and countless deadly techniques, without his expression really changing much.","But now, standing in front of the clan that had watched him rise through the conference, hearing them celebrate him so sincerely, he felt something quieter settle inside him.","For a moment, his thoughts drifted to his mother, his father, his sister, Caroline, Nancy, Jessica, and everyone else tied to the truth behind his bloodline and his past. Winning the Cosmic Ascension Conference wasn’t the end. It was just a step. An important one, but still just a step.","Aurelian still had the stolen source. His parents were still locked away. The people behind the old betrayal were still out there. There were still enemies waiting beyond this celebration.","But today, at least for this moment, Max let himself smile.","The crowd saw that smile and exploded again.","Lady Virelia’s smile deepened a little. Mathew Grimes stepped forward and clapped Max hard on the shoulder, though the impact meant nothing to Max after everything he’d been through.","\"Come,\" Mathew said with a grin. \"The whole clan has been waiting to celebrate. Don’t think you can come back as champion and just quietly disappear like nothing happened.\"","Max looked at the overflowing crowd, the banners in the sky, the cheering disciples, and the elders watching with shining eyes. Then he sighed lightly, though the smile stayed on his face.","\"Looks like I don’t have a choice.\"","Lady Virelia said calmly, \"You don’t.\"","The disciples nearby laughed. The celebration got even louder.","As Max walked forward into the heart of the Black Dragon Clan, voices rose all around him, chanting his name over and over.","Above the clan grounds, dragon-shaped lights circled the sky, and the golden words announcing his championship kept shining like a message to every nearby territory.","The Cosmic Ascension Conference had ended. Max Morgan had come home. And the Black Dragon Clan celebrated the birth of its champion.","The celebration in the Black Dragon Clan didn’t wind down quickly. For a full day and night, the clan grounds stayed brighter than most cities look in broad daylight.","Dragon-shaped fireworks crossed the sky in waves, celebration formations poured golden light over the main square, and disciples kept talking about the Cosmic Ascension Conference again and again, like they were retelling a legend that had just been born in front of them.","Every battle got discussed. Every opponent got brought up. Every moment where Max revealed a new power got repeated with even more excitement than the last telling.","Max himself got dragged from one hall to another, from one group of elders to the next, and from one crowd of disciples to another, until even he started to think that fighting Ervin’s forbidden final spear had been easier than escaping his own clan’s enthusiasm.","Mathew Grimes laughed every time Max tried to slip away quietly, while Lady Virelia watched from the side with a faint smile that made it clear she had no plans to rescue him.","It wasn’t until the second morning that the celebrations finally started to settle. The banners stayed up in the sky, and the golden words announcing Max as the Cosmic Ascension Conference Champion still hung above several major halls, but the big crowds had begun to thin out. Disciples went back to their courtyards with hoarse voices and shining eyes.","Elders returned to their duties with smiles they couldn’t quite hide. The whole Black Dragon Clan seemed to carry a new kind of pride, one that hadn’t come from old history, ancient bloodline status, or inherited power, but from a young man who had stood in front of the strongest geniuses in the Divine Realm and beaten every single one of them.","But before the clan could fully settle back into peace, another announcement shook the upper levels of the Black Dragon Clan.","Lady Virelia was summoned to the central ancestral hall."]},{"number":1931,"title":"Chapter 1931: Master of the 33rd Hall!","paragraphs":["The meeting wasn’t open to ordinary disciples, but word got around fast anyway.","The thirty-six halls of the Black Dragon Clan sat among the highest seats of power, just below the true ruling elders and the patriarch’s own authority. Each hall controlled its own resources, disciples, territories, experts, and duties.","A hall master wasn’t just an elder with a fancy title. A hall master was someone whose voice could shape the direction of the whole clan.","And now, Lady Virelia had been named one of the hall masters of the thirty-six halls.","When the news got out, nobody stayed surprised for long. Some elders had once questioned her choice to bring Max in from the mortal realm.","Some had wondered why a woman of her standing would personally get involved with a junior who, back then, had no deep foundation in the Divine Realm and no ancient divine background to match the native geniuses of the top forces. But all those doubts didn’t matter anymore.","Lady Virelia had chosen a mortal. That mortal had entered the Divine Realm. That mortal had represented the Black Dragon Clan.","And that mortal had become the strongest genius of the entire Cosmic Ascension Conference. No political argument could stand up against that. No internal faction could deny that kind of achievement.","Inside the ancestral hall, Virelia stood calmly in front of several supreme elders, her silver eyes steady and unreadable. The old experts around her carried deep auras and ancient authority, but none of them looked at her with the faint dismissiveness some might have shown in the past.","The champion’s spotlight hadn’t landed only on Max. It had also landed on the person who found him, chose him, protected him, and brought him into the Black Dragon Clan.","One old supreme elder looked at her and spoke slowly.","\"Virelia, your judgment has brought great fortune to the clan. Max Morgan’s victory has changed how the Divine Realm sees us, and it’s also given the younger generation of the Black Dragon Clan someone to look up to. Because of this achievement, and because of your past merits, the council has agreed to name you the new Hall Master of the 33rd hall.\"","The hall went quiet.","The 33rd hall wasn’t a weak one. It controlled several important cultivation grounds, a lot of elite disciples, and a big share of resources tied to combat training and bloodline tempering.","For Virelia to be named its hall master right after Max’s victory showed just how much weight the clan had put on her contribution.","Lady Virelia bowed slightly. \"I accept.\"","Her voice was calm, but the elders could tell her standing in the clan had shifted completely. From that day on, no one would think of her as just Max’s master or the woman who picked him up from the mortal realm.","She was now Lady Virelia, Hall Master of the Ninth Dragon Hall, one of the thirty-six hall masters of the Black Dragon Clan.","By the time the news spread through the clan, plenty of disciples got worked up all over again.","\"Lady Virelia became a hall master!\"","\"Of course she did. She’s the one who picked Senior Brother Max out of the mortal realm.\"","\"Can you imagine? A mortal genius she raised up ended up becoming champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","\"That alone is enough to shake the whole clan.\"","\"That means Senior Brother Max has even stronger backing inside the clan now too.\"","The talk kept going for hours.","Max heard the news later that same day. He wasn’t surprised. If anything, he felt she deserved it.","Lady Virelia had backed him back when his name carried no real weight in the Divine Realm, and even though Max had never needed anyone to carry him, he understood well enough that her decision had given him a place inside the Black Dragon Clan and a platform to rise faster.","The next day, the excitement in the clan had cooled down a bit, though things were still lively.","Max sat in a quiet spot inside one of the buildings in the Dimension of Genesis. The pavilion looked out over a lake covered in dark-gold lotus flowers, with thin streaks of spiritual mist drifting above the water.","Alice sat across from him, her eyes bright with curiosity, while Lenavira leaned against the side railing with a calm, faintly amused look.","Alice had been peppering him with questions for almost half an hour.","\"So when Revona used that Null Origin Tide and stripped away all your power, what did it actually feel like?\" she asked, leaning forward with both hands on the stone table. \"Everyone outside could only see the black flames die down and then that star-like light show up around you. I still don’t get how you got out of that.\"","Lenavira looked at him too. \"I’m curious about that as well. That woman beat both Ervin and Damian with the same attack. Even after watching it a few times, I still can’t tell how you broke through it.\"","Max lifted the tea cup in front of him and took a slow sip.","\"It felt awful,\" he said honestly.","Alice blinked. \"That’s it?\"","Max smiled faintly. \"What else do you want me to say?\"","\"I want details,\" Alice said right away. \"You became champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, beat Revona, Damian, and Ervin, and now you’re sitting here drinking tea like nothing happened. At least describe it properly.\"","Lenavira smiled lightly. \"She’s got a point. You’re way too calm for someone who just shook the whole Divine Realm.\"","Max set the cup down.","\"I’m calm because the conference is over. If I keep getting worked up after every win, I’ll wear myself out before the real problems show up.\"","Alice’s expression shifted slightly. \"Real problems?\"","Max didn’t answer right away. His gaze drifted across the lake.","The Cosmic Ascension Conference had ended, but his enemies hadn’t gone anywhere. Aurelian still held the stolen source of his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. His parents were still locked away in the Celestial Thorn Abyss.","The forces behind his family’s betrayal were still standing. And now that he was champion, even more eyes would be on him than before.","Lenavira noticed the shift in his expression and let it go.","Alice also went quiet for a moment before switching the subject.","\"Still, you really did beat everyone. Orion, Kaiden, Revona, Damian, Ervin. Even the people who doubted you before can’t say a thing now.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"They can still say plenty of things.\"","Alice shook her head. \"They can, but nobody’s going to believe them.\"","Just as she said that, the air above the courtyard shifted.","A deep bell sound rang out across the inner district of the Black Dragon Clan. Once. Then twice. Then a third time. It even reached the Dimension of Genesis, since Max had made sure that anything happening outside could be heard or seen from inside his dimensions.","The bell wasn’t a war alarm, but it carried a solemn weight that made Alice’s and Lenavira’s expressions change at the same time. Max turned his gaze toward the sky as well."]},{"number":1932,"title":"Chapter 1932: Envoy of the Primordial Race!","paragraphs":["A black-gold pathway opened above the clan’s outer boundary formation.","Several powerful auras rose from the Black Dragon Clan at once, not out of hostility but as a formal welcome. The sky above the main entrance filled with dragon-shaped formations, and a group of elders appeared beneath the opened pathway.","Among them stood Mathew Grimes, several hall masters, and Lady Virelia, who now wore the formal insignia of the Black Dragon Palace.","Alice stood up. \"Someone important arrived.\"","Lenavira narrowed her eyes. \"Very important. The clan wouldn’t use that kind of reception for an ordinary envoy.\"","Max’s eyes deepened.","A moment later, an elder’s voice echoed through the courtyard.","\"Max Morgan, the clan requests your presence at the main reception hall.\"","Max slowly stood.","Alice looked at him. \"Do you know who it is?\"","\"No,\" Max said calmly, \"but I’d guess it’s connected to the conference.\"","Lenavira’s gaze sharpened. \"The rewards?\"","Max didn’t answer, but he was thinking the same thing.","A few moments later, Max arrived at the main reception hall. The mood inside was solemn. Mathew Grimes stood at the front with several high-ranking elders, and Lady Virelia stood slightly to one side, her new hall master token hanging at her waist.","The moment Max walked in, several eyes turned toward him, but the strongest presence in the room didn’t come from the Black Dragon Clan.","It came from the stranger standing near the center.","The man looked tall and ancient, though his face didn’t seem old or young. His hair was silver-black, his eyes carried faint violet-gold rings, and his robe was woven from something that seemed to shift between starlight and darkness depending on the angle.","He didn’t give off overwhelming pressure, yet just being near him made the surrounding air feel denser than usual.","He wasn’t from any ordinary divine race. He was an envoy of the Primordial Race.","The moment Max entered, the envoy turned toward him. His gaze lingered on Max’s face for a second, then seemed to look deeper, as if he were reading through Max’s flesh, blood, aura, soul, and hidden foundation all at once.","But he didn’t act arrogant about it. Instead, he gave a slight nod.","\"Max Morgan.\"","Max looked at him calmly. \"I am.\"","The envoy’s voice was steady. \"I am Sarvion, envoy of the Primordial Race. I’ve come under the order of the Primordial Council to escort you to the Primordial Ancestral Domain.\"","The hall grew even quieter. Even though many had already guessed why he’d come, hearing it said out loud still landed with weight.","Sarvion went on. \"As the champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, you’ve earned the highest reward the Primordial Race grants to this generation.\"","Alice and Lenavira had only followed as far as the side entrance of the reception area, but even from there, they couldn’t hide their shock at hearing that.","The envoy looked straight at Max.","\"You are to receive the Primordial Award.\"","Several elders drew in a soft breath at those words.","It was no secret in the Divine Realm that the top ten of the Cosmic Ascension Conference weren’t just rewarded with treasures, cultivation resources, or ancient techniques. Those things had value, but the real meaning of the conference tied back to the Primordials themselves.","The top ten were said to be chosen by the Primordial Race. They’d be granted that race’s bloodline and given a chance to walk the path toward becoming Primordials themselves. For most geniuses, this was the single greatest opportunity of a lifetime.","The Primordial Race stood above countless divine bloodlines. Their foundation went older and deeper, closer to the original laws of existence, than most races could imagine.","Even a trace of their bloodline could reshape a genius’s body, talent, perception, and future. And an official shot at becoming a true Primordial was something even ancient clans would go mad over.","Max wasn’t just one of the top ten. He was the champion. That meant his reward would be the greatest of them all.","Sarvion continued. \"The rest of the top ten will be summoned in turn, but the champion has first right. You’ll be brought to the Primordial Ancestral Domain, where the inheritance ceremony will take place. If it succeeds, you’ll officially step onto the path of the Primordial Race and be recognized as a Primordial candidate.\"","The words \"Primordial candidate\" made the whole hall tighten up.","Mathew Grimes’s eyes lit up. Several elders couldn’t hide their excitement. Even Lady Virelia’s expression grew more serious.","Max, though, stayed calm.","He looked at Sarvion and asked, \"And if the ceremony fails?\"","The envoy’s eyes shifted slightly, as if he appreciated the question.","\"Then you’ll still receive a partial Primordial bloodline along with other rewards fitting for the champion. But if the ceremony fully succeeds, you won’t just get a bloodline. You’ll become one of us, in name, in foundation, and in future potential.\"","The hall went silent again.","Alice looked at Max with wide eyes. Lenavira’s expression turned complicated too.","Officially becoming a Primordial wasn’t a small thing. It wasn’t like joining a clan, taking a title, or accepting an ordinary inheritance.","It meant Max’s identity in the Divine Realm would shift again. He was already the champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, the strongest genius of the younger generation, and the pride of the Black Dragon Clan. If he also became tied to the Primordial Race, his standing would rise to a level that countless forces would find frightening.","Max looked at the envoy for a moment. Then he smiled faintly.","\"So the champion’s reward is to become a Primordial.\"","Sarvion nodded. \"That is the highest reward, among other things.\"","Max’s gaze stayed calm, but a thought passed through his mind.","’Another bloodline. Another inheritance. Another path.’","He already carried a lot. The Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline. The Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. The Dimensional Sovereign Body.","The Emotion Severing Path. Divine King Punishment. The Devouring Flames Domain. The Seven Divine Veins. Dragonheart. The Dimensional Keeper legacy. And now the Primordials were offering him a shot at becoming one of them.","Max didn’t yet know whether this opportunity would turn out simple, dangerous, or tangled up in deeper secrets of the Divine Realm.","But he knew one thing for sure. He hadn’t fought through the Cosmic Ascension Conference just for applause. If there was a reward out there that could make him stronger, he’d take it, because sooner or later, he’d need every bit of strength he could get."]},{"number":1933,"title":"Chapter 1933: Idle Time With Alice and Lenavira!","paragraphs":["Sarvion looked at him and spoke again.","\"The Primordial Ancestral Domain is ready. Once your clan has finished its arrangements, you may leave with me.\"","Lady Virelia stepped forward. \"How much time does he have?\"","Sarvion answered calmly. \"The champion has priority, but the ceremony can’t be pushed back for long. Three days at most.\"","Mathew Grimes looked at Max. \"Then you’ll prepare during those three days.\"","Max nodded.","Sarvion’s gaze stayed on him. \"Max Morgan, champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, the Primordial Race awaits you.\"","The reception hall fell into a heavy silence.","Outside the hall, the Black Dragon Clan was still soaking in the glow of Max’s victory. But inside, everyone understood that the next Chapter of his journey had already opened.","The Cosmic Ascension Conference had ended. The road to the Primordials had begun.","The three days before Max had to leave for the Primordial Ancestral Domain passed faster than he expected.","The Black Dragon Clan wanted him to rest, prepare, and settle after the conference, but Max had no plans to spend those days buried under endless visits, formal congratulations, and elders quietly trying to probe the powers he’d revealed.","The conference had already put too many eyes on him.","Every force in the Divine Realm was studying his abilities, his fighting style, his bloodline, his sword path, his lightning, his black flames, his physical strength, and the mysterious star-like power he’d used against Revona.","If he stayed openly in the clan, he wouldn’t get a single hour of peace.","So Max went to the Dimension of Genesis.","For him, it was an escape. For Alice and Lenavira, it was simply home. They already lived there. Lily tagged along too, buzzing around excitedly like a small spirit who could never sit still for long.","The moment Max arrived, the noise of the Black Dragon Clan faded behind him.","The Dimension of Genesis stretched out in its vast, peaceful glory, full of pure energy, ancient light, floating islands, spiritual lakes, and distant stars that looked close enough to touch yet far enough to remind anyone that this place wasn’t ordinary.","The air here carried a feeling of beginnings, as if every breath held a trace of creation itself.","Alice was already there, sitting on the edge of a floating platform like she’d never left. Lenavira stood nearby under a drifting veil of light, calm as always, as if she’d been standing there since the world began.","Neither of them looked surprised. This was their home. They just watched Max as he arrived.","\"You’re back,\" Alice said casually, like he’d only stepped out for a short walk.","Max paused for a moment, then smiled faintly. \"I suppose I am.\"","Lenavira gave a soft nod. \"Was it the Primordials?\"","\"Yes. I leave in three days.\"","Lily zipped around Max’s head in a circle, giggling. \"You always leave us!\"","She hovered in front of him, puffing her cheeks slightly like a kid complaining about being left behind.","Max glanced at her. \"You were with Alice and Lenavira the whole time.\"","Lily crossed her arms. \"Still boring!\"","Alice chuckled. \"She says that even when nothing’s wrong.\"","Lenavira’s lips curved slightly. \"She says it when everything’s wrong too.\"","Lily pointed at them both. \"Hey!\"","Max watched them for a moment and let out a light breath. For once, his mind didn’t jump straight to cultivation, battles, or enemies.","The Dimension of Genesis wasn’t a place he had to \"enter\" anymore. It was just where he came when he needed quiet. And Alice and Lenavira were already part of that quiet.","The days that followed were calm. Max didn’t spend every moment cultivating. Sometimes he walked with Alice beside the spiritual lake while she asked him about the conference, about Orion’s excitement, Rakan’s stubbornness, Damian’s sword, Revona’s terrifying Null Origin Tide, and Ervin’s final forbidden spear.","Sometimes Lenavira sat with him under an ancient tree on one of the floating islands, talking about the deeper meaning behind the Primordial Race’s arrival and what kind of test he might face in the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","Lily followed everywhere. Not quietly. She hovered, spun, complained, laughed, and occasionally tried to \"help\" by dramatically explaining things she barely understood.","At one point, she even tried to copy Max’s serious expression while floating upside down. Alice laughed so hard she nearly fell off the platform. Lenavira just shook her head, though her eyes stayed warm.","Max didn’t mind. For these few days, the outside world faded. There was no Cosmic Ascension Conference. No Aurelian. No stolen bloodline source. No imprisoned parents. No Primordial envoy waiting outside. Just the people close to him and the quiet passing of time inside the Dimension of Genesis.","During those three days, Max also did a fair bit of business. He first met up with Lucia and Isabella, then had a deep talk with Lucia about Crown and about how he was building his own force and would need people he could trust.","In the end, Max invited Lucia into Crown, and she accepted.","After that, Max told Isabella, Lucia, Jonathan, and Julie to keep working the plan of recruiting other geniuses using his name.","Now that Max had become the strongest genius in the Divine Realm, almost everyone would have heard of him. That was exactly the plan he’d had from the start: use his fame to pull people into his own force.","While all this was happening, Max’s cultivation didn’t sit still either.","In truth, his foundation had already reached its limit long before the final battle. Throughout the entire Cosmic Ascension Conference, Max had stood at the very peak of the Law Awakening Realm.","His accumulation was far beyond what ordinary geniuses could match.","Every battle had tempered him, and every clash with a Pseudo Cosmic Path had sharpened his understanding. Every life-and-death exchange against opponents like Revona, Damian, and Ervin had forced his laws, body, soul, and sword path to refine themselves again and again.","He hadn’t broken through during the conference simply because the timing hadn’t been right. He’d suppressed it. He’d controlled it. But now, in the calm of the Dimension of Genesis, the barrier finally loosened on its own."]},{"number":1934,"title":"Chapter 1934: Law Refinement Realm level 1","paragraphs":["On the third day, Max sat cross-legged on a floating island above a sea of silver mist. Alice and Lenavira were nearby as always, not watching from a distance like outsiders but simply there as part of the space itself.","Lily hovered above Max’s shoulder, swinging her legs in the air like a kid waiting for something interesting to happen.","Around Max, the laws of the Dimension of Genesis began to gather. At first the movement was gentle. Then it grew vast. Strands of law energy rose from every direction, circling him like countless rivers returning to their source.","The Law Awakening Realm was the stage where cultivators first sensed the deeper laws of the world, and Max had already reached its limit. Now his body, soul, and inner world weren’t just awakening to laws anymore. They were refining them.","The barrier shattered silently.","Boom!","A vast aura burst out of Max’s body. The Dimension of Genesis trembled softly, not from danger, but in response.","[Breakthrough Achieved.]","[Law Refinement Realm 1st Level.]","Max opened his eyes. For a moment, his pupils seemed to hold countless flowing laws. His aura was no longer wild. It had grown deeper, more condensed, more refined. The power inside him no longer felt newly awakened.","It felt like something being sharpened, purified, and folded into his foundation.","Alice smiled immediately. \"You broke through.\"","Lenavira nodded calmly. \"Law Refinement Realm, first level.\"","Lily clapped her hands excitedly. \"Finally! That took forever!\"","Max slowly stood, and the moment he did, his Pseudo Cosmic Paths responded.","First came the Emotion Severing Path. A cold, silent sword aura spread from him, but it was no longer rough or unstable. It had become cleaner, more precise, more complete. Every edge felt like it knew exactly what it was meant to cut.","Lily leaned forward curiously. \"Ooooh, it feels sharper.\"","Then Divine King Punishment stirred. Seven-colored lightning flickered above Max’s palm. The thunder no longer felt like raw wrath alone. It carried structure now, as if a divine tribunal was slowly taking shape inside it, and the authority behind it had deepened.","Lily’s eyes widened. \"That one looks scary now.\"","Then the Devouring Flames Domain woke up. Black flames appeared around Max’s fingers, silent and controlled. They no longer burned wildly. They devoured with precision, like something that had learned patience.","Lily immediately hid behind Alice. \"I don’t like that one.\"","Alice laughed softly. \"You’re the one who always gets too close.\"","The three Pseudo Cosmic Paths rose around Max at once. The Emotion Severing Path, Divine King Punishment, and the Devouring Flames Domain, along with other auras that also kept rising around his body.","Lenavira watched quietly. \"They’re nearing completion.\"","Max could feel it too. They were close. But not complete.","Lily peeked out again, serious for once. \"You’re still far from finishing them. Even if they look close, they’re not real Cosmic Paths yet.\"","Alice tilted her head. \"What’s missing?\"","Lily puffed her cheeks. \"Everything important!\"","Max closed his hand, and the paths sank back into his body.","\"So they’re nearing completion,\" he said quietly.","Lily nodded. \"Yes. But only on the edge. My inheritance memories told me a lot about the cosmic paths. You can refine them, strengthen them, make them scarier, but completing them before the Divine Lord Realm is impossible.\"","Alice looked at him. \"Even for you?\"","Lily shook her head firmly. \"Especially for him. The stronger the path, the harder it gets. And his are weirdly strong.\"","Lenavira’s gaze softened. \"So Law Refinement Realm only made them more stable.\"","Max nodded. \"That’s enough for now.\"","He could feel the difference clearly. A stronger body. Sharper laws. More refined control. And Pseudo Cosmic Paths that had stepped closer to something far greater.","Alice smiled. \"You just became champion, broke through, and now you’re already getting stronger again. People outside would lose their minds.\"","Max gave a faint smile. \"Then they don’t need to know.\"","Lily immediately pointed at him. \"Yes! That’s right! We hide it!\"","Alice looked at her. \"You’re very enthusiastic about hiding things.\"","Lily nodded proudly. \"It’s fun!\"","Lenavira sighed softly. \"That’s not a good reason.\"","Lily stuck her tongue out.","\"It’s about time. I should leave with the envoy of the Primordial Race,\" Max said suddenly. \"Three days have passed.\"","The mention of the Primordial Race settled the mood right away. The envoy would be waiting. The road to the Primordial Ancestral Domain was about to open.","Max looked toward the distant sky of the Dimension of Genesis, where countless stars shimmered over the sea of mist. The quiet days were ending. He turned back toward them.","\"I’ll visit you all later.\"","Alice and Lenavira both nodded solemnly. They understood that Max’s trip to the Primordial Race would matter a great deal. This wasn’t a simple reward trip, and it wasn’t just about accepting a title.","The Primordial Race stood above countless ancient bloodlines in the Divine Realm, and the chance to officially receive their bloodline and step onto the path of becoming a Primordial was something even supreme clans would dream of for their strongest descendants.","Alice looked at him for a few breaths, then smiled softly. \"Be careful.\"","Lenavira’s gaze was calmer, but the worry in her eyes wasn’t hidden. \"Don’t trust everything too easily. The Primordial Race may be handing you a reward, but a reward from a race like that is never simple.\"","Max nodded. \"I know.\"","Lily floated in front of him and put both hands on her waist, trying to look serious despite her small size. \"Come back soon.\"","\"I will,\" Max said with a smile.","Lily’s serious look melted away immediately. \"You better.\"","Max looked at Alice, Lenavira, and Lily one last time. The Dimension of Genesis stayed quiet around them, and for a moment, he felt the strange contrast between this peaceful world and the storm waiting outside.","Here, Alice and Lenavira had already become part of his life in a way that needed no explaining. Lily still acted noisy and childish, but she was also one of the few beings who understood the depth of his secrets.","Leaving them for this trip wasn’t hard because he feared for himself. It was hard because he knew every step forward would bring him closer to greater danger.","Still, he had to go."]},{"number":1935,"title":"Chapter 1935: Leaving!","paragraphs":["A moment later, Max vanished from the Dimension of Genesis.","When he returned to the Black Dragon Clan, the mood outside had already turned solemn. Sarvion, the envoy of the Primordial Race, was waiting near the main transfer square, standing calmly under the protection of several ancient formations.","His silver-black hair moved slightly in the wind, and his violet-gold ringed eyes held a depth ordinary cultivators couldn’t stare into for long. He didn’t look impatient. He simply stood there, as if three days were nothing more than a blink to him.","He wasn’t alone, though. Many members of the Black Dragon Clan had gathered to see Max off.","Lady Virelia stood at the front, wearing the formal insignia of the 33rd hall at her waist. After becoming one of the thirty-six hall masters, her authority in the clan had clearly grown.","The elders near her treated her with far more respect than before, but her attention wasn’t on them. Her eyes were on Max the moment he appeared.","Mathew Grimes stood nearby too, along with several family heads and high-ranking elders. Behind them stood rows of elite disciples, inner clan members, and guards, all quiet.","The earlier celebration had already ended, but the pride in their eyes hadn’t faded. If anything, watching Max prepare to leave for the Primordial Race made them even more aware of how far he’d risen.","A mortal genius chosen by Lady Virelia had entered the Divine Realm. That same genius had become champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference. Now he was being personally escorted by an envoy of the Primordial Race to receive the conference’s greatest reward.","For the Black Dragon Clan, this was glory. For Max, it was just another step.","Lady Virelia walked toward him first. \"You’re leaving alone?\"","Max nodded. \"The envoy came for me. No need for anyone else to come along.\"","Virelia looked at him quietly for a moment. \"The Primordial Ancestral Domain isn’t a place the Black Dragon Clan can easily step into. Once you’re on their territory, most of this will be up to you.\"","\"I understand.\"","\"Then remember one thing,\" Virelia said, her voice calm but serious. \"A reward strong enough to change your race and your foundation is never without risk. Don’t let the name of the Primordials blind you.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"I won’t.\"","Mathew Grimes laughed, though there was concern under it. \"You brat, you just became champion and now you’re already off somewhere even more troublesome. Can’t you let the clan enjoy your win a little longer?\"","Max looked at him. \"The Primordials only gave me three days.\"","Mathew clicked his tongue. \"Exactly. Arrogant old beings.\"","A few elders nearby coughed lightly at that, but Sarvion didn’t react. It was as if he hadn’t heard a word.","Max looked toward the gathered disciples. The moment his eyes swept over them, many straightened up at once.","\"Senior Brother Max, come back safe!\"","\"Become a Primordial and shock the Divine Realm again!\"","\"Don’t forget the Black Dragon Clan!\"","\"Senior Brother Max, we’ll wait for your return!\"","Their voices rose one after another until the whole transfer square filled with sound again. It wasn’t as wild as the celebration after his return from the conference, but it carried something deeper. There was excitement, pride, respect, and a faint reluctance to see him leave so soon after his biggest win.","Max gave them a slight nod. \"I’ll return.\"","Those three words were simple, but the disciples cheered again anyway.","Lady Virelia stepped back slightly.","Sarvion finally moved. \"Max Morgan, it’s time.\"","Max turned toward him. \"Let’s go.\"","Sarvion raised one hand, and the space above the transfer square changed instantly. It didn’t tear open violently like an ordinary spatial passage. Instead, countless violet-gold lines spread across the sky in an elegant pattern, forming a gate that looked carved from ancient starlight.","The gate’s aura felt strange. It wasn’t just connecting two places. It felt like it was opening a road through a higher layer of space, one guarded by laws that ordinary divine powers couldn’t easily touch.","The moment the gate appeared, many elders of the Black Dragon Clan grew solemn. Even Lady Virelia’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Sarvion looked at Max. \"This path leads to the outer reception boundary of the Primordial Ancestral Domain. Once we pass through, you’ll be under the Primordial Race’s watch.\"","Max nodded, then stepped forward.","Before entering the gate, he looked back once. Lady Virelia, Mathew Grimes, the elders, the disciples, and countless members of the Black Dragon Clan were all watching him.","The black and gold dragon banners above the square moved in the wind, and the huge formations around the clan glowed softly, as if sending him off.","Max turned back and entered the violet-gold gate with Sarvion.","The world changed. For a short while, there was no ground under his feet and no sky above his head. Max walked through a passage filled with streams of starlight, ancient symbols, and faint echoes of laws that seemed older than most inheritances he’d ever seen.","Sarvion walked ahead of him, his robe shifting between darkness and light with every step. The passage was silent, but Max could feel countless hidden restrictions around them.","Anyone who tried to force their way into this route would likely be erased before they even understood what they’d touched.","After a while, the starlight passage opened, and Max stepped out.","The moment he emerged, his eyes changed slightly.","Before him stood the land of the Primordial Race. It didn’t look like an ordinary territory. There was no single city, no normal mountain range, no simple palace complex. The whole region seemed to sit somewhere between ancient creation and divine order.","Vast continents floated in the sky, connected by bridges of light stretching across impossible distances. Rivers of liquid starlight flowed through the void between them.","Mountains taller than entire worlds rose from the edges of floating landmasses, and above it all, enormous rings of ancient runes rotated slowly, like wheels of law guarding the whole domain."]},{"number":1936,"title":"Chapter 1936: Primordial Ancestral Domain","paragraphs":["The energy here was incredibly dense. It wasn’t just divine energy. It was older, heavier, more primal. Every breath carried a strange pressure, as if the air itself held fragments of a beginning from before most races had ever been born.","Far in the distance, Max saw a colossal palace big enough to hold a world inside it. Its pillars were carved with images of ancient beings standing above stars, suns, moons, dragons, phoenixes, titans, and countless other races. The palace didn’t give off any overbearing pressure, yet Max could feel it was watching everything.","Sarvion stopped beside him. \"Welcome to the Primordial Ancestral Domain.\"","Max looked out across the floating continents. \"So this is where the Primordial Race lives.\"","\"One of our ancestral domains,\" Sarvion corrected calmly. \"Not the only one.\"","Max’s eyes flickered slightly. One of them. That alone said something about how deep the Primordial Race’s foundation went.","Sarvion kept walking, and Max followed him across a bridge of violet-gold light. As they got closer to the central reception platform, Max sensed several powerful auras gathering ahead. They weren’t old experts. Their vitality was young, but each aura carried a familiarity Max recognized from the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","When he reached the reception platform, he saw them.","Nine young geniuses were already waiting there. Revona stood quietly near the edge of the platform, her pale eyes half-open and unreadable. Damian Voss stood with his sword at his waist, calm and refined as always.","Ervin leaned slightly on his restored black spear, his expression faintly amused when he saw Max arrive. Orion Starfall crossed his arms with a bright smile, while Rakan Thorne grinned like he was already hoping something exciting would happen. Kaiden Voidmere stood silently, his silver-gray gaze fixed on the space around him.","Aurelian Lareth stood farther off, his expression controlled but stiff the moment Max showed up. Rosaline Lunara and Morgana Starveil were there too, rounding out the top ten geniuses the Primordials had chosen.","The moment Max stepped onto the platform, all nine of them turned toward him. For a brief moment, the air went still.","These were the top ten geniuses of the Cosmic Ascension Conference. Each of them had fought through countless battles.","Each had revealed a Pseudo Cosmic Path or a terrifying foundation. Each was strong enough to represent the very top of the younger generation in the Divine Realm. And now, all of them had been gathered by the Primordial Race.","Orion spoke first. \"Champion, you finally arrived.\"","Rakan laughed loudly. \"He had to arrive last. Otherwise how would everyone remember he’s the champion?\"","Morgana smiled faintly. \"That does sound like something fate would arrange.\"","Damian gave Max a slight nod. \"Max.\"","Ervin smiled lightly. \"You look stronger than before.\"","Revona’s eyes moved across Max once, and for a brief instant her gaze sharpened. She didn’t say anything, but Max could tell she’d sensed something different.","His breakthrough into the Law Refinement Realm wasn’t easy to hide from someone with the Void Origin Eyes, even if she couldn’t see everything clearly.","Aurelian said nothing. His eyes stayed on Max one breath too long before he looked away.","Max noticed but didn’t bother responding.","’All of them are at the very peak of the Law Manifestation Realm. Just one step from the Divine Lord Realm.’","He thought quietly to himself. He’d beaten every one of them, sure, but that had happened inside the Eternal Hourglass, where all their cultivation had been suppressed down to the peak of the Law Refinement Realm.","Now that their cultivation wasn’t held back, Max knew he’d stand no chance against any single one of them.","Sarvion stepped forward and addressed all ten of them.","\"The top ten of the Cosmic Ascension Conference have now gathered.\"","The platform fell silent. Sarvion’s voice carried across the ancient reception ground.","\"You’ve all been chosen by the Primordial Race. Each of you will get a chance to receive the Primordial bloodline and step onto the path of becoming a Primordial. Your ranking in the conference will decide the level of opportunity, the depth of ceremony access, and how much reward you’re permitted to attempt.\"","His gaze moved to Max.","\"As the champion, Max Morgan will receive the highest opportunity.\"","The other nine stayed quiet, though their expressions shifted in different ways. Some looked calm. Some looked curious. Some looked competitive. Aurelian’s eyes darkened faintly.","Max only looked toward the colossal palace in the distance. The Primordial Ancestral Domain stretched out before him, ancient and unfathomable.","The reception platform stayed silent after Sarvion finished speaking.","The ten geniuses stood under the sky of the Primordial Ancestral Domain, surrounded by floating continents, ancient rune rings, rivers of starlight, and a pressure so old that even their powerful foundations felt smaller than usual here. None of them were ordinary.","Everyone standing on this platform had made the top ten of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, and each had fought through countless battles to reach this place. Yet inside the Primordial Race’s territory, even their pride instinctively quieted down.","Max looked toward the colossal palace in the distance. It seemed to exist beyond its own size. From one angle it looked like a divine structure spread across a continent. From another, it looked like a throne hall standing above the beginning of time.","The pillars were carved with images of ancient races bowing, stars collapsing, worlds being born, and four towering figures standing at the center of it all, like rulers of an age no one else had witnessed.","Before Max could study it any further, the air above the reception platform changed. It didn’t tear. It didn’t distort. It simply went still. The rivers of starlight stopped flowing for a breath. The rotating rune rings above slowed down.","Even the ancient pressure of the domain seemed to lower itself, as if welcoming someone who stood above ordinary authority.","Sarvion bowed immediately. \"Primarch.\"","The moment that word left his mouth, the expressions of all ten young geniuses changed.","Primarch. The leaders of the Primordial Race. There were only four of them."]},{"number":1937,"title":"Chapter 1937: Secrets of Void Origin Eyes!","paragraphs":["Before Sarvion could say anything else, a figure appeared before the platform. He didn’t arrive through a gate. He didn’t descend from the sky. He was like he was already standing there for a long time.","The man wore a long robe woven from pale gold and deep violet light, and each thread of that robe seemed to hold an ancient rune moving on its own.","His hair was long and white-gold, falling behind him like a river of dawn, while his eyes carried four rotating rings of different colors, each one giving off the feeling of an ancient law refined down to its absolute limit. His face looked young, but the depth in his gaze made him seem older than the Divine Realm itself.","The moment Max saw him, his eyes narrowed slightly. He recognized this person. Not from the Cosmic Ascension Conference. Not from the Black Dragon Clan. But from the temporal domain on Orion’s planet.","Back then, through the strange temporal connection inside that domain, Max had seen the last user of the Dimensional Keeper legacy and had also caught the shadow of the Primordials.","Among them had been four terrifying figures standing above the Primordial Race like pillars holding up an ancient sky.","This man was one of them. One of the four Primarchs.","The Primarch’s gaze swept across the ten geniuses. No pressure came off him, but everyone on the platform felt seen clearly. Not judged. Not suppressed. Just seen.","Their cultivation, bloodline, soul, Pseudo Cosmic Paths, wounds, secrets, and hidden potential all seemed to pass under his gaze in a single instant.","Even Revona’s eyes widened slightly. Damian Voss lowered his gaze out of respect. Ervin’s relaxed expression disappeared.","Orion Starfall’s easy smile vanished.","Rakan Thorne went unusually quiet.","Kaiden Voidmere’s pupils contracted faintly.","Aurelian Lareth straightened at once, clearly aware that no amount of elven pride meant anything in front of a Primarch of the Primordial Race.","The Primarch finally spoke. \"I am Arvantos, one of the four Primarchs of the Primordial Race.\"","His voice wasn’t loud, but it carried across the whole reception platform and seemed to echo inside the ancient rune rings above them.","\"You’ve all fought well in the Cosmic Ascension Conference. Each of you has shown talent, foundation, will, and a path worth my race’s attention. Reaching the top ten wasn’t just about winning fights. It also proved that your power has already stepped beyond the ordinary limits of the younger generation.\"","His eyes moved across them one by one. Then Arvantos’s gaze landed on Revona.","\"And Revona.\"","The platform quieted further. Revona looked at him calmly.","Finally, the Primarch’s eyes shifted to Max.","\"And Max Morgan.\" A faint smile crossed Arvantos’s face. \"The champion.\"","That word tightened the atmosphere again. Max met his gaze without lowering his head.","Arvantos looked at him for several breaths, then said something that made every genius on the platform freeze.","\"I’ll be honest. Before the final stage ended, I believed this conference would be won by Revona.\"","Silence fell. Not ordinary silence. Complete silence. Even Sarvion stood motionless.","The Primarch continued calmly, as if he hadn’t just said something shocking. \"In fact, I didn’t just think she had a good chance of winning. I never seriously considered that anyone in this conference could beat her.\"","The nine other geniuses immediately turned toward Revona. Even Max looked at her with a flicker of interest.","Revona stayed calm. Her pale eyes didn’t ripple, and her expression didn’t change at all. She stood there as if Arvantos were talking about someone else entirely. It wasn’t arrogance. It wasn’t indifference either. It was the kind of calm that made her seem disconnected from ordinary surprise.","Orion Starfall frowned slightly. \"You never thought anyone could beat her?\"","Rakan Thorne couldn’t hold back. \"Even with Damian, Ervin, Max, Kaiden, and the rest of us there?\"","Arvantos looked at him calmly. \"Yes.\"","The blunt answer made Rakan’s expression stiffen.","Damian Voss’s eyes narrowed. \"Because of her Void Origin Eyes?\"","\"Because of the true secret of the Void Origin Eyes,\" Arvantos corrected.","The moment he said that, Revona’s gaze finally shifted slightly. Not in panic. Not in shock. Just acknowledgment.","Arvantos looked at the group and went on. \"The Void Origin Eyes aren’t just a powerful pair of eyes that can nullify, hollow, trace, and return power to nothing. Those are only the abilities you saw in battle. Their deeper mystery runs far more terrifying than that.\"","The ancient rune rings above the platform rotated slowly.","\"It’s said the holder of the Void Origin Eyes never truly dies.\"","The geniuses’ expressions changed again.","Arvantos continued. \"In old history, that saying was always treated as a half-myth. Some believed it meant the Void Origin Eyes could preserve the soul. Some believed the eye bloodline would just reappear in later generations. Some believed it was pure exaggeration born from fear. But Revona is a living example that it’s true.\"","He paused, then revealed the secret.","\"Revona is a reincarnated person.\"","The whole platform went heavy.","Aurelian’s expression changed drastically. \"Reincarnated?\"","Arvantos nodded. \"Not once. Not twice. Over and over. Generation after generation. Body after body. Era after era.\"","The shock spreading across the top ten was impossible to hide. Even those with the deepest composure felt their hearts skip. A person who reincarnated once was already shocking enough to most forces.","A person who reincarnated repeatedly, keeping memories and experience intact, was something far beyond ordinary understanding. That wasn’t just talent anymore. That was accumulation across generations.","Arvantos looked at Revona again. \"The Revona standing here isn’t just a young genius who awakened the Void Origin Eyes in this generation. She’s the same existence as the people who awakened those eyes before her. Different bodies. Different eras. Different identities. But the same person.\"","Every gaze turned back to Revona. She just stood there quietly, her expression as calm as ever, as if this revelation had nothing to do with her.","Arvantos went on. \"Nobody knows the full mystery behind this reincarnation. Not even the Primordial Race has fully uncovered its source. What we do know is that it’s tied to the Void Origin Eyes. Whenever the eyes awaken in a new body, memories of past lives start waking up too. At first they come back as fragments. Then as dreams. Then as instincts. Then as full experience.\"","He looked at Max. \"That’s why I believed she would win.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly."]},{"number":1938,"title":"Chapter 1938: Perfect Beings!","paragraphs":["Arvantos’s voice stayed steady. \"During the Cosmic Ascension Conference, most geniuses were drawing on the accumulation of a single life. Revona wasn’t. Her Void Origin Eyes kept awakening further with every battle, and with each awakening, more memories and experience from her past lives came back to her. Her battle instincts, her grasp of power, her sense of danger, her use of nullification, all of it was backed by far more than her current age.\"","The top ten fell into stunned silence.","Now Revona’s frightening calm made a lot more sense.","The way she’d adapted to Orion’s star power. The way she’d traced Kaiden’s Grand Void Labyrinth. The way she’d forced Max to reveal power after power. The way she’d beaten Ervin and Damian with Null Origin Tide after being pushed to the brink. All of it suddenly felt even more terrifying.","She hadn’t just been talented. She’d been remembering.","Morgana Starveil looked at Revona with deep curiosity. \"So the woman standing beside us is the same person who’s lived through countless past lives?\"","\"Yes,\" Arvantos answered.","Rakan Thorne stared at Revona, then scratched his head with a complicated look. \"That feels like cheating.\"","Orion Starfall let out a faint laugh, though his eyes stayed serious. \"If it’s cheating, it’s the most elegant kind I’ve ever seen.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked at Revona and asked, \"Do you remember everything?\"","Revona finally spoke. \"Not everything.\" Her voice was calm. \"But enough.\"","That single word made the platform even quieter.","Enough.","Enough to become the person the Primarch had expected to win the entire Cosmic Ascension Conference. Enough to make the Primordial Race believe no one should be able to beat her. Enough to make every genius present realize her loss to Max was even more shocking than they’d first thought.","Ervin slowly let out a breath. \"No wonder you defeated almost all of us.\"","Revona didn’t reply to him. She only looked at Max. Max looked back at her. Their gazes met quietly.","Arvantos smiled faintly when he saw that. \"That’s why Max Morgan surprised me.\"","His voice pulled everyone’s attention back to him.","\"Revona was the person I expected to become champion. Her Void Origin Eyes, combined with the awakening of her past-life memories, should have put her beyond anyone else in this conference. Yet Max beat her. Then he beat Damian. Then he beat Ervin. And he finished with a perfect record.\"","The Primarch’s eyes settled on Max.","\"So, Max Morgan, your win wasn’t impressive just because you became champion. It was impressive because you beat the one person even I believed shouldn’t lose.\"","The weight of those words was enormous. The other geniuses looked at Max differently now. They’d already known he was strong. They’d already accepted he was champion. But hearing one of the four Primarchs say he’d expected Revona to be unbeatable made Max’s win feel even more abnormal.","Max stayed calm. After a moment he smiled faintly. \"So she was even more trouble than I thought.\"","Revona looked at him quietly. \"You still won.\"","Max replied, \"Barely.\"","Revona didn’t respond, but for the first time, a faint trace of something almost like amusement crossed her pale eyes.","Arvantos watched the exchange, then turned back to the whole group.","\"You should all remember this. The Primordial Race didn’t gather you here just because you won battles. We gathered you because each of you carries something worth testing, refining, and possibly transforming. Some of you have ancient bloodlines. Some have rare Pseudo Cosmic Paths. Some have inheritances. Some have special bodies. Some have secrets even your own forces don’t fully understand.\"","His gaze swept over them again. \"And now, you’ll each be given a chance to step beyond what you were born as.\"","The mood on the platform turned solemn again. The secret of Revona’s reincarnation still hung in everyone’s mind, but the bigger reason they’d come here was pressing down on them once more.","The Primordial bloodline. The path to becoming a Primordial. The reward promised to the top ten.","Arvantos raised one hand, and the colossal palace in the distance began to shine.","\"Come,\" he said. \"The Primordial Selection Ceremony will begin soon.\"","Arvantos turned and walked toward the distant palace. The ten geniuses followed. Sarvion stayed behind them, silent and respectful, while the reception platform slowly moved forward on its own. It wasn’t flying in any normal sense.","The whole platform seemed to slide along a hidden law path, crossing bridges of violet-gold light, passing over rivers of liquid starlight, and pushing deeper into the Primordial Ancestral Domain with every breath.","As they traveled, the true scale of the Primordial Race’s territory unfolded before them. What they’d seen from the outer reception boundary had only been the surface. The deeper they went, the more impossible the domain became.","Some floating continents held ancient forests where every tree stood taller than mountains. Some held silent lakes that reflected not the sky above but scenes from different eras.","Some were covered in ruins large enough to make divine cities look like toys, and on the broken walls of those ruins were carvings of beings whose faces resembled humans, yet whose presence felt far more ancient and complete.","Max looked at those carvings quietly. The beings shown there were tall, flawless, and powerful. Their bodies were shaped like human bodies, but their eyes held strange rings, their bloodline marks ran far deeper, and their very posture carried a natural supremacy no ordinary divine race could imitate.","Arvantos noticed their stares and spoke without turning back. \"You’re looking at the earliest Primordials.\"","The ten geniuses immediately paid closer attention. Even Revona, who’d stayed calm through the reveal of her reincarnation, looked at the carvings with a flicker of interest.","Arvantos went on. \"Before humans existed, before most races of the current universe had built stable civilizations, the Primordial Race already existed.\"","His voice was calm, but the words carried enough weight to quiet the whole platform. \"Back then, we were the first complete race born from the ancient source of existence. Our bodies were powerful. Our souls were stable. Our grasp of law came naturally from birth. Compared to many races that came later, the Primordials could be called perfect beings, in a certain sense.\"","Rakan Thorne frowned slightly. \"Perfect beings?\"","Arvantos smiled faintly. \"In strength, foundation, and closeness to the laws of existence, yes. But perfection in one direction often creates a flaw in another.\""]},{"number":1939,"title":"Chapter 1939: Origin of Human Race!","paragraphs":["The platform passed through a great ring of ancient runes. Beyond it, the landscape changed again. They saw a vast mural stretched across the side of a floating mountain, showing countless Primordials standing together beneath a sky full of stars.","They looked magnificent, but there were no children among them. No families. No lines of descent. Just adults standing under the ancient heavens with solemn expressions.","Arvantos stopped before that mural. \"This was the flaw of the Primordial Race.\"","The ten geniuses waited. Then Arvantos said it plainly.","\"We could not reproduce.\"","The words changed almost everyone’s expression.","Orion Starfall blinked. \"The Primordial Race couldn’t reproduce?\"","Damian Voss’s gaze sharpened slightly.","Kaiden Voidmere looked at the mural again, as if trying to figure out whether the missing children had been intentional.","Morgana Starveil’s purple eyes glimmered with curiosity. \"A race that can’t reproduce shouldn’t have survived through the ages.\"","Arvantos nodded. \"That’s correct.\"","He turned toward them slightly, and for the first time a wry smile crossed his face.","\"We had long lives, supreme strength, and bodies that naturally held laws other races had to spend countless years learning. Yet we couldn’t create descendants. It was as if some limit had been placed on us the moment we were born.\"","Rosaline Lunara frowned. \"A natural law limitation?\"","\"Maybe,\" Arvantos said. \"Or maybe something imposed by entities beyond the understanding of even the earliest Primordials. Some of our oldest records call it a restriction. Some call it a punishment. Some call it the decision of gods. The truth’s never been fully confirmed.\"","Aurelian Lareth couldn’t help but ask, \"Did the Primordials try to reproduce with other races?\"","Arvantos looked at him calmly. \"Of course.\"","The blunt answer quieted the platform again.","\"The Primordials tried everything. We tried with our own race first. Nothing came of it. Later, when other races started appearing, we tried with them too. Humans didn’t exist yet in that era, but there were plenty of early races born from worlds, stars, beasts, spirits, laws, and other sources. The result was always the same.\" He paused. \"No child was born.\"","The shock in the ten geniuses’ eyes deepened. To them, the Primordial Race had always stood as a supreme race above nearly everything.","They’d assumed the Primordials were ancient simply because they’d existed a long time, not because the race itself had once been trapped in a fatal inability to continue.","Arvantos turned back to the mural. \"At first, we thought time would solve it. Then we thought power would. Then law. After that, we tried secret arts, soul division, bloodline imitation, body creation, artificial wombs, divine law fusion, reincarnation attempts, and countless other methods that later races couldn’t even imagine.\"","His wry smile faded. \"All of it failed.\"","The silence grew heavier. Even Rakan, who usually reacted loudly to everything, said nothing.","Arvantos continued. \"A race that can’t reproduce might look invincible for a while, especially if its members are strong enough. But even immortality isn’t absolute. Primordials could die in battle. Primordials could fall to disasters. Primordials could vanish inside forbidden zones. Primordials could be sealed, corrupted, or lost in ancient wars. We were powerful, but our numbers only shrank.\"","The platform started moving again, this time toward another region where a different set of murals appeared. These carvings showed Primordials seated in a great circle, their bodies glowing with bloodline light.","At the center of the circle stood a vast basin filled with golden-red liquid, and from that basin, countless streams flowed out toward smaller figures. The smaller figures looked human.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Arvantos stopped before the second mural. \"Eventually, the Primordials chose the most extreme method.\" His voice dropped slightly. \"We gave up our bloodline.\"","The ten geniuses froze. Even Max’s expression shifted a little.","Arvantos looked at the human-like figures carved beneath the Primordials. \"The first humans were born when some Primordials gave up their complete bloodline, sealed away their Primordial foundation, and let themselves fall into mortality. They lost the natural supremacy of the Primordial Race. Their bodies grew weaker. Their lifespans shortened. Their connection to the ancient source faded. Their law affinity declined. In exchange, they gained something the Primordials had never had.\"","He paused. \"The ability to reproduce.\"","A heavy silence settled over the platform. The ten geniuses stared at the mural.","The birth of the human race had plenty of legends across the Divine Realm. Some believed humans were created by ancient gods. Some believed they evolved from mortal life forms. Some believed they were fragments of a fallen supreme race. Some believed they were just one of countless ordinary races that rose through struggle. But none of them had expected this.","Humans had come from Primordials. Not as descendants in the ordinary sense. Not as a branch race born naturally. But as Primordials who had abandoned their bloodline entirely and turned themselves into mortals.","Rosaline covered her mouth slightly, unable to hide her shock. \"Humans were once Primordials?\"","\"The earliest humans were,\" Arvantos answered.","Kaiden Voidmere stared at the mural with a deep gaze. \"That explains the resemblance.\"","\"Yes,\" Arvantos said. \"Humans resemble Primordials because humans were shaped from Primordials. The outer form didn’t change much, but the foundation did.\"","Damian Voss said quietly, \"So humanity isn’t a lesser copy of the Primordial Race. It’s a fallen branch.\"","\"A transformed branch,\" Arvantos corrected. \"Fallen is a harsh word, though some ancient Primordials used it at the time.\"","Morgana Starveil smiled faintly, though her eyes stayed serious. \"And humans became capable of having children.\"","\"Yes.\" Arvantos looked back at the mural. \"Once the Primordials who’d given up their bloodline became human, they found out they could bear children. Those children didn’t carry the true Primordial bloodline. They were human. Mortal. Weaker than their origin. But they could grow, multiply, spread, adapt, and survive in ways the Primordial Race never could.\"","Orion Starfall let out a slow breath. \"So that was the start of the human race.\"","\"The start of the true human race,\" Arvantos replied. \"From those first mortals, humanity spread across worlds, star regions, and later the Divine Realm. They were weaker than a lot of ancient races at birth, but they had terrifying adaptability. They could cultivate many paths. They could awaken many bloodlines. They could intermarry with other races. They could rise from nothing again and again.\"","Rakan Thorne scratched his head, genuinely shaken. \"So humans exist because the strongest race in existence couldn’t have kids?\""]},{"number":1940,"title":"Chapter 1940: Compatability Test!","paragraphs":["Arvantos smiled wryly again. \"That’s one simple way to put it.\"","The words came out almost casual, but the meaning behind them shook the top ten deeply. Aurelian Lareth’s expression turned complicated.","The elven races had always taken pride in their bloodline purity, but standing in the Primordial Ancestral Domain and hearing that humans came from Primordials themselves, even he couldn’t hold onto the same sense of superiority.","Revona stayed calm, but her gaze lingered on the mural longer than before.","Ervin looked thoughtful. \"Then the current Primordial Race should have kept declining. If the original Primordials couldn’t reproduce, and a lot of them turned into humans, how did your race survive until now?\"","Arvantos’s smile faded into something deeper. \"That’s where the second half of our history begins.\"","The platform moved again. This time they approached a vast ceremonial ground surrounded by thirteen ancient pillars. Each pillar showed a carving of a human standing beneath a Primordial, with streams of bloodline light pouring into their body.","Some of those humans transformed partially. Some fully. Some broke apart. Some stood tall with new Primordial marks carved into their skin.","Arvantos pointed at the pillars. \"After humanity began, the Primordials found another path.\"","The ten geniuses looked at the carvings in silence.","Arvantos continued. \"If Primordials couldn’t reproduce naturally, then we’d create Primordials through transformation instead. Rather than birthing descendants, we’d choose humans with supreme potential, awaken the hidden compatibility left over from the origin of humanity, and give them a chance to receive the Primordial bloodline.\"","His gaze moved across all ten of them. \"That’s the reason you’re here.\"","The mood shifted immediately.","\"Since this system began, the Primordial Race has picked the most outstanding human geniuses from different eras, different worlds, and different forces. Some were chosen through wars. Some through trials. Some through bloodline resonance. In the current era, the Cosmic Ascension Conference is one of the most important ways we select candidates.\"","Max looked at the pillars. \"So the top ten get this opportunity because you’re looking for humans who can carry the Primordial bloodline.\"","\"Correct,\" Arvantos said. \"Not every human can carry it. Honestly, almost none can. The Primordial bloodline is too heavy for ordinary bodies and too ancient for ordinary souls. Even supreme geniuses can fail. Some get only a trace. Some get a partial bloodline. Some become candidates. A few, after many more trials, truly step into the ranks of the Primordials.\"","Alice and Lenavira weren’t here, but Max could almost guess what Lily would say if she heard all this. She’d probably say the Primordials were taking a ridiculously roundabout path just because they couldn’t have kids the normal way.","Orion Starfall looked at Arvantos. \"So the Primordial Race has survived by turning humans back into Primordials.\"","\"Yes,\" Arvantos said. \"Humanity came from Primordials who gave up their bloodline, and the Primordial Race keeps going by choosing extraordinary humans capable of receiving that bloodline again. It’s a cycle, though not a perfect one.\"","Damian Voss’s gaze sharpened. \"So humans are both the descendants of the Primordials and the source new Primordials get chosen from.\"","\"Exactly.\"","The shock on the platform deepened. The history was too big, too strange, too heavy. For countless years, humans had struggled, cultivated, fought, risen, fallen, founded clans, built forces, and established kingdoms, empires, dynasties, and divine powers.","Plenty of human forces believed their origins were ordinary compared to the ancient divine races. Now Arvantos had just told them the truth was far more astonishing.","Humans were born from Primordials. And Primordials kept existing through humans.","Max stayed quiet for a while. This secret changed a lot of things. It explained why the Primordial Race cared so much about the Cosmic Ascension Conference. It explained why the top ten got chosen.","It explained why becoming a Primordial wasn’t just receiving an outside reward, but returning to a source humans had once lost.","Arvantos looked at the ten geniuses and spoke slowly. \"Now you understand why the Primordial Race values potential over background. A divine clan bloodline might help you. A supreme inheritance might strengthen you. A rare Pseudo Cosmic Path might set you above others in battle. But none of that alone decides whether you can become a Primordial.\"","His gaze moved to Max. \"What matters most is whether your foundation can bear the return.\"","The word \"return\" quieted the platform again.","Arvantos raised his hand, and the thirteen pillars around the ceremonial ground began to glow.","\"This is where your first compatibility trial begins. Before any bloodline is granted, before any ceremony is performed, before any of you can be called Primordial candidates, we need to see how much of the ancient source your bodies and souls can handle.\"","The ten geniuses stood beneath the glowing pillars. The shock from the secret still hadn’t faded, but their eyes had already started to sharpen. Whatever their surprise, whatever they now thought about the origin of humanity, they hadn’t come here just to listen to history.","They’d come to seize an opportunity. They’d come to climb higher. And now the path back to the Primordial source was opening in front of them.","The thirteen ancient pillars around the ceremonial ground shone brighter and brighter until the whole area was drowned in pale gold light.","The moment the light hit its peak, the ground beneath the ten geniuses began to hum softly. Countless ancient runes rose up from the floor one after another, forming circles within circles beneath each of them. The air grew heavy, not with hostility, but with a deep, ancient pressure that seemed to come from the very origin of life itself.","Arvantos stood at the center of the group with his hands behind his back.","\"This is the Primordial Compatibility Test,\" he said calmly. \"It doesn’t just test combat strength, and it doesn’t care about fame, background, or a single victory. It measures your body, your soul, your bloodline adaptability, your law foundation, your life force, your capacity to withstand ancient pressure, and the depth of your future potential.\"","His gaze moved across all ten of them.","\"The stronger your compatibility, the higher the bloodline you may be able to receive. If your compatibility is too low, even if I personally wanted to give you a higher Primordial bloodline, your body would explode, your soul would collapse, or your foundation would shatter.\"","The geniuses’ expressions turned solemn."]},{"number":1941,"title":"Chapter 1941: Four Tiers of Primordial Bloodline!","paragraphs":["Arvantos raised one hand. \"Stand still. Don’t resist.\"","The next instant, beams of ancient light dropped from each of the thirteen pillars and connected with the central formation. The ceremonial ground came alive immediately.","Streams of golden liquid light started moving beneath the transparent floor like rivers flowing toward each of the ten participants.","At the same time, a huge illusory Primordial symbol appeared high above them, rotating slowly and sending out wave after wave of ancient aura.","The first thing Max felt was pressure. Not ordinary pressure. It felt like the entire history of an ancient race had come down onto his body and was trying to read every part of him.","The pressure didn’t attack him, but it pushed into him with unstoppable force, moving through his meridians, bones, flesh, bloodline, soul sea, and even the hidden corners of his foundation that ordinary people could never sense.","Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body reacted first. The space around his body twisted faintly, as if it were instinctively analyzing the invading ancient force.","Then his Seven Divine Veins gave off a low resonance, followed by the sleeping power of his draconic essences, his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, his multiple refined Pseudo Cosmic Paths, and the countless hidden inheritances resting inside him.","For a moment, Max felt like his whole existence had turned transparent under the ancient light.","Around him, the others went through their own tests.","Revona stood with her eyes half-open, and the moment the ancient force touched her, the Void Origin Eyes in her pupils spun faintly.","The air around her body turned hollow and deep, and for a short moment, faint shadows of other selves seemed to flicker behind her like reflections from countless past eras. It was as if the compatibility test wasn’t just measuring one life, but many.","Ervin’s body gave off a dark abyssal pressure. A black sea seemed to rise invisibly behind him, while the aura of the broken gate inside him showed itself faintly under the ancient light. His body, soul, and abyssal path all looked extremely stable.","Damian Voss’s sword intent rose on its own. He stayed motionless, yet his whole body felt like a perfectly forged divine sword. The test light passed through him, and every part of his foundation answered with a sharp, disciplined hum.","Orion Starfall was wrapped in starlight. It looked like an entire field of stars had woken up inside him, each one supporting his body and making his compatibility grow stronger with every passing breath.","Kaiden Voidmere seemed to merge with a faint void distortion. His space affinity was so high that even the Primordial light around him bent slightly as it passed through him.","Rosaline, Morgana, Rakan, Aurelian, and the rest also showed striking responses, each one different, each one showing exactly why they’d made the top ten.","The compatibility test dragged on for a long time. The thirteen pillars shifted color several times. First pale gold, then deeper gold, then white, then a rich ancient crimson. Each shift meant a deeper layer of examination.","By the time it hit the crimson stage, even the strongest among them wore serious expressions.","Rakan’s muscles were trembling. Orion’s smile was gone. Damian’s sword aura had turned much sharper. Rosaline’s brows had started to knit. Even Revona had fully opened her eyes by now.","Only Max still stood with a relatively steady look, though inside him the pressure had also climbed to an astonishing level. His foundation was simply too vast.","His body alone was already monstrous enough to suppress most geniuses, and then there was his Dimensional Sovereign Body, his Seven Divine Veins, his draconic essences, his Dragon Scales Transformation, his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, multiple strong inheritances, and his Pseudo Cosmic Paths.","All of it combined into a foundation so abnormal that even the Primordial Compatibility Test seemed to grow more active around him.","At last, the light slowly pulled back. The thirteen pillars dimmed one after another, and the huge Primordial symbol above the sky faded into countless streams of ancient runes.","The ceremony ground fell silent. Then, in front of all of them, a compatibility ranking appeared in the air.","Every genius looked up at once. At the very top sat one name.","[1. Max Morgan]","Below him came the rest.","[2. Revona]","[3. Ervin]","[4. Damian Voss]","[5. Orion Starfall]","[6. Kaiden Voidmere]","[7. Rosaline Lunara]","[8. Morgana Starveil]","[9. Rakan Thorne]","[10. Aurelian Lareth]","The moment the ranking appeared, several of the geniuses went quiet. Most weren’t shocked that Max ranked near the top. They were shocked he ranked first so clearly.","Even Arvantos had expected a lot from Max, but seeing the result laid out so plainly still put a faint smile on his face.","\"As expected,\" he said.","Orion let out a breath and laughed helplessly. \"So even here, he’s first.\"","Rakan crossed his arms and grinned. \"I knew his body was monstrous, but this is still annoying to look at.\"","Damian’s expression stayed calm, though his eyes sharpened slightly as he looked at Max. \"Your foundation really is absurd.\"","Ervin smiled faintly. \"After fighting him, I can’t say I’m surprised.\"","Rosaline looked at the ranking, then at Max, with a complicated smile. \"You really don’t leave any room for the rest of us.\"","Morgana’s purple eyes glimmered with interest. \"First in the conference and first in compatibility. How greedy.\"","Aurelian’s face had already gone cold. Landing last among the top ten wasn’t a light hit to his pride, especially given how highly he thought of himself as a chosen genius of the second elven faction.","Revona looked at the ranking calmly, then at Max. \"You really were the right person to beat me.\"","Max only smiled faintly. \"I’ll take that as a compliment.\"","Arvantos stepped forward again, drawing everyone’s attention back to him.","\"The compatibility ranking is done,\" he said. \"Next, I’ll explain the four tiers of Primordial Bloodline.\"","The mood turned solemn again. Arvantos raised one hand, and four streams of ancient bloodline light appeared before them, each one different in color and pressure.","\"The first tier is the General Primordial Bloodline. This is the bloodline most Primordials carry. It brings a major transformation to your body, soul, vitality, and law affinity. Even receiving this bloodline alone is enough to lift an ordinary genius far above his original race.\"","The first stream glowed steadily.","\"The second tier is the Special Primordial Bloodline. Only some Primordials have this one. Besides the natural boost the General Bloodline gives, this tier also produces one or more unique bloodline abilities. Those abilities depend on the source bloodline and the inheritor’s compatibility.\"","The second stream pulsed with a deeper aura.","\"The third tier is the Leader Primordial Bloodline. This belongs to the upper rulers and high authorities of the Primordial Race. It doesn’t just strengthen you. It transforms your fundamental level far more deeply and carries stronger source abilities, greater control over ancient laws, and a much higher ceiling for future growth.\"","The pressure from the third stream made even the top ten narrow their eyes.","Then Arvantos looked at the final stream. It was only a small amount of bloodline light, but its aura was enough to make the previous three streams look dim by comparison.","\"And the fourth tier,\" Arvantos said slowly, \"is the Primarch Bloodline.\"","The whole ceremonial ground went quiet.","\"This bloodline is extremely rare. Only the four Primarchs, myself included, carry it.\"","Even Max’s eyes sharpened at that."]},{"number":1942,"title":"Chapter 1942: A Painful Process!","paragraphs":["Arvantos continued. \"Don’t think this bloodline gets handed out just because someone plays favorites. It doesn’t. Even if I wanted to give it, the receiver would first have to survive it. This bloodline has the deepest connection to the origin of the Primordial Race, and the conditions needed to carry it are terrifyingly high.\"","His gaze moved over all ten of them. \"As for who gets which bloodline, the answer is simple. It comes down entirely to your body, your foundation, your compatibility, your soul, your potential, and a lot of other hidden factors.\"","He turned around. \"Come. The next stage is waiting.\"","With that, Arvantos led the ten geniuses away from the ceremonial ground and deeper into the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","Before long, they arrived at a huge structure hidden behind seven layers of ancient formations. It was a circular hall built from pale gold stone, yet the stone itself seemed alive, almost like condensed bloodline essence.","Ancient Primordial runes covered every wall, and at the center of the hall sat a vast circular chamber split into ten positions. Above each position floated a bloodline crystal the size of a human body, and inside each crystal swirled an ancient liquid light that looked like primordial blood.","The moment they walked in, everyone felt their own blood react.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly. This was no ordinary place. This was the Bloodline Chamber.","Arvantos turned to them. \"This chamber’s been prepared specifically for the ten of you. Sit cross-legged in your assigned positions. The formations will measure your compatibility again in finer detail and guide the bloodline transfer according to your limits.\"","No one hesitated. One by one, the top ten geniuses walked forward and sat cross-legged beneath their crystals.","Max sat in the foremost position. Revona sat not far from him. Damian, Ervin, Orion, Kaiden, Rosaline, Morgana, Rakan, and Aurelian all settled into their own spots.","Once all ten had sat down, the circular hall began to hum. Ancient runes across the walls lit up. Rings of golden light spread across the floor beneath each genius. The bloodline crystals above them brightened one after another, and the liquid primordial essence inside started spinning faster and faster.","Arvantos stood at the center of the chamber and raised both hands.","\"The process of transferring Primordial Bloodlines,\" he said solemnly, \"begins now.\"","The instant Arvantos’s words fell, the Bloodline Chamber changed completely.","The ten bloodline crystals hanging above the seated geniuses erupted with light at the same time. Ancient runes lit up across the walls, then spread toward the floor like living veins of gold, and in just a few breaths the whole circular chamber turned into a massive bloodline formation.","The rings beneath each genius started spinning in opposite directions, one inward and one outward, creating layered pressure that sank into their bodies from below while the ancient bloodline essence above pressed down from above.","Then the transfer began.","A stream of Primordial bloodline essence came down from each crystal. It didn’t flow gently. It fell like molten light.","The moment the first strand of that essence touched Max’s forehead, his whole body shook violently. Not from weakness. From overwhelming resonance. Everything inside him reacted at once.","His Dimensional Sovereign Body stirred like it had woken up from a deep sleep.","The Seven Divine Veins in his body pulsed rapidly one after another, each one responding to the invading authority. His draconic essence roared like a volcano cracking open after being held down too long.","The Dragon Scales Transformation source ignited on instinct. His Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline trembled as if it recognized something above it.","Even deeper, his other inheritances, refined foundations, Pseudo Cosmic Paths, and the faint trace of the Dimensional Keeper legacy all surged together.","For a brief moment, Max’s body became the meeting point of countless powers. And the Primordial Bloodline crashed straight into all of them.","The pain hit like a collapsing world.","Max’s fingers dug into his knees hard enough to make his joints creak. His back stiffened, and a low sound he couldn’t hold back escaped his throat as the bloodline essence forced its way into his flesh, bones, meridians, and blood. It wasn’t just entering him. It was rewriting him.","It felt like his marrow was being burned and reforged at the same time. It felt like every bone in his body was being crushed to dust and then rebuilt from an ancient blueprint.","It felt like his blood had turned to molten metal running through channels being forced wider by the second. It felt like his soul had been dragged into a primordial furnace, where existence itself was being carved into him.","His breathing turned heavy, each breath sharp and forced through clenched teeth. Even his heartbeat changed. Every beat echoed like a hammer striking ancient steel, deep, heavy, and almost unbearable.","The Primordial Bloodline didn’t ask permission. It simply imposed itself. And Max understood right away that this wasn’t an upgrade. It was transformation at the level of origin.","The pressure went deeper. The bloodline essence didn’t stop at his physical body. It pushed further, sinking into his soul sea. The moment it touched that layer, his whole consciousness trembled.","But instead of falling apart, something inside him steadied. His Dimensional Sovereign Body adjusted first, instinctively spreading the pressure across his whole existence. The Seven Divine Veins fell into a controlled rhythm instead of fighting back chaotically.","His draconic essence, instead of exploding outward, compressed and held on. Even the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline quieted down a little, as if it understood that resisting would only end in destruction.","Max’s face stayed tense, but his body was starting to adapt.","Still, the pain didn’t ease up. If anything, it went deeper. It wasn’t just physical anymore. It was existential. The Primordial Bloodline was reaching into the very idea of what he was.","His vision blurred for a second as waves of burning pain rolled through him. His body shook once, then steadied again through pure will. Sweat gathered at his temples, but he didn’t move.","He could feel it clearly now. If his foundation had been even a little weaker, he would have shattered instantly.","The transfer kept going without mercy. The bloodline essence thickened, pushing deeper into his origin. It felt like countless ancient hands were tearing open the structure of his existence and rebuilding it from a forgotten blueprint."]},{"number":1943,"title":"Chapter 1943: A Slow Process!","paragraphs":["Max lowered his head slightly, his white hair falling over his eyes, but his grip on himself never slipped.","He endured. Because there was no other choice.","The chamber around him hummed louder as the formation moved into its next stage. The pressure multiplied, and the Primordial Bloodline stopped flowing in strands. It started coming down in solid pillars of light.","The impact hit Max instantly. His body jolted again, and for a moment his aura flared out of control, bright enough to outshine everything else in the chamber. Then it got forced back down as the bloodline essence pressed even deeper into him.","The pain surged again, sharper, heavier, more absolute. Max’s teeth clenched so hard a faint crack echoed out.","But he didn’t lose consciousness. He couldn’t. Because the moment he did, the transformation wouldn’t stop. It would just break him.","So he held on. Inside him, every power he had was being forced into alignment. Not destroyed. Not erased. Just reshaped to fit the Primordial standard.","Slowly, against all that pain, his body started to adapt. Not comfortably. Not safely. But it happened anyway.","The runes in the chamber glowed brighter, as if acknowledging his resistance and his acceptance at the same time. The formation responded, sharpening the precision of the transfer instead of ramping up the brutality.","Max let out a slow breath through clenched teeth. The pain was still unbearable. But now, underneath it, he could feel something else.","Change. Deep, irreversible change.","The bloodline transfer didn’t end quickly. One hour passed. Then two. Then three. Inside the Bloodline Chamber, time seemed to stop meaning much. The ten geniuses stayed seated beneath their crystals, each one caught in a storm of ancient pain and transformation.","The formation beneath them kept rotating without pause, and the liquid primordial essence above them kept pouring down in controlled streams, sinking into their bodies, merging with their blood, and forcing their old foundations to either adapt or break.","No one spoke. No one had the energy to waste on words.","Even the weakest of these ten was a supreme genius who’d reached the top of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, but right now, every one of them looked like they were being crushed under an invisible mountain.","Their bodies shook from time to time. Their auras flared and dimmed. Their bloodlines resisted, gave in, pushed back, and adapted again. This wasn’t a simple transfer of power. It was a remaking of their existence into something closer to the ancient Primordial source.","Rakan Thorne’s huge body shook violently as golden bloodline light hammered into his bones and muscles again and again. The War God Body he was so proud of held up with terrifying toughness, but even that wasn’t enough to stop blood from leaking out of the corner of his mouth.","Orion Starfall’s star marks lit up one after another, each one going deeper under the pressure of the bloodline, while Kaiden Voidmere’s surrounding space warped so badly that the formation beneath him had to release extra stabilizing runes.","Damian Voss sat straight like a sword planted in the earth, but his face had gone pale, and the sharp aura around him had pulled in tight as he forced every scrap of his will into enduring the change.","Revona’s case was even stranger. Faint shadows of past lives kept appearing and disappearing behind her. Sometimes she looked like a pale young woman with quiet eyes. Sometimes, for the briefest instant, she looked like an ancient cultivator sitting under a ruined sky.","Other times she looked like a cold monarch, a wandering scholar, a battlefield survivor, or a faceless figure standing alone in an empty world. The Void Origin Eyes spun slowly, but they didn’t try to nullify the Primordial Bloodline. Instead, they watched it, endured it, and let it carve itself into her current body.","Ervin’s abyssal aura sank deeper and deeper. Every time the Primordial Bloodline entered him, it seemed to fall into an endless sea before rising back up, more ancient and more condensed than before.","Morgana’s curse aura wrapped around her body like black-violet threads, but the Primordial essence refined those threads without mercy.","Rosaline’s dawn light turned softer but purer, while Aurelian’s Heavenly Luminance aura flickered with unstable pride as the Primordial Bloodline forced itself into a foundation already carrying too many complications.","And at the center of it all, Max’s transformation kept going at the highest intensity.","The bloodline crystal above him had become almost blinding. The primordial essence pouring into his body was thicker than anyone else’s. It fell like a pillar of molten starlight, hitting his forehead, chest, and bloodline source all at once. His body had already adapted past the first stage, but the deeper stage was far worse.","Every time he thought the pain had hit its limit, the formation opened another layer, and the Primordial Bloodline sank even deeper, into places even his own senses rarely reached.","His bones weren’t just being strengthened anymore. They were being rewritten. His blood wasn’t just being refined anymore. It was starting to carry an ancient rhythm that had never existed in him before. His soul wasn’t just enduring pressure anymore. It was being forced to accept a new origin mark.","The Dimensional Sovereign Body, the Seven Divine Veins, the draconic essences, the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline the Dimensional Keeper legacy, and his refined Pseudo Cosmic Paths all kept resonating under the pressure. None of them got erased.","None of them got replaced. Instead, the Primordial Bloodline seemed to be finding a way to settle above all of them, not as an outside force, but as a higher foundation that could hold everything together.","Max’s head stayed lowered. His breathing stayed slow and heavy. Sweat slid down his face, but his body never bent.","The hours kept passing. At some point, the chamber entered its final stage.","The ten bloodline crystals above the geniuses cracked at the same time. The sound was clear. Not broken from failure. Broken because the essence inside them had been fully released.","Ancient runes surged out of the cracks and turned into ten separate beams of light, each one descending into the body of its chosen recipient."]},{"number":1944,"title":"Chapter 1944: Success!","paragraphs":["The pressure inside the chamber climbed to its highest point, and even Arvantos, who’d been calmly watching from the center, finally looked more serious.","\"This is the final imprint,\" he said.","The ten geniuses heard him, but none of them could answer.","The final imprint came down.","Boom!","Every genius trembled. Their bloodlines surged violently. Their souls shook. Their bodies gave off different colors of light as the Primordial essence finally stopped acting like a foreign force and started settling in as part of who they were.","The pain hit its peak, so intense that even Max’s consciousness blurred for a fraction of a breath.","Then something inside him opened.","Not a vein. Not a meridian. Not an ordinary bloodline source. It was like an ancient seal, hidden in the deepest part of his new Primordial foundation, had finally acknowledged him.","The system flashed before his vision.","[Primordial Bloodline Transfer Completed.]","[Bloodline Tier Acquired: Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline.]","[Primarch-Level Bloodline Detected.]","[Bloodline Integration Status: Stable.]","Max’s eyes opened slightly.","Tier 4. The highest tier Arvantos had mentioned. The same tier only the Four Primarchs carried.","Even Max, who’d stayed calm through most of the process, felt something shift in his chest at that moment. He’d expected a strong result given his foundation, but seeing the system confirm it still hit different. This wasn’t just a powerful bloodline.","This was a Primarch-level bloodline, rare enough that only four known beings in the whole Primordial Race carried it.","Before he could think it through, the final imprint finished settling into his body. The pain didn’t vanish right away. It slowly pulled back, leaving behind a deep, ancient heat in his blood.","The Bloodline Chamber went quiet. One by one, the beams of light faded. The ten geniuses stayed seated, their bodies still trembling faintly from the aftermath. The bloodline crystals above them had lost their glow and now hung empty, like shells after all their essence had drained out. The runes beneath them kept glowing faintly for a few more breaths before slowly dimming.","Arvantos raised one hand. A wave of gentle Primordial energy passed through the chamber, steadying all ten of them.","\"Open your eyes,\" he said.","They slowly did.","Some looked exhausted. Some looked pale. Some breathed like they’d just survived a disaster. But every single one of them had changed.","Rakan’s body now carried a faint ancient pressure under his War God aura. Orion’s star marks looked deeper and more refined. Damian’s sword presence felt heavier, like his body itself had picked up a more ancient sharpness.","Ervin’s abyssal aura had turned darker and more stable. Kaiden’s space fluctuations felt smoother and more natural. Morgana’s curse aura had picked up a strange golden-violet undertone. Rosaline’s dawn light had turned purer.","Aurelian’s Heavenly Luminance had grown brighter, though his face stayed tense. Revona’s Void Origin Eyes were quieter than before, but the emptiness inside them now carried a faint ancient ring of Primordial light.","Arvantos looked at them all in silence. Then his eyes shone. The four-colored rings in his pupils rotated once, and an invisible pressure swept through the chamber. It didn’t hurt anyone. It just examined the new bloodlines that had formed inside them.","A moment later, he nodded. \"The transfer has succeeded.\"","The ten geniuses looked toward him.","Arvantos continued, \"All of you have received Primordial Bloodlines.\"","The mood tightened. Even though they’d already made it through the process, hearing him say it out loud still brought a few quiet sighs of relief.","Then his gaze moved across them one by one.","\"Revona. Ervin. Damian Voss. Orion Starfall. Kaiden Voidmere. Rosaline Lunara. Morgana Starveil. Rakan Thorne. Aurelian Lareth.\"","He paused briefly. \"All nine of you have received Tier 3 Primordial Bloodlines.\"","The chamber fell silent.","Tier 3. Leader Primordial Bloodline. The bloodline carried by the upper rulers and high authorities of the Primordial Race. Even among Primordials, this level stood far above the ordinary.","Any single one of them getting a bloodline like this would have been enough to shake their home forces. For all nine of them to get Tier 3 bloodlines showed just how terrifying this generation’s top ten really was.","Rakan’s eyes went wide. \"Tier 3?\"","Orion let out a low laugh. \"That’s higher than I expected.\"","Damian Voss stayed calm, but even his gaze had sharpened.","Ervin looked down at his own hand, thoughtful, feeling the new ancient pressure flowing quietly through his blood.","Morgana smiled faintly. \"So all of us turned out fairly valuable.\"","Kaiden Voidmere said nothing, but his eyes clearly showed he was already working through the changes in his body.","Aurelian’s stiff expression finally eased up a bit. Tier 3 wasn’t the highest, but it was still a Leader Primordial Bloodline. Even his pride couldn’t brush that off.","Revona looked at Arvantos quietly. She’d already noticed he hadn’t mentioned Max. Everyone else noticed it a moment later too.","The chamber went even quieter.","Arvantos’s eyes moved to Max. A faint smile crossed his face.","\"As for Max Morgan.\"","Every gaze turned toward Max.","Arvantos spoke slowly, his voice carrying a weight heavy enough to make the whole Bloodline Chamber feel smaller.","\"He alone received a Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline.\"","The words hit the chamber like thunder.","For several breaths, no one said anything. Even the geniuses who’d just gotten Tier 3 bloodlines couldn’t keep their expressions steady. Tier 3 was already incredible, but Tier 4 was on a completely different level.","Arvantos had said it himself before the transfer started. The fourth tier was the Primarch Bloodline, an extremely rare bloodline only the Four Primarchs, him included, carried.","Now Max had it.","Revona’s pale eyes sharpened slightly.","Ervin stared at Max for a long breath before smiling helplessly.","Damian Voss lowered his gaze for a second, then looked back at Max with even deeper respect.","Orion laughed softly, though there was clear disbelief in his voice. \"Of course he did.\"","Rakan shook his head. \"This man doesn’t know how to be normal.\"","Morgana’s smile turned more amused and more serious at the same time. \"First in the conference, first in compatibility, and now the only Tier 4 bloodline. That’s excessive.\"","Kaiden Voidmere looked thoughtful. \"A Primarch-level bloodline.\"","Aurelian’s face darkened again. Whatever joy he’d felt from getting a Tier 3 bloodline got crushed the second he heard Max had gotten the one thing no one else had.","His fists tightened, but he still didn’t say anything. In this place, in front of Arvantos, any foolish show of resentment would only embarrass him further.","Max stayed seated quietly. His expression didn’t change much, but he could feel the bloodline inside him now. It wasn’t roaring. It was calm. Too calm. Like a sleeping ancient monarch resting in his blood, waiting for the day his body could fully wake up its authority.","Arvantos looked at Max with deep eyes. \"Your foundation was strong enough to bear it.\"","Max stood slowly. The moment he rose, a faint pressure moved through the chamber. It was subtle. Not overpowering. Not released on purpose. But all nine other geniuses felt it.","The aura of the new Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline was still asleep inside Max, yet even in that dormant state, it carried something that made their own Tier 3 bloodlines react faintly. It wasn’t suppression in any crude sense. It was hierarchy. A natural gap in origin.","Just then Max’s cultivation of 1st level Law Awakening Realm began to react violently.","\"It looks like you are leveling up.\" Arvantos smiled seeing the intense energy fluctuations around Max."]},{"number":1945,"title":"Chapter 1945 - 5th level of Law Refinement Realm!","paragraphs":["The other nine geniuses turned toward him at once, their expressions shifting again. They’d just gone through the bloodline transfer themselves.","Every one of them had gained a Tier 3 Leader Primordial Bloodline, and they could all feel their bodies, souls, and foundations changing in powerful ways. But none of them had triggered a breakthrough.","Their auras had deepened and their potential had clearly grown, but their cultivation realms hadn’t budged.","Max was different. The energy inside him wasn’t stopping. It was pushing his realm higher.","[Primordial Bloodline Integration Energy Detected.]","[Energy Absorption Beginning.]","[Law Refinement Realm 1st Level Stabilized.]","[Advancement Initiated.]","Max’s eyes sharpened slightly as the system prompts flashed in front of him, but he didn’t show anything outwardly. He just sat cross-legged in silence, letting the leftover Primordial Bloodline energy merge with his cultivation foundation.","Inside him, the laws he’d only recently started refining grew sharper and more condensed.","The Law Refinement Realm was all about taking awakened laws and tempering them into something stable, usable, and deeply tied to yourself.","The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline energy fit that process perfectly, since every strand of it carried an ancient law quality that naturally refined whatever it touched.","His foundation trembled. Then the first barrier broke.","Boom!","[Breakthrough Achieved.]","[Law Refinement Realm 2nd Level.]","The pressure around Max increased instantly. A faint wave of Primordial aura spread out from his body, and the nine geniuses felt their newly gained Tier 3 bloodlines react on instinct.","It wasn’t the crude kind of suppression a stronger cultivator throws at a weaker one. It was a deeper hierarchy, born from the gap between bloodline tiers.","Their bloodlines had only just awakened, yet even now they could sense that Max’s bloodline stood above theirs at the source level.","Aurelian’s expression turned extremely ugly. He’d just received a Tier 3 Primordial Bloodline, something that should have been one of the greatest moments of his life. But before he could even enjoy it, Max had gotten a Tier 4 Primarch Bloodline and was now breaking through right in front of everyone.","Orion Starfall stared for a second, then laughed helplessly. \"He really doesn’t leave any room for the rest of us to feel proud.\"","Rakan Thorne grinned, though disbelief still showed in his eyes. \"This bastard just finished the bloodline transfer and he’s already breaking through.\"","Damian Voss stayed quiet, but his gaze turned serious. He could feel that Max’s aura wasn’t just getting stronger. It was getting more refined and more dangerous.","Ervin smiled faintly. \"When I saw him back on the reception platform, I figured he’d already gotten stronger after the conference. Turns out that was just the beginning.\"","Revona watched quietly, her pale eyes reflecting the Primordial light around Max. Her expression stayed calm, but even she couldn’t ignore what was happening in front of her.","’This kid... Is he related to him?’ She thought looking deeply at Max.","Max’s cultivation didn’t stop at the 2nd level.","The remaining Primordial energy kept pouring through him. His newly formed Tier 4 bloodline worked like a supreme vessel, holding, filtering, and directing the energy into his law foundation without letting any of it scatter. His Dimensional Sovereign Body helped spread out the pressure.","His Seven Divine Veins kept the flow steady. His draconic essence and Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline and Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline stopped resisting altogether, and the Dimensional Keeper legacy stayed quiet but steady, deep in his foundation.","The second barrier broke.","Boom!","[Breakthrough Achieved.]","[Law Refinement Realm 3rd Level.]","Max’s aura rose again. The laws around him condensed into faint threads, each one carrying a trace of Primordial light.","His Emotion Severing Path, Divine King Punishment, and Devouring Flames Domain all stirred inside him, growing even more refined under the pressure of his rising cultivation and new bloodline.","They were still Pseudo Cosmic Paths, still incomplete, still nowhere near true Cosmic Paths before the Divine Lord Realm, but their structures grew sharper and deeper.","Another wave of energy burst out. The third barrier broke.","[Breakthrough Achieved.]","[Law Refinement Realm 4th Level.]","By now, the Bloodline Chamber was glowing almost as bright as it had during the transfer itself.","The ancient runes on the walls seemed to wake up again, not because the formation was still feeding Max more bloodline essence, but because his breakthrough was interacting with the chamber itself.","The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline inside him resonated with the chamber’s origin, and the whole space started humming softly.","Arvantos watched with real interest.","Sarvion, standing off to the side, could no longer fully hide his surprise.","\"Primarch,\" Sarvion said quietly, \"his absorption speed is abnormal.\"","Arvantos smiled. \"His foundation is abnormal. The absorption speed is just a result of that.\"","Max’s body shook once more. The remaining energy gathered into one final surge. It moved through his bloodline, entered his law foundation, and pushed toward the next small realm.","For an ordinary cultivator, jumping several levels at once inside the Law Refinement Realm would have caused instability.","But Max’s foundation was far too strong. He’d accumulated too much depth during the Cosmic Ascension Conference, and the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline had refined his base instead of straining it. Each breakthrough hit hard, but none of them felt hollow.","The final barrier shattered.","Boom!","[Breakthrough Achieved.]","[Law Refinement Realm 5th Level.]","[Remaining Primordial Integration Energy Stabilized.]","[Current Realm: Law Refinement Realm 5th Level.]","Max slowly opened his eyes. For a brief moment, his pupils carried faint primordial rings before they faded. His aura settled around him, no longer erupting wildly, but everyone in the Bloodline Chamber could feel that he’d changed again.","He’d walked into the chamber as a 1st level Law Refinement Realm cultivator. After receiving the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline and absorbing the leftover integration energy, he’d jumped straight to the 5th level of the Law Refinement Realm.","The chamber stayed silent. Even the top ten geniuses didn’t know what to say at first.","Max stood slowly. His aura was calm, but that calm only made him seem more dangerous.","The Primordial Bloodline he’d just gained wasn’t roaring out loud, but it sat inside him like an ancient source waiting for the day it could fully wake up. His cultivation had jumped four small levels, his law foundation had been refined, and his Pseudo Cosmic Paths had grown sharper.","Arvantos looked at the others and seemed to catch what they were thinking.","He spoke calmly. \"Don’t misunderstand. Integrating a Primordial Bloodline always leaves behind a large amount of energy, but whether that energy can trigger a breakthrough depends on the cultivator’s current realm and foundation.\"","The nine geniuses listened closely.","Arvantos continued. \"All of you were already at the peak of the Law Manifestation Realm before you entered the Bloodline Chamber. For you, the next step is the Divine Lord Realm. That’s not a small jump you can cross with leftover energy from a bloodline integration. The Divine Lord Realm needs full preparation, a stabilized foundation, deeper law transformation, and the true start of authority.\"","He paused, then glanced at Max.","\"Max Morgan was different. He was still in the Law Refinement Realm. The energy generated from integrating the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline was more than enough to push him through several small levels, especially given his foundation. If he’d also been at the peak of the Law Manifestation Realm like the rest of you, this same energy wouldn’t have been enough to push him into the Divine Lord Realm either.\"","Only then did some of the others relax a little.","Rakan let out a breath. \"So we weren’t cheated out of anything.\"","Arvantos smiled faintly. \"No, you weren’t. Honestly, getting Tier 3 bloodlines at your current realm is already an extraordinary result. Once you properly digest the bloodline and prepare for your Divine Lord breakthrough, the benefits will show a lot more clearly.\"","Orion nodded thoughtfully. \"So our gains run deeper, just not right away.\"","\"Correct,\" Arvantos said. \"The Primordial Bloodline isn’t just some cultivation pill. Its real value isn’t the instant jump in realm. It’s the change to your future ceiling.\"","Damian Voss looked at his own hand quietly. \"So once we break through to the Divine Lord Realm, the difference should start showing.\"","\"It will,\" Arvantos said. \"Your bodies, souls, law affinities, and future paths have all changed.\"","Ervin glanced at Max and smiled. \"Still, watching him climb four levels right in front of us isn’t exactly pleasant.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"You can take it up with the Primordials.\"","Arvantos looked amused. \"I don’t accept complaints.\"","For a moment, even the tense mood in the Bloodline Chamber loosened up a little."]},{"number":1946,"title":"Chapter 1946: A Major Crisis!","paragraphs":["The faint amusement that had settled over the Bloodline Chamber after Max’s breakthrough didn’t last long.","Arvantos’s expression turned serious. The shift was subtle, but everyone in the room felt it right away. The four-colored rings in his eyes slowed down, and the ancient pressure around him grew quieter instead of stronger.","That quiet made the whole chamber feel heavier, since it felt like the Primarch had stopped speaking to them as the man guiding a reward ceremony and started speaking as one of the four leaders of the Primordial Race.","The ten geniuses slowly fell silent.","Rakan, who’d been about to make another comment about Max’s strange breakthrough, closed his mouth. Orion’s faint smile disappeared. Damian’s gaze sharpened. Ervin looked at Arvantos with calm, serious eyes. Revona stayed as expressionless as always, but her Void Origin Eyes opened slightly wider.","Max also turned his full attention toward Arvantos.","Arvantos looked at each of them before speaking.","\"There are some things you should know.\"","The moment he said that, the mood in the room shifted again. Aurelian frowned slightly but didn’t dare interrupt. Rosaline and Morgana traded a quick glance, while Kaiden Voidmere’s silver-gray eyes narrowed in thought.","After everything they’d already been through, none of them believed Arvantos would suddenly change his tone over something small.","Orion finally asked, \"What do you mean?\"","Arvantos didn’t answer right away. He turned his gaze toward the walls of the Bloodline Chamber. The ancient runes there slowly dimmed, and for a moment the whole chamber seemed to sink into a deeper shade of gold. The silence that followed wasn’t long, but it was enough to make everyone uneasy.","Then Arvantos began.","\"A major crisis will soon spread across this universe.\"","The words came out quiet. But they hit the ten geniuses harder than any shout could have.","The entire universe. Not one clan. Not one region. Not one divine territory. Not even the Divine Realm alone. The entire universe.","The ten geniuses’ expressions all changed at once.","Rakan’s brows pulled tight. \"A crisis that big?\"","Morgana’s playful look vanished completely. \"What kind of crisis?\"","Kaiden Voidmere’s eyes turned sharp. \"Is it tied to another race? A war? Some kind of collapse in the laws?\"","Damian Voss looked at Arvantos too. \"How soon?\"","Arvantos stayed silent for a few breaths, then said, \"I can’t explain the details yet.\"","That answer only made the room feel heavier.","Rakan frowned. \"Can’t, or won’t?\"","Arvantos looked at him calmly. \"Both.\"","No one said anything.","Arvantos went on. \"Some truths can’t be carried by people who aren’t strong enough yet. Knowing too much too soon won’t help you. It might even become a weight that wrecks your confidence, warps your judgment, or draws attention you’re not ready to handle.\"","Even Rakan went quiet after that.","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly. He could tell Arvantos wasn’t holding back for the sake of being mysterious. The Primarch’s tone carried the weight of someone who genuinely understood the danger behind his own warning. If one of the four Primarchs chose not to explain the full crisis, then clearly this wasn’t something the current top ten were ready to touch.","Arvantos looked across the group.","\"What you need to know is simple. The peace you’ve known won’t last forever. The great forces of the Divine Realm, the Primordial Race, and plenty of ancient powers are already quietly preparing. Most people in the universe have no idea what’s coming, and for now, that’s for the best.\"","Rosaline’s face paled. \"Then why tell us anything at all?\"","\"Because you’re no longer ordinary geniuses,\" Arvantos replied. \"You’re the top ten of the Cosmic Ascension Conference. You’ve received Primordial Bloodlines. Each of you has stepped onto a path that will make you far more important than you were before. If you keep growing, you might end up part of the power that resists what’s coming.\"","His gaze lingered on Max for a moment.","\"Some of you might even become central to it.\"","The chamber went quiet again. The words were vague, but the weight behind them wasn’t.","Arvantos raised one hand, and faint Primordial light appeared around the ten geniuses before slowly sinking into their bodies. It wasn’t another bloodline transfer, just a stabilizing force meant to help settle the Primordial Bloodlines they’d just received.","\"Don’t waste time,\" Arvantos said. \"That’s the most important warning I can give you.\"","His voice deepened. \"Get stronger as fast as you can.\"","Every genius listened without blinking.","\"If you delay, if you get comfortable because of your current strength, if you assume that getting a Primordial Bloodline means your future is set, you might not get another chance to improve. The crisis heading our way won’t care about your talent, your background, your ranking, your bloodline tier, or your pride. When it arrives, only strength will matter.\"","The words pressed down on them like a mountain.","Even Aurelian, who’d spent most of this whole process feeling stung by how much more Max had gained, turned solemn. Even he understood Arvantos wasn’t exaggerating. A Primarch had no reason to scare a bunch of juniors just for entertainment.","Ervin lowered his gaze for a second, then smiled faintly. \"So the Cosmic Ascension Conference wasn’t just a competition.\"","\"No,\" Arvantos said. \"It was also a selection.\"","Damian Voss rested his hand lightly near his sword. \"And the bloodline transfer was preparation.\"","\"Yes.\"","Revona finally spoke. \"For whatever comes next.\"","Arvantos looked at her and nodded. \"Correct.\"","The Bloodline Chamber fell into a long silence after that.","The ten geniuses had walked into this place expecting rewards, transformation, and opportunity. They’d gotten all of that. Nine of them had gained Tier 3 Primordial Bloodlines, and Max had gained the Tier 4 Primarch Bloodline. Their bodies, souls, foundations, and futures had all changed in ways that would shock their home forces.","But now the meaning behind those rewards felt heavier. They weren’t just gifts. They were preparation for a disaster no one had named yet.","Max stayed quiet.","A major crisis that would soon spread across the entire universe. Arvantos hadn’t explained what it actually was, and that only made it feel more dangerous. Max already carried enough of his own burdens.","His parents were still imprisoned. Aurelian still held the stolen source of his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. His enemies hadn’t gone anywhere. The secrets behind the Dimensional Keeper legacy were still sitting unanswered in the dark.","And now another shadow had shown up on top of all of that."]},{"number":1947,"title":"Chapter 1947: A Promise!","paragraphs":["Max slowly closed his hand. The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline stirred faintly inside him. His cultivation, now steady at the 5th level of the Law Refinement Realm, felt nowhere near enough. Not for his own goals, and definitely not for whatever crisis could make one of the four Primarchs sound this serious.","Arvantos looked at all of them one last time.","\"You’ll stay in the Primordial Ancestral Domain for a short while to stabilize your bloodlines and learn the first stage of Primordial control. After that, you’ll return to your own forces.\"","His gaze grew heavier.","\"Make good use of the time you have.\"","No one answered right away. There was no need to. Each of them understood.","The Cosmic Ascension Conference had been the stage where they proved themselves. The Primordial Bloodline was the reward that transformed them. But the real trial waiting ahead was something far bigger than any tournament. And if they weren’t strong enough when it arrived, even the title of supreme genius wouldn’t mean anything.","Even though Arvantos’s warning left a heavy shadow over the ten geniuses, none of them kept asking about it.","They were curious, of course. How could they not be? A major crisis that would soon spread across the entire universe wasn’t a small thing to hear. If those words had come from an elder of some ordinary divine clan, a few of them might have suspected exaggeration meant to scare them into obedience.","But the person who’d said it was Arvantos, one of the four Primarchs of the Primordial Race. A being like him had no reason to exaggerate in front of the younger generation, and he certainly had no reason to invent fear without cause.","Still, curiosity alone wasn’t useful. Arvantos had already made it clear that they weren’t qualified to know the full truth yet, so dwelling on it would only waste time. Every one of them had just received a Primordial Bloodline, and that new power hadn’t fully settled into their bodies. If they left it unstable out of carelessness, even a heaven-sent opportunity could turn into a hidden danger.","So, under Sarvion’s guidance, the ten geniuses stayed in the Primordial Ancestral Domain for several more days.","Each of them was assigned a separate cultivation chamber in a quiet area behind the Bloodline Chamber. These chambers sat above streams of ancient primordial energy, and their walls were carved with stabilizing runes meant to ease the friction between each genius’s original foundation and their newly received bloodline.","Once inside, each of them began the long process of circulating their Primordial Bloodline, learning its rhythm, controlling its pressure, and making sure it didn’t clash with their existing powers.","Max sat alone in one of these chambers.","The room around him was circular, silent, and filled with faint golden mist. The floor beneath him held four interlocking runes that resonated faintly with the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline inside his body. Every time his blood circulated, those runes lit up softly, as if responding to a Primarch’s bloodline.","Max sat cross-legged with his eyes closed. Inside him, the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline stayed calm, but that calm felt more like the stillness of an ocean than the weakness of sleeping power. It hadn’t fully awakened yet. Max could tell that much clearly.","What he’d received was the source and foundation of the bloodline, but bringing out its true abilities would take time, battles, refinement, and deeper cultivation. Even so, in its current state, it had already transformed his body, strengthened his soul, refined his laws, and helped push his cultivation to the 5th level of the Law Refinement Realm.","His Emotion Severing Path, Divine King Punishment, and Devouring Flames Domain had also stabilized further thanks to the new bloodline. They were still Pseudo Cosmic Paths, but their edges had grown sharper and their structures more complete.","Max could sense the distant wall between pseudo and true cosmic paths more clearly than ever, and yet that wall also felt impossibly high. No matter how close he seemed to get, he knew he wouldn’t truly cross it until he reached the Divine Lord Realm.","For several days, Max focused only on stabilizing. He didn’t rush. He didn’t try to greedily force the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline to show off abilities before it was ready. He calmly guided it through his body, let it settle into his foundation, and made sure it wouldn’t disturb his other bloodlines.","His Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, draconic essence foundation, Seven Divine Veins, Dimensional Sovereign Body, and new Primordial Bloodline were all powerful on their own, but power without balance could destroy the person carrying it. Max had too many extraordinary things inside him, which meant his foundation needed even more control than most.","On the fifth day, while Max quietly circulated the Primordial Bloodline, a communication mark he carried suddenly lit up.","Max opened his eyes. A message appeared before him.","[Max, I need your help.]","[You promised you would help me once in return for me joining Crown.]","[Come to the coordinates I have sent. Come alone.]","[Rose.]","Max looked at the message for a few breaths.","Rose. The young woman who’d agreed to join his force, Crown, in exchange for one favor. She hadn’t asked for that favor right away back then, and Max hadn’t pushed her to explain. He’d simply given his word. Now, it looked like the time had come for her to collect on it.","Max stood up. He didn’t waste any time.","After letting Sarvion know he had a private matter to handle and getting permission to leave the Primordial Ancestral Domain for a while, Max used the coordinates Rose had sent.","A spatial path opened in front of him, and his Dimensional Sovereign Body guided him through the layers of space with far more ease than before. After stepping into the Law Refinement Realm and receiving the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline, his control over space had gotten even more natural, almost as if distance itself had softened around him.","A short while later, Max arrived at the location Rose had given him.","The first thing he saw was emptiness. Not the emptiness of void, and not the emptiness of destruction. Just an abandoned planet.","The sky was pale blue, the wind was gentle, and the land stretched endlessly in every direction, covered by vast grass fields rolling like waves under the breeze. There were no cities, no mountains of spiritual energy, no towering sects, no ancient ruins, no divine beasts, no obvious formations, and no visible sign of any powerful clan.","Max stood in the middle of the grass field and looked around silently.","\"This is the place?\"","For a moment, even he wondered if Rose had sent him to the wrong location by mistake.","Then his eyes narrowed. His Dimensional Sovereign Body reacted. The world looked empty on the surface, but the space here was anything but ordinary."]},{"number":1948,"title":"Chapter 1948: Secrets of the Four Sacred Clans!","paragraphs":["[A few scenes got cut here. Max would meet Rose here and then she would reveal she is part of the Evercrest Clan, one of the Four Sacred Clans and then took him to the Evercrest Clan]","Max looked toward the revealed world of the Evercrest Clan.","The abandoned grass planet had disappeared from his view, replaced by a hidden sacred territory folded inside countless layers of space.","Colossal trees rose like pillars between heaven and earth, emerald rivers of energy flowed through the air, and palaces carved from living wood and pale jade stood across floating gardens suspended between branches large enough to hold whole cities.","Everything before him looked ancient, peaceful, and beautiful, yet Max could sense a deep instability hiding beneath the surface, something ordinary eyes would never pick up on.","Rose didn’t take him inside right away. Instead, she stood beside him on the boundary between the abandoned outer world and the hidden clan territory, looking out at the vast Evercrest domain with a complicated expression.","\"Before I take you in,\" she said, \"there are some things you should know.\"","Max glanced at her. \"About your clan?\"","\"About all Four Sacred Clans,\" Rose replied.","Max’s eyes sharpened slightly.","Rose turned toward him, and the smile she usually wore was gone. \"You’ve received the Primordial Bloodline now, and not an ordinary one either. Since you’re already connected to the Primordial Race, there are some secrets about the Divine Realm you’re qualified to know.\"","Max didn’t interrupt her.","Rose looked back at the hidden domain and began speaking. \"Long ago, after humans came into existence, the first human forces to truly rise and establish themselves in the Divine Realm were the Four Sacred Clans. Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest.\"","Max stayed silent, but his expression shifted slightly. He’d heard of the Four Sacred Clans many times. Their names carried terrifying weight across the Divine Realm. Even forces like the Black Dragon Clan, the Sword God Palace, the War God Palace, the Nine Star Court, and the major world guilds didn’t treat the Four Sacred Clans lightly. They were ancient, mysterious, and powerful enough to sit near the top of human civilization.","But Rose’s next words made things far more complicated.","\"The Four Sacred Clans were the earliest great pillars of humanity,\" Rose continued. \"But their origin isn’t the same as ordinary humans.\"","Max looked at her. \"Different how?\"","Rose’s eyes grew deeper. \"Most humans supposedly descended from Primordials who gave up their bloodline and became mortal. That’s the history you should have been told, and it’s true for the vast majority of humanity.\"","\"The vast majority?\" Max repeated.","Rose nodded. \"But not all.\"","The wind moved across the grass behind them, and the hidden entrance to the Evercrest Clan shimmered softly in front of them, like a veil of folded light.","Rose lowered her voice slightly. \"The Four Sacred Clans aren’t descendants of those Primordials.\"","Max’s expression finally changed. He looked straight at her. \"Then what are they?\"","Rose met his gaze. \"The Four Sacred Clans are descended from a forbidden bloodline cursed by the world.\"","For a moment, even Max didn’t say anything.","A forbidden bloodline cursed by the world. Those words carried a different kind of weight than ordinary ancient secrets.","Max had seen plenty of powerful bloodlines. His own body carried the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, and now a Tier 4 Primarch Bloodline of the Primordial Race. He understood better than most how much a bloodline could shape destiny, power, inheritance, and status.","But a bloodline cursed by the world was something else entirely. For some reason, it reminded him of the Legacy of the Dimensional Keeper where every inheritor of the legacy would end up die in way or another before fully awakening their Dimensional Keeper Legacy.","From what that goddess had told him, Dimensional Keeper Legacy was also cursed by fate.","\"Cursed by the world,\" Max said slowly. \"That doesn’t sound like a figure of speech.\"","\"It isn’t,\" Rose replied.","Max studied her face and asked, \"What bloodline?\"","Rose didn’t answer right away. Her gaze drifted toward the hidden Evercrest domain, and for a brief moment, something unreadable crossed her eyes. It wasn’t quite fear, but it was close to caution, the kind shown by someone who knew certain names shouldn’t be spoken carelessly.","Rose said, \"I can show you inside the clan.\"","Max’s expression stayed calm, but his thoughts were racing.","The Four Sacred Clans weren’t descended from Primordials like other humans. They carried a forbidden bloodline cursed by the world. They were strong enough to rival Primordials despite lacking the Primordial Race’s own bloodline. And Rose had brought him here because the Evercrest Clan was in trouble.","The pieces were starting to form a dangerous picture.","Max looked at Rose again. \"You said the Four Sacred Clans don’t carry the Primordial Race’s bloodline, yet they’re as strong as the Primordials.\"","Rose nodded. \"Yes. That’s why the Four Sacred Clans have always held a special position. They’re human, but not human in the same way most humans are. They don’t carry Primordial Bloodline, yet their inherited power can stand against the Primordial Race. Their ancestors never relied on returning to the Primordial source. They walked a different path, one the world itself rejected.\"","\"Then why are they still called human forces?\"","\"Because they chose to stand with humanity,\" Rose said. \"Whatever their origin, the Four Sacred Clans protected early humans back when humanity was weak. They built the first great shelters, the first sacred cities, the first human law academies, and the first supreme inheritance grounds. Without them, humanity might have been wiped out before it ever became a major race.\"","Max listened quietly. This was another hidden layer of history. Arvantos had told the top ten that humans were born from Primordials who gave up their bloodline. Now Rose was telling him that the strongest and oldest human forces didn’t come from that same origin at all.","They came from something forbidden, something cursed, something powerful enough to rival Primordials yet dangerous enough that even its name couldn’t be spoken outside the clan.","Max asked, \"Does the Primordial Race know about this?\"","Rose smiled faintly. \"Of course. The Primordial Race and the Four Sacred Clans have known each other’s secrets for a very long time.\"","\"And they still coexist?\"","\"They don’t have much choice,\" Rose replied calmly. \"The Divine Realm isn’t peaceful enough for its strongest pillars to destroy each other over old origins. Besides, the Primordial Race and the Four Sacred Clans aren’t enemies. Not usually.\"","\"Not usually?\" Max repeated."]},{"number":1949,"title":"Chapter 1949: Unknown Reactions!","paragraphs":["Rose’s smile turned a little tired. \"Ancient relationships get complicated.\"","Max looked at her for a moment before asking the question that mattered most.","\"What’s the problem you needed my help with?\"","Rose didn’t answer right away. The hidden world of the Evercrest Clan shimmered behind her, and the deeper spatial fluctuations grew more intense for a brief instant.","Max felt it clearly this time. Somewhere inside the clan, space was being stretched, folded, torn, and sealed all at once. It wasn’t a natural spatial storm. It felt like something trapped was pressing against the clan’s structure from within.","Rose’s expression turned solemn.","\"You’ll know soon.\"","Max looked at her silently.","Rose turned and walked toward the entrance of the Evercrest Clan. As she stepped forward, the folded space opened for her, revealing a path made of emerald light and silver spatial runes. Each step she took made the hidden domain recognize her bloodline, and the path stretched deeper into the sacred territory.","After a few steps, she looked back at Max.","\"Come. I’ll take you inside.\"","Max didn’t hesitate. He followed her.","The moment he crossed the boundary, the outer abandoned planet vanished completely. The endless grass field, the pale sky, and the ordinary wind disappeared behind him as if they’d never existed. In their place, the Evercrest Clan unfolded in full.","The air grew denser. The laws felt older. The spatial layers turned unbelievably complex. Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body immediately picked up on countless hidden passages, sealed regions, folded courtyards, inverted spaces, and secret domains nested inside one another like an endless maze.","This wasn’t just a clan territory. It was a living spatial fortress built across generations by experts who understood space on a terrifying level.","Rose walked ahead of him. The emerald path carried them across a river of floating energy and toward a massive tree whose trunk was wider than a mountain range. Palaces grew from its branches, glowing softly under the light of hanging spirit moons.","Disciples in green, silver, and white robes moved across the bridges between branches, but when they spotted Rose leading a white-haired young man into the clan, their expressions changed.","Some looked curious. Some looked shocked. Some seemed to recognize Max immediately.","\"That’s Max Morgan.\"","\"The champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference?\"","\"Why did Lady Rose bring him here?\"","\"Lady Rose? Haha, more like Abandoned Rose...\"","\"Is Max really the one who beat Revona?\"","\"He looks younger than I expected.\"","Whispers spread quietly. Max ignored them, and Rose paid them no attention either.","She kept leading him deeper into the clan, past the beautiful palaces and floating gardens, past the disciples and elders who turned to watch them, and toward the area where the spatial fluctuations were strongest.","The deeper they went, the more serious Max’s expression became. The Evercrest Clan looked beautiful on the surface, but the closer they got to the core region, the clearer the hidden wound became.","Behind the elegant spatial layers, Max could sense a vast sealed region trembling nonstop. Something inside it was unstable. Something powerful. Something tied to the forbidden bloodline Rose had mentioned.","At last, Rose stopped before a massive gate formed from intertwined roots, silver spatial chains, and emerald crystal. The gate was closed. Beyond it, Max could feel a terrifying distortion.","Rose looked at the gate quietly, then said, \"Inside this place, you’ll see the bloodline I couldn’t name outside.\"","Max stood beside her and looked at the sealed gate. His Dimensional Sovereign Body stirred. His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline gave off a faint reaction too.","Rose’s voice softened even more.","\"And after that, you’ll understand why I needed your help.\"","The massive gate of intertwined roots, silver spatial chains, and emerald crystal opened without a sound.","Beyond it wasn’t a palace. It wasn’t a battlefield. It wasn’t even a sealed chamber packed with treasures and inheritance stones. It was a vast circular hall hidden beneath the deepest spatial layer of the Evercrest Clan.","The hall was silent, dim, and ancient, its walls made from dark green stone that seemed to breathe softly with the rhythm of space itself. Countless silver chains stretched from the walls into the center of the chamber, not to bind a living being, but to hold the whole space stable around a single statue.","At the center stood the statue of a man. He was tall and calm, with long hair flowing behind him and one hand resting lightly at his side.","His face wasn’t carved with excessive detail, yet every line seemed to hold an indescribable presence. He didn’t look like a tyrant, a king, or a god, but simply like someone who stood before the world without needing to prove anything. His eyes were closed, but even so, Max felt like those stone eyes could open at any moment and look straight through him.","Rose walked a few steps forward and stopped in front of the statue.","\"This is him,\" she said softly.","Max looked at the statue in silence.","Rose continued, \"The ancestor of the Four Sacred Clans. Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest all descend from this man. The forbidden bloodline carried by the Four Sacred Clans came from him.\"","Max didn’t answer, because the moment he saw the statue, something inside him reacted. Violently. His blood surged without warning. Not just one bloodline. Something deeper.","For an instant, Max felt the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline stir. Then the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline trembled. His newly obtained Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline let out a faint pulse, as if it were recognizing and rejecting something at the same time.","Even the hidden depths of his foundation, places that normally stayed silent unless he actively called on them, suddenly shook, as though an ancient echo had woken up inside him.","Max’s fingers moved slightly. He got the reaction under control right away. His expression stayed the same on the outside.","But inwardly, he was shocked.","’What is this?’","He didn’t know this man. He’d never seen this face before. He had no memory of meeting anyone related to him, yet the reaction inside his body was too strong to ignore.","It wasn’t the simple resonance that happens when two powerful bloodlines sense each other. It ran deeper than that, as if something inside Max recognized the statue on an instinctive level, beyond memory.","His blood kept surging. His Dimensional Sovereign Body also reacted faintly, picking up strange spatial traces around the statue that didn’t belong to ordinary space.","His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline stayed calm on the surface, but Max could feel a hidden tremor inside it, like a sleeping ancient monarch had just sensed another authority somewhere in the distance.","Still, Max kept it all hidden. Rose stood beside him, and even though she trusted him enough to bring him here, Max had no plans to reveal every strange reaction happening inside his body. He quietly pushed down the turmoil in his blood and kept his gaze steady."]},{"number":1950,"title":"Chapter 1950: Bloodline Legacy Battle!","paragraphs":["Rose didn’t notice anything unusual. Or maybe she did and simply didn’t show it. She looked at the statue with a complicated expression.","\"The Four Sacred Clans worship him as the First Progenitor. His name isn’t spoken casually, and his true bloodline is even more restricted. Most people in the Divine Realm only know the Four Sacred Clans as ancient human pillars, but very few know that our bloodline doesn’t come from Primordials like ordinary humans. It comes from him.\"","Max asked calmly, \"And this bloodline is why the Four Sacred Clans can rival the Primordials?\"","Rose nodded. \"Yes. Anyone who awakens even a trace of the forbidden bloodline becomes different. Their body, soul, laws, and inheritance all change. Every sacred clan carries the bloodline in a different way, and each branch expresses that power differently. Evercrest specializes in space, life, and sealed domains, but that’s only the outer form. The source is still the same forbidden bloodline.\"","Max looked at the statue again. His blood gave another faint tremor, and he suppressed it once more.","\"Then why did you bring me here?\"","Rose went quiet for a moment. The question seemed simple, but her expression shifted in a way that made it clear the answer wasn’t easy for her. She looked away from the statue and turned toward one of the silver chains stretching across the hall. The chain shimmered faintly with spatial light, reflecting her face in broken fragments.","\"I’m a direct descendant of the Evercrest Clan,\" she said quietly.","Max looked at her. \"I figured as much.\"","Rose smiled faintly, though there was no real amusement in it. \"Direct descendant in blood, but not in value.\"","Max didn’t interrupt.","Rose continued, \"I was born without the forbidden bloodline.\"","The hall went quiet. The silver chains hummed softly around them.","Rose’s voice stayed calm, but Max could hear the weight underneath it. \"In the Evercrest Clan, bloodline decides everything. Talent matters. Cultivation matters. Intelligence matters. But all of that comes after the forbidden bloodline. Those who awaken it get treated as true heirs. Those who don’t get treated as incomplete descendants.\"","Max’s gaze deepened slightly.","Rose looked at the statue again. \"Children born without the forbidden bloodline aren’t allowed to live on the main premises of the Evercrest Clan. Some get sent to branch territories. Some get placed on distant planets. Some get handed minor resources and told to survive on their own. In name, they still belong to Evercrest. In reality, they’re as good as abandoned.\"","Max remembered where he’d first met her. Planet Orion. A place far from the heart of the Evercrest Clan.","\"So that’s why you were living on Orion,\" Max said.","Rose nodded. \"Yes. Of all places, the direct descendant of one of the Four Sacred Clans was living on Planet Orion like someone with no background at all. Sounds ridiculous, doesn’t it?\"","Max said calmly, \"It sounds like something old clans would do.\"","Rose glanced at him. For a moment she smiled, and this time there was a trace of real amusement in it.","\"You’re not wrong.\"","Then her expression turned serious again.","\"I wasn’t completely abandoned because I had no talent. Even without the forbidden bloodline, my talent was good enough that some elders thought it was a shame. But pity doesn’t change clan rules. Without the bloodline, I had no right to stay in the sacred territory, no right to compete for true inheritance, and no right to be treated as an heir.\"","Max looked toward the statue. \"And now?\"","\"Now, an opportunity has come up.\"","Rose turned fully toward him.","\"In a few days, the Four Sacred Clans will hold the Bloodline Legacy Battle.\"","Max raised an eyebrow slightly. \"The Four Sacred Clans?\"","Rose nodded. \"Yes. This isn’t a ceremony held by the Evercrest Clan alone. Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest will all take part. The Bloodline Legacy Battle is one of the few ancient events shared by all four sacred clans, since the forbidden bloodline carried by all four comes from the same source.\"","Max’s gaze shifted slightly toward the statue at the center of the hall.","\"The First Progenitor.\"","\"Yes,\" Rose said softly. \"All four sacred clans descend from him. Even though each clan developed a different branch of the forbidden bloodline, the root is the same. Because of that, the Bloodline Legacy Battle isn’t run by just one clan. It’s held jointly by all four, and every sacred clan sends descendants, heirs, representatives, and challengers to compete for legacy merit.\"","Max looked at her. \"So this is much bigger than an internal Evercrest matter.\"","\"It is,\" Rose replied. \"That’s why I needed someone like you.\"","Her expression grew more solemn.","\"In the Evercrest Clan, a castaway direct descendant like me would normally never get close to the true inheritance. But during the Bloodline Legacy Battle, there’s an old rule left over from the age of the Four Sacred Ancestors.","Any direct descendant of one of the Four Sacred Clans, even one born without the forbidden bloodline, can request one chance to participate through a chosen representative. If that representative wins enough battles and gathers enough legacy merit, the descendant who chose him gets a chance to inherit or awaken the forbidden bloodline.\"","Max understood the weight of it right away.","\"So I won’t only be fighting Evercrest representatives.\"","Rose nodded. \"You may end up fighting representatives from all four sacred clans.\"","The hall grew quieter.","Rose continued, \"Some will be direct heirs of Valerius. Some will come from Ashbourne. Some will represent Ravenhart. Some will belong to Evercrest. And some will be outsiders hired by sacred clan descendants trying to boost their chances. Everyone there will be dangerous, because no one brings a weak representative to the Bloodline Legacy Battle.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"That sounds better.\"","Rose looked at him with a complicated expression. \"Only you would call that better.\"","\"If the stage belongs to all Four Sacred Clans, then winning there matters more.\"","Rose’s eyes trembled slightly. For her, this wasn’t just a competition. It was her one chance to return to the bloodline that had rejected her since birth.","If Max won enough battles for her, she wouldn’t just gain some resources or status. She’d gain the chance to enter the Bloodline Inheritance Pool shared by the sacred clans, a place where even someone born without the forbidden bloodline might still awaken it.","She looked toward the statue of the First Progenitor.","\"The Bloodline Legacy Battle was created because even the Four Sacred Clans couldn’t fully control the forbidden bloodline. Some direct descendants are born with it. Some aren’t. Some awaken it later. Some die without ever touching it. The ancient ancestors left this ceremony behind so that those rejected by birth could still fight for one chance.\"","Max looked at her. \"And you want that chance.\"","Rose nodded. \"Yes. I want that chance.\"","She turned back to him and said quietly, \"When I joined Crown, I told you I’d need your help one day. This is that help. Represent me in the Bloodline Legacy Battle. Win enough battles to gather legacy merit for me. If you do, I can enter the inheritance trial and try to awaken the forbidden bloodline of the Four Sacred Clans.\"","Max looked at her for a few breaths.","Then he said, \"I’ll represent you.\"","Rose’s expression softened. \"Thank you.\"","Max glanced once more at the statue of the First Progenitor. The strange reaction inside his blood had finally settled, but the mystery hadn’t."]},{"number":1951,"title":"Chapter 1951: A Week of Time!","paragraphs":["After Max agreed to represent her in the Bloodline Legacy Battle, Rose didn’t keep him in the ancestral hall for long.","She looked once more at the statue of the First Progenitor, and for a brief moment her expression turned complicated again. There was longing in her eyes, but also frustration, restraint, and a faint trace of resentment that had clearly been buried for years.","To the true heirs of the Four Sacred Clans, this statue represented origin, pride, and inheritance. To Rose, it represented everything she’d been denied since birth.","Then she turned away.","\"Come with me,\" she said. \"I’ll take you to the place prepared for you.\"","Max gave the statue one last glance before following her out of the sealed hall. The moment he stepped away from the chamber, the strange reaction inside his blood eased a little, though it didn’t vanish completely.","It stayed deep inside him like a disturbed echo, quiet for now but not settled. He couldn’t make sense of it, and since Rose was still beside him, he kept it to himself.","The gate closed behind them. The silver spatial chains around the hall tightened again, and the entrance disappeared beneath layers of folded space as if it had never existed. Rose led him through several hidden corridors that didn’t seem tied to normal distance.","Each corridor twisted gently and changed direction in ways that should have been impossible, yet Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body could still follow the spatial logic behind them. The Evercrest Clan hadn’t just built a residence inside space. It had turned space itself into architecture.","Soon, they arrived at a quiet courtyard.","The courtyard sat on one of the higher branches of an enormous ancient tree. Its walls were made of pale green jade and living wood, and silver spatial runes flowed across the entrance like water.","A small magical pond lay at the center, surrounded by soft grass, flowering vines, and a few stone paths leading toward several rooms.","Above the courtyard, a faint dome of hidden space separated it from the outside world, giving the whole place a peaceful, isolated feel.","Rose stopped in front of the main room and looked at Max.","\"This will be your residence until the Bloodline Legacy Battle begins.\"","Max looked around once. The place was quiet but not simple. The energy density here was extremely high, and the spatial runes hidden inside the walls were strong enough to block most forms of spying.","There was also a separate training chamber attached to the residence, and from the faint pressure coming off it, Max could tell it was built to withstand attacks from powerful geniuses.","Rose noticed him looking and explained, \"Your room has its own training chamber. It can adjust pressure, simulate different spatial environments, and block most energy leakage. You can cultivate, stabilize your power, or train there without disturbing anyone.\"","Max nodded. \"Good.\"","\"The Bloodline Legacy Battle starts in one week,\" Rose continued. \"Until then, you can rest here. I still need to sort out some things related to registering you as my representative, so I might not come around much these next few days.\"","\"That’s fine.\"","Rose looked at him for a moment, then said, \"Max, the Bloodline Legacy Battle isn’t like the Cosmic Ascension Conference. The conference was watched by the whole Divine Realm, so the rules had to look fair. The Four Sacred Clans have rules too, but theirs are older, harsher, and full of hidden meaning. Some people won’t be happy that I brought you here.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Then they can dislike me all they want. I’m here to fulfill a promise, not to entertain them.\"","Rose’s lips curved slightly. \"I figured you’d say something like that.\"","She turned to leave, then paused at the entrance of the courtyard.","\"Rest for now. I’ll send you information about the battle once I confirm the final list of participants.\"","Max nodded. \"Go.\"","Rose looked at him one last time before stepping into a silver spatial ripple and disappearing from the courtyard.","The courtyard went quiet.","Max stood alone in the room prepared for him. For a while, he didn’t move. His gaze slowly drifted toward the direction of the ancestral hall, even though it was no longer visible from here. The image of the statue stayed clear in his mind.","The tall man with closed eyes. The calm face. The hand resting near his side. That indescribable presence that didn’t feel like tyranny, divinity, or ordinary supremacy, but something even stranger.","And more importantly, the reaction inside Max’s blood.","The moment he’d seen that statue, several powers inside him had stirred violently. His Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline had reacted. His Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline had trembled. His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline had pulsed. Even the deeper parts of his foundation had shown signs of movement.","That shouldn’t have happened.","Max frowned slightly.","’Why did my blood react like that?’","He couldn’t think of any clear reason. He didn’t know the First Progenitor of the Four Sacred Clans. He’d never heard his name, never seen his face, and never received any inheritance connected to him. Max’s major bloodlines and powers all had known sources.","The Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline came from the Black Dragon side. The Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline came from his mother’s lineage. The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline had just been granted by the Primordial Race. His Dimensional Sovereign Body came from his Dimensional Keeper’s legacy.","None of them should have reacted so strongly to that statue. Unless there was a deeper connection he didn’t know about.","Max stayed silent for a long time. Then he shook his head. There was no point guessing without information.","The Bloodline Legacy Battle would start in a week. Rose had said the forbidden bloodline could only be properly shown inside the clan, and the ancestral statue had already caused a reaction.","As long as he stayed here, there would likely be more chances to uncover the truth.","For now, there was something more practical to handle."]},{"number":1952,"title":"Chapter 1952: A new attack!","paragraphs":["Max walked toward the training chamber. The doors opened automatically, revealing a wide circular space reinforced with countless spatial runes.","The floor was black stone, the walls were layered with silver patterns, and the ceiling held several floating crystals that seemed able to adjust gravity, space pressure, and energy density. It was a solid chamber, especially for a guest room.","But Max didn’t plan to use only this chamber.","He raised his hand. Space rippled. A moment later, Max entered his Dimension of Time.","The world around him changed. The quiet Evercrest room disappeared, replaced by the familiar space where time flowed according to his will. Here, he could think, train, refine, and analyze far more deeply than in the outside world.","The week before the Bloodline Legacy Battle wasn’t long, but for Max, with the Dimension of Time at his disposal, it was enough to prepare a great deal.","He sat cross-legged at the center of the dimension. Soon, his thoughts turned to one battle in particular.","His battle with Revona.","Among all the fights in the Cosmic Ascension Conference, Revona had pushed him into the toughest spot. Damian’s sword had been terrifying. Ervin’s abyss had been dangerous. Orion’s stars had been powerful. Kaiden’s space path had run deep.","But Revona had been different.","Her Void Origin Eyes hadn’t just attacked him. They’d stripped him bare. They’d shut down his powers one after another. Return To Nothing had already been dangerous enough on its own, but Null Origin Tide had been the real problem.","The moment that pale gray tide spread out, Max’s draconic essences, Dragon Scales Transformation, Divine Veins, Divine King Punishment, Devouring Flames Domain, and even his clone’s time concept had all gotten stripped away or suppressed.","His Emotion Severing Path had barely held on, and even that had been weakened to a dangerous degree.","In the end, Max had turned to the Dimensional Keeper legacy. That power had let him stand beyond Revona’s level of nullification, cut through Null Origin Tide, and beat her. But Max didn’t like relying on a power he couldn’t fully control.","The Dimensional Keeper legacy was strong, but it wasn’t something he could call on as naturally as his own sword, bloodline, or Pseudo Cosmic Paths yet. In a real life-or-death fight, leaning on a power that might not answer at the right moment was foolish.","He needed another way. A way to beat Revona’s abilities without leaning on the Dimensional Keeper legacy.","Max closed his eyes. The battle replayed in his mind.","Revona standing calmly in the arena. The Void Origin Eyes opening fully. The Void Origin Realm spreading out. His attacks being traced, hollowed, delayed, and erased. His black flames devouring but never fully consuming Return To Nothing.","His Emotion Severing Path cutting connections, but struggling once her nullification spread out in every direction.","Then the Null Origin Tide. A wave that didn’t target one attack or one technique but flooded the whole battlefield with origin-level nullification. Dodging it wasn’t enough.","Overpowering it with raw force wasn’t enough either. It attacked the very existence of his powers before they could properly take shape.","Max’s thoughts sharpened.","’The problem wasn’t only strength. It was structure.’","Revona’s ability worked because her Void Origin Eyes could identify, trace, and nullify the foundation of whatever they touched.","If Max threw a normal attack, she could hollow it out. If he released a domain, she could weaken its source. If he used bloodline power, she could drag it toward emptiness. Even the Devouring Flames Domain, built for consuming things, still had a definable structure she could target.","In other words, anything clear enough to be understood could be nullified.","That was terrifying. But not unbeatable.","Max started thinking through possible counters.","The first was speed. If he attacked faster than Revona could properly trace, he might land a hit before her nullification finished forming. But against her fully awakened Void Origin Eyes, that wasn’t reliable.","Her perception was too sharp, and her past-life experience made her reactions almost inhuman.","The second was overwhelming force. If his attack went beyond what her current realm could nullify, it would break through.","That was essentially what the Dimensional Keeper legacy had done. But without relying on that legacy, Max needed another source of overwhelming authority. His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline might eventually help, but it was too newly integrated and not yet awake enough to work as a stable counter.","The third was concealment. If Revona couldn’t identify the true source of an attack, her nullification might lose precision. Max had already used the Devouring Flames Domain and a time clone to throw off her Void Origin Eyes, but that had only delayed her. It hadn’t solved the root problem.","The fourth was layering. If one attack carried multiple false structures, false sources, and shifting cores, Revona might end up nullifying the wrong layer first. While she stripped away one part, the true killing intent could slip through along another path. This one had potential.","Max opened his eyes slightly.","’An attack with no fixed origin. A sword strike whose source keeps shifting between bloodline, law, domain, body, emotion, and space.’","His gaze deepened. Revona’s Void Origin Eyes were terrifying because they could trace an attack back to its foundation.","So what if the foundation kept changing every instant? What if the attack carried several foundations at once? What if the visible source was fake, the second source was bait, and the true source only existed at the moment of impact?","Max raised one hand. A faint sword light appeared above his palm. The Emotion Severing Path flowed into it first. Then Divine King Punishment flickered around it as seven-colored lightning. Then the Devouring Flames Domain formed a thin black flame along the edge. Space folded faintly around the sword light.","The first attempt collapsed almost instantly.","Max frowned slightly. The powers rejected each other because their structures were too different. Emotion Severing wanted to cut connection.","Divine King Punishment wanted to judge and punish. Devouring Flames wanted to consume. Space wanted to shift and fold. If he forced them together carelessly, the result would be unstable and easy to read.","That wouldn’t work against Revona.","He let the sword light disperse and tried again. This time, he didn’t combine the powers from the outside. He started from the intent itself.","A sword meant to keep the enemy from locating its true source. A sword meant to keep changing its foundation. A sword meant to survive nullification by never staying one thing long enough to be fully erased.","Max’s expression settled into calm. He had one week outside. Inside the Dimension of Time, that could stretch into much longer.","He didn’t need to finish a perfect counter in one session. He just needed to start forming a path. The next time he faced Revona’s Null Origin Tide, he didn’t want to rely only on the Dimensional Keeper legacy.","He wanted an answer of his own.","Max lifted Dragonheart. His white hair moved slightly in the silent space.","\"Let’s begin.\"","The Dimension of Time filled with sword light."]},{"number":1953,"title":"Chapter 1953: A Week Passed By!","paragraphs":["A week wasn’t much time.","For ordinary people, seven days might feel like enough to rest, think, prepare, and slowly settle into a new environment.","But for someone like Max, who’d just stepped into the heart of the Evercrest Clan, learned the deeper secret behind the Four Sacred Clans, sensed a mysterious reaction from the statue of the First Progenitor, and was about to represent Rose in the Bloodline Legacy Battle, one week went by almost too fast.","Inside the Dimension of Time, though, that week stretched out much longer.","Max spent most of it cultivating, stabilizing, and training.","The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline had fully settled into his body during this stretch.","At first, its presence had felt like a sleeping ancient ocean inside his blood, calm on the surface but unbelievably heavy underneath. Whenever he circulated his power, the bloodline responded with quiet authority, shaping his body, soul, laws, and even his Pseudo Cosmic Paths.","It didn’t clash with his other bloodlines as much as he’d expected. Instead, it seemed to settle at the very top of his foundation, like a supreme framework that could hold everything else together.","By the end of the week, Max had grown fully used to it. His body no longer felt strange when the Primordial Bloodline stirred. His laws no longer trembled when primordial energy flowed through them.","Even his Emotion Severing Path, Divine King Punishment, and Devouring Flames Domain had adapted to the new foundation.","They were still Pseudo Cosmic Paths, still unable to become true Cosmic Paths before the Divine Lord Realm, but they now carried a faint primordial quality that made them deeper and harder to shake loose.","His cultivation rose again too. The breakthrough didn’t come as violently as the jump from the 1st to the 5th level of the Law Refinement Realm, which had been forced along by the leftover integration energy of the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline.","This time, Max advanced through steady accumulation. He used the Dimension of Time to refine his laws, stabilize the new bloodline, digest the energy still sitting in his body, and keep polishing his foundation until the next small barrier loosened on its own.","On the sixth day by the outer world’s count, that barrier broke.","[Breakthrough Achieved.]","[Law Refinement Realm 6th Level.]","Max opened his eyes inside the Dimension of Time and felt the change settle in quietly. His aura hadn’t turned wildly unstable. It had simply grown deeper. The laws flowing around him were more condensed than before, and every movement of his power felt smoother.","The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline circulated more naturally too, no longer like something newly acquired, but like something that had always belonged inside him.","Max didn’t spend the whole week only on cultivation, though. He kept thinking through his battle with Revona too.","Again and again, he replayed the moment Null Origin Tide had stripped his powers away. Again and again, he tested sword structures built to shift their source, hide their foundation, and survive nullification by refusing to stay fixed.","Many attempts failed. Some collapsed instantly. Some turned unstable. Some worked for a moment but lacked real power. Still, every failure taught him something.","By the time the seventh day came, Max hadn’t built a perfect counter to Revona’s Void Origin Eyes, but he’d taken the first real step.","A new sword concept was starting to take shape in his mind. A sword with a layered source. A sword with a shifting foundation. A sword that didn’t fight nullification through raw power alone, but through deception, shifting origin, and momentary truth.","It wasn’t finished yet. But it existed. That was enough for now.","On the seventh day, Max stepped out of the Dimension of Time.","The quiet room prepared for him inside the Evercrest Clan came back into view. The silver spatial runes on the walls glowed faintly, and the training chamber behind him slowly closed.","The magical pond outside rippled beneath the morning wind, while emerald light filtered through the leaves of the massive ancient tree holding up the courtyard.","Rose was already waiting for him. She stood near the entrance of the courtyard, wearing a formal green and silver robe, different from the pale dress she’d worn before.","Her long hair was tied back with an emerald ribbon, and a thin jade ornament hung at her waist, marked with the Evercrest Clan’s insignia. She looked more elegant and dignified than before, but Max could sense the tension hidden beneath her calm face.","The moment she saw him, her eyes sharpened slightly.","\"You got stronger again.\"","Max walked toward her. \"A little.\"","Rose stared at him for a breath. Then she smiled faintly.","\"Only you would call reaching the 6th level of the Law Refinement Realm in one week ’a little.’\"","Max didn’t deny it.","Rose looked at him more closely, and her expression turned a bit more serious. \"Your aura’s different too. The Primordial Bloodline has fully settled?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Good,\" Rose said. \"The Bloodline Legacy Battle starts today. The people from the Four Sacred Clans have already gathered.\"","Max nodded. \"Then let’s go.\"","Rose turned without wasting any more words. The space at the edge of the courtyard opened, forming a path of emerald and silver light. She stepped into it first, and Max followed.","This time, Rose didn’t lead him deeper into the Evercrest Clan. Instead, she took him away from the main sacred territory. The two of them passed through several folded spatial layers, crossed hidden bridges of light, and moved through passages that seemed to curve around the outside of the clan’s core world.","Gradually, the elegant palaces and enormous ancient trees faded behind them. The atmosphere shifted from peaceful and sacred to solemn and ancient.","After a while, the spatial passage opened. Max and Rose stepped out.","Before them stood an arena. It was enormous. Calling it an arena almost felt like an understatement, since it was large enough to hold several cities. The whole structure floated inside a separate spatial field, surrounded by six vast platforms arranged in a grand hexagon.","Each platform was built like its own world facing the central battlefield below. The ground of the battlefield was carved with countless old runes, many so ancient that even Max couldn’t immediately tell what they were for."]},{"number":1954,"title":"Chapter 1954: Start of the Bloodline Legacy Battle!","paragraphs":["At one end of the arena stood the statue of the First Progenitor. It wasn’t the same statue Max had seen in the sealed hall, but it carried the same face, the same posture, and the same strange calmness.","This statue was far larger, standing above one whole end of the arena like a silent judge watching over every descendant of the Four Sacred Clans. Its eyes were closed, its robes carved from dark stone, and its presence made the whole battlefield feel like something more than just a competition ground.","The other four ends belonged to the Four Sacred Clans.","One end belonged to Valerius. It was built from white-gold stone, covered in sunlike patterns and sharp sacred banners.","The people seated there carried proud, brilliant auras, and many wore robes decorated with golden flame-like markings. Their presence was bright, domineering, and noble, as if they’d been born to stand beneath a higher light.","Another end belonged to Ashbourne. Their platform was darker, built from black stone and crimson metal. The aura there was heavy, fierce, and oppressive. Many Ashbourne descendants had sharp eyes and battle-hardened expressions, and even their silence felt like restrained violence.","The third end belonged to Ravenhart. That platform was elegant and mysterious, filled with deep purple banners, black-feathered motifs, and moonlike crystals hanging in the air.","The people there looked calm, strange, and hard to read. Some carried scholarly auras, while others seemed as dangerous as hidden blades.","The fourth end belonged to Evercrest. It was covered in green-gold light, living wood, jade stone, and layered spatial formations.","Max immediately recognized the same refined spatial style he’d seen throughout the Evercrest Clan. The people there wore robes of green, silver, and white, and their gazes turned toward Rose and Max almost instantly when the two of them arrived.","Then there was the sixth end.","It was abandoned. No banners hung there. No clan insignia marked it. The platform sat dark, empty, and silent, covered in broken stone seats and old cracks.","Compared to the other five ends, it looked forgotten, almost deliberately left untouched. Still, Max’s eyes lingered on it longer than he expected.","Something about that abandoned end felt strange. It wasn’t completely dead. It felt like a place kept reserved for something that no longer existed.","Rose noticed where he was looking and said quietly, \"That’s the abandoned end.\"","Max glanced at her. \"Who did it used to belong to?\"","Rose stayed silent for a moment. Then she said, \"That’s not something people talk about during the Bloodline Legacy Battle.\"","Max looked at her calmly and didn’t push it further. He looked around and didn’t see any crowd at that end either. It was suspiciously empty.","’Huh?’ It was then that Max noticed the sixth end wasn’t completely empty after all. There was an old man sitting alone at that end, his eyes closed. ’Very strange.’","There would be time to find out more later.","The arena was already overflowing with people from the Four Sacred Clans. Countless descendants, elders, guardians, representatives, servants, branch family members, and invited observers filled the four clan platforms.","Their voices blended into a deep roar that rolled across the arena like thunder. This battle wasn’t open to the whole Divine Realm the way the Cosmic Ascension Conference had been, but the pressure here was no weaker. In some ways it felt even heavier, since everyone present carried blood ties to one of the oldest, most mysterious human forces in existence.","The moment Rose and Max appeared, plenty of eyes shifted toward them.","At first, some people only looked at Rose. Then they recognized Max. A wave of whispers spread quickly across the Evercrest platform first, then across the other sacred clan ends.","\"That’s Rose.\"","\"She actually came.\"","\"So the castaway descendant dared to use the old rule?\"","\"Who’s the man beside her?\"","\"Are you blind? That’s Max Morgan.\"","\"The champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference?\"","\"The one who beat Revona?\"","\"He got the Primordial Race’s reward, didn’t he?\"","\"Why would someone like him represent Rose?\"","The whispers grew louder. Some people looked shocked. Some looked curious. Some looked unhappy. Some looked openly hostile.","Max ignored all of it.","Rose felt those stares more deeply, though. She kept her back straight and her expression calm, but Max could sense the tension in her breathing. This was the place that had rejected her.","These were the people who’d looked down on her since birth just because she’d been born without the forbidden bloodline. Coming back here under all these eyes wasn’t easy for her, even if she didn’t let it show.","Max walked beside her without changing his pace. That alone made a fair number of people quiet down a little.","Rose led him toward a smaller waiting area beneath the Evercrest end. It wasn’t among the main Evercrest heirs, but on a lower platform set aside for special challengers and castaway descendants invoking old rules.","There weren’t many people there. In fact, Rose seemed to be the only one from Evercrest using that path this time.","The message was clear. She was allowed to take part. But she wasn’t welcome.","As they reached the waiting area, an elder from the Evercrest side looked down at them with cold eyes.","\"Rose Evercrest,\" the elder said, his voice carrying across the lower platform. \"You’ve come back to invoke the castaway challenge right.\"","Rose raised her head and answered calmly, \"Yes.\"","The elder’s gaze moved to Max. \"And this is your chosen representative?\"","\"Yes.\"","The elder narrowed his eyes slightly. Even with his cold expression, he couldn’t deny who Max was.","The young man in front of him wasn’t some ordinary outsider. He was the champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, the genius personally rewarded by the Primordial Race, and someone whose name had already spread across the Divine Realm.","The elder stayed silent for a moment before saying, \"The old rule allows it. But remember, Rose Evercrest, if your representative fails, you’ll bear the consequences yourself.\"","Rose’s hands tightened slightly at her sides. \"I know.\"","The statue of the First Progenitor stood silently at one end. Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest each held their own sacred platforms. The abandoned sixth end stayed empty and dark.","Max looked across the packed arena, sensing the countless powerful auras, hidden bloodline pressures, and hostile stares gathering around them.","The Bloodline Legacy Battle hadn’t even started yet. But the stage was already alive."]},{"number":1955,"title":"Chapter 1955: Strongest Warriors of the Four Sacred Clans!","paragraphs":["Max stood beside Rose on the lower waiting platform beneath the Evercrest end and looked out over the vast arena.","The Bloodline Legacy Battle hadn’t officially started yet, but the pressure from the gathered crowd was already heavy. The Four Sacred Clans didn’t carry the same public noise as the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","Their atmosphere felt different. There were fewer outsiders, fewer excited spectators, and no grand proclamations meant for the whole Divine Realm. Still, the feeling here ran sharper, older, and more suffocating, since everyone present came from bloodlines that had stood at the top of humanity since the earliest eras.","Valerius. Ashbourne. Ravenhart. Evercrest.","Each clan held one end of the arena, and each end carried a completely different aura.","The Valerius platform shone with white-gold brilliance, as if every disciple there had been born beneath a sacred sun.","The Ashbourne platform felt like a silent battlefield soaked in old blood and iron will.","The Ravenhart platform was mysterious and elegant, filled with shadowed gazes and faint purple light.","The Evercrest platform was layered with life, space, and sealed domains, beautiful on the surface but hard to see through.","Max’s gaze moved calmly across those platforms.","Then he asked, \"Who are the strongest participants?\"","Rose seemed to have expected the question. She stood beside him with her hands folded in front of her, her expression composed, though the tension in her eyes hadn’t fully faded.","This arena was full of people who’d once treated her like a discarded descendant. Even without showing weakness, coming back here clearly weighed on her.","\"There are a few people you need to watch closely,\" Rose said. \"The Bloodline Legacy Battle isn’t like an ordinary tournament where everyone fights randomly until one champion comes out on top. The structure changes depending on the number of challengers, representatives, and legacy claims. But the strongest geniuses of the Four Sacred Clans will definitely show up, and if you want to gather enough legacy merit for me, you’ll probably have to beat some of them.\"","Max nodded. \"Tell me.\"","Rose looked toward the Valerius end first.","\"The strongest genius of Valerius this generation is Cassian Valerius.\"","Max followed her gaze.","At the highest row of the Valerius platform, a young man sat with his eyes closed. He wore a white-gold robe embroidered with sun patterns, and even sitting still, he looked wrapped in a faint halo of sacred light.","His hair was golden-white, his posture straight, and the aura around him didn’t spread out wildly. It stayed condensed close to his body, which only made him seem more dangerous.","Rose’s voice turned serious. \"Cassian is known as the Sun-Crowned Heir of Valerius. He awakened the Valerius branch of the forbidden bloodline very young, and his control over sacred solar law is terrifying. Among the younger generation of the Four Sacred Clans, he’s considered one of the most stable and complete fighters. He doesn’t have any obvious weaknesses, and his attacks only get stronger the longer a battle drags on.\"","\"What cultivation level?\" Max asked.","\"Peak of the Law Manifestation Realm.\"","Max didn’t look surprised.","Rose continued, \"Most of the strongest participants sit at that level. The Law Manifestation Realm is a special boundary among the younger generation. Before entering the Divine Lord Realm, a cultivator still counts as part of the younger generation in most supreme forces. But once someone steps into the Divine Lord Realm, their status changes. They stop being treated as a young genius. They get the authority and standing of an elder, or at least a quasi-elder, depending on the force.\"","Max understood right away. \"So battle cultivation is capped at peak Law Manifestation Realm.\"","\"Yes,\" Rose said. \"The Bloodline Legacy Battle exists for descendants and representatives fighting for bloodline opportunities. It’s not built for elders. If Divine Lord Realm cultivators were allowed to join freely, the whole point of the battle would change. So most young genius battles stop at the peak of Law Manifestation Realm. Anyone who breaks through to the Divine Lord Realm usually steps away from this kind of competition and moves into the elder hierarchy.\"","Max looked at Cassian Valerius again. Peak Law Manifestation Realm. That sat several levels above Max’s current position at Law Refinement Realm 6th level. But Max had never cared much about ordinary realm gaps.","During the Cosmic Ascension Conference, he’d fought and beaten monsters standing at the very top of the younger generation while he himself was still only at the peak of the Law Awakening Realm.","Now he’d entered the Law Refinement Realm, gained a Tier 4 Primarch Bloodline, and strengthened every part of his foundation.","Rose knew that too. That was exactly why she’d brought him.","Her gaze moved toward the Ashbourne platform next.","\"The strongest genius of Ashbourne is Draven Ashbourne.\"","Max looked over. On the black and crimson platform, a tall young man stood with his arms crossed. Unlike Cassian, he didn’t sit quietly like a noble heir. He stood out in plain view, wearing dark armor over a simple black battle robe.","His hair was dark red, and his eyes carried a cold brutality that made a lot of people instinctively look away after a moment. Several Ashbourne disciples kept a respectful distance from him, as if they didn’t dare stand too close unless called over.","Rose’s tone grew heavier. \"Draven is called the Blood-Iron Demon of Ashbourne. The Ashbourne branch of the forbidden bloodline is famous for destructive physical power, blood refinement, and battle endurance.","Draven inherited all of that to a terrifying degree. He’s fought a lot of battles outside the public eye, and there are rumors that a few older peak Law Manifestation experts died at his hands even before he reached his current level.\"","\"Peak Law Manifestation Realm?\" Max asked.","\"Yes. But even among peak Law Manifestation Realm geniuses, he’s one of the most dangerous in direct combat. If Rakan Thorne from the War God Palace is a battle maniac with an overwhelming physique, Draven is something darker. He fights to break his opponent, not just beat them.\"","Max’s eyes lingered on Draven for a moment. As if sensing the gaze, Draven Ashbourne turned slightly and looked straight at him. Their eyes met across the arena. Draven didn’t smile. Max didn’t look away.","After a few breaths, Draven’s lips curved faintly, but there was no warmth in it. It was the smile of someone who’d just found a target worth crushing."]},{"number":1956,"title":"Chapter 1956: Sharpening Me!","paragraphs":["Rose noticed and said quietly, \"He’s already noticed you.\"","\"That’s fine,\" Max said.","Rose glanced at him. \"You don’t look worried.\"","\"Should I be?\"","Rose stayed quiet for a moment. Then she sighed lightly. \"I forgot who I was talking to.\"","She looked toward the Ravenhart end next.","\"The strongest genius of Ravenhart is Seraphine Ravenhart.\"","Max’s gaze shifted. The Ravenhart platform was the quietest of the four clan ends, and the people seated there looked far more restrained than the rest. Near the center of the highest seating area sat a young woman in a deep violet dress, her black hair falling over one shoulder like silk.","A faint feather-shaped mark rested between her brows, and her eyes carried a strange shade of silver-purple. She looked gentle at first glance, almost scholarly, but the space around her felt off somehow. The shadows near her chair moved slightly even though there was no wind.","Rose’s expression turned even more cautious. \"Seraphine is probably the hardest one to read. Ravenhart’s forbidden bloodline branch is tied to shadows, prophecy fragments, soul silence, and fate-like perception. No one really knows how much she can actually see. Some say she can predict where a battle is headed several moves before it happens. Some say she doesn’t predict at all, but instead listens to the hidden rhythm of her opponent’s soul.\"","Max raised an eyebrow slightly. \"Soul and prediction abilities.\"","\"Yes. And unlike Draven, who’s dangerous because of his direct brutality, Seraphine is dangerous because you might not even understand how you lost until the battle’s already over. She’s also at the peak of Law Manifestation Realm.\"","Max looked at Seraphine Ravenhart. As if sensing his attention, the young woman slowly turned toward him and smiled. It was a small, polite smile, but Max’s eyes narrowed slightly, because for one instant, it felt like her gaze hadn’t landed on his face at all, but somewhere deeper.","Not deep enough to see his real secrets, but enough to make his soul react faintly.","His Dimension of Soul stirred. The slight probing sensation disappeared right away.","Seraphine’s smile didn’t change, but her eyes flickered with interest.","Rose caught the brief exchange. \"Don’t underestimate her.\"","\"I won’t.\"","Rose then turned toward the Evercrest end.","\"As for Evercrest, the strongest genius is Aelric Evercrest.\"","Max looked up. At the center of the Evercrest platform sat a young man in green and silver robes. Compared to Cassian’s sacred brilliance, Draven’s brutal pressure, and Seraphine’s mysterious calm, Aelric looked more refined and elegant.","His face was handsome, his posture relaxed, and his eyes carried the natural confidence of someone who’d been praised his whole life. A lot of Evercrest descendants sat around him with clear respect, and several elders glanced his way with obvious satisfaction.","Rose’s voice turned colder when she said his name.","\"Aelric awakened the Evercrest forbidden bloodline at a very high purity. He’s considered the strongest Evercrest heir of the current generation. His mastery over space and life-sealing techniques goes way beyond mine. He can fold the battlefield, seal off movement routes, create hidden domains, and use life force itself as a binding tool.\"","Max looked at her. \"You don’t like him.\"","Rose’s expression didn’t shift much, but her eyes turned colder. \"He was one of the people who told me I should be grateful the clan even let me keep the Evercrest name.\"","Max looked at Aelric again.","Aelric had noticed them too. Unlike Draven, he didn’t show open hostility. He just looked down from the higher platform with a faint smile, as if Rose’s return amused him more than it bothered him. His gaze shifted to Max next, and that smile turned slightly more polite, though Max could still feel the pride running underneath it.","Rose continued, \"Aelric is also at the peak of Law Manifestation Realm. Among Evercrest’s younger generation, he’s almost untouchable. Most people believe he’ll eventually inherit one of the clan’s highest positions once he enters the Divine Lord Realm.\"","\"And if I beat him?\" Max asked.","Rose paused, then looked at him.","\"If you beat Aelric in the Bloodline Legacy Battle, the Evercrest Clan loses face, and I gain far more legacy merit than I would from beating an ordinary representative.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Then he’s useful.\"","Rose looked at him for a moment before shaking her head. \"You really do treat them like stepping stones.\"","\"Aren’t they?\"","For a second, Rose didn’t know whether to laugh or sigh.","Then she went on, \"Besides those four, there are other strong participants. Valerius has Lucara Valerius, known for her Sacred Flame Mandate. Ashbourne has Kaelric Ashbourne, Draven’s cousin, who specializes in bone-crushing martial arts and blood armor. Ravenhart has Nox Ravenhart, who’s extremely dangerous in assassination-style fights. Evercrest also has several high-level heirs, including Mirena Evercrest and Solan Evercrest. All of them are at peak Law Manifestation Realm or very close to it.\"","Max asked, \"Are outsiders allowed to represent people too?\"","\"Yes,\" Rose said. \"Several descendants from the Four Sacred Clans have brought in outsiders. Most of them are hidden monsters from ancient forces, supreme guilds, and forbidden training grounds. Some might not be as famous as the top geniuses from the Cosmic Ascension Conference, but don’t assume that means they’re weak. The Four Sacred Clans have enough influence to invite genuinely dangerous people.\"","Max nodded slowly.","Rose looked at him seriously. \"Your fame from the Cosmic Ascension Conference cuts both ways here. On one hand, no one can dismiss you as some ordinary outsider. On the other hand, plenty of them will want to beat you just to prove themselves. Some will see you as the champion of the Divine Realm’s younger generation. Some will see you as the outsider who dared to step onto the sacred clans’ stage. Some will just hate you because you’re representing me.\"","Max’s expression stayed calm. \"That makes things simple.\"","\"How?\"","\"They’ll come to me.\"","Rose looked at him in silence.","Below them, the central battlefield began to glow as the ancient runes woke up one after another. The noise in the arena grew louder. Representatives from the four clans started entering their waiting zones.","Several powerful auras rose up across the platforms, each one belonging to a genius with no intention of staying unnoticed.","Rose took a slow breath.","\"Max, remember this. Most of them are at the peak of Law Manifestation Realm. That’s the highest realm allowed in the true young genius battles. Once someone enters the Divine Lord Realm, they’re considered to have crossed the line between genius and elder. That’s why this battle has so many peak Law Manifestation Realm cultivators. They’re all standing right at the last step before becoming elder-level figures.\"","Max looked out at the arena. Peak Law Manifestation Realm geniuses from the Four Sacred Clans.","Forbidden bloodline inheritors. Ancient clan representatives. Outsider monsters. A battlefield tied to the bloodline legacy of the First Progenitor. And somewhere behind all of it, the mystery of why his own blood had reacted so violently to that statue.","Max’s smile deepened slightly. \"Good.\"","Rose glanced at him. \"You keep saying that.\"","Max kept his gaze fixed on the central battlefield as the runes finished lighting up.","\"The stronger they are, the more useful they’ll be.\"","Rose’s eyes shifted slightly. \"Useful for what?\"","Max’s gaze stayed locked on the arena.","\"For sharpening me.\""]},{"number":1957,"title":"Chapter 1957: Bloodline Legacy Battle Begins!","paragraphs":["The central battlefield finished lighting up.","Ancient runes spread across the vast arena floor one after another, forming a web of golden, crimson, purple, green, silver, and black light.","Each color linked faintly to one of the powers gathered there, but the whole formation ultimately pointed toward the towering statue of the First Progenitor standing at one end of the arena.","The statue’s closed eyes stayed silent, yet once the runes fully woke up, the entire arena felt like it had come under that ancient ancestor’s watch.","The noise from the four sacred clan platforms slowly faded. Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest all turned their attention to the central battlefield.","Even the abandoned sixth end of the arena seemed darker and quieter than before, sitting apart from the other five like a forgotten wound in this grand sacred place.","Then space shimmered above the battlefield. A woman stepped out.","She wore a white-gold robe marked with the Valerius insignia, and her long golden hair fell behind her like flowing sunlight. Her face was beautiful, dignified, and familiar. The moment Max saw her, his eyes shifted slightly.","Angelina Valerius.","She had presided over the Cosmic Ascension Conference. Back then, she’d stood above the Eternal Hourglass as the announcer and judge, calmly watching the greatest geniuses of the Divine Realm clash one after another. Now she’d appeared here again, not as a representative of the conference, but as a member of the Valerius Clan, one of the Four Sacred Clans.","The moment Angelina arrived, many younger members of the Four Sacred Clans straightened up instinctively. Her status was clearly not low.","She descended slowly toward the center of the battlefield, her robe moving gently despite the absence of wind. The white-gold light around her wasn’t oppressive, but it carried a natural authority that made people listen.","When her feet touched the arena floor, the surrounding runes brightened once before settling back down.","Angelina looked around the whole arena. Her gaze passed over the Valerius platform, the Ashbourne platform, the Ravenhart platform, the Evercrest platform, the statue of the First Progenitor, and finally the lower challenger areas where Rose and Max stood.","For a brief instant, her eyes lingered on Max. A faint smile crossed her lips. Then she looked away and spoke.","\"Descendants of Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest. Representatives chosen by bloodline claimants. Elders and witnesses of the Four Sacred Clans. Today, the Bloodline Legacy Battle begins.\"","Her voice was clear, steady, and carried through every corner of the arena. The already solemn atmosphere grew heavier.","\"This battle is held under the authority of the First Progenitor’s legacy and witnessed by the Four Sacred Clans. Every descendant who seeks legacy merit, every representative who fights on behalf of a claimant, and every challenger who steps onto this battlefield must accept the ancient rules of the Bloodline Legacy Battle.\"","Angelina raised one hand. A massive circular projection appeared above the battlefield, showing the rules laid out through ancient script.","\"The rules are simple.\" Her gaze swept over everyone. \"Anyone may challenge anyone.\"","The arena stirred. Even though many people already knew the rules, hearing them announced officially still sent a wave of tension through the crowd.","Angelina continued, \"There are no fixed brackets, no arranged order, and no protection from being challenged because of reputation, bloodline, clan, or status. If you stand as a participant in the Bloodline Legacy Battle, you may challenge another participant, and another participant may challenge you.\"","Her voice sharpened slightly. \"If the challenged party refuses without a valid reason recognized by the battle formation, they’ll lose legacy merit and face a penalty based on their claim level. If they accept, both sides enter combat under the protection of the arena laws.\"","She then pointed toward the First Progenitor statue.","\"The battle continues until no one dares challenge the standing victor, or until one participant remains undefeated after all others have either lost, withdrawn, or refused to continue.\"","The projection above the arena shifted, showing a single figure standing beneath the statue while everyone else stood below.","\"That person will become the winner of the Bloodline Legacy Battle.\"","The arena went silent. It was a brutal rule, simple, direct, and merciless. There was no hiding behind brackets, no dodging powerful opponents through luck, and no waiting for others to eliminate the dangerous ones. Anyone who wanted merit had to fight.","Anyone who wanted to prove themselves had to step forward. Anyone who wanted the final victory had to stand where everyone could challenge them and still come out undefeated.","Rose quietly clenched her hands. This rule was exactly why the Bloodline Legacy Battle was so hard for someone like her.","A castaway descendant could only rely on a representative, and that representative had to be strong enough not just to win one battle, but to keep standing as stronger and stronger enemies kept showing up.","Max, on the other hand, smiled faintly. This kind of rule suited him.","Angelina lowered her hand.","\"The use of killing techniques is allowed, but deliberate killing after victory has already been decided is forbidden. The arena formation will suppress fatal intent only after one side has lost the ability to continue or has admitted defeat. Before that point, every participant has to protect themselves with their own strength.\"","Several young geniuses narrowed their eyes. This meant the battles would be dangerous, not staged sparring or symbolic exchanges. Real battles.","Angelina’s gaze swept across the participant areas.","\"The Bloodline Legacy Battle now begins.\"","The moment those words fell, the whole arena erupted. The crowd from the Four Sacred Clans released a wave of noise that rolled across the battlefield like thunder. Clan descendants started looking at one another.","Representatives straightened their backs. Several powerful auras rose from the waiting zones, each one carrying challenge, pride, and killing intent. Plenty of people had already picked their targets before the battle even started.","But before anyone else could move, Max stepped forward. He didn’t say anything at first. He just walked towards the arena."]},{"number":1958,"title":"Chapter 1958: Max’s First Challenge!","paragraphs":["From the lower Evercrest challenger platform, Max moved toward the central battlefield with calm steps. His white hair shifted gently in the wind stirred up by the arena formation, and his black robe carried no sacred clan insignia.","Next to the clan heirs wearing robes marked by Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest, he looked like a total outsider.","Yet the moment he entered the arena, every eye turned toward him. The noise started to fade. It didn’t vanish all at once. It rolled down slowly, section by section, platform by platform, until the whole massive arena grew quieter than before.","Max Morgan. The champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference. The man who’d defeated Revona, Damian Voss, Ervin, Orion Starfall, Kaiden Voidmere, Rakan Thorne, Aurelian Lareth, and every other opponent placed before him.","The strongest genius of the Divine Realm’s younger generation. Even inside the Four Sacred Clans, his name had already spread everywhere.","Some looked curious. Some looked excited. Some looked displeased. Some looked hostile. The younger descendants of the Four Sacred Clans had pride carved into their bones. They didn’t easily accept an outsider being called the strongest genius of the Divine Realm, especially not on their own sacred stage.","But none of them could deny what Max had actually accomplished. The Cosmic Ascension Conference had been watched by countless forces, and his perfect record had already become impossible to ignore.","Angelina watched him approach with a smile that carried both familiarity and interest. When Max stopped at the center of the battlefield, she looked at him and asked, \"Max Morgan. You’re the first to enter the arena. Who do you wish to challenge?\"","The arena grew even quieter. Plenty of people leaned forward.","Rose stood beneath the Evercrest end, her chest tightening despite herself. She knew Max wouldn’t shy away from strong opponents, but she hadn’t expected him to step forward before anyone else. In this kind of battle, the first challenger naturally drew the most attention. It was bold, arrogant, and dangerous.","Max looked across the four sacred clan platforms. His gaze didn’t stop on Valerius. It didn’t stop on Ashbourne. It didn’t stop on Ravenhart. It moved straight to Evercrest.","Above the Evercrest platform, several expressions shifted. Aelric Evercrest sat calmly among the main heirs, his posture relaxed and his expression faintly amused. When Max’s gaze landed on him, his smile deepened slightly, as if he’d already guessed what might happen but still found it entertaining.","Then Max raised his hand and pointed directly at Aelric Evercrest.","\"I challenge him.\"","The arena fell silent. For one breath, no one reacted. Then the entire Evercrest platform stirred violently.","\"What?\"","\"He challenged Aelric directly?\"","\"Is he insane?\"","\"He’s Rose’s representative, and the first person he challenges is the strongest heir of Evercrest?\"","\"He didn’t pick a weaker opponent to build up merit first?\"","\"He went straight for Aelric?\"","The shock spread beyond Evercrest. Valerius descendants looked surprised. Ashbourne descendants grinned with interest. Ravenhart descendants narrowed their eyes, sensing the battle had turned interesting far sooner than they’d expected. Even some elders traded glances.","Rose stared at Max from below, her eyes widening slightly. She’d expected him to target Aelric eventually, since beating him would bring huge legacy merit. She’d even hoped it would happen after Max won a few smaller battles and built up some momentum.","But Max hadn’t waited. He’d chosen Aelric as his very first challenge.","On the Evercrest platform, the elder who’d warned Rose earlier frowned deeply. \"Audacious.\"","Another Evercrest elder’s expression turned cold. \"An outsider steps onto our sacred stage and challenges Aelric directly?\"","Some younger Evercrest descendants looked furious, but others looked uneasy. After all, the challenger wasn’t some unknown fool. It was Max Morgan.","Aelric himself didn’t stand up right away. He looked down at Max from the higher platform with that same refined smile.","\"Max Morgan,\" he said, his voice carrying smoothly across the arena, \"I didn’t expect you to pick me so quickly.\"","Max looked at him calmly. \"Rose needs merit.\"","Aelric’s eyes drifted toward Rose for a moment. His smile turned slightly colder. \"So this is for her.\"","\"Yes.\"","The simplicity of Max’s answer made the mood even heavier.","Aelric slowly stood. The moment he rose, the Evercrest platform quieted down. The green-gold light around him stirred, and faint spatial ripples appeared beneath his feet. His aura didn’t burst out violently, but the space around him folded gently, as if the world itself were clearing a path for him.","Rose’s expression turned tense. \"Aelric,\" she whispered.","Max had already heard everything she’d told him about him. The strongest genius of the Evercrest Clan’s current generation.","A direct heir who’d awakened the Evercrest forbidden bloodline at high purity. A master of space, life-sealing techniques, hidden domains, and battlefield control. A peak Law Manifestation Realm cultivator.","Aelric stepped down from the Evercrest platform. He didn’t fly in the normal sense. He walked through folded space, appearing closer with each step until he stood inside the central battlefield across from Max. His robes moved softly, and his refined face carried calm pride.","Angelina looked between them. \"Aelric Evercrest,\" she said. \"You’ve been challenged by Max Morgan, representative of Rose Evercrest. Do you accept?\"","Aelric smiled. \"How could I refuse?\"","The formation beneath the battlefield brightened instantly. A circular boundary rose around the arena, cutting Max and Aelric off from the outside world.","The runes on the floor began rotating slowly, and the statue of the First Progenitor at the far end seemed to grow more solemn under the shifting light.","Angelina stepped back. \"Then the first battle of the Bloodline Legacy Battle shall begin.\"","Aelric looked at Max with calm eyes.","\"Champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference,\" he said softly. \"You may have dominated the conference, but this isn’t the Eternal Hourglass. This is the sacred stage of the Four Sacred Clans.\"","Max held out his hand. Dragonheart appeared. The black sword let out a low hum, and the moment it settled into his grip, Max’s aura changed.","He looked at Aelric and smiled faintly. \"Then show me what makes this stage different.\""]},{"number":1959,"title":"Chapter 1959: Max vs Aelric Evercrest!","paragraphs":["The formation beneath the central battlefield kept brightening as Max and Aelric stood facing each other.","The first battle of the Bloodline Legacy Battle had already been decided before anyone else even got the chance to move. Max Morgan, the champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference and Rose Evercrest’s chosen representative, had stepped into the arena first and challenged Aelric Evercrest directly.","To outsiders, it looked like arrogance. To the Evercrest Clan, it looked like provocation. To Rose, it was both a dangerous gamble and the fastest path to the legacy merit she needed.","Aelric Evercrest stood across from Max with his hands behind his back, his green and silver robe stirring gently as faint spatial ripples flowed around him. He didn’t draw a weapon. He didn’t release his aura right away. Instead, he looked at Max with a faint sneer.","\"Show me what I have got? Don’t make laugh,\" Aelric said, his voice smooth but cold enough to carry across the battlefield, \"don’t think too highly of yourself just because you won the Cosmic Ascension Conference.\"","The moment he spoke, the whole arena quieted a little. Plenty of people from the Four Sacred Clans narrowed their eyes with interest. Aelric’s words weren’t just aimed at Max. They also voiced what a lot of sacred clan geniuses secretly felt.","The Cosmic Ascension Conference had been grand, and Max’s win had shaken the Divine Realm, but the Four Sacred Clans hadn’t actually sent their strongest hidden heirs into that stage. To them, the conference mattered, but it hadn’t fully represented the deepest strength the sacred clans held.","Aelric continued, \"The Divine Realm might call you the strongest genius of this generation, but that title only stuck because the stage you stood on was incomplete.\"","Rose’s expression turned colder. On the Evercrest platform, several young descendants smiled faintly, clearly pleased with Aelric’s words.","Aelric kept his eyes fixed on Max. \"If the geniuses of the Four Sacred Clans had taken part in the Cosmic Ascension Conference, things would’ve gone differently. Do you really think you’d have walked away with twenty-four wins and no losses if Cassian Valerius, Draven Ashbourne, Seraphine Ravenhart, or I had stood across from you inside the Eternal Hourglass?\"","A wave of murmurs moved through the arena. The Valerius platform stayed dignified, but several descendants there looked toward Cassian with pride. The Ashbourne platform burst into a few low laughs, as if they were already picturing Draven tearing through the so-called conference champion.","The Ravenhart side stayed quiet, but plenty of silver-purple eyes watched Max carefully, waiting to see how he’d respond. The Evercrest side was the loudest, since Aelric’s words had directly defended their pride.","\"Being called the strongest genius of the Divine Realm without ever facing the sacred clans’ strongest heirs,\" Aelric said, his sneer deepening, \"is almost funny.\"","Max listened calmly. He didn’t get angry. He didn’t release any killing intent. He didn’t bother pointing out that he’d defeated Revona, Damian Voss, Ervin, Orion Starfall, Kaiden Voidmere, and countless other top geniuses.","He also didn’t remind Aelric that the Primordial Race itself had acknowledged his victory, granted him the champion’s highest reward, and chosen him above everyone else.","He only smiled. That smile was light, almost casual. And somehow that casualness made Aelric’s expression turn colder.","Max looked at him and said, \"Are you done?\"","The arena went quiet again. Aelric’s eyes narrowed.","Max continued, \"You’ve already said the Four Sacred Clans are stronger. You’ve said the Cosmic Ascension Conference was incomplete. You’ve said things would’ve gone differently if you’d taken part.\"","His smile stayed exactly the same. \"Now show me.\"","The words were simple, but they hit harder than any angry outburst would have.","Aelric’s sneer froze slightly.","Max raised Dragonheart and let the black blade rest casually at his side.","\"Show your strength instead of just talking.\"","For a breath, the battlefield went completely silent. Then the Ashbourne platform burst into laughter.","\"Hahaha! Good!\"","\"That outsider’s got some nerve!\"","\"Talking’s useless. Fight if you’re strong!\"","Even a few Ravenhart descendants smiled faintly, while the Valerius side watched with more interest than before. On the Evercrest platform, plenty of expressions turned ugly. Aelric was their strongest heir of the current generation, and Max had just brushed off his words in front of all Four Sacred Clans.","Rose stood below the Evercrest end and quietly let out a breath she hadn’t realized she’d been holding. This was Max. He didn’t need speeches to defend his title. He only needed his sword.","Aelric looked at Max for a long moment. The faint sneer slowly faded from his face, replaced by a cold, elegant smile.","\"Very well,\" Aelric said. \"Since you’re so eager to see the difference between the Cosmic Ascension Conference and the sacred clans’ stage, I’ll show you.\"","His aura finally began to rise. The green-gold light around him deepened. At first it looked gentle, almost beautiful, like the vitality of an ancient forest waking up under sunlight.","But the next moment, that beauty turned strange. Space around Aelric folded in layers. The air split into faint transparent surfaces, each one reflecting a different angle of the battlefield. Thin threads of life force spread out from beneath his feet and sank into the arena floor, merging with the runes as if trying to claim the battlefield for himself.","The pressure of peak Law Manifestation Realm came down over the arena. It was powerful, far stronger than what ordinary young geniuses could put out. Aelric hadn’t exaggerated about being one of the strongest heirs of the Four Sacred Clans.","His cultivation sat at the peak of Law Manifestation Realm, and his forbidden bloodline had clearly pushed his foundation past normal limits. The moment his aura spread, plenty of ordinary descendants in the arena felt their chests tighten.","Rose’s expression turned tense. \"Aelric’s Evercrest bloodline,\" she whispered.","Max’s eyes stayed calm. His Dimensional Sovereign Body immediately picked up on the shifts in space around him. Aelric wasn’t just releasing aura. He was quietly folding the battlefield into layers, getting ready to turn the arena into a domain that favored him.","The life force threads sinking into the ground weren’t harmless either. They were anchors. Once enough of them spread, Aelric would likely be able to seal off movement, redirect attacks, and restrict space itself.","Max smiled slightly. \"As expected, you’re better when you stop talking.\"","Aelric’s gaze turned colder. \"Let’s see how long your arrogance lasts.\"","Angelina Valerius, who’d stepped back to the edge of the battlefield, raised her hand. The formation between Max and Aelric lit up fully. Her voice rang across the arena.","\"First battle of the Bloodline Legacy Battle.\"","\"Max Morgan, representative of Rose Evercrest, against Aelric Evercrest of the Evercrest Clan.\"","She lowered her hand. \"Begin.\""]},{"number":1960,"title":"Chapter 1960: The Profound Primordial Bloodline!","paragraphs":["The moment the word fell, Aelric vanished. Not through speed. Through folded space. One moment he stood across the battlefield.","The next, his figure appeared above Max’s left side, his palm already coming down with a green-gold seal forming at its center. The seal was made from life force and spatial law, and the moment it appeared, the air around Max tightened, as if an invisible cage had closed around him.","\"Evercrest Life-Sealing Palm.\"","Aelric’s voice came from above, calm and cold. The palm descended.","But Max didn’t step back. His eyes sharpened. The Dimensional Sovereign Body activated silently. The cage around him twisted.","Then Max raised Dragonheart and slashed upward. A black sword light cut through the sealed air, meeting Aelric’s palm seal head on.","Boom!","The first collision exploded across the battlefield. Green-gold light and black sword aura spread out in every direction, striking the arena boundary hard enough to make the runes flash violently.","Aelric’s figure got pushed back half a step in the folded space, while Max stayed right where he’d been standing, his sword raised and his white hair moving under the shockwave.","The whole arena went quiet.","Aelric’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Max lowered Dragonheart and looked at him. \"Is that all?\"","The question came out calm. But to everyone listening, it sounded far more arrogant than anything Aelric had said.","The first collision had only been a greeting.","Aelric understood that the moment Max cut through his Evercrest Life-Sealing Palm. The refined smile on his face finally disappeared completely, and the green-gold light around his body grew much denser than before.","The space around him folded layer after layer, while threads of life force spread out from beneath his feet and sank deep into the battlefield. He no longer looked like a noble heir casually teaching an outsider a lesson. He looked like the strongest Evercrest genius of his generation, getting ready to protect his pride in front of all Four Sacred Clans.","\"Good,\" Aelric said coldly. \"At least you’re not completely unworthy of your reputation.\"","Max lowered Dragonheart slightly. \"You’re still talking.\"","Aelric’s eyes went cold. The next instant, his aura erupted fully.","Peak Law Manifestation Realm pressure swept across the battlefield like a storm. The central arena trembled as the green-gold light around him expanded, forming a massive domain of folded space and ancient vitality.","Layers of transparent space appeared around Max from every direction, each one reflecting Aelric’s figure. In one reflection, Aelric stood above him. In another, he stood behind him. In another, he stood a thousand meters away. In another, he was already striking toward Max’s heart.","The whole battlefield turned uncertain.","\"Evercrest Hidden Domain,\" Rose muttered from the lower platform, her expression turning solemn. \"He’s getting serious now.\"","The Evercrest platform erupted with excitement.","\"Aelric’s using the Hidden Domain!\"","\"That outsider is finished.\"","\"Once Evercrest’s space layers close around him, even a peak Law Manifestation Realm opponent can’t find the real way out.\"","\"Max Morgan might be strong, but this isn’t the Cosmic Ascension Conference. This is Evercrest’s sacred field.\"","Aelric raised both hands. The countless reflections moved with him.","\"Let me show you the difference between an outsider and a sacred clan heir.\"","The transparent layers of space around Max suddenly collapsed inward. At the same time, green-gold vines made of life force burst out of the floor. They didn’t grow like ordinary plants.","They appeared out of different folded spaces, bypassing normal distance entirely, and wrapped toward Max’s limbs, sword arm, neck, and chest. Each vine carried sealing power, and every spatial layer around him tried to lock down his movement from a different angle.","Aelric wasn’t holding back anymore. He wanted to crush Max completely.","Max stood still and watched the storm coming at him. His Dimensional Sovereign Body could track the path of each folded layer. He could sense where the real Aelric hid and where the false reflections stood. But this time, Max didn’t counter with space right away. He wanted to test something else.","His Primordial Bloodline stirred. A faint ancient pulse spread out from inside him. It was quiet. But the moment it moved, the laws around Max changed.","His eyes sharpened slightly. The world felt closer.","That was the first sensation. It wasn’t that Max’s understanding had suddenly grown in some ordinary way. It felt like the laws of the world, which normally sat around him like distant rivers, had suddenly pulled in close to his skin.","Space, lightning, flame, emotion, sword, vitality, resistance, body, soul, and every trace of law on the battlefield became clearer.","The Primordial Bloodline didn’t force these laws under its control like a tyrant. It made Max feel like he naturally belonged closer to the source they all flowed from.","Then power surged through him. Not as an ability. Not as a technique. As direct enhancement.","His body, soul, law affinity, and foundation all rose at once. Ten times over. Max felt it clearly.","Just activating the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline pushed his strength to ten times his normal state.","This worked completely differently from his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline and his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. Those bloodlines gave him powerful abilities, transformations, bloodline techniques, light authority, chaotic dragon force, and other tools he could use to boost his combat power under the right circumstances.","But they didn’t directly multiply his base strength the moment they stirred.","The Primordial Bloodline did. It was simple. Terrifyingly simple.","His strength increased. His control increased. His closeness to the laws increased. His foundation grew heavier. His Pseudo Cosmic Paths, already refined far beyond their original state, suddenly turned ten times stronger under this primordial condition.","The Emotion Severing Path became sharper, as if every invisible connection in the world had drawn closer to the edge of his sword.","Divine King Punishment became more majestic, as if the thunder tribunal behind it had gained deeper authority.","The Devouring Flames Domain turned darker and more controlled, as if the black flames could now bite closer to the source of whatever they consumed.","Max’s heart stirred faintly.","’This bloodline still isn’t fully awake.’","That much was unmistakable. The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline had only started showing its surface. Even this tenfold boost wasn’t the full potential of the bloodline. It was only the most basic expression of the Primarch-level foundation resting inside him."]},{"number":1961,"title":"Chapter 1961: Evercrest Forbidden Art!","paragraphs":["Max closed his hand around Dragonheart. At the same time, the Seven Divine Veins inside his body began to open.","One. The Vein of Origin opened, stabilizing his foundation and making his whole body feel like a world-rooted vessel.","Two. The Vein of Vitality opened, flooding his flesh, blood, and organs with terrifying life force.","Three. The Vein of Speed opened, sharpening his movement and reactions until the whole battlefield seemed to slow down.","Four. The Vein of Strength opened, sending his physical power surging upward.","Then came the fifth. The Vein of Resilience opened.","This was the vein Max had opened over the past few days inside the Dimension of Time. Unlike the Vein of Strength, which boosted his destructive power, or the Vein of Speed, which sharpened his movement, the Vein of Resilience strengthened the durability of his body to a terrifying degree.","It hardened his flesh, bones, organs, meridians, and even the defensive resistance of his inner foundation. It boosted his resistance against every kind of attack, whether physical, elemental, spiritual, law-based, bloodline-based, sealing-based, or pressure-based.","The moment the Vein of Resilience opened, Max’s body turned into something like an indestructible divine mountain wrapped in living law.","The green-gold vines reached him first. They wrapped around his arms, shoulders, waist, and legs. Then they tightened. The spatial layers collapsed inward at the same time.","For a brief instant, the Evercrest platform smiled. Then their smiles froze.","Max stood there without moving. The vines tightened with enough force to crush an ordinary peak Law Manifestation Realm cultivator, and the folded space pressed down on him like overlapping worlds.","Yet Max’s body didn’t bend. His bones didn’t creak. His flesh didn’t tear.","The sealing force pushed into his body, but the Vein of Resilience held it back like an ancient wall. The life-sealing power tried to sink into his blood, but his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline burned quietly and pushed it right back out.","Max looked at the vines around him. Then he moved his arm.","Crack.","A vine snapped. Then another. Then ten. The entire binding formation shattered, as if it had wrapped itself around something it was never meant to hold.","Aelric’s expression changed.","Max took one step forward. The folded space beneath his foot cracked. The entire Evercrest Hidden Domain trembled.","Aelric immediately shifted his hand seals, and countless spatial mirrors around the battlefield fired green-gold beams at Max.","Each beam carried life-sealing power and spatial compression. Some went for his body. Some targeted his movement route. Some tried to seal Dragonheart. Some aimed at his aura circulation.","Max only raised his sword. The Emotion Severing Path flowed into Dragonheart. But now, under the influence of the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline, this power worked completely differently from before.","The severing aura became colder, cleaner, and frighteningly close to the true essence of law. It didn’t just cut the beams. It cut the connections holding them together.","One slash. The green-gold beams collapsed.","Another slash. The spatial mirrors cracked.","A third slash. The Evercrest Hidden Domain split open in front of him.","Aelric retreated through folded space, but Max moved at almost the same instant. With the Vein of Speed active and the Primordial Bloodline boosting him tenfold, Max’s speed was terrifying. He crossed the broken spatial layers before Aelric could fully reposition himself.","Dragonheart came down. Aelric raised both palms and formed a green-gold barrier.","\"Evercrest Worldwood Guard!\"","A vast tree silhouette appeared behind him, its branches spreading out like a defensive sky. The barrier held both life force and folded space, making it hard to break through with a normal attack. But Max’s blade carried more than just strength. It carried severing authority.","The sword struck.","Boom!","The Worldwood Guard split from top to bottom. Aelric got thrown backward, his feet tearing across the battlefield as he coughed up a mouthful of blood.","The whole arena fell silent.","The Evercrest descendants stared in disbelief. Aelric had used his full strength. He’d opened the Evercrest Hidden Domain, used life-sealing vines, spatial mirrors, and the Worldwood Guard.","Every one of those techniques was strong enough to beat most peak Law Manifestation Realm geniuses on its own. Yet Max had broken through all of them almost casually after activating his new state.","Rose looked at Max with wide eyes. She’d known he was strong. Everyone knew he was strong. But this was different. Max sat only at the 6th level of the Law Refinement Realm, yet after activating the Primordial Bloodline and five Divine Veins, he was overpowering Aelric Evercrest, a peak Law Manifestation Realm sacred clan heir, in front of all Four Sacred Clans.","Aelric slowly stood back up. His refined appearance had finally been ruined. Blood stained the corner of his mouth, and several cuts had opened across his robe. His eyes were no longer calm. They carried anger, disbelief, and humiliation.","\"You...\"","He clenched his fists. The space behind him began to twist violently.","\"You think you can beat me that easily?\"","The green-gold light around Aelric erupted again, far stronger than before. This time, the entire battlefield reacted. The runes beneath the arena flashed repeatedly, and the hidden spatial layers of the Evercrest end resonated with him.","Aelric placed both hands in front of his chest, and a mark appeared between his brows. It was leaf-shaped, but it wasn’t gentle. It looked like a blade.","Rose’s face changed. \"He’s using the forbidden bloodline mark.\"","The Evercrest platform turned serious. Several elders leaned forward.","Aelric’s aura climbed again, and a massive tree formed behind him. This tree looked nothing like the defensive silhouette from before. It was ancient, enormous, and dark green, its branches stretching into folded space and its roots piercing into the battlefield.","Every root carried life-sealing power. Every branch held a spatial domain. Every leaf shone with runes that could tear, bind, seal, or redirect power.","Aelric’s voice rang across the arena.","\"Evercrest Forbidden Art.\"","\"Ancestor Wood Seals the Ten Thousand Spaces.\"","The whole arena shook. The massive tree behind him expanded so fast it looked ready to swallow the entire battlefield. Branches pierced into space and pulled out layers of hidden domains.","Roots spread across the arena floor and locked down every movement path. Countless green-gold seals appeared in the air, forming a cage so vast and complex that even the audience outside the battlefield felt suffocated."]},{"number":1962,"title":"Chapter 1962: Shocked Max!","paragraphs":["This was Aelric’s strongest attack. A forbidden art powered by his Evercrest bloodline. It didn’t just attack the opponent. It tried to seal the entire battlefield, fold every direction, bind every escape route, and crush the enemy beneath the combined weight of space and life.","Moreover, this was also his pseudo cosmic path. His pseudo cosmic path was so strong that it couldn’t be utilized without using an external technique or having an external source of power.","The arena formation trembled under the pressure. Even Angelina Valerius narrowed her eyes slightly. The people of Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest all fell silent. No one had expected Aelric to be forced into using such a powerful attack in the very first battle.","Max looked at the enormous sealing tree descending toward him. The pressure was strong, far stronger than anything Aelric had used earlier.","The entire battlefield seemed to turn into a cage, and every part of that cage was closing in around Max. If he’d been an ordinary genius, even a peak Law Manifestation Realm genius, this attack could have decided the battle instantly.","But Max wasn’t ordinary.","His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline pulsed again. The laws around him drew even closer. The five Divine Veins inside him blazed with power.","The Vein of Origin. The Vein of Vitality. The Vein of Speed. The Vein of Strength. The Vein of Resilience. His body turned stable, full of life, fast, powerful, and nearly unbreakable.","The Vein of Resilience resisted the sealing pressure trying to push into his body. The Vein of Strength drove terrifying force into his arms. The Vein of Speed sharpened his reaction to every closing spatial layer. The Vein of Vitality kept his blood and flesh in perfect condition. The Vein of Origin anchored everything together.","Then Max raised Dragonheart. This time, he didn’t rely on the Emotion Severing Path alone. Divine King Punishment descended. Seven-colored lightning wrapped around the blade, forming the faint image of a divine tribunal above him.","At the same time, the Devouring Flames Domain condensed into black fire along the sword edge. The Emotion Severing Path flowed through the center, turning the slash into a blade that could cut through more than matter alone. It could cut connection, sealing roots, law threads, and the very structure holding Aelric’s forbidden art together.","Under the boost from the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline, all three Pseudo Cosmic Paths became terrifying. Ten times stronger. Ten times sharper. Ten times closer to the laws they represented.","Max’s white hair moved in the storm of green-gold light. He stepped forward. The arena shook.","Aelric roared, \"Seal him!\"","The enormous ancestor tree descended.","Max swung Dragonheart. \"Break.\"","One word. One slash. A black, seven-colored, and invisible sword light tore across the battlefield.","The slash cut through the first layer of space. Then the second. Then the third. The roots of the ancestor tree were severed from the battlefield. The branches lost their connection to the folded domains.","The life-sealing runes were judged by Divine King Punishment and shattered under seven-colored lightning. The black flames devoured the loosened power. The Emotion Severing Path cut through the final structure holding the forbidden art together.","For a moment, the entire arena turned silent. Then the massive tree split apart.","Boom!","The explosion shook the arena violently. Green-gold light scattered like broken stars. Spatial layers collapsed one after another.","The sealing roots snapped across the battlefield, and the runes beneath the arena flashed madly to suppress the aftershock. Even the four sacred clan platforms felt the vibration under their feet.","Aelric stood frozen behind the collapsing forbidden art. His eyes went wide. He couldn’t believe it. His strongest attack had been broken. Not avoided. Not delayed. Broken straight from the front.","Max appeared before him through the storm of shattered light. Aelric tried to raise his hand, but Max was faster. Dragonheart stopped at Aelric’s throat. The black blade touched his skin lightly, and a thin line of blood appeared.","Aelric’s body stiffened. The battlefield went completely silent.","Max looked at him calmly. \"You lose.\"","Aelric’s face turned pale. The strongest Evercrest heir of the current generation had been defeated. Not after a long battle. Not after exhausting Max. Defeated cleanly, in front of the statue of the First Progenitor, before the eyes of Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest.","For several breaths, no one spoke. Then Angelina Valerius’s voice rang across the arena.","\"Aelric Evercrest is defeated.\"","She looked at Max, and even her eyes carried a trace of amazement.","\"Winner, Max Morgan.\"","Angelina’s eyes remained on Max for several moments. She could feel that Max had grown way stronger than what he was at during the Cosmic Ascension Conference.","’Is it the Primordial Race bloodline?’ She wondered. Though she wasn’t certain if it was only the Primordial Race bloodline or something else was boosting Max’s power.","The entire arena erupted. The Evercrest platform filled with disbelief and humiliation. The Ashbourne side burst into excited laughter.","The Valerius side turned solemn. The Ravenhart descendants watched Max with eyes that had grown far more serious. Rose stood on the lower platform, staring at the scene with emotions she couldn’t fully hide.","Max lowered Dragonheart. His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline slowly quieted down. The five Divine Veins closed one after another. The tenfold strength faded, but the memory of that power stayed inside him like a promise.","He could feel it clearly. This was only the beginning of the Primordial Bloodline’s power. He hadn’t even unlocked its true potential yet.","But more than that, something else about the fight had left Max troubled. All through the battle with Aelric, he kept sensing that Aelric’s bloodline felt strangely familiar, and the more Aelric drew on it, the more Max felt something stirring inside himself in response.","By the very end, Max finally realized what part of him had been reacting to Aelric’s bloodline.","What he found shocked him to his core.","Even more than that, it left him with a flood of questions, questions he had no way of answering yet."]},{"number":1963,"title":"Chapter 1963: A Connection!","paragraphs":["Aelric’s bloodline, Max’s own bloodline, and the statue were somehow connected. That much was obvious from the fight itself. But the question was how.","What truly disturbed Max wasn’t the connection itself. It was the way his own blood had responded to it.","The moment Aelric’s forbidden bloodline mark appeared, something inside Max’s foundation had stirred again. Not just the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline. Not just the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline or the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline. Something deeper had reacted, something that didn’t clearly belong to any bloodline he could name.","It felt like his body had heard a call.","For the first time, Max realized that this reaction might not stay passive. Maybe it could be tested.","His eyes moved toward the statue of the First Progenitor standing at one end of the arena. The stone figure stayed silent, its eyes closed, its massive form towering over the Bloodline Legacy Battle like an ancient judge.","When Max looked at it now, his blood pulsed faintly again. The reaction stayed subtle because he’d kept it suppressed, but it was there.","Max’s gaze deepened.","’There’s a connection.’","He didn’t know what that connection meant. He didn’t know if it was dangerous. He didn’t know if it would benefit him, Rose, or neither of them.","But he knew one thing. If he did nothing, he might lose the chance to uncover it.","A daring thought rose in his mind. It was reckless. It was bold. It would definitely alarm the Four Sacred Clans. But the longer Max looked at the statue, the more certain he became that ordinary methods wouldn’t be enough to pull out the truth. The forbidden bloodline of the Four Sacred Clans was buried too deep.","Rose couldn’t even say its true name outside the clan. The Evercrest elders would never willingly explain the deeper secret to an outsider, no matter how famous he was. If Max wanted answers, he had to force the hidden connection to respond.","He made up his mind.","At that moment, Angelina Valerius looked toward him from the edge of the battlefield.","\"Max Morgan,\" she said, her voice carrying across the arena once the noise started to settle. \"As the victor, you may remain in the arena. Do you wish to challenge anyone else?\"","The question pulled everyone’s attention back to him. Many people from the Four Sacred Clans straightened up. After beating Aelric Evercrest, Max had already earned Rose an enormous amount of legacy merit.","If he kept challenging others, the Bloodline Legacy Battle might turn into a stage where he swept through the sacred clan heirs one by one.","Cassian Valerius opened his eyes on the Valerius platform. Draven Ashbourne grinned coldly. Seraphine Ravenhart watched with calm interest. Several other heirs and representatives tensed up too, wondering if Max would point at them next.","Rose looked at Max from the lower platform. She was still stunned by his win over Aelric, but the second she saw his expression, her chest tightened.","She knew that look. Max was about to do something unexpected.","Max looked at Angelina and shook his head. \"I don’t want to challenge anyone else.\"","The arena stirred slightly. Some people relaxed. Some frowned.","Angelina raised an eyebrow with faint interest. \"Then do you wish to leave the battlefield?\"","\"No.\"","Angelina’s smile deepened. \"Then what do you want to do?\"","Max looked toward the statue of the First Progenitor. \"I want to try something else.\"","The arena quieted again.","Angelina’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"Try what?\"","Max lowered Dragonheart, then slowly put the sword away. That alone confused a lot of people. A swordsman putting his sword away in the middle of the Bloodline Legacy Battle was strange enough on its own, but Max’s next words made things even more peculiar.","\"I don’t know.\"","The words carried clearly across the arena. For a moment, nobody understood what he meant. Even Angelina fell silent.","Max didn’t explain. He raised his right hand slowly, then clenched it into a fist.","Deep inside his foundation, he reached toward a power he didn’t fully control and didn’t casually reveal. The Dimensional Keeper legacy had been the reason he’d beaten Revona’s Null Origin Tide, but after that battle, he’d only used it cautiously. It was too mysterious, too vast, too far beyond his current understanding.","But now Max needed something capable of touching the hidden layer behind the forbidden bloodline. Ordinary power wouldn’t be enough.","His Primordial Bloodline stirred. His Dimensional Sovereign Body woke up. His blood pulsed toward the statue.","Then the Dimensional Keeper legacy answered.","A dark starry light began gathering around Max’s fist. At first, it looked like faint specks of silver shining beneath his skin. Then those specks multiplied, spreading across his hand like a night sky being born inside flesh.","Each point of light looked small, but if you looked closely, each star seemed to hold a sealed dimension. They shimmered, rotated, and folded inward, making Max’s fist look like it was no longer made of flesh but of countless small worlds hidden inside a dark cosmic sky.","The whole arena went silent.","A star fist. That was the only way to describe it. Max’s fist looked like a piece of the universe had condensed around his hand.","The moment this power appeared, the Four Sacred Clans reacted instantly. Bloodline pressure erupted across the arena, not from Max attacking anyone, but from their own bloodlines reacting.","Every member of Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest felt it at once. Their forbidden bloodlines trembled inside their bodies, then sank, as if an invisible weight had come down from above.","Some weaker descendants clutched their chests. Some heirs stood up in disbelief. Several elders’ expressions changed sharply. Even the strongest young geniuses of the four clans couldn’t stay fully calm.","Cassian Valerius opened his eyes fully, sacred solar light flickering around him in an unstable rhythm. Draven Ashbourne’s grin vanished as the blood-iron aura inside his body shook. Seraphine Ravenhart’s silver-purple eyes widened slightly for the first time, and the shadows around her seat pulled back as if afraid.","On the Evercrest platform, Aelric’s face turned pale again even though he’d already lost. The bloodline mark between his brows flickered weakly, as if it wanted to bow and resist at the same time.","Rose staggered half a step. Her eyes widened as she stared at Max’s fist. Even though she’d been born without the forbidden bloodline, she was still a direct descendant of Evercrest.","She could feel something calling from deep within the ancestral arena. It felt faint, painful, and overwhelming, like a sealed inheritance had suddenly sensed a key.","\"What is that?\" someone whispered.","No one answered. Because no one knew."]},{"number":1964,"title":"Chapter 1964: A Traitor’s Bloodline!","paragraphs":["The leaders of the Four Sacred Clans, who’d been watching from the highest seats, finally reacted.","On the Valerius end, an old man in white-gold robes stood up, his eyes blazing with sacred light. On the Ashbourne end, a dark-armored patriarch leaned forward, the stone beneath his hand cracking silently. On the Ravenhart end, a veiled matriarch’s shadow spread across half the platform. On the Evercrest end, several elders rose at the same time, their faces filled with shock and alarm.","One of them shouted, \"Max Morgan, what are you doing?\"","Another elder’s voice followed right after. \"Stop!\"","Even Angelina Valerius’s expression changed.","\"Max,\" she said, her voice sharper than before. \"Wait.\"","But Max didn’t wait. His eyes stayed fixed on the statue of the First Progenitor. The starry light around his fist grew brighter. The arena formation trembled, not because it was being destroyed, but because it couldn’t understand the nature of the power gathering inside his hand.","It wasn’t ordinary spatial power. It wasn’t pure dimensional power either. It was legacy power, sealed-world power, and a kind of authority that seemed to stand outside the rules the Four Sacred Clans had placed inside the battlefield.","Max inhaled slowly. Then he took one step forward.","The ground beneath his foot cracked. The suppressed bloodline reactions across the four clan platforms grew even stronger.","The statue of the First Progenitor, which had stayed silent since the battle began, finally reacted. A faint vibration came from within it. It was so soft that most people probably missed it. But Max heard it. His blood heard it. The Dimensional Keeper legacy around his fist pulsed in response.","The leaders of the Four Sacred Clans were about to speak again, but Max had already raised his fist. He didn’t aim at Aelric. He didn’t aim at the clan platforms. He aimed at the ground beneath the arena.","Then he slammed his star-like fist down.","Boom.","The moment Max’s star-like fist struck the arena floor, the entire Bloodline Legacy Battle arena trembled as if something ancient beneath it had finally been woken up.","The first thing to react was the statue of the First Progenitor. The enormous stone figure that had stood silently at one end of the arena began to glow.","At first the light was faint, just a thin line spreading along the closed eyelids of the statue. Then that light moved across its face, down its neck, through the folds of its stone robe, and into the hand resting near its side.","Every line carved into the statue lit up with a deep starry radiance, not gold, not green, not crimson, not purple, but a color that seemed to hold the dark sky and countless hidden worlds inside it.","The pressure on the Four Sacred Clans increased at once. It didn’t come from Max alone. It came from the statue.","The bloodlines of Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest trembled violently, and this time the suppression was far worse than before. Countless descendants who’d awakened the forbidden bloodline clutched their chests and went pale.","Some younger heirs dropped to one knee, their faces filled with disbelief as their bloodline marks flickered uncontrollably. Even powerful elders felt the flow of their blood slow down, as if the very source of their inherited power had been pressed beneath a higher authority.","\"What is happening?\"","\"My bloodline is being suppressed!\"","\"How is this possible? This is the First Progenitor’s arena!\"","\"The statue’s reacting to him!\"","\"No, impossible. He’s an outsider!\"","The voices spread across the four clan ends in a wave of panic and disbelief.","Max stood at the center of the battlefield with his fist still pressed against the cracked arena floor. The Dimensional Keeper legacy kept shining around his hand like a miniature universe, and the starry light flowing from his fist had already sunk into the deepest formation beneath the battlefield.","He could feel it now. The arena wasn’t just an arena. It was a sealed structure, a lock placed over something hidden, and his fist had struck exactly the layer that the Four Sacred Clans themselves seemed to have forgotten or deliberately buried.","The statue’s closed eyes glowed brighter. Then the fifth end of the arena lit up. Not the Valerius end. Not Ashbourne. Not Ravenhart. Not Evercrest. Not even the end where the statue stood.","The abandoned end.","The broken, dark, empty platform that no one had occupied since the Bloodline Legacy Battle began suddenly erupted with light. Ancient cracks across its surface filled with starry radiance.","Broken stone seats repaired themselves in flashes of silver and black. Old banners that hadn’t been visible before slowly appeared out of the air, torn and faded, yet still carrying a symbol that made the blood of the Four Sacred Clans tremble even harder.","The entire arena froze. Even Max was surprised. His eyes moved toward the abandoned end, and for the first time since he’d entered this arena, his expression changed openly.","The abandoned platform wasn’t empty anymore. It had never been truly empty. It had been sealed. Forgotten. Erased from open memory. But not destroyed.","The starry symbol above that end began to take shape. It didn’t look like the sacred sun of Valerius, the blood-iron mark of Ashbourne, the shadow-feather of Ravenhart, or the worldwood emblem of Evercrest.","It looked like a dark star surrounded by broken dimensional rings, and every time the symbol pulsed, the Dimensional Keeper legacy around Max’s fist responded.","The leaders of the Four Sacred Clans all stood up at once. Their expressions had completely changed. Shock. Fear. Rage. Recognition.","The old man from Valerius stared at Max, his white-gold eyes no longer calm. \"That symbol...\"","The dark-armored leader of Ashbourne clenched his hand so hard the space around his fingers cracked. \"Impossible. That bloodline should have disappeared.\"","The veiled matriarch of Ravenhart whispered, but her voice still carried strangely across the arena. \"The abandoned end has awakened.\"","The Evercrest patriarch looked at Max as if he’d finally seen a ghost from an ancient nightmare. \"No wonder the statue reacted.\"","Rose stood below the Evercrest platform, completely stunned. She looked from Max to the glowing abandoned end, then back to Max. All the color had drained from her face.","She didn’t understand everything, but she understood enough to realize that something far bigger than the Bloodline Legacy Battle had just happened. Max wasn’t merely a powerful outsider who’d come to represent her.","The arena had recognized him. Or rather, something hidden inside the arena had recognized his power.","Angelina Valerius stood at the edge of the battlefield with narrowed eyes, her expression more serious than Max had ever seen it. She looked at the abandoned end, then at the statue, then at Max’s star-like fist.","For a moment, no one moved.","Then the Valerius leader spoke in a cold voice.","\"He carries it.\"","The Ashbourne leader’s eyes filled with killing intent. \"The traitor’s bloodline.\"","The words hit the arena like thunder. The descendants of the Four Sacred Clans turned toward Max in disbelief.","\"The traitor’s bloodline?\"","\"What does that mean?\"","\"Is he connected to the abandoned end?\"","\"But he’s Max Morgan. Wasn’t he from the Black Dragon Clan?\"","\"Did the traitor’s line survive?\"","\"How can a descendant of that bloodline show up here now?\""]},{"number":1965,"title":"Chapter 1965: Blood of traitor!","paragraphs":["Max slowly stood up straight. The starry light around his fist hadn’t disappeared. It kept flowing faintly, and every pulse from it made the abandoned end brighter. His gaze swept across the leaders of the Four Sacred Clans, and his mind raced.","’Traitor’s bloodline?’","He’d expected a reaction. He’d expected the statue to reveal something. He hadn’t expected the Four Sacred Clans to recognize him as the descendant of something they called a traitor.","The Evercrest patriarch’s voice turned colder. \"No outsider could awaken the abandoned end. No outsider could make the First Progenitor statue glow like this. No outsider could suppress the bloodlines of the Four Sacred Clans through that cursed star power.\"","The Ravenhart matriarch said softly, \"He’s using the stolen legacy to suppress us. So it was true after all. The Voidwalker really did steal the true legacy and betray us.\"","The Ashbourne leader took one step forward, and the entire Ashbourne end shook beneath him. \"I told you this many times, and it was true. There’s no need to keep going with the Bloodline Legacy Battle.\"","Rose’s expression changed. \"Wait!\"","No one listened to her.","The Valerius leader raised his hand. \"Seal the arena.\"","The moment his command fell, the ancient formations around the entire battlefield activated at full power. Golden chains rose from the Valerius end. Crimson-black chains erupted from Ashbourne.","Purple shadow chains extended from Ravenhart. Green-silver spatial chains surged from Evercrest. All four sacred clan ends released their authority at once, and the chains shot toward the central battlefield like divine serpents.","Their target was Max.","Angelina’s face changed slightly. \"Elders, this is still the Bloodline Legacy Battle.\"","The Valerius leader said coldly, \"This is no longer a matter of the battle.\"","The Evercrest patriarch’s voice followed. \"A descendant of the traitor’s bloodline has appeared in the First Progenitor Arena. He must be imprisoned immediately.\"","Max’s eyes turned cold. \"So that’s your decision?\"","The Ashbourne leader sneered. \"You dare to awaken that abandoned end and still ask about our decision? Do you even know whose bloodline you’re carrying?\"","Max’s eyes narrowed at that question, but he didn’t need to think it over.","The chains descended. Max sensed right away how powerful they were. These weren’t ordinary sealing chains. They were formed from the combined bloodline authority of the Four Sacred Clans and empowered by the arena itself.","If they caught him, even his current strength might get heavily suppressed, especially with the First Progenitor Arena acting as the foundation.","The first golden chain reached him. Max raised his hand and struck it with his star-like fist.","Boom!","The chain trembled violently and cracked halfway, but it didn’t break completely. The crimson-black chain from Ashbourne wrapped around from the side, carrying brutal bloodline force.","The purple chain from Ravenhart vanished into shadow and appeared behind his back. The Evercrest chain folded through space and tried to bind his legs.","Max’s Dimensional Sovereign Body activated. His Primordial Bloodline stirred. The five Divine Veins inside him opened in rapid succession.","The Vein of Origin. The Vein of Vitality. The Vein of Speed. The Vein of Strength. The Vein of Resilience.","His body erupted with terrifying power, and the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline multiplied his strength tenfold again. For a moment, the air around him twisted under the combined force of Primordial authority, Divine Veins, and the Dimensional Keeper legacy.","Yet the four chains were still dangerous. They weren’t coming from young geniuses. They were coming from the leaders and formations of the Four Sacred Clans.","Max moved. The Vein of Speed pushed him out of the first sealing layer, while his Dimensional Sovereign Body tore open a gap in the folded space. The Evercrest chain chased him through the gap. Max turned, Dragonheart appearing in his hand again, and slashed down with the Emotion Severing Path.","The green-silver chain got cut apart from its spatial anchor. But before it could fully collapse, the Ravenhart shadow chain struck his back. The Vein of Resilience flared. The chain failed to pierce him, but its shadow force still wrapped around his aura and tried to pull his soul into stillness.","Max’s eyes sharpened. His Dimension of Soul opened faintly inside him, swallowing the soul-stilling force before it could settle.","The arena erupted into chaos. The crowd scattered backward as the sealing pressure spread. Many younger descendants couldn’t even stand. Some elders hurriedly shielded their clan members, while others stared at Max in shock.","\"He resisted the four-clan seal!\"","\"How is that possible?\"","\"He’s only at the Law Refinement Realm!\"","\"That fist, that starry power, and his body, what kind of monster is he?\"","Rose tried to rush forward, but several Evercrest elders appeared in front of her and blocked her path.","\"Move!\" Rose shouted.","One elder looked at her coldly. \"Rose Evercrest, you brought him here.\"","Her face went pale.","The elder’s voice grew heavier. \"If he truly carries the traitor’s bloodline, then you’ve committed a serious offense.\"","Rose clenched her fists. \"I didn’t know.\"","\"Then pray that ignorance is enough to save you.\"","On the battlefield, Max glanced toward Rose for a brief instant and saw what was happening around her. His gaze turned colder.","The Valerius leader’s voice rang out again.","\"Max Morgan, you carry the bloodline of the traitors. You are a Voidwalker. Do not resist. The Four Sacred Clans will investigate your origin. If you’re innocent, you’ll be given an explanation.\"","Max laughed. It wasn’t loud, but it carried clearly across the battlefield.","\"Innocent?\"","His grip on Dragonheart tightened.","\"You call me the descendant of a traitor’s bloodline, try to imprison me in front of everyone, and then talk about innocence?\"","The Ashbourne leader’s eyes burned with dark killing intent. \"You are not qualified to argue.\"","Max’s smile disappeared. The Dimensional Keeper legacy around his fist grew brighter. The abandoned end of the arena pulsed again in response, and the pressure suppressing the Four Sacred Clans grew even heavier.","Several elders’ faces changed as they realized that the more they tried to seal Max, the more the abandoned end woke up.","The statue of the First Progenitor glowed brighter. Its closed eyes trembled. A deep, ancient voice seemed to echo faintly from beneath the arena, too unclear to make out, but powerful enough to make every forbidden bloodline in the arena shake.","Max looked at the leaders of the Four Sacred Clans. His expression settled back into calm. But this calm ran far colder than before.","\"I came here to repay a promise,\" he said. \"I didn’t come here to be chained.\"","The golden, crimson-black, purple, and green-silver chains attacked again, this time with even greater force.","Max raised Dragonheart in one hand and kept the star-like fist clenched in the other. His white hair moved in the storm of bloodline pressure.","\"If you want to imprison me,\" Max said, his voice cutting through the entire arena, \"then you’d better be ready to pay the price.\"","He finally understood why Freya had told him to never reveal his Voidwalker name. It turned out Voidwalker was tied to the Four Sacred Clans. And from the looks of things, Voidwalker had done something pretty ugly to the other four."]},{"number":1966,"title":"Chapter 1966: A Grave Sin!","paragraphs":["The four bloodline chains coming down from the sacred clan platforms slowed for the smallest instant, not because the leaders of the Four Sacred Clans were scared, but because the pressure coming off Max had changed.","Up until now, he’d only resisted. He’d cut, dodged, countered, and broken through their seals with the Dimensional Keeper legacy, the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline, the five Divine Veins, and Dragonheart.","But the aura spreading from him now no longer belonged to someone simply defending himself.","It belonged to someone who’d decided to stop holding back.","Max’s eyes swept across the four clan leaders standing high above the arena. Valerius. Ashbourne. Ravenhart. Evercrest.","All four looked at him with cold recognition and hostility. They weren’t treating him as the champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference anymore, or as a Primordial inheritor, or as Rose’s representative. In their eyes, something older had woken up the moment the abandoned end of the arena lit up.","The Valerius leader raised his hand again, and golden sacred fire wrapped around the chain stretching from his platform. \"Max Morgan, there’s no use resisting. You carry the blood of traitors.\"","The Ashbourne leader’s voice followed like iron grinding against bone. \"The blood of the Voidwalker Clan.\"","The moment that name was spoken, the whole arena seemed to freeze.","Voidwalker.","Many younger descendants didn’t understand the weight behind that name, but the elders did. The instant they heard it, their expressions shifted. Some showed fear. Some showed hatred. Some showed disbelief, as if an ancient taboo had been dragged back from the dead and dropped right into the center of the First Progenitor Arena.","Max’s gaze sharpened.","\"Traitors?\" he repeated slowly. \"Voidwalker betrayed you?\"","The Ravenhart matriarch’s veiled face turned toward him. \"Not just betrayed us. They abandoned their sacred duty and turned their blades against the Four Sacred Clans.\"","The Evercrest patriarch’s voice was cold enough to freeze space itself. \"They tried to sever the foundation of the First Progenitor’s order.\"","Max’s expression darkened slightly.","\"That’s your claim,\" he said. \"But what did the Voidwalker Clan actually do?\"","Silence. A heavy, suffocating silence. None of the four leaders answered.","Instead, the Valerius leader’s sacred fire burned brighter. \"You are not qualified to question ancient judgment.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed further. \"So you’re telling me nothing.\"","The Ashbourne leader’s tone turned sharper. \"You carry their blood. That’s enough.\"","Max let out a slow breath. \"So I’m an enemy just because of blood?\"","The Ravenhart matriarch spoke again, colder this time. \"The Voidwalker Clan are a sin to the Four Sacred Clan and that makes you a sin as well.\"","The Evercrest patriarch raised his hand slightly. \"By sacred law, any inheritor of the Voidwalker lineage must be sealed.\"","Rose’s face went pale.","\"Max!\" she shouted from below. \"This is insane! He hasn’t done anything!\"","But several Evercrest elders immediately smothered her voice with pressure and forced her back. Her eyes trembled as she struggled, realizing she was being treated as a liability just for bringing him here.","Max’s gaze flicked toward her for a moment. That alone was enough. His expression cooled completely. Then he looked back at the four leaders.","\"You still haven’t told me anything,\" he said quietly. \"What did the Voidwalker do? What are their sins?\"","The Valerius leader’s eyes burned. \"You do not need to know.\"","The Ashbourne leader added, \"You will be imprisoned for the sins your Voidwalker Clan committed.\"","Max’s voice dropped. \"So that’s it.\"","A faint, humorless smile crossed his face. \"You want to seal me without even explaining why.\"","The Ravenhart matriarch’s voice turned final. \"Seal him.\"","The Evercrest patriarch followed immediately. \"By order of the Four Sacred Clans, Max Morgan is to be imprisoned as a Voidwalker inheritor.\"","The moment those words landed, the chains changed. They no longer aimed to restrain him. Now they carried execution-level sealing intent.","Max stood still for a heartbeat. Then he exhaled.","\"Then I guess I don’t have a choice.\"","The Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline erupted, and it didn’t build up gradually. It happened violently. Black-gold scales surged across his skin as his body began rejecting its human form entirely. His pupils narrowed into vertical slits, and a draconic pressure exploded outward, crashing into the Four Sacred Clans’ sealing force.","The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline stabilized the foundation underneath it. The five Divine Veins ignited all at once. And the Dimensional Keeper legacy resonated with the abandoned fifth end of the arena, as if something there was answering him.","Max’s voice dropped low.","\"Dragon Transformation.\"","Black light detonated outward. His body expanded, his bones reshaping and his flesh rewriting itself under ancient draconic law. Wings tore out from his back, massive and overwhelming. Horns curved like dark crowns. His form stretched and grew until a gigantic black dragon stood at the center of the arena.","This wasn’t an illusion. It was a true transformation.","The arena erupted in shock.","\"A dragon?!\"","\"He’s a Voidwalker and a dragon bloodline user?!\"","\"No wonder the clans want him sealed!\"","Rose stared upward, her hands trembling.","\"Max,\" she whispered, fear and helplessness mixing in her voice. \"Don’t push yourself too far.\"","But she already knew he had no other choice.","Angelina Valerius stood silently at the edge of the platform, her eyes narrowing slightly.","Above, the four leaders moved at once.","\"Suppress him!\" the Valerius leader ordered.","The chains came down again, stronger, deeper, more absolute this time. But Max’s dragon eyes opened, and he roared. The sound shattered space itself.","ROAR!","The golden chain got bitten apart instantly. The Ashbourne chain struck his wing but failed to break it. The Ravenhart soul threads pushed into his mind but sank straight into the vast Dimension of Soul. The Evercrest spatial seal tried to lock his body but got redirected into a false dimension and crushed.","The arena trembled violently.","Max lifted his enormous dragon head.","\"You want to imprison me,\" his voice rumbled like collapsing stars, \"without even telling me what I’m guilty of?\"","The abandoned fifth end of the arena pulsed brighter. The broken dimensional rings above it flickered as if responding.","The Valerius leader’s expression turned cold. \"No more words. Seal him completely.\"","The Ashbourne leader’s killing intent sharpened. \"Voidwalker Clan has a committed a grave sin and so they must be punished for their actions.\"","The Ravenhart matriarch whispered, almost reluctantly, \"Even if the truth stays buried with him.\"","The Evercrest patriarch finished, \"He will not leave this arena.\"","Four massive sealing formations rose.","Rose’s eyes widened in panic. \"No!\"","But Max had already moved. Black flames gathered in his mouth. The Primordial Bloodline surged. The five Divine Veins burned brighter than ever. And the Dimensional Keeper legacy wrapped around his claw like a star-forged weapon.","Max lowered his dragon body slightly, not retreating but preparing. Then he roared again.","\"Then come!\"","And the black dragon launched forward to meet the Four Sacred Clans head on."]},{"number":1967,"title":"Chapter 1967: Max vs Four Sacred Clan Heads!","paragraphs":["The black dragon launched forward.","His massive wings tore through the air with enough force to stir up a storm across the entire arena. Black chaotic flames burned between his scales, and the starry light of the Dimensional Keeper legacy wrapped around one of his claws like a weapon forged from sealed worlds.","The five Divine Veins burned inside his dragon body, each one magnified by the enormous true-dragon form, and the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline sat above everything like an ancient source pulling him closer to the laws of the world.","The first sealing formation came down from Valerius. A white-gold sun appeared above the arena, and from that sun came countless sacred chains, each one wrapped in burning light. They didn’t simply fall toward Max.","They tried to define him as guilty, brand his bloodline as sinful, and force his dragon body under the judgment of the Four Sacred Clans.","Max roared. Black dragon flames burst from his mouth and collided with the golden chains.","Boom!","The whole sky above the arena exploded in black and white-gold light. The golden chains burned through the dragon flames and kept descending, but their speed dropped sharply.","Max’s enormous claw swept upward, and the starry Dimensional Keeper light around it smashed into the first cluster of chains. Dozens of chains shattered instantly, their fragments falling like broken sunlight across the battlefield.","But the Valerius leader didn’t move. His eyes only turned colder.","\"His attacks are fierce,\" he said, \"but his realm is still too low.\"","The truth in those words showed itself in the next breath. Even though Max shattered dozens of chains, the white-gold sun above him didn’t collapse. The Valerius leader stood far above Max in cultivation, and that gap wasn’t something bloodline and talent alone could erase. Max’s dragon form made him terrifyingly durable.","His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline gave him ten times his normal strength. His five Divine Veins, especially the Vein of Resilience, made his defense almost monstrous. Yet when his attack hit the full formation controlled by a sacred clan head, it could only break part of it, not destroy its source.","Then Ashbourne’s formation arrived. A crimson-black mountain of blood iron dropped from the sky, covered in battle runes and ancient killing marks. It crashed straight onto Max’s back, trying to pin his dragon body to the arena floor.","Boom!","The arena sank. Cracks spread out in every direction. Many descendants from the Four Sacred Clans cried out as the shockwave slammed into the protective barriers around the platforms.","Max’s dragon body bent slightly under the enormous weight, but it didn’t break. His scales shone with black-gold light, and the Vein of Resilience erupted with terrifying defensive power.","The blood-iron mountain pressed down with the might of a sacred clan head, but Max’s body held. His bones didn’t shatter. His wings didn’t snap. His organs didn’t burst. The force poured into his body, only to be resisted by the combined durability of his dragon form, his fifth Divine Vein, and the stabilizing power of the Primordial Bloodline.","The Ashbourne leader’s pupils contracted. \"He endured it?\"","Max twisted his massive body and slammed his tail against the crimson-black mountain. The impact sent cracks across its lower half, but the mountain didn’t fully break.","It trembled, shifted, and kept pressing down. Max’s attack was powerful enough to stun every younger genius present, but against the deeper formation of Ashbourne’s clan head, it still wasn’t enough to fully throw off the suppression.","The gap in cultivation was too wide. Max understood this instantly.","’Their attacks can’t easily hurt me, but my attacks can’t easily destroy their foundations either.’","That was the problem. Their attacks bounced off him because his defensive foundation had grown too terrifying. His dragon form was simply too durable to be damaged by anything they threw at him.","On top of that, Max could feel his own abilities reinforcing his dragon body. The Vein of Resilience made it resistant to physical, spiritual, elemental, law-based, sealing, and bloodline attacks.","His Dimension of Soul swallowed any soul interference. His Dimensional Sovereign Body twisted spatial restraints out of shape. His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline pulled him closer to the laws and made his Pseudo Cosmic Paths stronger than ever.","But the four people attacking him weren’t young geniuses. They were the heads of the Four Sacred Clans. Their cultivation stood far above his, and their command over sacred clan formations gave every attack the weight of ancient inheritance.","Max could resist them, break parts of their seals, and force them to take him seriously, but beating all four outright was a different matter entirely.","The Ravenhart matriarch raised her hand. The world darkened. A shadow feather appeared above Max’s head and dissolved into thousands of silent threads. These threads didn’t go for his scales or flesh.","They slipped into the gaps between perception, thought, and reaction, trying to make his mind hesitate for one breath.","One breath was all the four leaders needed. But Max’s dragon eyes glowed coldly. The Dimension of Soul opened up like an endless inner night, and the shadow threads entered him and vanished.","The Ravenhart matriarch’s voice turned solemn. \"His soul defense isn’t normal. Don’t waste subtle attacks on him.\"","The Evercrest patriarch’s face had already darkened. He raised both hands, and the spatial layers around the battlefield folded inward. Green-silver roots appeared from every direction, but unlike Aelric’s roots, these carried the authority of an entire sacred clan head.","They pierced through folded space and wrapped around Max’s wings, claws, horns, and tail, trying to lock the enormous dragon form in place.","Max tore through the first wave. Then the second. Then the third. But more roots kept coming. And more.","The four leaders had already figured out the problem. Max was too hard to injure. His dragon form was too durable, his bloodline too strange, and his fifth Divine Vein made most direct attacks nearly useless unless they threw overwhelming force at him. Since they couldn’t easily destroy his body, they’d try to seal it instead.","The Valerius sun lowered. The Ashbourne blood-iron mountain expanded. The Ravenhart shadow feather spread across the arena like a dark sky. The Evercrest spatial roots tightened. Four greater seals formed together.","The pressure that came down this time worked completely differently from before. It didn’t try to cut Max, burn him, crush him, or pierce his soul. It tried to deny his movement, suppress his bloodline, lock down his dragon form, and bury him under the combined authority of the Four Sacred Clans.","Max’s wings strained. His claws dug into the arena floor. The abandoned Voidwalker end pulsed violently, but even its reaction couldn’t fully break the seals coming down from all four clan heads.","The Valerius leader spoke coldly. \"He’s durable, but durability is useless against eternal imprisonment.\"","The Ashbourne leader clenched his fist. \"Seal the dragon body first. Once he’s back in human form, pulling out the truth will be easier.\"","Rose struggled below, her eyes red with anger and fear. \"You call yourselves sacred clans, yet four clan heads are ganging up on one young cultivator?\"","An Evercrest elder looked at her coldly. \"Silence. You’ve already caused enough trouble.\"","Rose’s face went pale from the pressure, but she kept glaring at them.","On the battlefield, Max heard her voice. His dragon eyes turned colder.","The four greater seals tightened. His massive dragon body began sinking inch by inch toward the arena floor.","The younger descendants watched in shock and awe.","None of them had expected Max to hold out this long against the leaders of the Four Sacred Clans. Most people at his realm would have been sealed in the first exchange. Yet Max, in true dragon form, had taken attacks from all four sides, shattered parts of their formations, and forced the clan heads to combine their greater seals.","But now, even he seemed to be getting pushed down."]},{"number":1968,"title":"Chapter 1968: Arrival of the Anceastors!","paragraphs":["Angelina Valerius watched from the side with a complicated look on her face.","’If this keeps going, they’ll seal him.’","At that moment, Max stopped resisting randomly. His enormous dragon body lowered slightly, not because he was giving up, but because he was gathering power.","The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline pulsed once. Then twice. The five Divine Veins burned brighter.","The Vein of Origin anchored his entire dragon body. The Vein of Vitality poured life force into every scale and muscle. The Vein of Speed sharpened the movement of his blood, energy, and law. The Vein of Strength gathered all his destructive force into his chest. The Vein of Resilience let him endure the four seals long enough to prepare.","Then the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline erupted to its absolute limit. The black-gold patterns across Max’s dragon scales lit up like chaotic stars. His wings spread as wide as they could under the pressure of the seals. His massive chest expanded, and all the black flames surrounding his body rushed toward his mouth.","But this wasn’t an ordinary breath attack. The Dimensional Keeper legacy gathered inside the flames.","The Devouring Flames Domain condensed at the core. Divine King Punishment wrapped around it as seven-colored lightning. The Emotion Severing Path became the edge that would cut through sealing foundations. The Primordial Bloodline pulled all of it ten times closer to the source of law.","The entire arena felt the attack coming.","The Valerius leader’s expression shifted. \"Stop him.\"","The Evercrest patriarch immediately tightened the spatial roots. The Ravenhart matriarch sent shadow seals toward Max’s throat. The Ashbourne leader pushed the blood-iron mountain down with both hands.","But Max had already finished gathering his power. His dragon eyes locked onto the Evercrest patriarch.","Among the four clan heads, the Evercrest patriarch’s spatial seal posed the greatest danger to Rose and the biggest restriction on Max’s movement. If Max wanted to break the encirclement, he needed to injure one of them, and the Evercrest patriarch was the right target.","Then Max opened his mouth.","\"Black Dragon Cataclysm Breath.\"","A beam of black-gold dragon fire burst from his mouth. It was enormous. It tore through the battlefield like a collapsing night, carrying chaotic dragon force, primordial closeness to the laws, seven-colored punishment lightning, devouring black flames, and the starry fragments of the Dimensional Keeper legacy.","The moment it moved, the arena formation screamed under the pressure. The attack didn’t spread out randomly. It compressed into a single terrifying line and shot straight toward the Evercrest end.","The Evercrest patriarch’s face changed drastically. He crossed his hands, and countless spatial walls formed in front of him.","\"Evercrest Sacred Spatial Wall!\"","The first wall shattered. The second wall shattered. The third, fourth, fifth, and sixth walls shattered one after another. The Evercrest patriarch roared and summoned a massive tree of green-silver light in front of him, but the Cataclysm Breath pierced straight through its trunk. Devouring flames ate away its vitality.","The Emotion Severing Path cut its spatial anchors. Divine King Punishment shattered the defensive laws. The Dimensional Keeper legacy warped the distance between the attack and the target, making it arrive faster than the patriarch expected.","Boom!","The breath struck the Evercrest patriarch. The entire Evercrest platform exploded with light. Several elders screamed in shock as the protective formations cracked. The Evercrest patriarch got thrown backward, blood spraying from his mouth.","His robe tore apart across the chest, his aura collapsed violently, and a massive wound burned with black-gold flames that refused to go out right away.","The arena went dead silent. A clan head had been injured. Not by another elder. Not by a Divine Lord ancestor. By Max. By a young cultivator in dragon form.","Even though the Evercrest patriarch hadn’t been killed, and even though he’d blocked most of the attack with layers of sacred defenses, the fact remained that Max had heavily wounded one of the heads of the Four Sacred Clans in front of everyone.","The Valerius leader’s eyes went wide. The Ashbourne leader froze for half a breath. The Ravenhart matriarch’s veil fluttered violently. Angelina stared at Max, her expression finally showing open shock. Rose covered her mouth, unable to speak.","The Evercrest patriarch slowly pushed himself up from the shattered platform, blood still dripping from his lips. The wound on his chest kept burning, and his eyes filled with humiliation and killing intent.","\"You...\"","His voice shook with rage.","\"You dare injure me?\"","Max’s dragon voice rumbled across the arena.","\"You tried to imprison me.\"","That answer only made the silence heavier.","Then the air above the arena changed. Ancient pressure descended, not from the four clan heads, but from deeper within the Four Sacred Clans. One after another, old auras woke up from the sacred clan platforms.","These auras felt far more terrifying than the clan heads. They were ancient, heavy, and carried the weight of countless years. The younger descendants could barely breathe as the sky above Valerius turned white-gold, Ashbourne turned crimson-black, Ravenhart turned shadow-purple, and Evercrest turned green-silver.","The ancestors of the Four Sacred Clans were coming out.","An old voice from Valerius echoed first. \"The Voidwalker bloodline has returned.\"","A brutal voice from Ashbourne followed. \"And it’s already injured a clan head.\"","A soft, eerie voice from Ravenhart whispered across the arena. \"The Voidwalker Bloodline.\"","Then, from the depths of Evercrest, an ancient and furious voice came down. \"Let’s seal him before history repeats itself.\"","Four ancestral figures began forming above the arena. The pressure was so overwhelming that even Max’s massive dragon body felt the weight of it. His eyes narrowed.","This was bad. The clan heads had already given him trouble because of the gap in cultivation and the arena formations working against him. If the ancestors of the Four Sacred Clans stepped in personally, even Max’s current cards might not be enough to get out easily, especially while trying to protect Rose.","But just as the four ancestral pressures were about to fully descend, the abandoned fifth end of the arena erupted. The dark star and broken dimensional rings above it blazed with ancient light. The pressure from the Four Sacred Clan ancestors froze.","A crack opened above the abandoned platform. Not in space. In history. It felt like a sealed presence had been waiting there for countless years, and Max’s bloodline, his Dimensional Keeper legacy, and his defiance as a dragon had finally given it enough reason to appear.","A calm voice echoed from the abandoned end.","\"Enough.\"","One word. The entire arena stopped. The four ancestral figures stiffened. The statue of the First Progenitor glowed brighter.","Max slowly turned his dragon head toward the abandoned end. From the starry crack above that forgotten platform, an old man walked out. He wore a black robe marked with faint silver dimensional rings.","His hair was long and gray, and his eyes looked like two quiet stars surrounded by darkness. He didn’t give off any wild pressure, yet the moment he appeared, the Dimensional Keeper legacy around Max’s body resonated so strongly that the starry light across his dragon scales grew brighter.","The old man stood above the abandoned end and looked at Max. For a moment, his expression softened.","\"So one of our blood finally returned.\"","The Four Sacred Clan ancestors looked at him in shock and fury.","The Valerius ancestor’s voice trembled with disbelief. \"You...\"","The Ashbourne ancestor growled, \"What are you doing here?\"","The Ravenhart ancestor whispered, \"You should have stayed sealed.\"","The Evercrest ancestor’s killing intent surged. \"So you were still hiding beneath the abandoned end.\"","The old man didn’t look at them right away. He kept his eyes on Max. Then he raised one hand.","The four greater seals pressing on Max cracked at the same time. The pressure around Max let up instantly.","Only then did the old man turn toward the Four Sacred Clans. His voice stayed calm, but the entire arena trembled beneath it.","\"You dare attack my descendant in front of me?\"","The arena fell into a silence so heavy that even the younger generation forgot how to breathe.","The ancestor of the Voidwalker Clan had revealed himself. And he had come to protect Max."]},{"number":1969,"title":"Chapter 1969: Ancestor of Voidwalker!","paragraphs":["The old man’s voice echoed across the First Progenitor Arena, calm yet heavy enough to silence the chaos that had swallowed the battlefield.","\"You dare attack my descendant in front of me?\"","The four ancestral figures that had started descending from the sacred clan platforms froze in midair. Their bodies weren’t fully physical yet, but the pressure coming off them was enough to make the whole arena feel like it had sunk beneath four ancient heavens. One stood wrapped in white-gold light, his eyes burning like sacred suns.","One was covered in crimson-black battle aura, his armor lined with old scars and blood iron marks. One stayed half-hidden beneath a veil of shadow and purple feathers, silent and eerie. The last was surrounded by green-silver spatial roots, his old eyes filled with cold fury as he stared at both Max and the Voidwalker Ancestor.","The Voidwalker Ancestor stood above the abandoned fifth end. Compared to the other four, he looked simple. He wore only a black robe marked with faint silver dimensional rings.","His long gray hair drifted slightly in the wind, and his eyes looked like two quiet stars resting inside an endless night. He didn’t release overwhelming rage. He didn’t roar. He didn’t even raise his voice after that first sentence.","Yet the abandoned fifth end glowed beneath his feet. The dark star and broken dimensional rings above it pulsed brighter and brighter, and every pulse made the bloodlines of the Four Sacred Clans tremble, as if being forced to remember a history they’d tried hard to bury.","Max, still in his enormous black dragon form, looked at the old man in silence. The Dimensional Keeper legacy across his scales resonated with the Voidwalker Ancestor’s presence. It wasn’t the simple resonance of similar techniques.","It felt like blood recognizing blood, legacy recognizing its source, and a forgotten seat recognizing the return of its heir. For the first time since the Four Sacred Clans had tried to imprison him, Max felt like the battlefield was no longer completely against him.","The pressure binding his dragon body had loosened. The greater seals from the four clan heads had cracked. Even the ancestors of the Four Sacred Clans had paused.","The Valerius ancestor’s eyes narrowed. \"Voidwalker, you still dare call him your descendant?\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor turned toward him slowly. \"He carries our blood. Of course he’s my descendant.\"","The Ashbourne ancestor let out a cold laugh laced with killing intent. \"Your blood? You talk like that’s something to be proud of. That bloodline should have stayed buried with the rest of your clan.\"","The Ravenhart ancestor’s voice drifted across the arena like a whisper from a grave. \"The abandoned end was sealed. Your name was erased from the sacred records. Your descendants were forbidden from ever coming back. Yet now one’s appeared, holding the stolen legacy in his hands.\"","Max’s dragon eyes sharpened.","Stolen legacy. That phrase again.","The Evercrest ancestor’s expression was colder than anyone else’s. His descendant, the Evercrest patriarch, had just been badly injured by Max’s Black Dragon Cataclysm Breath, and the wound still burned with black-gold flames across his chest despite several elders’ efforts to suppress it.","That humiliation had already pushed the Evercrest side into fury.","The Evercrest ancestor raised his hand, and the green-silver roots beneath his feet coiled like living serpents. \"This boy carries the blood of traitors, and he’s woken up the abandoned Voidwalker end. He has to be sealed, just like the others.\"","Those words spread across the whole arena.","Just like the others.","Max’s gaze turned colder.","’So there are others.’","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s expression barely shifted, but the air around him grew slightly heavier.","\"The others,\" he repeated softly.","The Valerius ancestor looked at him with stern eyes. \"Don’t pretend you’ve forgotten. After the Voidwalker Clan betrayed the sacred pact and stole the legacy that should have belonged to all five clans together, the judgment was already made. Your line was sealed. Your descendants were sealed. Your ancestral end was abandoned. That was the decision of the Four Sacred Clans.\"","\"The four clans,\" the Voidwalker Ancestor said, his voice still calm. \"Not the five?\"","The Ashbourne ancestor’s battle aura flared. \"Because the fifth lost the right to stand with us.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked toward the glowing statue of the First Progenitor. For a brief moment, something old and painful crossed his eyes.","\"Did we lose that right,\" he said, \"or did you take it from us after deciding the truth was inconvenient?\"","The arena went deathly silent. The younger generation of the Four Sacred Clans didn’t dare breathe too loudly.","Most of them had grown up hearing fragments of old warnings, forbidden names, and vague mentions of a traitorous bloodline. They’d been told the Voidwalker Clan was cursed, dangerous, and sealed for the sins it committed. But no one had ever laid out the full story for them.","Now, standing in the First Progenitor Arena, they could sense the truth might not be as simple as their elders claimed.","The Ravenhart ancestor’s shadow stirred. \"Don’t twist the past. The Voidwalker Clan took what should never have been taken.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at her. \"We protected what should never have been handed over.\"","The Valerius ancestor’s eyes burned brighter. \"Lies.\"","\"Convenient word,\" the Voidwalker Ancestor replied. \"You used it last time too.\"","The Evercrest ancestor stepped forward in the air, and the spatial roots around him spread toward the abandoned fifth end. \"Enough. Whatever words you use, the result won’t change. The boy has woken up the Voidwalker legacy. He carries the stolen inheritance. If he leaves this place, everything we sealed away might come back.\"","Max’s massive dragon body shifted slightly. His claws pressed against the broken arena floor, and the black-gold scales along his body gave off a faint chaotic glow.","The Vein of Resilience still strengthened his body, the Primordial Bloodline still multiplied his foundation, and the Dimensional Keeper legacy still shimmered across him, but he didn’t attack. Not yet. He wanted to hear more."]},{"number":1970,"title":"Chapter 1970: Voidwalker Bloodline!","paragraphs":["The Voidwalker Ancestor, though, took one step forward. The abandoned fifth end brightened beneath him.","\"You talk about sealing him like he’s some criminal,\" he said. \"What crime has he actually committed?\"","The Ashbourne ancestor growled, \"He carries the traitor’s blood.\"","\"So do your descendants,\" the Voidwalker Ancestor said. \"They carry the blood of your clans. Does that mean they personally answer for every sin you committed?\"","The words landed like a blade. Several elders’ expressions changed.","The Valerius ancestor’s voice turned colder. \"Don’t compare our clans to yours.\"","\"I’ll compare them however I please,\" the Voidwalker Ancestor said. \"You’re judging a young man who hasn’t even heard the truth of our history. You call him a traitor because his blood woke up a seat you failed to destroy. You call his legacy stolen because you couldn’t take it back yourselves. You’re trying to seal him because you’re afraid of what he might learn.\"","The Evercrest ancestor’s killing intent surged. \"Careful, Voidwalker.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor finally smiled faintly. It wasn’t a warm smile. It was tired and cold.","\"Don’t speak to me like you still hold the chains around my neck.\"","The entire arena trembled. The four ancestors froze. For the first time, their expressions showed genuine shock.","The Valerius ancestor’s voice dropped. \"You agreed to the seal.\"","\"Yes,\" the Voidwalker Ancestor said. \"I agreed.\"","His gaze moved across the four ancestors one by one.","\"I agreed last time for the sake of the five clans.\" The words carried across the arena like thunder hidden beneath calm speech. \"Not because I believed your judgment was right. Not because I admitted guilt. Not because the Voidwalker Clan deserved to be erased. I agreed because if the five clans had fought to the end back then, the First Progenitor’s inheritance would have shattered, and every sacred bloodline descended from him would have suffered damage that could never be undone.\"","The younger descendants stared in shock. This wasn’t the version of history they’d been told.","The Ashbourne ancestor’s face darkened. \"You dare bring up old matters in front of juniors?\"","\"They deserve to know why you’re trying to chain a young man in front of them,\" the Voidwalker Ancestor said.","The Ravenhart ancestor’s voice turned dangerous. \"Some truths are sealed for a reason.\"","\"And some lies are sealed because the people who told them are afraid of being questioned.\"","The statue of the First Progenitor glowed brighter after those words. The light from its closed eyes deepened, and a pulse passed through the arena.","Max noticed. So did the four ancestors.","The Evercrest ancestor’s expression turned uglier.","The Voidwalker Ancestor continued, \"I let myself be sealed because the five clans were already on the edge of collapse. I let the Voidwalker end be abandoned because I thought time might cool your fear and anger. I let your version of history stand because I thought protecting the sacred inheritance mattered more than proving who was right.\"","His eyes turned colder. \"But I won’t make that mistake again.\"","The arena went silent. The words came out calm. Yet they felt like a declaration of war.","The Valerius ancestor’s sacred light rose higher. \"You’d break the old pact?\"","\"The old pact was between five clans,\" the Voidwalker Ancestor said. \"You four turned it into a prison.\"","The Ashbourne ancestor clenched his fist, and crimson-black blood iron light spread out behind him like a battlefield of ancient corpses. \"If you protect him, you’re standing against the Four Sacred Clans.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at him without fear. \"I’ve stood against worse.\"","The Ravenhart ancestor whispered, \"You’re only a remnant.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor nodded. \"Yes. I’m only a remnant.\"","Then his gaze moved to Max. \"But he isn’t.\"","The whole arena turned toward the black dragon. Max’s enormous eyes met the old man’s gaze. There wasn’t full understanding between them yet.","Max still didn’t know the truth about the Voidwalker Clan, the so-called stolen legacy, the old betrayal, or why his blood had awakened the abandoned end. But when the Voidwalker Ancestor looked at him, there was no hatred in it, no suspicion, and no urge to use him as a tool.","There was only protection. Fierce, absolute protection. The kind Max had rarely ever gotten from ancient powers.","The Voidwalker Ancestor turned back to the four ancestors.","\"You sealed me. You sealed the others. You buried our end, erased our name, and taught your descendants to spit on a bloodline whose truth they never even knew. I stayed silent once because I thought it would keep the five clans together.\"","His voice deepened. \"This time, I won’t.\"","The abandoned end erupted with starry light. The dark star symbol above it expanded, and broken dimensional rings rotated around the whole arena. Space folded, not the way Evercrest’s life-space seals did, but in a deeper, more absolute way.","For a moment, everyone present felt like the arena had been pulled out of normal space and placed inside a vast hidden dimension under the Voidwalker Ancestor’s control.","The four ancestors released their auras at once. White-gold fire. Crimson-black blood iron. Shadow-purple fate feathers. Green-silver worldwood space. Four ancient powers pressed toward the abandoned end.","The Voidwalker Ancestor raised one hand. A starry barrier appeared between Max and the four ancestors. Their pressure struck the barrier and spread across it like waves crashing into an endless night sky. The barrier trembled. But it held.","The Valerius ancestor shouted, \"Voidwalker, step aside. The boy has to be sealed before the stolen legacy fully wakes up.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s expression turned cold. \"No.\" The word was simple. Final.","The Evercrest ancestor’s eyes narrowed. \"You’d risk everything for one descendant you just met?\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked back at Max. \"He’s not just one descendant,\" he said. \"He’s proof the Voidwalker bloodline survived despite everything you did to stop it.\"","Max’s heart stirred faintly.","Rose stood below, still surrounded by Evercrest elders, her face full of shock and confusion. She’d brought Max here for her own shot at bloodline inheritance, never expecting to uncover an ancient conflict between the Four Sacred Clans and a hidden fifth sacred clan. But watching the Voidwalker Ancestor stand in front of Max, she understood one thing clearly.","This wasn’t just her battle anymore. This was history coming back."]},{"number":1971,"title":"Chapter 1971: Arrival of the Others!","paragraphs":["The Ashbourne ancestor roared, \"Then you leave us no choice.\"","The four ancestors moved.","At the same time, the Voidwalker Ancestor stepped forward. The starry barrier around Max expanded, and the broken dimensional rings above the abandoned end spun faster. The statue of the First Progenitor glowed even brighter, as if watching a scene that had happened once before, long ago, now repeating in front of its closed eyes.","Max’s dragon claws dug into the ground. His voice rumbled behind the barrier.","\"Ancestor.\"","The old man didn’t turn back. But he answered.","\"Stay behind me for now.\"","Max’s dragon eyes narrowed.","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s voice softened just slightly. \"You’ve done enough. You woke up the fifth end. You forced the buried truth to the surface. Now let this old man do what he failed to do properly last time.\"","The four ancestral powers descended. The Voidwalker Ancestor raised both hands. A sea of stars opened up behind him. And the abandoned fifth end, forgotten for countless years, finally returned to the Bloodline Legacy Battle.","The sea of stars behind the Voidwalker Ancestor had just started to open when the sky above the Bloodline Legacy Battle arena changed again.","This time, the change didn’t come from the abandoned fifth end. It came from outside.","A tremendous spatial pressure came down from above the arena, and the protective boundary around the Bloodline Legacy Battle shook, as if countless hands had grabbed it from every direction at once.","The four ancestors, who’d been ready to clash with the Voidwalker Ancestor, lifted their heads almost at the same moment. The clan heads and elders looked upward too, their expressions shifting sharply as they sensed thousands of auras appearing beyond the sacred arena’s outer sky.","Max also lifted his massive dragon head. He didn’t need to look carefully to know who stood at the front. His blood recognized her before his eyes did.","High above the arena, a crack opened across the sky like a blade slicing through silk. Figures emerged from that crack one after another. Not dozens. Not hundreds. Thousands.","They appeared in perfect formation, surrounding the entire Bloodline Legacy Battle arena from the sky, each one carrying a cold, disciplined aura.","Their robes were dark, marked with silver dimensional lines, and many of them held weapons glowing faintly with the same star-like light that had woken from the abandoned fifth end.","At the front stood a woman with long silver-white hair flowing behind her like a river of moonlight.","Freya.","Max’s dragon eyes went wide. For a moment, even the storm of battle inside him went still.","He’d known she was alive, known she existed somewhere outside the ordinary reach of his current life. But knowing and seeing were two different things. Now she stood above the Bloodline Legacy Battle arena, alive, powerful, carrying an aura that felt deeply familiar.","His big sister.","Max’s heart shook in a way no battle had ever managed to shake it.","\"Freya,\" he murmured, though it came out as a deep dragon rumble.","A strange kind of happiness rose in him, sharp enough to cut through all the danger surrounding him.","The Four Sacred Clans were trying to seal him. Their ancestors had shown up. The Voidwalker Ancestor stood in front of him. The truth about his bloodline was turning the whole arena upside down. Yet for that one breath, Max only looked at Freya.","She was here. His big sister was here.","Freya’s gaze found him immediately. She saw the enormous black dragon standing in the ruined central battlefield, saw the broken seals around him, saw the bloodline pressure surrounding him, and saw the glow of the abandoned Voidwalker end beneath the ancestor. Her expression barely changed, but her eyes softened for the smallest instant.","Then her gaze turned cold. Very cold.","She looked toward the four ancestors of Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest.","\"Stop.\"","Her voice wasn’t loud, but it carried across the whole arena with terrifying clarity.","The four ancestors looked at her, eyes narrowed.","The Valerius ancestor’s sacred light burned brighter. \"Who are you to give orders to the Four Sacred Clans?\"","Freya didn’t answer right away. She raised one hand.","At that instant, the thousands of figures who’d arrived with her moved. They spread across the sky and completely surrounded the Bloodline Legacy Battle arena. Space rippled around them as formation flags, star-like seals, and dimensional weapons activated one after another.","A ring of Voidwalker power formed above the arena, and for the first time since the conflict began, the descendants of the Four Sacred Clans felt danger coming not from inside the battlefield, but from above their own heads.","Freya’s voice stayed calm.","\"If you keep this fight going, we’ll attack the descendants of the Four Sacred Clans.\"","The entire arena froze. For a breath, nobody believed what they’d just heard.","Then the sacred clan platforms erupted.","\"What did she just say?\"","\"She dares threaten us?\"","\"She wants to attack sacred clan descendants?\"","\"Who are these people?\"","\"Are they out of their minds?\"","The younger descendants of Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest looked up in shock and anger. The elders’ faces darkened instantly. The clan heads, already shaken by Max injuring the Evercrest patriarch, grew furious.","The Four Sacred Clans had stood at the top of humanity for countless ages. Even supreme forces treated them with caution. Yet now a woman had shown up with thousands of people and openly threatened their descendants right inside the First Progenitor Arena.","The Ashbourne ancestor’s battle aura exploded. \"How bold.\"","The crimson-black sky behind him shook, as if an ancient battlefield had come back to life. \"You dare threaten the bloodlines of the Four Sacred Clans?\"","Freya looked at him without fear. \"Yes.\"","The answer came so direct that the air around them turned even colder.","The Evercrest ancestor’s spatial roots twisted violently. \"You think surrounding the arena gives you leverage?\"","Freya’s eyes stayed calm. \"It does actually.\"","The Ravenhart ancestor’s shadow spread across the air. \"If you attack them, none of you will leave here alive.\"","Freya replied, \"If Max gets sealed, none of them will live long enough to care whether we leave or not.\""]},{"number":1972,"title":"Chapter 1972: Secret of the Four Sacred Clans!","paragraphs":["A deadly silence fell over everything. The descendants of the Four Sacred Clans suddenly felt the full weight of the situation. This wasn’t an empty threat. Freya’s people had already positioned themselves above every major platform.","Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest each had crowds of younger descendants gathered to watch the Bloodline Legacy Battle.","The Four Sacred Clan ancestors were powerful, terrifyingly powerful, but their descendants weren’t invincible. If thousands of Voidwalker fighters struck at once from prepared positions, even a moment’s hesitation could turn into a massacre.","The four ancestors’ faces turned unbelievably dark. No one had dared threaten them like this in countless years.","Then the Valerius ancestor’s expression changed. His eyes fixed on Freya. The sacred light around him flickered slightly, as if he’d sensed something.","\"You...\"","The Ashbourne ancestor narrowed his eyes too. His battle aura, which had been raging wildly, suddenly sharpened into focus.","The Ravenhart ancestor’s veil moved without any wind.","The Evercrest ancestor stared at Freya with disbelief and anger.","\"She carries it too.\"","The Valerius ancestor’s voice turned colder. \"Voidwalker bloodline.\"","Those words spread across the arena again. The sacred clan descendants looked up at Freya in shock.","Freya stood calmly in the sky, surrounded by thousands of her people, and the star-like dimensional light around her made the abandoned fifth end pulse even stronger.","Unlike Max, whose Voidwalker connection had stayed hidden beneath layers of other bloodlines and legacies, Freya’s presence carried that bloodline out in the open. It felt cold, deep, and wrapped in the quiet authority of distance, space, and hidden worlds.","The Ashbourne ancestor’s killing intent grew heavier. \"How many of you got away?\"","The Ravenhart ancestor whispered, \"How many of these traitors weren’t sealed last time?\"","The Evercrest ancestor’s eyes turned vicious. \"So the Voidwalker remnants have been hiding this whole time.\"","Freya looked at them with cold eyes. \"Some of us managed to survive.\"","The word was simple. But it hit the four ancestors like a slap.","The Voidwalker Ancestor, still standing in front of Max, looked up at Freya. For the first time since he’d appeared, his expression shifted more visibly. He stared at her for a long moment, and something like sorrow and relief passed through his old eyes.","\"You two must be his son and daughter,\" he said softly.","Freya lowered her gaze toward him. \"Ancestor.\"","That one word confirmed everything.","The whole arena stirred again. The black dragon at the center of the battlefield was a descendant of the Voidwalker Clan. The woman in the sky was also a descendant of the Voidwalker Clan. The thousands surrounding the arena were likely Voidwalker remnants as well.","The fifth sacred end, which everyone had believed abandoned forever, was waking up right in front of them. The Four Sacred Clans had tried to bury this bloodline, but it had come back, and everyone was watching it happen.","Max looked up at Freya, his happiness now tangled with a flood of questions. He wanted to ask where she’d been all this time, how she’d survived, how many Voidwalkers were left, why she’d never told him the truth, and what had actually happened between the Voidwalker Clan and the Four Sacred Clans.","But this wasn’t the time.","Freya seemed to know that too. Her gaze stayed on the Voidwalker Ancestor.","\"Ancestor,\" she said, her voice carrying across the arena, \"it’s time.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor didn’t answer right away.","Freya continued, \"For many years, the Four Sacred Clans have called us traitors. They sealed our people, abandoned our sacred end, erased our name, and taught their descendants that Voidwalker blood is a sin. Today, Max was nearly imprisoned without even being told what crime he was supposed to have committed.\"","Her eyes swept across the four ancestors. \"They keep talking about stolen legacy. They keep talking about betrayal. They keep talking about ancient judgment. But they never explain the actual truth.\"","The Valerius ancestor’s face turned stern. \"Some truths should stay sealed.\"","Freya looked at him. \"No.\" Her voice turned colder. \"Not anymore.\"","The thousands of Voidwalker descendants above the arena released their auras all at once. Their power didn’t attack yet, but it pressed downward, reminding everyone that Freya’s threat still stood. If the Four Sacred Clan ancestors chose to fight, the younger descendants below them would be the first to pay for it.","Freya turned back to the Voidwalker Ancestor. \"Tell the truth.\"","The whole arena went silent.","Rose stood below, surrounded by Evercrest elders, staring up at Freya with wide eyes. Angelina Valerius stayed motionless at the edge of the battlefield, her expression heavy with thought. Cassian Valerius, Draven Ashbourne, Seraphine Ravenhart, and the other sacred clan geniuses looked between Freya, Max, the Voidwalker Ancestor, and their own ancestors, realizing that the Bloodline Legacy Battle had turned into something far bigger than any of them had expected.","Max’s massive dragon body stayed still, his eyes fixed on the Voidwalker Ancestor.","Freya’s voice rang out again, calm but impossible to ignore.","\"Tell everyone what the Voidwalker Clan actually did. Tell them why we were called traitors. Tell them what legacy was supposedly stolen. Tell them what really happened to the fifth sacred clan.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor slowly closed his eyes. For a long moment, he said nothing.","The glowing statue of the First Progenitor stood behind the arena, its closed eyes shining like stars trapped in stone. The abandoned fifth end burned with dark light. The Four Sacred Clan ancestors stayed silent, furious and unwilling, but unable to act recklessly with their descendants surrounded.","At last, the Voidwalker Ancestor opened his eyes. He looked at the four ancestors. Then at Freya. Then at Max.","The old man’s voice came out quiet.","\"Very well.\"","The whole arena held its breath.","\"Then let the buried truth return.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s expression became solemn.","\"It is time everyone knows the history of the sacred clans.\"","He looked across the arena.","\"Or should I say, the history of the Five Sacred Clans.\"","The whole arena went still.","Above, Freya lowered her gaze in silence.","Below, Max’s enormous dragon body remained unmoving, his heart pounding with questions that were finally about to receive answers."]},{"number":1973,"title":"Chapter 1973: History of the Four Sacred Clans - 1","paragraphs":["The Voidwalker Ancestor stood above the awakened fifth end for a long moment before speaking again.","The entire Bloodline Legacy Battle arena stayed silent. The thousands of Voidwalker descendants in the sky held their formation, surrounding the arena like a dark starry net. Freya stood at the front of them with her silver-white hair moving in the wind, her gaze cold and steady.","The four sacred ancestors had already pulled back their pressure, while the four current clan leaders stood below them with ugly expressions, unable to accept that the truth they’d worked so hard to bury was about to come out in front of the whole younger generation.","Max stayed in his true dragon form at the center of the ruined battlefield. His enormous black-gold body had gone quiet, but the chaotic flames between his scales hadn’t fully died down.","He watched the old man closely, his mind racing with thoughts.","The Four Sacred Clans had called him a descendant of traitors. They’d accused him of carrying the stolen legacy. They’d tried to imprison him without ever explaining why. Now, finally, he was about to understand why Freya had once warned him never to reveal the name Voidwalker.","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked toward the statue of the First Progenitor.","\"Before the Four Sacred Clans existed,\" he said slowly, \"there were the Five Sacred Clans.\"","His voice wasn’t loud, but it reached every corner of the arena. The younger descendants of Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest listened with tense faces. Some of them had already guessed as much from what had just happened, but hearing the Voidwalker Ancestor say it outright still shook them.","The official history they’d grown up learning only spoke of four sacred bloodlines descending from the First Progenitor. The fifth had been erased so completely that even mentioning it felt like trespassing on forbidden ground.","The Voidwalker Ancestor raised his hand slightly. The starry screen behind him brightened, and ancient images began to appear across it. There stood a younger First Progenitor Arena, whole, undivided, and unscarred by abandonment.","Five platforms surrounded the statue. Valerius shone with sacred white-gold light. Ashbourne burned with crimson-black battle force. Ravenhart stood beneath silent purple shadows. Evercrest bloomed with green-silver life-space radiance. And the fifth platform, the one now awake beneath the Voidwalker Ancestor, glowed with dark stars and silver dimensional rings.","\"Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, Evercrest, and Voidwalker,\" the old man continued. \"Those were the Five Sacred Clans born from the legacy of the First Progenitor. Each clan inherited a different branch of his forbidden bloodline, and each carried a different duty.\"","His gaze moved across the four clan platforms.","\"Valerius guarded the sacred flame and the judgment of light. Ashbourne guarded the martial body and the blood-iron battlefield. Ravenhart guarded shadows, prophecy fragments, and the silence of the soul. Evercrest guarded life, space, and sealed domains.\"","Then his gaze returned to the fifth end.","\"And Voidwalker guarded distance, hidden worlds, dimensional passage, and the deepest seal placed around the sacred legacy itself.\"","Those words changed a lot of expressions in the crowd.","The Voidwalker Ancestor went on. \"The sacred legacy of the First Progenitor wasn’t a simple inheritance technique. It wasn’t a martial art anyone could learn through effort. It was the deepest thing he left behind, the core inheritance holding the reason the five sacred bloodlines existed and the secret of what our ancestor truly carried.\"","The four sacred ancestors lowered their eyes slightly. The clan leaders’ faces turned even uglier. The young geniuses of the Four Sacred Clans stared at the starry screen, unable to look away.","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s voice grew heavier. \"Since ancient times, the duty of the Five Sacred Clans was to protect that sacred legacy. None of us owned it. None of us had the right to use it however we wanted. None of us could force it open. The five clans were only guardians, waiting for the day the sacred legacy would choose an inheritor on its own.\"","On the starry screen, the five ancient clans could be seen kneeling before the First Progenitor’s statue, their bloodline marks glowing as they formed a vast seal around a dark, mysterious light hidden beneath the arena.","\"For countless years, the sacred legacy stayed silent,\" the Voidwalker Ancestor said. \"Generation after generation guarded it. Ancestors rose and fell. Heirs were born and died. Wars came and went. The clans changed leaders again and again, yet the sacred legacy never once chose anyone.\"","His old eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Then, one day, everything changed.\"","The image on the starry screen trembled. The peaceful arena from ancient times turned darker. Beneath the statue of the First Progenitor, the sealed sacred legacy suddenly pulsed. Its light wasn’t ordinary. It looked like a folded universe, a starry abyss, and a hidden world all rolled into one.","The moment it moved, the five platforms shook, and the Voidwalker platform reacted more violently than the rest.","The descendants in the current arena held their breath.","The Voidwalker Ancestor said, \"According to the history written by the other four clans, the Voidwalker Clan betrayed the sacred pact. We stole the sacred legacy of the First Progenitor, the very thing we’d sworn to protect with our lives, and fled from the Five Sacred Clans.\"","The Valerius platform fell silent. The Ashbourne descendants clenched their fists. The Ravenhart geniuses traded shocked looks. The Evercrest descendants looked unsettled. This was the version most of them had heard before, though never spelled out so directly.","The Voidwalker Ancestor didn’t deny the story right away. He only looked at the starry screen.","\"That’s what they saw.\"","The image changed. Several members of the ancient Voidwalker Clan stood before the sealed sacred legacy, their eyes glowing with a strange starry light. Their faces looked dazed, pained, and reverent all at once. They didn’t look like thieves who’d come for greed. They looked like people being pulled along by a voice no one else could hear.","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s voice went quiet.","\"But it wasn’t that simple.\"","The whole arena leaned into the silence.","\"It wasn’t the Voidwalker Clan that first chose to steal the sacred legacy,\" he said. \"It was the sacred legacy that chose to move.\""]},{"number":1974,"title":"Chapter 1974: History of the Four Sacred Clans - 2","paragraphs":["A wave of shock rolled through the arena.","\"What?\"","\"The sacred legacy moved on its own?\"","\"How is that even possible?\"","\"Wasn’t it just an inheritance?\"","The young geniuses of the Four Sacred Clans looked the most shaken. Cassian Valerius opened his eyes fully, his sacred solar aura unstable for the first time. Draven Ashbourne frowned deeply, his usual battle hunger replaced by solemn confusion. Seraphine Ravenhart’s silver-purple eyes shone with a strange light, as if the truth itself had disturbed the shadows around her. Aelric Evercrest, still injured and humiliated from his loss to Max, stared at the screen with a pale face.","The Voidwalker Ancestor continued, \"For countless years, we protected the sacred legacy, yet it never once chose an inheritor. But in that era, for reasons even I never understood, the sacred legacy suddenly responded to the Voidwalker bloodline.\"","The starry screen showed several Voidwalker elders clutching their heads as the legacy’s light poured into their bodies.","\"It didn’t just resonate with them. It influenced them. It called to them. It possessed them.\"","The four sacred clan platforms erupted in disbelief.","The Valerius leader’s face twisted. \"Nonsense.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor ignored him.","\"Some members of the Voidwalker Clan were affected lightly. They heard whispers. They had dreams. They saw hidden doors in their bloodline. But others were pulled in much deeper. They started believing the sacred legacy didn’t belong under the Five Sacred Clans anymore. They believed it had chosen Voidwalker, and that if they didn’t take it, the chance would vanish forever.\"","On the screen, the ancient Voidwalker members moved under the legacy’s influence. They broke through several layers of the seal their own clan had helped maintain. Other Voidwalker members tried to stop them, but the sacred legacy’s light warped space and turned the entire platform into a maze of folded worlds.","The old man’s voice grew heavier.","\"In the end, a group of Voidwalker clan members took the sacred legacy and fled.\"","The arena buzzed with murmurs. The image showed the five ancient platforms erupting into chaos. Valerius sacred fire rose into the sky. Ashbourne battle aura split the ground. Ravenhart shadows tried to trace the escape path.","Evercrest space roots sealed off countless directions. The Voidwalker platform tore itself apart as some Voidwalkers chased the thieves, some protected their clan members, and some just stood frozen in disbelief.","\"The five clans were shocked,\" the Voidwalker Ancestor said. \"The other four clans watched the sacred legacy vanish in the hands of Voidwalker members. They watched the very guardians closest to the seal break it. They watched the fifth clan become the path through which the legacy disappeared.\"","His eyes lowered faintly.","\"At that time, even I believed the fault belonged to my own clan members.\"","Those words stunned everyone all over again.","Max’s dragon eyes narrowed slightly. The Voidwalker Ancestor wasn’t hiding his own past mistake.","\"I believed those who took the legacy had betrayed the sacred pact. I believed they’d been overcome by greed, ambition, and bloodline pride. I believed the Voidwalker Clan had failed in its duty, and that our failure had nearly torn apart the Five Sacred Clans.\"","The starry screen showed battles breaking out across ancient domains. Voidwalkers got seized, sealed, hunted, interrogated, and imprisoned. Some resisted. Some surrendered. Some tried to explain that the legacy had called to them. Few people believed them.","\"That belief,\" the old man said, \"is what led to the imprisonment and sealing of the Voidwalker Clan.\"","Freya’s expression turned colder up in the sky. The thousands of Voidwalker descendants behind her let out a faint wave of restrained fury.","The old man continued, \"I agreed to be sealed because I thought my clan had committed an unforgivable failure. I thought that if I resisted, the five clans would collapse completely. I thought accepting the seal would preserve the inheritance, protect the remaining bloodlines, and stop an all-out war.\"","His voice dropped even quieter.","\"But time turned out to be a cruel teacher.\"","The starry screen faded a bit, leaving only the glow of the sacred legacy.","\"Slowly, over the long years of being sealed, I started to think. I started to recall the faces of those who’d taken the sacred legacy. I remembered their eyes. Their fear. Their madness. Their devotion. Their pain. I remembered the way the sacred legacy moved before they ever did.\"","His eyes sharpened.","\"And eventually, I began to wonder whether the real fault belonged not to my clan members, but to the sacred legacy itself.\"","A heavy silence spread. This time, even the four sacred ancestors didn’t rush to respond.","The younger geniuses of the Four Sacred Clans looked completely stunned. This wasn’t the history they’d been taught. They’d been told the Voidwalker Clan betrayed the First Progenitor and stole the sacred legacy. They’d been told the fifth clan was sealed because of greed.","They’d been told the four clans protected the world from traitors. Nobody had told them the sacred legacy might have influenced the Voidwalker Clan first. Nobody had told them the Voidwalker Ancestor himself once believed in the punishment. Nobody had told them the whole tragedy might have started because the sacred legacy wanted something.","Rose stared at the old man in disbelief.","Angelina Valerius stood silently, her eyes deep in thought.","Freya didn’t look surprised. Maybe she’d already known part of it. Maybe she’d carried this weight for a long time.","Max, though, was thinking about something else. The Dimensional Keeper legacy. The starry fist. The sealed worlds inside his body. The way the abandoned Voidwalker end had reacted to him. The way the First Progenitor’s statue had glowed. The way everyone kept repeating the words stolen sacred legacy.","A thought took shape in his mind.","’Could the Dimensional Keeper legacy be the sacred legacy of the First Progenitor?’","His dragon head lowered slightly as he looked at the Voidwalker Ancestor.","\"What happened to the sacred legacy?\"","His voice came out deep and heavy in his dragon form, rumbling across the arena. Everyone turned toward him. The question sounded simple, but it carried a thought many others hadn’t dared to voice."]},{"number":1975,"title":"Chapter 1975: The Lost Legacy!","paragraphs":["The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at Max for a moment. Then he shrugged lightly. For such a solemn moment, the gesture felt strangely casual.","\"It was lost.\"","The arena froze.","Max’s eyes narrowed. \"Lost?\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor nodded. \"Since the day those Voidwalker members took it, the sacred legacy of the First Progenitor never returned to the Five Sacred Clans. Those who fled disappeared. The legacy disappeared with them. Every trace of it became uncertain.\"","The Valerius leader immediately shouted, unable to hold back. \"Lies! The sacred legacy isn’t lost. It’s standing right in front of us!\"","His furious gaze locked onto Max.","The Ashbourne leader jumped in right after. \"Max Voidwalker carries it. That star-like dimensional power, the awakening of the fifth end, the way the First Progenitor’s statue reacted, all of it proves he’s inherited the stolen sacred legacy.\"","The Ravenhart leader’s eyes flashed. \"The Voidwalker bloodline has been hiding it all these years.\"","The Evercrest leader, still pale from his injuries, pointed at Max with a trembling, furious hand. \"That’s why the abandoned end reacted. That’s why our bloodlines got suppressed. That’s why the statue lit up. Max Voidwalker has the sacred legacy.\"","Several elders from the Four Sacred Clans started shouting too.","\"He has to be sealed!\"","\"The legacy has to be recovered!\"","\"The Voidwalker Clan has been hiding it this whole time!\"","\"They came back because the sacred legacy found a new vessel!\"","The mood surged back toward chaos. Freya’s eyes turned cold, and the thousands of Voidwalker descendants above the arena immediately tightened their formation.","Max’s dragon eyes narrowed dangerously.","But before things could explode, the Voidwalker Ancestor raised his hand.","\"Wrong.\"","His voice stayed calm. But it cut through every accusation at once.","The Four Sacred Clan leaders glared at him.","The Valerius leader said coldly, \"You still want to deny it?\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor shook his head. \"If Max carried the true sacred legacy of the First Progenitor, the statue would have lit up the second he entered the domain of the Four Sacred Clans.\"","The arena quieted down a bit.","The Voidwalker Ancestor continued, \"He entered Evercrest territory earlier. He passed through the outer spatial layers. He stood in front of the statue. He walked into the Bloodline Legacy Battle arena. The statue reacted faintly, yes, but it didn’t fully wake up. The fifth end didn’t light up. The bloodlines of the Four Sacred Clans weren’t fully suppressed.\"","Max remembered that moment clearly. When he’d first seen the First Progenitor’s statue, his blood had reacted violently, but the statue itself had stayed silent. He’d hidden that reaction from Rose, and nothing more happened until he used the star-like fist formed by the Dimensional Keeper legacy.","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at the glowing statue.","\"The true sacred legacy was bound too deeply to the First Progenitor’s statue and the five-clan arena. If it had come back in its real form, this place would have known instantly. The statue would have woken up before Max even stepped onto the battlefield. All five ends would have reacted together. The old seal would have opened on its own without him needing to strike the ground.\"","The four sacred ancestors stayed silent. None of them denied it. That silence made a lot of elders and descendants uneasy.","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s gaze returned to Max.","\"What Max carries is indeed oddly similar to the sacred legacy of the First Progenitor. The dimensional resonance, the sealed-world feel, the way it suppresses the five bloodline branches, and the way it can wake the forgotten end are all too close to ignore.\"","Max listened carefully. The old man’s expression grew more serious.","\"But it isn’t the true sacred legacy.\"","The whole arena held its breath.","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at the starry traces flickering around Max’s massive dragon body.","\"What he carries is different. Older in feeling, but not necessarily older in time. Higher in structure, but not something I can fully pin down. It resembles the sacred legacy, yet it isn’t bound by the First Progenitor’s seal. It answers to the Voidwalker bloodline, but it doesn’t belong only to the Voidwalker Clan. It can touch the statue, but it isn’t controlled by it.\"","His eyes narrowed faintly.","\"And when it woke up through his fist, I felt something even the sacred legacy never once gave me.\"","Max’s heart stirred.","The Voidwalker Ancestor said slowly, \"Whatever Max carries isn’t the stolen sacred legacy of the First Progenitor.\"","The old man paused. Then his voice dropped lower and heavier.","\"It’s something beyond it.\"","A wave of shock ran through the arena. Even the four sacred ancestors’ expressions shifted.","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at Max with eyes full of confusion, caution, and a trace of awe.","\"Something even I can’t understand.\"","Max frowned.","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s final words echoed through the arena like a stone dropped into a bottomless well.","Something beyond the sacred legacy. Something even he couldn’t understand. Those words should have cleared things up, but instead they only made everything more confusing.","Max’s enormous dragon body stayed still at the center of the shattered battlefield, but his mind kept racing. From the moment he’d entered the hidden domain of the Four Sacred Clans, he’d felt something off.","When he first saw the statue of the First Progenitor, his blood had reacted violently. When Aelric awakened the Evercrest forbidden bloodline, Max’s foundation had stirred again. When he gathered the power of the Dimensional Keeper legacy into his fist and struck the ground, the statue had glowed, the abandoned fifth end had woken up, and the bloodlines of the Four Sacred Clans had been suppressed.","All of it pointed in one direction. His Dimensional Keeper legacy was connected to this place. It was connected to the Four Sacred Clans. It was connected to the Voidwalker Clan. It was connected to the First Progenitor’s statue.","Yet now the Voidwalker Ancestor, the very ancestor of the clan that had guarded the sacred legacy most closely, was saying that what Max carried wasn’t the true sacred legacy of the First Progenitor.","Max’s dragon eyes narrowed. ’Maybe it wasn’t the Dimensional Keeper legacy reacting; maybe it was my Voidwalker Bloodline reacting to them...’"]},{"number":1976,"title":"Chapter 1976: Who was the First Progenitor?!","paragraphs":["The Dimensional Keeper legacy had always felt strange. It wasn’t like his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline. It wasn’t like his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. It wasn’t even like his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline.","Those powers had sources, traits, and growth paths he could at least make sense of. The Dimensional Keeper legacy was different. It felt vast, ancient, and hidden in a way that went beyond ordinary inheritance.","Back then, he’d just assumed the legacy was powerful beyond his current level. Now he wasn’t so sure.","He looked toward the statue of the First Progenitor. It still glowed. Its eyes stayed closed, but the star-like light running through its stone body made it look less like a lifeless sculpture and more like a sleeping presence that had noticed him. That reaction made Max uneasy. Not because it felt hostile, but because it felt too familiar, like the statue was waiting for something from him.","’The true sacred legacy was lost after those Voidwalker members ran off with it,’ Max thought. ’But why did the legacy choose the Voidwalker Clan in the first place? Why did it possess them? Why did it leave the five clans? And if what I carry isn’t that legacy, why does it feel so similar?’","His thoughts dug deeper. What was the sacred legacy even about?","The Voidwalker Ancestor had said it wasn’t a simple martial art or inheritance technique. It was the deepest thing the First Progenitor had left behind, the core inheritance holding the reason the five sacred bloodlines existed and the secret of what the First Progenitor truly carried.","That sentence bothered Max the most. The reason the five sacred bloodlines existed. The secret of what the First Progenitor truly carried.","Max slowly lifted his dragon head and looked at the glowing stone figure towering over the arena.","Who was the First Progenitor?","Rose had told him the Four Sacred Clans didn’t descend from Primordials like ordinary humans. They descended from the First Progenitor. Their forbidden bloodlines came from him. The Four Sacred Clans, or really the Five Sacred Clans, could rival Primordials despite lacking Primordial Race bloodline because they carried that forbidden source instead.","But what kind of man could stand outside the Primordial origin of humanity? If humans came from Primordials who’d given up their bloodline to become mortal and have children, where did the First Progenitor fit into that history?","Was he a Primordial? Was he something beyond the Primordials? Was he the first true human? Or was he something else entirely?","Max felt the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline inside him stir faintly as he turned the question over. The bloodline he’d gotten from the Primarchs made him closer to the laws of the world and multiplied his strength tenfold, but standing in front of the First Progenitor’s statue, even that Primarch-level bloodline had reacted. It hadn’t rejected the statue, but it hadn’t fully submitted either. It had trembled, pulsed, and seemed to acknowledge that the figure before it wasn’t simple.","The more Max thought about it, the heavier his heart grew.","’Even the Primordials might not know the full truth about this man.’","The arena stayed silent around him. The young geniuses of the Four Sacred Clans were still frozen in shock after hearing the Voidwalker Ancestor’s explanation. Cassian Valerius sat with his brows tightly furrowed, no longer carrying the calm pride of the Sun-Crowned Heir.","Draven Ashbourne’s fists stayed clenched, but for once there was no battle hunger on his face, only rare seriousness. Seraphine Ravenhart’s silver-purple eyes looked distant, as if she were digging through fragments of fate and memory for something her clan had never let her see.","Aelric Evercrest’s face stayed pale, his loss to Max now almost forgotten next to the collapse of the history he’d believed his whole life.","Rose stayed quiet too. She looked at the Evercrest elders around her, then at the Voidwalker Ancestor, then at Max’s huge dragon body. She’d grown up cast aside by the Evercrest Clan for being born without the forbidden bloodline, but now she realized the sacred clans’ cruelty wasn’t simply personal.","Their entire history had been built on selective memory, fear, and punishment that could stretch across countless generations.","Freya stayed in the sky, watching Max. Her expression was calm, but Max could feel the emotion underneath it. She’d known more than him.","Maybe she’d carried this weight for years. Maybe she’d wanted to tell him and couldn’t. Maybe she’d warned him not to reveal the Voidwalker name because she knew exactly what would happen if the Four Sacred Clans recognized him.","Max wanted to ask her everything. But first, he needed to understand the core of this mystery.","His gaze went back to the Voidwalker Ancestor. The old man stood above the awakened fifth end, still looking at Max with a complicated expression. There was relief in his eyes, but also uncertainty. He clearly knew a lot about the Voidwalker Clan and the sacred legacy, yet even he didn’t fully understand the power Max carried.","Max spoke slowly. His dragon voice rumbled across the arena, deep and heavy.","\"If what I carry isn’t the sacred legacy, then what happened to the real sacred legacy after it disappeared?\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s gaze shifted slightly.","Max continued, \"You said those Voidwalker members were influenced by it. You said they stole it and fled. You said it was lost after that. But something like that shouldn’t just vanish forever. If it was powerful enough to possess members of your clan and make them break the seal of the Five Sacred Clans, it must have had a purpose.\"","The old man didn’t answer right away.","Max’s eyes moved back to the statue.","\"And what exactly is the sacred legacy? What did the First Progenitor leave behind that made the Five Sacred Clans guard it for countless years? What did it choose those Voidwalkers for? What did it actually want?\"","His voice dropped lower.","\"And who was the First Progenitor?\"","That final question hit the arena harder than all the rest. The younger descendants immediately looked toward the statue. To them, the First Progenitor had always been a sacred figure, the origin of their clans, the source of their forbidden bloodlines, and the ancestor whose name stood above everything else.","But because he was so sacred, nobody ever questioned him. They worshiped him. They inherited from him. They carried his bloodline branches. But how many of them actually knew who he really was?","The four sacred ancestors grew visibly tense. The Valerius ancestor’s sacred light flickered. The Ashbourne ancestor lowered his gaze. The Ravenhart ancestor’s shadow went still. The Evercrest ancestor looked at the statue with an expression carrying both reverence and fear.","Their reactions told Max one thing clearly. They knew something. Maybe not everything, but enough to make them afraid of the question."]},{"number":1977,"title":"Chapter 1977: A Way To Find The Truth!","paragraphs":["The Voidwalker Ancestor sighed softly.","\"Those are the same questions I asked myself after being sealed.\"","His voice came out quieter than before.","\"At first, I thought the sacred legacy was simply an inheritance the First Progenitor left behind for one chosen descendant. I thought it held a supreme path, a forbidden technique, or maybe the complete source of the five bloodline branches. That’s what all five clans believed. We protected it because our ancestors told us to. We feared it because our bloodlines feared it. We worshiped it because it came from him.\"","The old man looked up at the glowing statue.","\"But after the legacy moved on its own, after it influenced members of my clan and disappeared, I started to question whether we’d ever really understood it at all.\"","A cold silence spread through the arena.","The Voidwalker Ancestor continued, \"The sacred legacy may not have been waiting for an inheritor the way we believed. It may have been waiting for a condition. A moment. A bloodline resonance. Or maybe a door that only the Voidwalker branch could open.\"","Max’s heart stirred. A door.","The old man noticed the reaction, and his eyes deepened.","\"That’s why I said what you carry is similar. The sacred legacy also gave me the feeling of hidden worlds, sealed dimensions, and doors beyond ordinary law. But yours is different. The sacred legacy was tied to the First Progenitor. It was anchored here. It belonged to the origin of the Five Sacred Clans.\"","He paused.","\"What you carry feels like something that can touch that origin, but isn’t limited by it.\"","Max frowned even more. That answer didn’t solve the mystery. It only made it bigger.","The Valerius leader suddenly spoke up, unable to hold back. \"This is absurd. You’re trying to protect him by making his legacy sound different.\"","The Ashbourne leader followed coldly, \"Whether it’s the original sacred legacy or something beyond it, it’s connected to the stolen inheritance. That alone makes him dangerous.\"","The Evercrest leader’s eyes burned with anger. \"Max Voidwalker woke up the abandoned end and suppressed our bloodlines. You expect us to believe this has nothing to do with the sacred legacy?\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at them with mild annoyance.","\"I didn’t say it has nothing to do with the sacred legacy.\"","The leaders fell silent.","The old man continued, \"I said it isn’t the sacred legacy.\"","Freya’s voice came down from the sky. \"There’s a difference.\"","The Ravenhart leader’s expression darkened, but she didn’t argue the point.","Max’s mind sharpened even further. Not the sacred legacy, but connected to it. Similar, but beyond it. Able to awaken the fifth end, but not recognized immediately by the statue. Able to suppress the Four Sacred Clan bloodlines, yet not controlled by the First Progenitor’s arena.","’Then maybe the Dimensional Keeper legacy isn’t something the First Progenitor left behind. That goddess told me an inheritor of the Dimensional Keeper legacy gets born every era, which in a way means it has nothing to do with the Five Sacred Clans,’ Max thought.","Max stared at the statue. For the first time, that calm stone face seemed to carry more mystery than majesty.","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s voice rang out again.","\"I can’t tell you what happened to the true sacred legacy after it was taken. I only know it never came back to us. I can’t tell you its final purpose because I no longer believe any of the Five Sacred Clans ever truly understood it. As for the First Progenitor...\"","The old man stopped. The entire arena held its breath. Even the four sacred ancestors looked at him with solemn expressions.","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s gaze turned distant.","\"He wasn’t just the ancestor of the Five Sacred Clans.\"","The statue glowed brighter.","\"He was the first being who carried the forbidden source that let us stand beside Primordials without being Primordials themselves.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed.","The old man looked at him.","\"And if your legacy is truly beyond the sacred legacy he left behind, then Max Voidwalker, you may one day uncover something even the First Progenitor never managed to reveal.\"","The arena sank into a suffocating silence. Max looked at the glowing statue, the awakened fifth end, the four sacred ancestors, Freya in the sky, and the Voidwalker Ancestor standing beneath the dark star.","For the first time since this mystery began, he realized the truth about the Voidwalker Clan might only be the outer layer. The deeper secret wasn’t just what happened to the sacred legacy. It was what the sacred legacy had been connected to in the first place.","\"Hmph, we’ll know once this kid touches the statue of the First Progenitor,\" the head of the Valerius Clan said.","His voice came out cold and full of distrust, but the moment he said it, several people in the arena fell into thought.","The Valerius ancestor, still standing in the dim glow of sacred white-gold light, narrowed his eyes and looked at the statue. After a brief silence, he nodded slowly. \"That’s true. If Max Voidwalker really carries the Sacred Legacy of the Five Sacred Clans, the statue of the First Progenitor won’t stay silent once he touches it.\"","The Ashbourne ancestor crossed his arms, his crimson-black aura still rolling around him like a sleeping battlefield. \"The sacred legacy came from the First Progenitor’s deepest source. It can’t hide from his statue. If the boy carries it, the statue will react in a way none of us can deny.\"","The Ravenhart ancestor’s shadow feathers drifted around her veil as her soft voice spread across the arena. \"The statue already reacted to his star-like power, but that reaction was indirect. It woke up when he struck the arena and stirred the hidden formation beneath the fifth end. Touching the statue directly will be different. It’ll show whether his legacy actually belongs to the First Progenitor’s sacred inheritance or just resembles it.\"","The Evercrest ancestor looked at Max with cold eyes, his expression still ugly since the Evercrest patriarch had been badly hurt earlier. \"If the statue confirms he carries the sacred legacy, then no excuse from the Voidwalker Clan will save him.\"","Freya’s eyes turned cold up above the arena. The thousands of Voidwalker descendants surrounding the Bloodline Legacy Battle arena let out a faint pressure at the same time, but Freya didn’t speak right away.","She just stared at the Evercrest ancestor as if memorizing his words. The threat she’d placed over the four clans’ descendants hadn’t gone anywhere. If they tried to use this test as an excuse to attack Max again, she wouldn’t hesitate.","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at the statue for a long while.","The enormous stone figure kept glowing faintly. Its closed eyes shone with a star-like light, and the lines across its body pulsed in rhythm with the awakened fifth end. It looked calm, majestic, and mysterious, as if it had been waiting through countless years for exactly this moment.","No one could say for sure whether the statue’s current reaction came from Max, the Voidwalker end, the Dimensional Keeper legacy, the starry fist, or the old history that had finally come to light."]},{"number":1978,"title":"Chapter 1978: Touching The Statue!","paragraphs":["The Voidwalker Ancestor nodded slowly.","\"That method can confirm some things, yes.\"","His voice carried across the arena.","\"If Max carries the true Sacred Legacy of the Five Sacred Clans, the statue of the First Progenitor will recognize it the moment he touches it directly. The sacred legacy and this statue were connected at their deepest roots. Even if the legacy changed hands, even if it hid for countless years, that connection wouldn’t just disappear.\"","Max listened quietly. His enormous black dragon body stayed at the center of the shattered arena. The chaotic flames between his scales had slowly dimmed, but his golden-black eyes were still sharp. He looked at the statue, then at the Voidwalker Ancestor, then up at Freya.","He was curious about the test. More than curious. This whole time, he’d been trying to make sense of the Dimensional Keeper legacy. It had saved him against Revona’s Null Origin Tide. It had resonated with the abandoned Voidwalker end.","It had woken up the First Progenitor Arena. It had suppressed the bloodlines of the Four Sacred Clans. Even the Voidwalker Ancestor said it resembled the sacred legacy without actually being it.","If touching the statue could hand him even one more clue, Max wanted to try it.","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at him.","\"Go back to your human form first.\"","Max’s dragon eyes shifted slightly.","The old man explained, \"The statue doesn’t just respond to power. It responds to bloodline, origin, and legacy. Your true dragon form is powerful, but it’s also wrapped heavily in the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline. If you approach the First Progenitor’s statue like that, the reaction might get muddled. Let the statue sense your human foundation clearly.\"","Max understood. His massive dragon head lowered slightly.","\"Fine.\"","The moment he said it, black-gold light began shrinking around his huge body. The transformation didn’t happen all at once. His wings folded first, turning into streams of chaotic black light that flowed back into his back.","His enormous claws pulled in, the sharp talons reshaping into fingers. The black-gold scales across his body dissolved one after another, sinking beneath his skin like fragments of night returning to blood. His long dragon body condensed, compressed, and reshaped itself under his control.","The pressure of the true dragon form faded. The enormous shadow covering the battlefield disappeared.","A few breaths later, Max stood in human form again at the center of the ruined arena. His white hair fell around his shoulders. His black robe was slightly torn from the earlier fighting, but his aura stayed calm and terrifyingly steady.","Faint traces of black-gold scales still flickered at the edges of his skin before vanishing completely. The five Divine Veins closed one by one, and the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline settled back into silence.","The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline also pulled back beneath his foundation, leaving only a faint ancient pulse that even the sacred ancestors couldn’t fully read.","Dragonheart appeared in his hand for a moment, then disappeared again.","He wasn’t here to fight now. He was here to test the truth.","Freya watched him from the sky, and for the first time since her arrival, a trace of worry crossed her eyes.","\"Max,\" she said.","He looked up at her.","Her voice softened. \"Be careful.\"","Max smiled faintly. It was a small smile, but it was real.","\"I will.\"","For a moment, the tense mood of the arena seemed to shift. The younger geniuses of the Four Sacred Clans watched this exchange in silence.","Many of them had only known Max as the champion of the Cosmic Ascension Conference, the terrifying outsider who’d beaten Aelric, injured an Evercrest clan head, turned into a huge black dragon, and dragged ancient history back into the light.","But now, watching Freya talk to him like that, they suddenly remembered that underneath all those impossible powers, Max was also someone’s little brother.","That thought made the whole situation feel stranger. More human. More dangerous.","The head of the Valerius Clan looked impatient. \"Enough delays. Let him touch the statue.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s gaze turned cold. \"He’ll touch it because he chooses to. Not because you order him to.\"","The Valerius head’s expression darkened.","The Valerius ancestor raised a hand slightly, stopping him from saying more.","\"Let the test proceed.\"","The four sacred ancestors stayed alert. Their auras didn’t press down on Max, but none of them relaxed either.","The four clan heads watched with heavy suspicion, while the elders of Valerius, Ashbourne, Ravenhart, and Evercrest formed protective barriers around their descendants. Above the arena, Freya’s Voidwalker forces stayed in formation, ready to act if the Four Sacred Clans tried anything.","Rose stood near the Evercrest platform, still surrounded by elders, though no one dared pressure her as harshly now. Too much had happened.","The Evercrest elders no longer knew how to treat her. She’d brought Max here as her representative, and that one decision had cracked open an ancient secret buried beneath the Four Sacred Clans themselves.","Angelina Valerius stood silently at the edge of the battlefield, looking at Max with a complicated expression. The Bloodline Legacy Battle had completely lost its original meaning.","This was no longer a contest between young geniuses fighting for legacy merit. It had turned into a trial of history, bloodline, and inheritance, with the statue of the First Progenitor about to sit in judgment.","Max started walking toward the statue. Each step echoed clearly across the arena. The shattered battlefield repaired itself faintly beneath his feet, not because the formation had fully healed, but because the First Progenitor Arena seemed to be clearing a path for him.","The light from the abandoned fifth end followed him quietly. The other four clan platforms trembled slightly as he passed, and the forbidden bloodlines inside many descendants stirred again, though not as violently as before.","Max’s own blood pulsed in response.","The closer he got to the statue, the more clearly he felt that strange connection. It wasn’t the same feeling as when he tapped into his Primordial Bloodline. It wasn’t the same as using the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline. It wasn’t the same as the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline either. It felt deeper, stranger, and far harder to put into words.","The Dimensional Keeper legacy inside him stayed silent for now, but that silence felt deliberate, like a hidden beast watching another ancient existence from behind a closed door.","Max stopped in front of the statue. The First Progenitor towered above him. The stone face stayed calm, the eyes closed, the hand resting near its side. Up close, Max could feel the ancient pressure much more clearly. It didn’t crush him. It didn’t push him away. It just watched, even with its eyes still shut.","The entire arena held its breath.","The Valerius head said coldly, \"Touch it.\"","Max ignored him. He looked up at the statue and narrowed his eyes slightly.","’If you really know something, then show me.’","Then he raised his hand. Slowly, under the eyes of the Five Sacred Clan descendants, the four sacred ancestors, the Voidwalker Ancestor, Freya, Rose, Angelina, and the countless elders gathered across the arena, Max placed his palm against the statue of the First Progenitor.","For one breath, nothing happened.","Then..."]},{"number":1979,"title":"Chapter 1979: Meeting the First Progenitor!","paragraphs":["For one breath, the whole arena seemed to stop with Max’s hand resting against the statue of the First Progenitor.","Then another breath passed. Nothing happened. The statue stayed still. The glowing lines that had appeared earlier across its stone body didn’t grow brighter. The closed eyes stayed shut. The enormous hand resting near its side didn’t move.","The ancient pressure around the statue didn’t shift in any obvious way. Even the awakened Voidwalker end, which had been pulsing with dark starry light, went strangely quiet, as if it too were waiting for a response that refused to show up.","Three seconds passed. Five seconds passed. Ten seconds passed.","The expressions of the Four Sacred Clan leaders began to shift. The head of the Valerius Clan narrowed his eyes, and a cold smile slowly crept onto his face. The Ashbourne head crossed his arms with a heavy snort.","The Ravenhart head looked thoughtful, while the Evercrest head’s pale, injured face showed a flash of unwillingness mixed with relief. If Max really carried the Sacred Legacy of the Five Sacred Clans, there should have been an undeniable reaction the moment he touched the statue directly.","The statue had once anchored the sacred legacy. No disguise, no bloodline concealment, and no Voidwalker trick should have been able to hide the legacy from it at this close range.","Yet nothing had happened.","The younger descendants of the Four Sacred Clans started whispering again.","\"So he really doesn’t carry the sacred legacy?\"","\"But his power woke up the fifth end.\"","\"Maybe the Voidwalker Ancestor was right. It’s similar, but not the true sacred legacy.\"","\"Then what exactly is that power?\"","Rose watched nervously from the Evercrest side, her hands clenched tight. Freya stood in the sky without a word, but her gaze never left Max for even a moment.","The Voidwalker Ancestor stood above the fifth end, his eyes deep and solemn as he watched the statue. Even he seemed uncertain now, since the statue’s silence confirmed part of what he’d said, yet it also deepened the mystery around Max.","But while everyone outside saw nothing, Max was no longer standing in front of the statue.","The moment his palm touched the stone, his senses had shifted. At first, there was only silence. Then the arena, the clan platforms, Freya’s figure in the sky, Rose, Angelina, the four ancestors, the Voidwalker Ancestor, and the countless watching descendants all vanished without warning.","Max found himself standing in a different world.","There was no arena here. No clan platforms. Only a vast land beneath a starless sky. The ground under his feet looked like dark glass, smooth and endless, reflecting faint points of light that didn’t exist above him.","In the distance, countless doors floated in the air, each one half open, each one showing a different scene behind it. Some doors showed burning worlds. Some showed silent oceans. Some showed battlefields littered with broken stars. Some showed empty palaces. Some showed nothing but darkness.","Max’s eyes narrowed.","’A dimensional world.’","He felt it right away. This place wasn’t an ordinary illusion, and it wasn’t a simple memory either. It carried the feel of sealed dimensions, hidden passages, and forgotten worlds.","It felt far too close to the deeper sensation of the Dimensional Keeper legacy, but at the same time it felt weaker, older, and incomplete, like a shadow left behind by someone who’d once touched the same source.","Then a man appeared in front of him. He stood with his back to Max, dressed in a plain long robe.","His hair was long and dark, falling down his back with no crown or ornament. His figure looked calm, not tall enough to seem monstrous, not majestic enough to resemble an emperor, yet the moment Max saw him, an invisible weight settled over his heart.","The man didn’t need to release any aura. His presence alone carried a stillness heavy enough to stop the countless floating doors from moving.","Max recognized him instantly. It was the man from the statue. The First Progenitor.","The man slowly turned around. His face matched the statue’s exactly, but alive. His eyes were deep and quiet, holding neither arrogance nor hostility. He looked at Max for a long time, as if measuring not his strength, but something hidden deeper in his foundation.","Then he spoke.","\"So you’re the one carrying the current legacy.\"","Max frowned. The current legacy. Those words hit harder than he expected.","He didn’t answer right away. His body stayed tense, and his senses spread out through the strange world around him.","He couldn’t feel the arena outside anymore. He couldn’t feel Freya, Rose, or the Voidwalker Ancestor. He could still feel his own powers, but they sat quiet here, as if this world had no intention of suppressing him, yet could still see every part of him clearly.","Max looked at the man in front of him and asked, \"Who are you?\"","The man’s expression didn’t change.","\"My descendants called me many things,\" he said. \"Ancestor. Origin. First Progenitor. Founder of the Five Sacred Clans.\"","He paused. Then his voice dropped quieter.","\"But before all of that, I was the first inheritor of the Dimensional Keeper Legacy.\"","Max’s pupils contracted. For a moment, even his breathing stopped.","The first inheritor of the Dimensional Keeper Legacy.","His mind raced. The forbidden bloodline of the Five Sacred Clans, the sacred legacy of the First Progenitor, the Voidwalker Clan’s connection to hidden worlds, the statue’s reaction to him, the strange pulse in his own blood, and the way his Dimensional Keeper legacy had responded to the arena all started fitting together in a way that finally made sense.","The forbidden bloodline everyone had been talking about this whole time hadn’t simply come from a man blessed by some unknown power. It came from the first inheritor of the Dimensional Keeper Legacy.","The First Progenitor wasn’t the source of the legacy. He’d been one of its inheritors. His descendants became the Five Sacred Clans because his bloodline had been transformed by that inheritance.","That was why they weren’t like ordinary humans descended from Primordials. That was why their forbidden bloodlines could rival Primordial Race bloodlines. That was why their sacred legacy felt similar to the Dimensional Keeper legacy without actually being the same thing.","It wasn’t the original source. It was a trace, an inheritance fragment, or maybe a bloodline echo left behind by the first inheritor.","Max’s frown deepened.","’So that’s why my blood reacted.’"]},{"number":1980,"title":"Chapter 1980: Anover!","paragraphs":["The Dimensional Keeper legacy hadn’t reacted because the First Progenitor was its master. It had reacted because the statue belonged to a previous inheritor. The bloodlines of the Five Sacred Clans hadn’t trembled because Max carried their stolen legacy.","They’d trembled because his current Dimensional Keeper legacy stood closer to the true source than their inherited fragments ever could.","The First Progenitor looked at him quietly, then smiled. There was no pride in that smile. Only pity.","\"I didn’t expect it,\" he said softly. \"Even after countless generations, one of my descendants would once again become the carrier of the legacy.\"","Max’s eyes sharpened. \"One of your descendants?\"","The man nodded. \"Voidwalker blood flows in you. Faint after so many generations, mixed with plenty of other powers, buried beneath bloodlines even I can’t fully read, but it’s still there.\"","Max fell silent. He’d known his surname carried danger. He’d known Freya had hidden their identity for a reason. But hearing the First Progenitor himself call him a descendant carried a completely different weight.","The man’s pity deepened.","\"To ordinary people, inheriting something like this looks like fortune,\" the First Progenitor said. \"To ambitious cultivators, it looks like destiny. To clans, forces, and races, it looks like supremacy. But I know better.\"","His gaze drifted toward the countless doors floating behind him.","\"The Dimensional Keeper Legacy isn’t a blessing.\"","Max’s expression turned serious.","The First Progenitor looked back at him.","\"It’s cursed by fate.\"","The strange world grew colder. The floating doors trembled faintly, and for a moment Max thought he heard sounds coming from behind them. Screams. Prayers. Battles. Collapsing worlds. Chains dragging across empty space. Then all of it vanished.","The First Progenitor continued, \"Those who carry this legacy get pulled into conflicts that started long before they were even born. Doors will open in front of them whether they want to walk through or not. Powers hidden from ordinary law will take notice of them. Enemies they never wronged will hunt them down. Allies will fear them. Bloodlines will react to them. Ancient seals will wake up because of them. Fate itself will try to use them as a key.\"","Max’s heart sank slightly. That explanation sounded far too close to everything that had already happened to him. He hadn’t chosen to get tangled up in the Five Sacred Clans’ ancient history. He’d simply come to help Rose.","Yet because of the Dimensional Keeper legacy, the whole buried conflict had woken up, the Voidwalker Clan had come back out into the open, and the sacred ancestors had nearly gone to war.","The First Progenitor’s voice turned more urgent.","\"You have to be careful out there. The legacy will make you stronger, but every step forward will drag out things that should’ve stayed asleep. Don’t trust every door it opens. Don’t assume every inheritance that recognizes you is on your side. And most importantly.\"","His expression suddenly shifted. For the first time, the calm in his eyes cracked. He looked past Max, as if seeing something through him, something distant and terrifying.","\"Watch out for Anover-\"","Before he could finish the sentence, the world shattered. Max’s vision blurred. The endless dark glass land disappeared. The floating doors vanished. The First Progenitor’s figure broke apart into countless fragments of light.","The next instant, Max found himself standing back in the Bloodline Legacy Battle arena.","His hand was still touching the statue. His body hadn’t moved. The arena looked exactly as it had before. The Four Sacred Clan leaders were watching him with suspicion. The four sacred ancestors stayed silent.","The Voidwalker Ancestor stood above the fifth end with a deep gaze. Freya still hovered in the sky with thousands of Voidwalker descendants. Rose watched anxiously from the Evercrest side. Angelina stood at the edge of the battlefield, her expression unreadable.","To everyone else, nothing had happened. Not one flash. Not one tremor. Not one shift in pressure. The statue of the First Progenitor didn’t glow brighter. Its closed eyes stayed shut. The five ends of the arena didn’t resonate. The bloodlines of the Four Sacred Clans weren’t suppressed any further.","In the eyes of everyone watching, the test had failed to prove that Max carried the Sacred Legacy of the Five Sacred Clans.","The Valerius Clan head sneered.","\"As expected.\" His voice carried across the arena. \"The statue didn’t react.\"","The Ashbourne head narrowed his eyes. \"So he doesn’t carry the sacred legacy.\"","The Ravenhart head looked thoughtful. \"At least not the one sealed by the Five Sacred Clans.\"","The Evercrest head gritted his teeth in frustration, but even he couldn’t deny what everyone had just witnessed. \"Then whatever he carries is something else.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at Max carefully.","Freya noticed something strange too. Max’s expression had changed. It was subtle, but she knew him too well. Everyone else saw the statue stay silent and assumed nothing had happened. Freya saw the look in Max’s eyes, the brief heaviness in his gaze, and the tension hidden beneath his calm face.","Something had happened. Only Max had seen it.","Max slowly pulled his hand back from the statue. His face stayed composed, but his mind was still echoing with that unfinished warning.","’Anover.’","He had no idea who or what Anover was. But the First Progenitor, the first inheritor of the Dimensional Keeper Legacy, had warned him with actual fear in his eyes. That alone was enough to make Max hold onto the name.","He turned away from the statue and looked at the crowd. The test had cleared him of carrying the sacred legacy in front of everyone.","But it had handed Max a far more dangerous truth. The sacred legacy of the Five Sacred Clans wasn’t the Dimensional Keeper Legacy. It was only something left behind by the first person who’d once carried it. And now, countless generations later, Max had inherited the current legacy.","A legacy cursed by fate.","’Even the goddess had warned me the Dimensional Keeper Legacy was cursed by fate, that every inheritor of it had died a brutal death.’ Max’s expression turned solemn.","That, combined with the fear he’d just seen in the First Progenitor’s eyes, told him he hadn’t experienced much of what this so-called curse of fate really meant yet.","Max slowly turned away from the statue of the First Progenitor. His hand had already left the stone, but the cold feeling from that strange world still lingered on his palm. The unfinished warning kept echoing in his mind.","Anover.","He didn’t know whether that was a person, a race, an organization, a world, or something even stranger, but he’d already carved the name into his memory.","Anything capable of making the First Progenitor, the first inheritor of the Dimensional Keeper Legacy, show fear right before his remnant vanished wasn’t something Max could afford to ignore.","Even so, now wasn’t the time to reveal what he’d seen. To everyone else, the test had ended without any reaction. The statue hadn’t brightened. Its eyes hadn’t opened.","The five clan platforms hadn’t resonated. The bloodlines of the Four Sacred Clans hadn’t been suppressed any further. In the eyes of the whole arena, the conclusion seemed obvious.","Max didn’t carry the Sacred Legacy of the Five Sacred Clans. The four clan heads and the four sacred ancestors could no longer use that excuse to imprison him."]},{"number":1981,"title":"Chapter 1981: A Shocking News!","paragraphs":["Max’s gaze swept across them. The head of the Valerius Clan still looked cold, but the arrogance in his eyes had faded a little. The Ashbourne head frowned deeply, clearly unwilling to accept the result but unable to deny what had just happened in front of everyone.","The Ravenhart head stayed silent, her gaze thoughtful, as if she suspected there was more to this than met the eye. The Evercrest head, his chest still carrying faint traces of the wound Max had given him, looked at Max with anger, humiliation, and restrained killing intent.","Above them, the four sacred ancestors stayed equally silent, their expressions complicated. They’d wanted to test whether Max carried the stolen sacred legacy.","The test had failed to prove that. Worse for them, it had happened in front of the entire younger generation, in front of the Voidwalker remnants, in front of Freya, and in front of the awakened fifth end.","They could still distrust Max. They could still fear the Dimensional Keeper Legacy. But they couldn’t openly claim he was the vessel of the stolen sacred legacy anymore without making themselves look unreasonable.","Max’s voice broke the silence.","\"Now that it’s proven I don’t carry your sacred legacy.\"","His tone stayed calm, but every word carried clearly across the arena. The four clan heads all looked at him at once.","Max continued, \"Will you unseal the Voidwalker Clan?\"","That question hit the arena like a thunderclap. Many descendants of the Four Sacred Clans widened their eyes. The elders frowned sharply. Several clan guards tightened their grips on their weapons without meaning to.","Even Rose looked at Max in surprise, and Angelina Valerius’s expression shifted slightly. Freya, though, stayed still in the sky, her gaze locked on the four sacred ancestors. The thousands of Voidwalker descendants behind her didn’t say anything, but their auras turned colder.","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at Max. For the first time since revealing the buried history, the old man’s expression softened again.","The question was simple. But it carried a weight that had lasted countless years. The Voidwalker Clan had been sealed because of the sacred legacy.","The Four Sacred Clans had called them traitors, imprisoned their people, abandoned their platform, erased their name, and hunted down or suppressed their remaining bloodline branches.","Now the very reason they’d used to imprison Max had been weakened in front of everyone. If Max didn’t carry the stolen sacred legacy, the old accusation couldn’t be thrown around so carelessly anymore.","The Valerius head’s face darkened.","\"Unseal the Voidwalker Clan?\" he repeated coldly.","The Ashbourne head snorted. \"You think one test is enough to overturn countless years of judgment?\"","Freya’s eyes turned icy.","Max looked at him calmly. \"Then what would be enough? You accused me of carrying the stolen legacy. I touched the statue. Nothing happened. Your own ancestors said the statue would react if I carried it.\"","The Ravenhart head narrowed her eyes. \"The test only proves you don’t carry the true sacred legacy. It doesn’t erase the old crimes of the Voidwalker Clan.\"","Max’s eyes turned colder. \"Old crimes committed by some members influenced by the sacred legacy itself.\"","The Evercrest head gritted his teeth. \"You’re in no position to lecture us about our own history.\"","Max smiled faintly. \"Your history seems like it could use some correcting.\"","The mood tightened at once. Several Evercrest elders glared furiously at him, while Ashbourne warriors let out low growls of battle intent. The Valerius descendants looked offended, and even a few Ravenhart elders frowned.","But among the younger geniuses, the reactions weren’t so simple. Cassian Valerius stayed silent. Draven Ashbourne looked at Max with a strange expression, no longer dismissing him as just arrogant. Seraphine Ravenhart watched everything with deep, thoughtful eyes. Aelric Evercrest stood pale and wounded, but even he seemed shaken by how far this had all gone.","The Valerius ancestor slowly raised his hand, and the sacred clan heads immediately fell silent.","His old eyes settled on Max.","\"The sealing of the Voidwalker Clan can’t be undone with one sentence,\" he said. \"Even if you don’t carry the sacred legacy, even if the history is more complicated than our descendants ever knew, the Voidwalker Clan still broke the seal and caused the sacred legacy to disappear. A matter like this can’t be settled in the middle of an arena.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s gaze turned cold. \"How convenient.\"","The Ashbourne ancestor said heavily, \"Voidwalker, don’t test our patience. We agreed to stop the fighting because the truth needed to come out. That doesn’t mean the old judgment has been erased.\"","Freya’s voice came down from the sky. \"Then when will it be erased?\"","No one answered right away. The silence itself was the answer.","Max’s expression turned colder.","Before the four clan heads could say anything more, a disturbance suddenly broke out from outside the arena. A spatial gate tore open violently near the outer entrance of the Bloodline Legacy Battle grounds.","The gate looked unstable, trembling as if whoever opened it had used emergency authority without waiting for proper clearance. Several guards immediately stepped forward, but before they could stop the newcomer, a figure rushed through the gate and stumbled into the arena.","It was a messenger of the Four Sacred Clans. His robe was torn. His face was pale. Blood stained the corner of his mouth, and his aura felt chaotic, as if he’d crossed several emergency transfer formations back to back without stabilizing himself. The moment he appeared, everyone’s attention snapped toward him.","The Valerius head frowned. \"What’s the meaning of this?\"","The messenger didn’t even manage a proper bow at first. He nearly collapsed to the ground, caught himself with one hand, and then lifted his head with a look of panic that instantly tightened the chests of several elders.","\"Masters!\" His voice cracked. \"Devils!\"","The entire arena went still. That single word carried a chill sharp enough to cut through every argument going on.","The messenger’s eyes were wide with panic.","\"Devils have appeared in the Divine Realm!\"","For a moment, no one reacted. Then the whole arena exploded with disbelief.","\"Impossible!\"","\"How could devils show up in our Divine Realm?\"","\"How could they have even reached our universe?\"","\"Devils? Here?\"","\"Are you certain?\"","The messenger trembled under the weight of every gaze fixed on him.","The Valerius head’s expression changed drastically. \"What did you just say?\"","The Ashbourne head stepped forward, his voice booming across the arena. \"How could devils get into our universe? Weren’t all the devils supposed to have been wiped out long ago?\"","\"That’s impossible!\" an elder shouted. \"The ancient records clearly say the last devil army was completely exterminated!\"","\"The remaining devils were sealed outside the universe!\"","\"There shouldn’t be a single devil left anywhere in the Divine Realm!\"","\"Did the border seals break?\"","\"Who opened the passage?\"","The descendants of the Four Sacred Clans were completely shaken, their faces filled with disbelief, fear, and confusion. Many of them had grown up hearing that the devils were eradicated from the Divine Realm countless years ago.","To them, devils weren’t a living race that could just suddenly come back. They were remnants of an ancient catastrophe, enemies already destroyed and buried in history."]},{"number":1982,"title":"Chapter 1982: Devils!","paragraphs":["’Devils?!’ Max’s expression also turned dark. He hadn’t forgotten what had happened to his world just because of a drop of blood from a being called True Origin Devil.","Even the four sacred ancestors had lost their calm.","The Valerius Ancestor’s sacred light erupted around him. \"Impossible. Every devil in the Divine Realm was killed during the final war. The surviving remnants were driven out of the universe and sealed away. How could they possibly show up here?\"","The Ravenhart Ancestor’s eyes narrowed sharply. \"Unless the ancient records were wrong.\"","\"No,\" the Ashbourne Ancestor said coldly, though a trace of shock slipped into his voice. \"The records weren’t wrong. I personally saw the remnants of the devil army get destroyed.\"","The Evercrest Ancestor’s spatial roots twisted violently around him. \"Then how did they get into our universe?\"","The messenger forced himself to keep talking.","\"They attacked several planets in a small star realm out near the outer regions. Local forces intercepted them, but the damage has already spread across multiple worlds. We got urgent reports through the sacred warning network. The aura’s been confirmed.\"","He swallowed hard.","\"They’re not corrupted beasts. They’re not abyssal cultivators. They’re not some disguised race.\"","His voice trembled even more.","\"They’re devils.\"","The arena fell into an even deeper uproar.","\"Impossible!\"","\"Devils can’t exist in the Divine Realm!\"","\"They were all killed!\"","\"How could they have survived this long?\"","\"Were they hiding somewhere in the universe?\"","\"Could they have come from another universe?\"","\"Is there a passage connecting our universe to the outside?\"","The shock was so massive that even the dispute between Max and the Voidwalker Clan got pushed aside for the moment. This wasn’t an internal conflict, an old historical dispute, or a bloodline accusation you could argue through ancestors and legacy tests. This was something that should have been impossible.","Devils had appeared in their Divine Realm. In their universe.","The younger descendants, already shaken by the Voidwalker truth, now turned pale for an entirely different reason. Many of them had only ever heard about devils in old war scriptures and ancestral warnings.","They’d been taught the devil race was exterminated from the Divine Realm long ago, that the final devil army had been destroyed, and that no devil could ever come back.","Yet now a messenger stood in front of them claiming devils had attacked their planets.","The clan heads’ expressions shifted sharply.","The Valerius head stared at the messenger. \"You’re certain of this?\"","\"Yes!\" the messenger replied urgently. \"The aura was verified through the ancient devil-suppression formations. There’s no mistake. They’re genuine devils.\"","The Ashbourne head’s face turned grim. \"How many?\"","\"The exact number’s unknown. The first report says only a vanguard showed up, but their power was strange. Some were weak, but a few were strong enough to destroy planetary defense formations. Local star realm forces are holding them off for now, but they’ve asked for immediate reinforcement.\"","The Ravenhart head’s gaze darkened. \"Were there any warning signs before the attack?\"","The messenger shook his head. \"None that we detected. They just appeared suddenly, like a crack opened out of nowhere.\"","Max’s heart stirred.","A crack opened out of nowhere.","The First Progenitor’s unfinished warning echoed in his mind again.","’Watch out for Anover.’","His eyes narrowed slightly. He didn’t know if this devil attack was connected, but the timing felt far too strange to ignore.","The Evercrest head looked toward the four ancestors. \"Ancestors, how is this even possible? If all the devils were killed in the Divine Realm long ago, where did these come from?\"","The four sacred ancestors didn’t answer right away. Their expressions had turned extremely grave. Even the Voidwalker Ancestor frowned deeply. The old man had lived through the ancient era and understood better than anyone just how terrifying the devil race had once been. If devils had truly come back to the Divine Realm, the consequences would be unimaginable.","Freya’s face changed slightly too, and the thousands of Voidwalker descendants in the sky shifted their formation, their earlier hostility toward the Four Sacred Clans momentarily pushed aside by the sudden news.","The Valerius Ancestor looked at the messenger. \"Which star realm?\"","The messenger answered quickly. \"The Veyrith Star Realm. It’s a small star realm under the protection route of the eastern Divine Realm forces.\"","The Ashbourne Ancestor’s eyes turned fierce. \"How long ago did this start?\"","\"The first attack began less than an hour ago,\" the messenger said. \"The report reached us through emergency channels only moments ago.\"","The Ravenhart Ancestor’s shadow feathers trembled faintly. \"Less than an hour, and they’ve already hit several planets.\"","The Evercrest Ancestor’s spatial roots coiled tight. \"This isn’t some random breach.\"","The Valerius Ancestor’s expression turned terrifyingly cold.","\"If the devils were truly wiped out of the Divine Realm, then their appearance means someone opened a passage into our universe.\"","His gaze swept across the arena.","\"Or something from outside the universe found a way in.\"","A heavy pressure spread across the arena. The Bloodline Legacy Battle had already collapsed into chaos, but now even that chaos felt beside the point.","The dispute between the Four Sacred Clans and the Voidwalker Clan was still unresolved.","Max still stood at the center of a mystery tangled up with the Dimensional Keeper Legacy, the sacred legacy, and the First Progenitor. The Voidwalker Clan was still sealed, and the four sacred ancestors hadn’t agreed to release them.","But the universe had moved before any of that could get settled.","Devils had appeared. Not in some distant, forgotten realm. Not on an ancient battlefield. They’d appeared right in the Divine Realm, inside their own universe. The entire Divine Realm might be about to get shaken to its core.","Max slowly looked up at Freya. Freya looked back down at him. Neither of them said anything. But both understood this was no ordinary interruption.","The Four Sacred Clans had just been forced to face their buried past. And at that exact moment, an ancient enemy that should have gone extinct had returned to their universe.","The head of the Valerius Clan looked at Max, then at the Voidwalker Ancestor, then at the messenger. His expression was ugly, but even he understood the situation had changed.","The argument over the Voidwalker Clan wouldn’t end here. But for now, the whole arena had been hit with news carrying the weight of war.","The messenger lowered his head and said in a shaking voice, \"Masters, the forces of the Veyrith Star Realm are asking for immediate aid. If reinforcements don’t arrive soon, the devils might break through their defense line and spread into nearby star realms.\"","The arena sank into a grim silence. No one dared treat the devils as some distant legend anymore. They’d entered their universe. They’d attacked their planets. And no one knew how they’d come back.","The four sacred ancestors traded grave glances. The Voidwalker Ancestor looked toward the glowing statue of the First Progenitor.","Max’s hand slowly curled into a fist. And in his mind, one name echoed again.","Anover."]},{"number":1983,"title":"Chapter 1983: Sending Help!","paragraphs":["The arena stayed silent after the messenger’s report.","For a few moments, even the ancient conflict between the Four Sacred Clans and the Voidwalker Clan seemed to fade beneath the weight of that one word.","Devils.","The Bloodline Legacy Battle had already turned into something far bigger than a battle between young geniuses, but the sudden news of devils in the Divine Realm changed the whole mood.","This was no longer just about buried history, a stolen sacred legacy, or whether the Voidwalker Clan should stay sealed. If devils had really entered their universe again, every supreme force in the Divine Realm would have to respond.","The Valerius head’s expression turned sharp and decisive.","\"Summon the third and seventh sacred response teams,\" he ordered right away. \"Send them to the Veyrith Star Realm immediately. Have them assist the local forces, stabilize the planetary defense lines, rescue important survivors where possible, and eliminate every devil they find.\"","Several Valerius elders bowed at once.","\"Yes, Clan Head!\"","The Ashbourne head stepped forward, his earlier anger at Max still there but pushed down beneath battle intent. \"Send Ashbourne’s Blood-Iron Vanguard with them. If devils have really shown up, ordinary reinforcements might not cut it. Let our warriors find out whether these devils are remnants, scouts, or part of something bigger.\"","The Ravenhart head’s eyes stayed cold and thoughtful. \"Ravenhart will send a shadow-prophecy unit too. We need information more than we need blind slaughter. Find out where the crack opened, whether it’s stable, whether it can be traced, and whether there are signs of a second breach.\"","The Evercrest head, still wounded from Max’s attack, clenched his teeth and gave his own order. \"Evercrest will send a spatial sealing team. If the devils came through a crack, space itself needs to be locked down before more of them cross over.\"","The messenger lowered his head quickly, relief flashing across his pale face.","The Valerius head looked at the gathered elders and younger participants. \"Don’t assume this is only our problem. The Primordial Race and the other top first-rate forces should have gotten the warning by now too. If they have any sense, they’ll have already sent a team or two.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\"But we are the Four Sacred Clans. We don’t wait for others to move before we act.\"","The Ashbourne head said coldly, \"Whoever’s chosen to go needs to treat this like a real battlefield, not an investigation. If the report’s true, kill every devil you see. Only capture one if it doesn’t risk the defense line.\"","The Ravenhart head added, \"And don’t trust how they look. Devils aren’t always mindless monsters. Some can think, deceive, possess, and hide their aura. Confirm with devil-suppression formations before you bring anything back.\"","The Evercrest head looked at his people. \"Prepare cross-realm spatial gates. I want the first reinforcement team gone within a hundred breaths.\"","The whole arena moved at once. Elders passed on orders. Sacred clan guards rushed out. Formation masters started activating emergency platforms behind the clan seats. Several young geniuses who’d been watching the Bloodline Legacy Battle with pride and excitement now stood with grim faces, realizing the stage they’d come to compete on might soon turn into a battlefield soaked in devil blood.","Cassian Valerius rose from his seat. \"I’ll go too.\"","The Valerius head looked at him. \"You’re one of the main participants in the Bloodline Legacy Battle here.\"","Cassian’s expression didn’t change. \"The battle’s already been interrupted. If devils have returned, sitting here to protect our reputation doesn’t mean anything.\"","Draven Ashbourne laughed coldly and stood as well. \"Good. I was getting tired of listening to old secrets anyway. Devils sound more interesting.\"","The Ashbourne head glared at him. \"This isn’t a hunt for your entertainment.\"","Draven’s grin faded slightly, but the battle intent in his eyes only grew stronger. \"I know.\"","Seraphine Ravenhart also stood, her silver-purple eyes distant. \"I’ll go with the Ravenhart unit and give them whatever help I can.\"","Aelric Evercrest tried to stand, but the wound from Max’s Black Dragon Cataclysm Breath flared up again, twisting his face with pain. An Evercrest elder immediately pressed a hand on his shoulder.","\"You’re not going anywhere in your condition.\"","Aelric’s expression turned ugly, but he didn’t argue. Today’s defeat had already crushed enough of his pride.","Max watched all of this in silence. The speed at which the Four Sacred Clans switched from internal conflict to war preparation explained why they’d stayed at the top for so long. Their history might be ugly, and their treatment of the Voidwalker Clan might be built on lies and fear, but when an ancient enemy showed up, they moved without hesitation.","Freya descended slightly from the sky, though she didn’t dismiss the thousands of Voidwalker descendants surrounding the arena. Her gaze moved from the emergency formations to Max, then to the Voidwalker Ancestor.","The Voidwalker Ancestor had stayed quiet since the messenger appeared. His expression looked grave, but there was something deeper in his eyes too. Recognition. Worry. A faint trace of old fear.","Max noticed it right away. The old man knew more about the devils than he’d let on. Maybe everyone from that ancient generation did.","The Valerius ancestor looked at the Voidwalker Ancestor and said coldly, \"Don’t think this matter is finished.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor replied calmly, \"I never thought it was.\"","The Ashbourne ancestor’s voice came out heavy. \"The question of unsealing the Voidwalker Clan gets discussed once the devil situation is contained.\"","Freya’s eyes narrowed. \"Discussed?\"","The Ravenhart ancestor looked at her. \"Don’t push too far. You threatened the descendants of the Four Sacred Clans in our own arena. If it weren’t for the devil report, this place would already be drowning in blood.\"","Freya’s expression didn’t change. \"If it weren’t for your attempt to seal my brother, we wouldn’t even be here.\"","The Evercrest ancestor’s spatial roots stirred, but the Valerius ancestor raised his hand slightly and kept things from getting worse.","\"Enough.\" His gaze turned toward the emergency gates forming behind the clan platforms. \"The devil matter comes first.\"","Nobody liked that conclusion. Not the Four Sacred Clans. Not Freya. Not the Voidwalker descendants. Not even Max. But for now, it was the only thing keeping the arena from turning into a battlefield between five ancient bloodlines while devils attacked planets somewhere else."]},{"number":1984,"title":"Chapter 1984: Voidwalker Clan!","paragraphs":["At that moment, the Voidwalker Ancestor looked at Max and Freya.","\"Come with me.\"","Max turned toward him.","Freya’s eyes shifted slightly. \"Where to?\"","The old man glanced once at the glowing statue of the First Progenitor, then at the abandoned fifth end beneath him.","\"Somewhere we can talk peacefully.\"","The four sacred ancestors immediately looked at him.","The Valerius ancestor’s eyes narrowed. \"Voidwalker.\"","The Ashbourne ancestor’s aura pressed down slightly. \"What are you planning?\"","The Ravenhart ancestor’s shadow moved silently, as if trying to trace whatever path the old man was about to open.","The Evercrest ancestor said coldly, \"You expect us to let you take him away after everything that just happened?\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at them without fear.","\"You’ve got devils in the Veyrith Star Realm, a possible breach into the universe, panic spreading through your own descendants, and emergency teams waiting on your orders. If you’d still rather spend your attention watching an old remnant talk with two descendants of my clan, then maybe the Four Sacred Clans really have gotten weaker than I thought.\"","The words came out calm, but they hit hard.","The four ancestors’ expressions darkened. The four clan heads looked furious too, but none of them stopped him right away. He was right. They were suspicious of him. They were suspicious of Max. They were suspicious of Freya and the thousands of Voidwalker descendants surrounding the arena. But right now, they had something much worse to deal with.","Devils had shown up in the Divine Realm. If the first reinforcements arrived too late, the Veyrith Star Realm might fall apart. If the crack widened, nearby star realms could descend into chaos. If this was just the start of a bigger invasion, every delay would cost them dearly.","The Valerius ancestor finally said, \"Don’t leave the sacred domain.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor smiled faintly. \"This whole domain used to belong to five clans. Don’t talk to me like I’m some guest here.\"","The Valerius ancestor’s face turned colder, but he didn’t push further.","Freya raised her hand. The Voidwalker formations above the arena shifted, but didn’t pull back completely. The thousands of descendants stayed in position, though their pressure eased slightly. It was a quiet message. They wouldn’t strike first if the Four Sacred Clans didn’t, but they wouldn’t drop their guard either.","Max looked toward Rose. She still stood near the Evercrest platform, surrounded by elders who no longer dared treat her too harshly.","Too much had changed. Her representative had beaten Aelric, injured the Evercrest head, awakened the fifth sacred end, and dragged out the truth about the Voidwalker Clan. The Evercrest elders could hate her, blame her, or fear her, but they couldn’t dismiss her as some useless castaway anymore.","Rose met Max’s gaze. For a moment, she looked conflicted. This whole disaster had started because she’d asked him for help, yet it had also given her something she’d never expected. The Evercrest Clan could no longer hide behind a spotless sacred image. Their history had cracked wide open in front of everyone.","Max gave her a slight nod. It wasn’t a promise that everything was fixed. It was just a sign that he hadn’t forgotten why he’d come.","Rose’s eyes softened slightly.","The Voidwalker Ancestor raised his hand, and the abandoned fifth end opened beneath him. Not a door. Not a gate. A ring of dark starry light unfolded in the air, filled with layers of space twisting inward like a passage leading into a sealed dimensional chamber. It carried the same feel as the fifth end, but deeper, older, and far more private.","Freya descended from the sky and landed near Max. For the first time in years, brother and sister stood close enough to touch.","Max looked at her. Freya looked back. There was so much between them. Questions, secrets, warnings, years apart, the sudden reveal of the Voidwalker Clan, and the heavy shadow of the devils’ return. But underneath all of that, there was relief.","Freya reached out and touched his shoulder lightly.","\"How have you been, Maxy?\" she asked softly.","Max gave a faint smile and said solemnly, \"I’m fine. Just a little shocked that the Voidwalker name has this much history behind it.\"","Freya sighed. \"I’m sorry. Father asked me not to tell you about any of this. But who could’ve guessed you’d end up at the Four Sacred Clans anyway.\"","Max laughed lightly.","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at the two of them, and for a moment, the heaviness in his eyes eased. Then he turned and stepped into the starry passage.","\"Come. We don’t have much time.\"","Max and Freya followed him. Behind them, the Bloodline Legacy Battle arena stayed tense and chaotic. The Four Sacred Clans kept preparing their reinforcements. Emergency gates lit up. Chosen teams gathered. The four sacred ancestors watched the Voidwalker passage with suspicion, but they didn’t stop it.","The starry passage closed behind Max and Freya without a sound.","One moment, the chaos of the Bloodline Legacy Battle arena had been right behind them, full of emergency orders, rushing elders, glowing spatial gates, and the heavy pressure of the Four Sacred Clans preparing for the sudden devil invasion. The next moment, all of it disappeared, replaced by a silence so complete that even Max’s own breathing sounded loud.","They’d arrived inside a chamber.","It wasn’t large in the ordinary sense, yet it felt vast because of how much space had been folded inside it. The walls were made of dark stone that shimmered faintly like a night sky, and countless silver lines ran across them in circular patterns, forming dimensional rings that overlapped one another. Some rings rotated slowly.","Some were cracked. Some sat dim, as if they hadn’t woken up in countless years. At the center of the chamber floated a black crystal sphere, and inside it drifted tiny points of light that looked like sealed worlds sitting in silence.","Max’s eyes narrowed. The aura here felt different from the arena. The Bloodline Legacy Battle arena carried the weight of the Five Sacred Clans and the statue of the First Progenitor, but this chamber carried only one thing.","Voidwalker."]},{"number":1985,"title":"Chapter 1985: Oliver Voidwalker!","paragraphs":["Every stone, every mark, every folded layer of space, and every star-like point of light carried that same deep bloodline resonance that had been stirring inside Max ever since the abandoned fifth end woke up. Even Freya, who’d stayed calm in front of the Four Sacred Clans and their ancestors, went quieter after stepping into this place.","The Voidwalker Ancestor walked ahead of them. His figure still looked faint, and Max could tell this wasn’t his full body. He was a remnant, a projection, or something bound to this sealed chamber. But inside this place, his presence felt far more stable. The dark starry light around him no longer flickered like a dying flame. Instead, it moved with calm strength, as if the chamber itself were lending him support.","He stopped in front of the floating black crystal sphere and turned around, his eyes moving from Freya to Max.","Then he asked, \"Was your father named Oliver Voidwalker?\"","The question was simple. But the moment it came out, something inside Max tightened.","Oliver Voidwalker. His father. The man who’d disappeared into the Celestial Thorn Abyss along with his mother, Divine Queen Caelira. The man Max had been searching for, tied up in the mysteries of the second elven faction, the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, Freya, and now the Voidwalker Clan itself.","Max looked at Freya. Her expression had shifted slightly too. For a brief moment, the strong, cold woman who’d surrounded the Bloodline Legacy Battle arena with thousands of Voidwalker descendants looked less like a commander and more like a daughter hearing her father’s name after far too long.","Both of them nodded.","\"Yes,\" Max said.","Freya’s voice followed quietly. \"Oliver Voidwalker is our father.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor closed his eyes. For a long moment, he said nothing. The chamber stayed silent, but the silver rings on the walls trembled faintly, as if the name Oliver had stirred up some old memory buried inside the Voidwalker inheritance.","At last, the old man sighed.","\"Oliver was a good kid.\"","His voice came out softer now. Not the voice of an ancient being facing down four sacred ancestors. Not the voice of a sealed remnant exposing buried history in front of an entire arena. It was the voice of an old man remembering someone from his own bloodline.","\"One of the few who managed to escape,\" he continued.","Max’s eyes sharpened. \"Escape from where?\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at him. \"From the sealing net of the Four Sacred Clans. After the main Voidwalker bloodline got sealed, not every branch was captured at once. Some outer descendants had already been sent away before the final judgment. Some hid in folded worlds. Some changed their names. Some joined other races and forces. Some got hunted down over the years. Some survived.\"","His gaze moved to Freya.","\"Your father was one of the ones who survived.\"","Freya’s hands tightened slightly. \"He never told us everything.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor nodded. \"He probably couldn’t. The Four Sacred Clans placed bloodline restrictions, memory traps, and tracking seals across a lot of old records. Those who escaped carried pieces of the history, but talking too much could expose them. In the end, most of our descendants learned to stay quiet, not because they were ashamed of the Voidwalker name, but because silence kept them alive.\"","Max’s expression turned colder. Freya had once warned him never to say the Voidwalker name out loud. Now he finally understood why.","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at him with a trace of regret. \"Oliver should’ve been able to stand here himself one day. He had talent. He had patience. More importantly, he had the stubbornness that runs through our clan. But fate wasn’t kind to him.\"","Max’s eyes deepened. \"My parents are still alive.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at him.","Max continued, \"They’re imprisoned in the Celestial Thorn Abyss.\"","A heavy silence filled the chamber. Freya looked at Max sharply. She’d known more than most, but hearing Max say it so plainly still sent a flash of pain through her eyes.","The Voidwalker Ancestor’s expression turned complicated.","\"Celestial Thorn Abyss,\" he repeated softly. \"So that’s where they ended up.\"","Max stepped forward. \"You know it?\"","\"I know of that prison,\" the old man said. \"That place isn’t simple. If Oliver’s really imprisoned there, rescuing him won’t be easy. The elves are one of the three races of the Divine Realm, and they’re not to be underestimated.\"","Max’s gaze didn’t waver. \"I know.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at him for a long moment. Then he nodded.","\"Good. At least you understand that much.\"","He turned and raised his hand toward the floating black crystal sphere. The sphere trembled, and the silver rings across the walls started rotating faster. A path opened at the far end of the chamber, but it wasn’t a normal door. It was a corridor made from overlapping dimensional rings, each one leading deeper into a hidden part of the abandoned Voidwalker end.","The old man spoke again.","\"Since both of you are Oliver’s children, and both of you carry the Voidwalker bloodline, you’re members of my clan.\"","His gaze turned solemn.","\"And members of my clan shouldn’t stand before the world without our inheritance.\"","Max and Freya both looked at him.","The Voidwalker Ancestor continued, \"The Four Sacred Clans called us traitors and sealed our main bloodline, but they never destroyed the true inheritance of the Voidwalker Clan. They could abandon our end. They could erase our name from public history. They could imprison our people. But the inheritance chamber was hidden away before the final sealing, and only a descendant with the true Voidwalker bloodline can get inside.\"","The corridor of dimensional rings brightened. Max could feel it calling to him from within. It wasn’t as overwhelming as the Dimensional Keeper Legacy. It didn’t make his soul tremble the way the First Progenitor’s remnant had. But it still felt powerful, ancient, and deeply tied to his blood. It felt like a road that had been waiting for him since before he even knew his surname mattered.","Freya’s eyes changed too. She’d clearly known about the Voidwalker remnants, and she’d brought thousands of them to the arena, but from her expression, even she hadn’t stepped into this place before.","The Voidwalker Ancestor noticed her look and nodded faintly. \"The outer descendants held onto what they could, but this chamber was sealed with me. Neither of you could enter until the abandoned fifth end woke up again. Max’s arrival opened up what had been buried for so many years.\"","Freya glanced at Max. Max looked back at her. For a moment, neither of them spoke."]},{"number":1986,"title":"Chapter 1986: Awakening of the Voidwalker Bloodline!","paragraphs":["The Voidwalker Ancestor started walking toward the dimensional corridor.","\"Come.\"","The two siblings followed. As they stepped into the corridor, the world around them stretched out. Max felt like he was walking through several spaces at once. One step crossed a dark bridge under a starry sky. Another step passed through a silent hall filled with floating weapons.","Another step moved across a battlefield where countless Voidwalker warriors had once stood with silver rings glowing behind them. None of these were real places. They were memory fragments built into the inheritance path, letting descendants feel the weight of the clan before receiving its legacy.","The deeper they went, the stronger the bloodline resonance grew.","At last, the corridor opened. Max and Freya arrived in front of an enormous door. The door was black, but it wasn’t lifeless. Silver dimensional rings were carved across its surface, and at the center sat the same dark star symbol that had appeared above the abandoned fifth end.","Beneath that symbol were countless names carved into the stone. Some names shone bright. Some sat dim. Some had been scratched away by old battle scars. Some were covered in cracks, as if their owners had died while the clan was being sealed.","The Voidwalker Ancestor stopped in front of the door.","\"This is the Inheritance Chamber of the Voidwalker Clan.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\"Inside lies what’s left of our techniques, bloodline arts, spatial scriptures, dimensional weapons, ancestral records, and the paths left behind by our greatest descendants. Some are complete. Some are broken. Some are dangerous. Some might not even recognize the current era anymore. But they belong to our clan, and now they belong to both of you.\"","Max looked at the door. His heart, which had stayed steady even in front of the four sacred ancestors, stirred slightly.","This felt different from the Primordial Bloodline. Different from the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline. Different from the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. Different even from the Dimensional Keeper Legacy.","This wasn’t some power he’d seized through a trial or awakened through battle. This was his family’s inheritance.","Freya stood beside him, silent.","The Voidwalker Ancestor placed one hand on the door. The dark star symbol lit up. Then he looked back at them.","\"Max Voidwalker. Freya Voidwalker.\"","His old eyes carried pride, sorrow, and expectation all at once.","\"You both carry the blood of my Voidwalker Clan, but without the inheritance, that bloodline is going to waste in you two. Go on and inherit what belongs to the Voidwalker Clan.\"","He looked at Max next.","\"And Max, make sure you use this chance to push your strength up to the Law Manifestation Realm. Devils have invaded our universe, and there’s no telling how big this invasion is going to get. You’ll need every bit of strength you can get right now. An upheaval is coming, and no one knows when the whole Divine Realm might turn into a battlefield. So push your strength up as fast as you can.\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor paused for a moment, his gaze deepening.","\"I’m sure the Primordial Race has plans for you and the other top geniuses, but you still need to be strong enough to actually use those opportunities when they come. Opportunity without strength is just another kind of danger.\"","Then he stepped aside.","\"Now go ahead.\"","Max looked at the open door. Beyond it wasn’t a room in the ordinary sense. The inside of the Inheritance Chamber looked like a silent universe sealed beneath stone. There was no floor at first glance, only a path made of dark crystal floating above a vast starry abyss.","Countless silver rings rotated slowly in the darkness, each one holding an image, a scripture, a weapon’s shadow, a memory fragment, or a sealed bloodline mark.","Some rings showed ancient Voidwalker warriors standing before broken worlds. Some held diagrams of dimensional passages and folded spaces. Some showed battle arts where a single step crossed ten thousand realms. Some contained defensive techniques that turned the body into a hidden world. Some held killing arts that cut through distance itself.","Max felt his blood stir. Not his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline. Not his Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline. Not even his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline. It was the buried Voidwalker blood inside him.","That bloodline had always been there, but it had stayed faint, hidden, and underdeveloped. It had reacted to the First Progenitor, to the abandoned fifth end, to the Dimensional Keeper Legacy, and to Freya, but it had never fully awakened as a complete inheritance. It was like a sword buried in stone, sharp by nature but never drawn from its sheath.","Now that sheath was opening.","Freya stepped forward first. Max followed beside her. The moment both of them crossed the threshold, the enormous black door closed behind them with a deep sound, cutting off the outside chamber. The Voidwalker Ancestor stayed beyond the door, but his voice still reached the Inheritance Chamber, as if the entire place carried his will.","\"Don’t resist the bloodline memories. Let them enter you. What you can inherit depends on your foundation, your bloodline purity, your soul, your comprehension, and your own path. Don’t chase everything. Let the inheritance choose what belongs to you.\"","Max and Freya stopped at the center of the dark crystal path. A moment later, the starry abyss below them woke up.","Boom!","Two pillars of dark silver light burst up from beneath their feet. One wrapped around Freya. One wrapped around Max.","Freya’s eyes closed almost immediately, and a powerful Voidwalker aura surged out of her body. Her silver-white hair lifted without any wind, and countless small dimensional rings formed around her like halos.","She’d already cultivated the Voidwalker bloodline for years, but even for her, this inheritance felt different. The moment it entered her, her aura turned purer, deeper, and more complete.","Max also closed his eyes as the inheritance entered his body. It didn’t feel like ordinary energy. It felt like memories made of blood.","Ancient Voidwalker scriptures appeared in his mind. Dimensional seals, spatial folding arts, hidden world construction methods, bloodline movement techniques, and secret combat footwork poured into him like a river flowing out of a forgotten era.","He saw ancestors stepping through battlefield cracks, warriors hiding entire armies inside pocket dimensions, assassins striking from impossible distances, elders sealing off worlds between breaths, and children of the clan training in front of the dark star symbol.","Then the bloodline inheritance reached deeper. It touched his own foundation. The Voidwalker blood inside him woke up.","For a moment, Max felt like an invisible door had opened in his veins. Power that had been asleep since birth started flowing through his body."]},{"number":1987,"title":"Chapter 1987: Into the Law Manifestation Realm!","paragraphs":["It didn’t clash with his other bloodlines.","The Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline stayed wild and ancient. The Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline stayed radiant and noble. The Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline stayed vast and close to the laws of the world. But the Voidwalker bloodline moved differently from all of them.","It didn’t roar. It opened paths.","His body suddenly felt full of doors, layers, corridors, and hidden spaces. His Dimensional Sovereign Body reacted first, resonating so violently that the entire inheritance pillar around him shook.","The Dimensional Keeper Legacy, which had stayed quiet since the First Progenitor’s test, stirred again, but this time it didn’t push back against the Voidwalker inheritance. It watched, accepted it, and let it settle in, as if the bloodline inheritance were a smaller branch returning to a much larger tree.","Max’s aura began rising. At first, the change came slowly. Then it turned terrifying.","His cultivation, sitting at the 6th level of the Law Refinement Realm, started loosening up. The energy from the inheritance didn’t behave like ordinary spiritual power. It was extremely pure, carrying bloodline source energy, dimensional law resonance, and ancestral will. It didn’t just pour into his realm. It refined the framework of his laws, widened his foundation, and pushed his cultivation upward with an almost frightening smoothness.","[Law Refinement Realm 7th Level]","Max’s aura expanded. The dark crystal path beneath his feet trembled. The inheritance rings around him rotated faster, and several ancient Voidwalker scriptures broke apart into streams of light before sinking into his body.","[Law Refinement Realm 8th Level]","The starry abyss below the path stirred. Silver rings formed around Max’s body, layer upon layer, as if multiple hidden dimensions were being born around him. His understanding of space, distance, concealment, and dimensional passage deepened rapidly. What he’d once grasped through the Dimensional Sovereign Body and the Dimensional Keeper Legacy now had the foundation of an actual bloodline system behind it.","[Law Refinement Realm 9th Level]","The Inheritance Chamber shook. Freya, still absorbing her own inheritance, opened her eyes slightly and glanced at Max. Even though she’d expected him to gain a lot, watching his cultivation climb this fast still made surprise flash across her eyes. But she soon closed her eyes again, since her own inheritance was reaching a critical point too.","[Law Refinement Realm 10th Level]","Max’s aura reached the peak of the Law Refinement Realm. The laws around him began to tremble.","Normally, breaking into the Law Manifestation Realm wasn’t a simple thing. It wasn’t just about piling up energy.","A cultivator had to refine their laws to the point where they could manifest outward, forming a true law image, a visible law phenomenon, or a manifestation that could directly influence the world. Plenty of geniuses got stuck at the peak of the Law Refinement Realm for years because their foundation wasn’t complete enough to support a stable manifestation.","But Max was different. His foundation ran too deep. The Emotion Severing Path, Divine King Punishment, the Devouring Flames Domain, the Dimensional Sovereign Body, the Dimension of Soul, the Dimension of Light, the Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, the Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline, the five Divine Veins, Dragonheart, and now the Voidwalker bloodline inheritance had all pushed his foundation to a terrifying level.","He didn’t lack laws. He had too many of them.","The moment he hit the peak of the Law Refinement Realm, the barrier to the Law Manifestation Realm appeared in front of him. Then it cracked.","Outside the Inheritance Chamber, the Voidwalker Ancestor suddenly lifted his head, his expression shifting.","\"This...\"","The next instant, a terrifying roar of laws erupted from inside the Inheritance Chamber.","Boom!","The entire abandoned Voidwalker end shook. Then the entire First Progenitor Arena shook. Then the entire hidden domain of the Five Sacred Clans trembled.","In the Bloodline Legacy Battle arena, the Four Sacred Clans had been preparing emergency reinforcements for the Veyrith Star Realm. Spatial gates were glowing, sacred response teams were gathering, and elders were shouting urgent orders. But the moment Max’s breakthrough aura erupted, everyone froze and turned toward the abandoned fifth end.","The dark star above the Voidwalker platform blazed brighter than it ever had. A pillar of light tore into the sky. Inside that pillar, laws began manifesting one after another.","First came space. The sky above the arena folded into countless transparent layers. Doors appeared in the air, each one leading to a different hidden distance. Silver rings rotated around them, each carrying the aura of the Voidwalker bloodline.","Then came emotion. An invisible sword light passed through the sky, and for a brief instant, countless people felt their anger, fear, hatred, pride, and killing intent go strangely still. It wasn’t suppression by force. It was severance. The Emotion Severing Path manifested as a pale, invisible sword shadow hanging in the sky like a blade aimed at the heart of every living being below.","Then came punishment. Seven-colored lightning gathered out of nothing and formed the vague image of a divine tribunal above the arena. A throne appeared inside the thunder, vast and solemn, as if some ancient law of judgment had come down to inspect everyone below.","Then came black flames. A dark domain opened up behind the lightning. Devouring flames surged inside it, swallowing stray energy from the air and turning the edges of the sky black. The flames didn’t spread recklessly, but their hunger still made even the elders uneasy.","Then came dragon law. A massive black dragon shadow appeared behind the pillar of light, coiling through the sky with chaotic golden patterns across its scales. It opened its eyes and released a silent pressure that made the beast-blooded descendants and dragon-related cultivators in the sacred domain tremble.","Then came light. A radiant white-gold glow spread across one side of the sky, not quite the same as the Valerius sacred sun, but purer, softer, and noble in a different way. The Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline manifested briefly as a domain of dawn-like light that made several Evercrest and Valerius elders stare at it in astonishment.","Then came soul. The sky seemed to sink into a boundless inner world. A vast, silent dimension appeared faintly behind Max’s breakthrough aura, so deep and empty that even the Ravenhart ancestor’s eyes changed. Soul attacks, soul perception, and fate-like observation all felt small next to that silent dimension.","Then came resilience, vitality, origin, speed, and strength. Five divine vein shadows appeared around the pillar of light like five ancient channels carved into the body of heaven itself. One stabilized the breakthrough like a world-root."]},{"number":1988,"title":"Chapter 1988 - 1st level of Law Manifestation Realm!","paragraphs":["One poured endless life force into the manifestation. One moved like a flash across every law phenomenon. One carried raw physical might that shook the arena floor. The last stood like an indestructible wall, holding off pressure from every direction.","And above all of them, faint but terrifying, the Primordial Bloodline pulsed. The laws of the world drew closer, and every manifestation became clearer, stronger, and more complete.","The entire Five Sacred Clan domain shook under the breakthrough. Not just the arena. The Valerius platform trembled, and sacred flames bent toward the sky as if acknowledging a higher law reaction.","The Ashbourne platform cracked in several places, and blood-iron battle marks lit up defensively. The Ravenhart shadows scattered and reformed, unable to decide whether to hide or watch. The Evercrest spatial layers rippled violently, and several sealed gardens inside the hidden domain opened by themselves for a brief moment.","The abandoned Voidwalker end roared with starry light, as if after countless years of silence, it had finally watched a descendant step into a realm worth announcing.","The younger geniuses of the Four Sacred Clans stared in disbelief.","Cassian Valerius stood frozen, his eyes reflecting the seven-colored lightning, the black flames, the spatial doors, the dragon shadow, and the silent soul law above the sky. He’d seen plenty of breakthroughs into the Law Manifestation Realm. As the Sun-Crowned Heir of Valerius, he’d even caused a grand manifestation himself when he broke into that realm.","But compared to this, his own breakthrough had been simple.","Draven Ashbourne’s face filled with rare shock. \"How many laws does this guy cultivate?\"","No one answered him.","Seraphine Ravenhart’s silver-purple eyes trembled slightly. \"Not just laws. Pseudo Cosmic Paths, bloodline laws, body laws, soul laws, and a bunch of others. They’re all manifesting together.\"","Aelric Evercrest, who’d once bragged that Max wouldn’t have dominated the Cosmic Ascension Conference if the Four Sacred Clan heirs had taken part, now sat pale and speechless.","He’d already lost to Max before this breakthrough. And now Max had entered the Law Manifestation Realm.","The four clan heads looked even uglier. The Evercrest head clenched his fists so tight his wound reopened, but he didn’t even notice the blood running down his chest. The Valerius head stared at the breakthrough pillar with a stiff expression. The Ashbourne head looked like he wanted to curse out loud. The Ravenhart head stayed silent, but deep caution showed in her eyes.","The four sacred ancestors looked shaken too.","\"This isn’t a normal Law Manifestation breakthrough,\" the Valerius ancestor said in a low voice.","The Ashbourne ancestor’s expression darkened. \"Normal? Even the word monster doesn’t cover this.\"","The Ravenhart ancestor whispered, \"The laws aren’t fighting each other. They’re in harmony. That’s the terrifying part.\"","The Evercrest ancestor looked toward the abandoned fifth end with a grim face. \"This kid is monstrous, to put it lightly. And with the Primordial Bloodline and now the Voidwalker Bloodline both truly awake, I don’t think any young genius in the Divine Realm could stand up to him.\"","Inside the Inheritance Chamber, Max felt the barrier shatter. His laws no longer stayed refined only inside his body. They manifested outward. Every path he carried gained a visible form and deeper authority.","His entire foundation seemed to expand from an internal world into something that could directly touch reality. The Voidwalker inheritance flowed through him, filling in a missing layer in his bloodline and giving his dimensional understanding a proper ancestral foundation.","Then his cultivation broke through.","[Breakthrough Successful.]","[Law Manifestation Realm 1st Level.]","Max opened his eyes. The moment he did, the countless law manifestations above the Five Sacred Clan domain trembled once more before slowly starting to withdraw.","But even after they faded, the shock they’d caused didn’t go away. The entire Five Sacred Clan domain stayed silent. Even the emergency teams preparing to rush toward the devil attack had stopped for a few breaths, staring up at the sky with wide eyes.","The Voidwalker Ancestor stood outside the Inheritance Chamber, his old face filled with emotion.","\"He really broke through.\"","His voice came out soft.","\"He reached the Law Manifestation Realm.\"","Inside the chamber, Max slowly raised his hand. Silver Voidwalker rings appeared faintly around his wrist before fading away. His aura felt much stronger than before, but more importantly, it felt more complete. The Voidwalker bloodline that had once slept inside him had finally woken up properly, and the inheritance had given it a real direction.","Freya opened her eyes not far away. Her aura had also grown deeper and purer. The Voidwalker inheritance had refined her bloodline, strengthened her foundation, and given her access to techniques she’d never had before. But even she looked at Max with a complicated expression.","\"You really know how to make noise,\" she said.","Max looked at her and smiled faintly. \"I was told to reach the Law Manifestation Realm.\"","Freya stared at him for a moment. Then she shook her head, though a faint warmth showed in her eyes.","Outside the chamber, the Voidwalker Ancestor’s voice came through again.","\"Good. Both of you keep absorbing what you can. The inheritance won’t stay open forever.\"","Max closed his eyes again. But this time, his foundation was different.","He was no longer at the Law Refinement Realm. He had stepped into the Law Manifestation Realm.","Max then began focusing on understanding the inheritance of the Voidwalker Bloodline. Just like that, a month went by.","\"There are so many techniques and moves in the Voidwalker Bloodline inheritance,\" Max muttered as he stood up. \"And any single one of them could pass as a sacred art even for a first-rate force.\"","It was at that moment Max finally understood why the Four Sacred Clans stood above every first-rate force in the Divine Realm.","When he reached the exit door, he found Freya already waiting there.","\"Done comprehending the inheritance?\" Freya asked, curious.","Max nodded. \"It was vast, but not impossible.\"","He looked at her and added, \"I’m surprised you finished before me.\""]},{"number":1989,"title":"Chapter 1989: Another Summon to the Primordial Race!","paragraphs":["Freya raised her brows with a cheeky smile. \"Well, I’m your big sister after all. Of course I’d learn faster than you.\"","Her expression turned a bit more serious as she went on. \"Jokes aside, I’m way more powerful than you, and my understanding of laws runs a lot deeper than yours right now. It only makes sense I’d comprehend the inheritance faster.\"","Max got curious hearing that and couldn’t help but ask, \"What’s your cultivation realm?\"","Honestly, he couldn’t sense her strength at all.","\"I’ve recovered my old strength and gone past it,\" Freya said with a smile. \"Right now, I’m at the Holy Lord Realm.\"","Max’s eyes went wide.","Holy Lord Realm. If he remembered right, that sat two full realms above his own. Law Manifestation Realm, Divine Lord Realm, Divine King Realm, and then Holy Lord Realm.","In that moment, Max realized just how big the gap really was between him and his sister. She was way more powerful than he’d ever imagined.","\"Don’t look so shocked, Maxy,\" Freya said with a smile. \"I’m older than you, so of course my cultivation sits higher. Don’t overthink it.\"","With that, she opened the door to the Inheritance Chamber and walked out. Max nodded and followed her.","The Voidwalker Ancestor was already waiting for them outside.","\"Good,\" he said, nodding as he sensed the awakened Voidwalker Bloodline aura in both of them.","Then he added, \"Max, the Primordial Race has summoned you. An envoy is waiting outside for you.\"","Max frowned. \"Another summon?\"","The Voidwalker Ancestor nodded with a sigh. \"Things have taken a turn for the worse across the Divine Realm.\"","\"The devils?\" Max asked, frowning again.","The Voidwalker Ancestor nodded. \"That last attack you heard about wasn’t the only one. It looks like the devils have found a way into our universe, and because of that, there’ve already been several attacks across the Divine Realm. I think another war might be about to break out between the devils and the people of this universe.\"","Max and Freya both turned solemn hearing that.","\"Max, go ahead and report to the Primordial Race,\" the Voidwalker Ancestor said calmly. \"I believe they’ve already planned something for the growth of all the top geniuses in the Divine Realm. Don’t waste this chance.\"","Max nodded solemnly. Now that he understood the devils had truly invaded their universe, he knew a war could break out at any moment. He hadn’t forgotten the scene on Orion, where the war between the devils and the Primordials had once played out. Something like that could easily happen again in the Divine Realm.","\"Go on,\" Freya said, smiling.","Max nodded, but he hesitated over something. \"About mother and father...\"","\"Don’t worry about them,\" Freya cut in. \"Now that I’ve come to the Four Sacred Clans, I’m not leaving anytime soon. My team will join me here in a few days too. After that, I’ll do everything I can to free the members of the Voidwalker Clan from the seal. Once that’s done, we’ll have an army ready to move against the elves.\"","She sighed. \"But it’ll take time. I don’t think the four clans are in any mood to break the seal on our Voidwalker Clan right now.\"","Max understood.","\"In the meantime, I want you to push your strength up as fast as you can,\" Freya said solemnly. \"At your current level, thinking about waging war against the elves is basically suicide. You know that, right?\"","Max nodded in understanding.","Freya then stepped forward and hugged him. \"Now go, Maxy. Next time you come back to the Four Sacred Clans, it’ll be time to wipe those elves off the Divine Realm.\"","Max hugged her back tightly.","A moment later, they let go of each other.","Max looked at Freya. \"I’ll see you soon.\"","With that, he turned and headed toward the exit of the Voidwalker Clan.","Once Max was gone, the Voidwalker Ancestor turned to Freya, his expression calm. \"Do you really intend to wage war against the elves?\"","Freya nodded, her expression turning cold. \"Not just wage war. I want to wipe out every single one of them from the Divine Realm.\"","An aura of slaughter radiated off her body in that moment.","The Voidwalker Ancestor looked at her for a long moment, then said calmly, \"Well, anything’s possible when you’re a Voidwalker.\"","Meanwhile, Max appeared outside the gate of the Voidwalker Clan and saw a figure waiting for him. It was Sarvion, the same envoy who’d picked him up from the Black Dragon Clan.","\"How should I address you?\" Max asked, walking over. \"Sarvion, Sir Sarvion, or something else you’d prefer?\"","Sarvion smiled politely. \"Just call me Sarvion.\"","As he said it, he tapped Max on the shoulder, and the world around Max changed. This time, Max could see they were flying through some kind of space vortex. Only a few seconds later, they arrived at the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","\"That was fast,\" Max muttered before turning to Sarvion. \"How’d you do that? Is that some cosmic path or law you’ve comprehended?\"","Sarvion smiled. \"No laws or cosmic paths involved. Once you’re as strong as me, you can cut through space to travel long distances. And for people carrying Primordial Race bloodline, it’s even easier.\"","He added, \"Since you already have a Tier 4 bloodline from our race, it’s only a matter of time before you can do this too.\"","Max nodded lightly as they started walking. \"How’s the situation in the Divine Realm? I heard another war might break out between the devils and our world.\"","Sarvion’s expression turned solemn. \"The situation isn’t looking good. The devils have somehow found a way into our universe after all these years. If I’m not wrong, things are only going to get worse from here.\"","Max’s expression hardened. He thought for a moment before asking, \"About the Black Dragon Clan, they’re just a third-rate force, but since they’re the first force I joined in the Divine Realm, I care about them a lot. Can the Primordial Race send some protectors to look after the Black Dragon Clan?\"","Sarvion answered without looking back. \"You don’t need to worry about the Black Dragon Clan. Now that you’ve become a Primordial, every force you’re connected to falls under the Primordial Race, which means they’re under our protection at all times.\"","Max nodded, relieved to hear that.","A moment later, Max arrived at a hall where the other top geniuses were already standing, waiting."]},{"number":1990,"title":"Chapter 1990: A Week of Time!","paragraphs":["\"So, everyone is here,\" Max said as his gaze moved across the hall.","The others had already gathered inside the wide chamber, and even Aurelian had appeared among them. His presence made Max’s eyes pause for a brief moment, but he did not say anything about it. The atmosphere in the hall was already strange enough without him adding more tension.","Orion leaned back against the wall and grinned the moment he saw Max. \"You sure took your sweet time getting here.\"","Max smiled a little awkwardly. \"I was in seclusion. I did not even know I had been summoned.\"","\"It is good that you still arrived in time,\" Rosaline said, her expression unusually solemn.","Max nodded to her, then looked around the hall once more. Aside from the top geniuses, he did not see any Primordials present. There were no elders, no envoys, and no guards standing nearby. When he glanced behind him, he also noticed that Sarvion had already disappeared without a sound.","\"Does anyone know what this summons is about?\" Max asked, his curiosity growing.","Damian frowned. \"No one has told us anything. We have already been waiting here for a full day, yet no one has appeared to explain the situation.\"","\"A whole day?\" Max’s frown deepened when he heard that.","Ervin crossed his arms and spoke in a calm voice. \"From what we were told, we were supposed to wait for only a few hours while some preparation was being arranged for us.\"","The group exchanged glances after hearing that, and the uneasiness in the hall became even heavier.","Morgana let out a light sneer. \"I think this is nonsense. The Primordials are clearly trying to hide something from us. It is suspicious enough that they summoned us here without explanation, but making us wait this long without showing themselves makes it even more suspicious.\"","Revona, who had been quietly leaning against a wall until now, finally opened her eyes and spoke. \"You are all too impatient. Calm down and wait as instructed. What is the hurry?\"","Kaiden, standing beside her, nodded. \"I think Revona is right. Let us wait a few more hours before anyone does anything foolish.\"","\"Fine, we will wait,\" Max said with a shrug.","He walked to a corner of the hall and sat down against the wall. The Primordials had summoned the ten of them, but they had not even prepared chairs or tables for them.","That small detail made the situation feel even stranger, as though the summons had been issued in a hurry or the Primordials simply had no intention of making them comfortable.","Another day passed like that.","By then, even Revona and Ervin, who were usually far calmer than the others, had begun to show signs of impatience.","Then, without warning, a massive rumble tore through the hall.","The entire chamber shook.","Orion instantly sprang to his feet, his grin vanishing as he entered a defensive stance. \"What was that?\"","Another rumble followed almost immediately, louder and deeper than the first.","Max stood up as well, his expression turning serious. \"Is that a battle?\"","Rakan’s eyes widened slightly. \"Who would dare attack the Primordials?\"","Damian’s face turned cold. \"Devils?\"","A third rumble echoed across the Primordial Ancestral Domain, and this time, the walls themselves trembled as if the impact had come from somewhere close.","Ervin had already started moving toward the exit. \"Let us go see what is happening.\"","Damian followed him without hesitation.","\"Let us go,\" Max said as his aura stirred, and he flew out with them.","Revona, Morgana, Kaiden, Orion, Rakan, Rosaline, Aurelian, and the others followed soon after. None of them knew what was happening outside, but all of them understood one thing clearly. If someone had truly attacked the Primordial Race inside their own ancestral domain, then the situation was far more serious than a delayed summons.","When they arrived outside the Primordial Ancestral Domain, they saw two groups facing each other across the sky.","On one side stood the Primordials.","At their front were the four Primarchs, their auras vast and terrifying even while restrained. Behind them stood many other powerful Primordials, each one carrying a pressure far beyond what ordinary Divine Realm experts could release.","On the other side stood a group of beings that looked somewhat similar to demons, yet were clearly not ordinary demons.","Their bodies were taller and more muscular than most demons, and strange tattoos covered them from head to toe. Those tattoos resembled Infernal Demon Tattoos, but they were more ancient, more savage, and far more oppressive. The markings seemed to grow from the two glowing horns on top of their heads, spreading downward across their faces, necks, chests, arms, and legs like living brands of destruction.","Max’s eyes narrowed.","They were devils.","The one standing at the front of the devils was not an old warlord covered in scars, nor was he a brutish monster releasing endless killing intent. Instead, he looked young. His face was handsome in a cruel and vicious way, and his body was wrapped in a calm confidence that made him seem even more dangerous than the devils behind him.","\"So, what will it be?\" the young devil asked, his voice carrying clearly across the sky. \"A war that wipes out your entire universe, or will you meet our demands?\"","The Primordials became quiet after hearing him.","They were not truly silent, however. Max could feel faint fluctuations of divine transmission passing between the four Primarchs and the other high-ranking Primordials. Clearly, they were discussing the matter privately while keeping their expressions calm on the surface.","After a moment, one of the four Primarchs stepped forward.","\"Varok,\" he said in a steady voice, \"we need some time to consider this matter. How about this? We will hold a meeting one week from today, and we will discuss your terms then. What do you say?\"","Varok, the young devil, sneered.","He did not answer immediately. Instead, his gaze moved across the faces of the Primordials one by one, as if he was memorizing their expressions.","\"You Primordials are always like this,\" he said. \"Stalling for time again and again. Last time, the war ended peacefully because of an unforeseen variable, but I am quite sure this time will not end the same way.\"","His sneer deepened.","\"Anyway, take your time if you want. Just do not think one week will change anything. If it even matters at all.\"","The moment he finished speaking, the space around the devils twisted.","Then all of them vanished.","The sky fell silent."]},{"number":1991,"title":"Chapter 1991: Lesser Beings!","paragraphs":["Only after the devils disappeared did the four Primarchs let out faint sighs.","Arvantos, one of the Primarchs, glanced behind him and said, \"You children can come out now.\"","Max, Damian, Ervin, and the others stepped out from where they had been standing. Their expressions were dark because none of them had missed the conversation between the devils and the Primordials.","\"Were those devils?\" Orion asked with a frown.","\"Are they declaring war on us?\" Ervin asked.","Damian’s eyes were cold. \"What demands were they talking about?\"","The others began asking questions as well, and in only a few breaths, Arvantos was surrounded by the confusion and pressure of the top geniuses.","Only Max and Revona remained silent.","Max was thinking about the sudden appearance of the devils, while Revona watched Arvantos with a calm gaze that suggested she might already know more than the rest of them.","\"I will explain everything,\" Arvantos said. \"Give me a moment.\"","He then turned toward the other three Primarchs.","\"I will return after I brief them. It is time they knew the truth.\"","The other three Primarchs nodded. Soon after, they vanished along with the rest of the Primordials, leaving only Arvantos and the ten geniuses behind.","\"Follow me,\" Arvantos said.","Without waiting for further questions, he turned and walked back into the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","The ten geniuses followed him into a different hall. Unlike the previous chamber where they had been forced to wait without explanation, this hall was solemn and ancient. Strange symbols covered the walls, and a massive star map floated above the center of the room. Countless points of light moved within it, some bright, some dim, and some surrounded by faint crimson marks.","Arvantos stopped beneath the star map and turned to face them.","\"What do you all know about the last war between the races?\" he asked.","Orion blinked. \"Nothing?\"","Revona spoke right after him. \"That we almost lost.\"","Rakan frowned as if trying to recall something. \"I heard some elders mention that it happened on a planet called Orion, or something like that.\"","Arvantos nodded slowly. \"The last time that war happened, we very nearly lost everything. It shook the entire universe. Both the Divine Realm and the Mortal Realm were pushed to the edge of destruction because of those devils.\"","He sighed, and for the first time, the ten geniuses saw a trace of exhaustion on the face of a Primarch.","\"It was only because of a miracle that the last war ended peacefully.\"","Max looked at him and asked, \"What caused the war? What do the devils actually want from our universe?\"","Arvantos looked at Max and smiled faintly.","\"That is a good question.\"","He turned his gaze toward the whole group.","\"Before I explain that, I must first tell you something about what exists beyond our universe.\"","The moment Arvantos said those words, the expressions of the ten geniuses changed.","Beyond their universe.","None of them had ever seriously thought about such a thing before. Some had been born in the Divine Realm, while others had climbed up from the Mortal Realm, but all of them had grown up believing that their universe was the highest stage they could reach.","They knew the Divine Realm was vast beyond imagination, and they knew the Mortal Realm contained countless worlds, but the idea that something existed beyond the universe itself was enough to shake even their powerful minds.","In that instant, every one of them focused fully on Arvantos.","Whatever he was about to say next would not only explain the devils.","It might also change their understanding of the entire world they lived in.","Arvantos looked at the ten geniuses for a moment before he began speaking.","\"Our Primordial Race is not the only first race beyond this universe. In fact, apart from us Primordials, there are four other races that exist outside our universe.\"","The hall fell into silence.","\"Four other races...\" Orion muttered, his expression slowly changing.","The ten geniuses were visibly shocked. Until this moment, most of them had only known about devils through old records, ancient warnings, and the sudden confrontation they had just witnessed outside the Primordial Ancestral Domain. They had never imagined that beyond their own universe, there were not only devils, but four completely different first races standing on a similar level as the Primordial Race.","Arvantos did not look surprised by their reaction.","To these young geniuses, the Divine Realm was already unimaginably vast. The Mortal Realm below it contained countless worlds, planets, star fields, and civilizations.","For most cultivators, even the Divine Realm alone was too large to fully explore in a lifetime. Yet now, Arvantos had casually told them that their entire universe was not the only one, and that beyond its boundaries existed other universes ruled by other first races.","That truth was enough to overturn the understanding they had carried since birth.","Arvantos continued in a calm but serious voice. \"Demons and elves also came from special racial origins, but they are not on the same level as the five first races. Their relationship to those higher races is somewhat similar to the relationship between humans and Primordials. In a certain sense, they are lesser beings.\"","He did not soften his words at all.","The moment he said this, several geniuses became quiet. Max’s eyes moved slightly, especially because of his connection to the elves through his mother’s side and the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline.","However, he did not interrupt Arvantos. He could tell that Arvantos was not speaking with contempt for the sake of contempt. He was explaining the cosmic hierarchy as the Primordials understood it.","\"To put it more clearly,\" Arvantos said, \"demons and elves may be powerful races within certain worlds, realms, and civilizations, but their racial foundation does not place them at the peak of existence. Their strongest members may become terrifying experts, and their bloodlines may possess unique powers, but their origin is still not equal to that of the first races. The first races are different. They were not merely born as inhabitants of a universe. Their existence is tied to the structure, laws, and ancient order beyond ordinary worlds.\"","The expressions of the ten geniuses became even more serious."]},{"number":1992,"title":"Chapter 1992: Five Races!","paragraphs":["Arvantos then said, \"I will explain the details about demons and elves later. For now, you only need to understand the five first races. Aside from us Primordials, there is the Devil Race, the Spirit Race, the Angel Race, and lastly, the Dragon Race.\"","The names echoed through the hall.","Devil Race.","Spirit Race.","Angel Race.","Dragon Race.","To the ten geniuses, each name carried an invisible pressure. The Devil Race had already appeared before them, arrogant enough to stand in front of the four Primarchs and threaten the entire universe. If the Devil Race was only one of the other four first races, then it was difficult to imagine how powerful the remaining three could be.","Arvantos raised his hand, and the star map above the hall shifted. Four enormous shadows appeared around the image of their universe. One was dark and crimson, burning with the aura of slaughter and conquest.","One was pale green and silver, filled with life, nature, and spiritual light. One was bright and vast, surrounded by rings of sacred radiance. The last was immense and ancient, carrying the faint outline of coiling dragons whose bodies seemed large enough to wrap around stars.","\"Among those four races,\" Arvantos continued, \"the Angel Race and the Dragon Race are the most threatening to us.\"","Everyone immediately focused on him.","\"During the last war, the Devil Race was the one that directly invaded our universe, but the situation could have been much worse. At that time, the Angel Race and the Dragon Race were locked in a conflict of their own. Their attention was elsewhere, and they had no reason to spend their forces on us. That was our fortune.\"","His tone became heavier.","\"If the Angel Race and the Dragon Race had entered the war at the same time as the Devil Race, then we would have surely lost. There is no need to dress it up with pride. That is the truth.\"","The hall became still.","No one mocked him. No one questioned him. No one thought he was exaggerating.","Arvantos was a Primarch. If someone like him was willing to say that the Primordial Race would have lost, then the threat of the Angel Race and Dragon Race had to be almost unimaginable.","Max’s gaze sharpened slightly.","The Dragon Race caught his attention more than the others.","His Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline was already one of his strongest foundations. It had given him dragon transformation, terrifying defense, chaotic dragon force, and the power of the Black Dragon Cataclysm Breath.","But now, hearing Arvantos speak of a Dragon Race beyond their universe made him wonder whether his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline was somehow connected to that race, or whether it came from another branch entirely.","For now, he kept the question to himself.","Everyone remained silent for a while after hearing about the other four first races.","Then Max asked curiously, \"Is the Spirit Race the same race that spirits came from?\"","Arvantos nodded. \"Yes, it is the same Spirit Race you are thinking of, but not in the simple way most people understand spirits.\"","He looked at Max and explained further, \"The spirits you know within our universe are often incomplete manifestations of spiritual energy, nature, laws, memories, or special environments. Some are born from treasures, some from natural lands, some from ancient battlefields, and some from the lingering will of powerful beings. They may have intelligence, emotion, and even cultivation, but they are not the true first race.\"","Arvantos raised his hand, and the spirit-like shadow on the star map became clearer.","\"The true Spirit Race beyond our universe exists in humanoid form. They have flesh, soul, bloodline, and spiritual origin. However, unlike ordinary races, their bodies are naturally close to the laws of nature and the pure forces of existence. They are born with an affinity toward life, elemental laws, soul energy, and natural order. That is why many ancient records describe them as a race blessed by gods.\"","He paused briefly, then corrected himself in a calmer tone.","\"Of course, whether gods truly blessed them or whether it is only the blessing of nature is something no one can say with certainty. But among the five first races, the Spirit Race is indeed the one most closely aligned with balance, life, and natural law.\"","Ervin’s eyes brightened slightly. \"Then they are not hostile?\"","\"Not usually,\" Arvantos said. \"The Spirit Race is considered the most peaceful among the five first races. They do not like invasion, conquest, or meaningless slaughter. They prefer to remain within their own universe, protect their sacred lands, and avoid wars unless their survival or core interests are threatened.\"","His voice then turned colder.","\"The Devil Race is the complete opposite.\"","The atmosphere shifted again.","\"The Devil Race is the most hated race among the five. Their society is built around conquest, domination, bloodline hierarchy, and endless expansion. To them, invading another universe is not a moral question. It is only a matter of whether the benefits are worth the cost. They devour resources, enslave worlds, corrupt races, and turn conquered territories into war engines for future invasions.\"","Damian’s expression turned grim.","Arvantos looked at the young geniuses and continued, \"If only the Devil Race wants to invade our universe, the situation will be dangerous, but not hopeless. Our Primordial Race, together with the top forces of the Divine Realm, can still resist them if we move properly. The true problem is whether the Angel Race and Dragon Race become involved.\"","Rosaline frowned. \"Why would they join?\"","\"Because war between universes does not remain simple for long,\" Arvantos answered. \"If the Devil Race gains something from invading us, the other races will not sit still. If we weaken too much while fighting the devils, others may see an opportunity. If the hidden secret they seek truly exists here, then every first race will eventually turn its eyes toward us.\"","His expression became solemn.","\"So, while the devils are the ones standing at our gate right now, they may not remain our only enemy.\"","A heavy silence filled the hall.","After a moment, Damian asked, \"Then what do the devils actually want from our universe?\"","Arvantos sighed.","\"That is a long story.\"","He looked toward the star map above them. With a wave of his hand, the image expanded again, revealing their universe at the center and four other vast cosmic forms surrounding it from different directions."]},{"number":1993,"title":"Chapter 1993: Primal Treasure!","paragraphs":["\"You should first understand the structure of the five universes,\" Arvantos said. \"Each of the five first races exists within its own universe. We Primordials belong to this universe. The Devil Race has its own universe. The Spirit Race has its own universe. The Angel Race and Dragon Race also each occupy their own universe. In other words, apart from ours, there are four other universes outside.\"","The ten geniuses stared at the star map without blinking.","Arvantos continued, \"The arrangement of these five universes is unusual. Our universe is positioned at the center, while the other four universes surround it. This arrangement has existed since ancient times. No one knows whether it was formed naturally or arranged by an existence beyond our understanding.\"","The central universe on the star map glowed faintly.","\"Because of this structure, the other four races have always believed that our universe hides something special. More specifically, they believe our universe contains the entrance to a god-like realm.\"","\"A god-like realm?\" Orion asked, his voice filled with disbelief.","Arvantos nodded. \"A realm beyond the five universes. A place that may contain opportunities to break through the final barrier and step into the True God Realm.\"","The eyes of all ten geniuses changed.","True God Realm.","Even for them, that was a realm that sounded distant and almost mythical.","Arvantos explained, \"You should understand that even among the first races, reaching the peak is not the same as transcending all limitations. The so-called True God Realm is believed to be a level beyond the normal ceiling of the five universes. It is said that those who enter that realm may no longer be bound by the laws of their birth universe. They may stand above ordinary fate, lifespan, law, and cosmic restriction.\"","He shook his head slightly.","\"But belief is not proof.\"","Ervin looked at him with curiosity. \"Does such a place really exist in our universe?\"","Arvantos sighed. \"We do not know.\"","That answer made everyone frown.","He continued, \"We have searched our entire universe for countless years. The Primordial Race searched. The ancient sacred clans searched. Other first-rate forces also searched in secret. We examined forbidden regions, ancient ruins, collapsed star realms, sealed worlds, cosmic rifts, and places where the laws behaved strangely. Yet we never found anything that could truly be called the entrance to a god realm.\"","His gaze became distant.","\"Even during the last war, when the enemy tried to force their way toward the place they believed to be the entrance, we investigated that location thoroughly after the war ended. There was nothing there. No gate. No hidden realm. No divine passage. Nothing that could explain why the devils had been so obsessed with it.\"","Max’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Arvantos continued, \"However, that belief was enough to ignite war. The other races wanted to find the entrance first. The Devil Race wanted to seize it by force. The Angel Race and Dragon Race watched from outside, each with their own motives. The Spirit Race remained the most restrained, but even they could not completely ignore a rumor involving the True God Realm.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\"That was the reason the great war broke out hundreds of thousands of years ago. A war that pushed both the Divine Realm and Mortal Realm to the edge of destruction.\"","The hall became quiet again.","Arvantos then added, \"By now, I suspect the other races may have also realized that our universe may not contain the entrance they once imagined. At the very least, if it does exist, it is not something that can be found through ordinary searching or brute force. But that does not mean they will leave us alone.\"","Damian’s eyes were cold. \"Because they already see our universe as a target.\"","\"Exactly,\" Arvantos said. \"Once a race invades another universe, hatred does not disappear simply because the original goal becomes uncertain. The Devil Race lost warriors during the last war. We killed many of their experts. They killed many of ours. Blood debts were formed, territories were ruined, and both sides remembered the humiliation. Even if the entrance to the God Realm is only a false legend, the devils still have reasons to return.\"","His expression became grim.","\"And among the Devil Race, there is one being we must be especially wary of.\"","Max looked at him.","Arvantos said, \"Devil Emperor Abaddon.\"","The name alone seemed to make the atmosphere in the hall colder.","\"One of the leaders of the Devil Race,\" Arvantos continued. \"A ruthless conqueror who cares nothing for life outside his own ambition. He is not the kind of ruler who invades only because of a legend. If he wants something, he will move armies to obtain it. If a world resists, he will slaughter it. If a universe blocks his path, he will try to burn through that universe until nothing remains.\"","His gaze swept across the ten geniuses.","\"If Abaddon is behind this invasion, then we cannot assume the devils are only testing us. He may be preparing for something much larger.\"","The pressure in the hall became suffocating.","Arvantos looked back at the star map. \"With the Devil Race making a move, and with the Angel Race and Dragon Race watching from beyond the boundaries, the long-term situation does not look good for us if war truly begins again.\"","Max remained silent for a moment before asking, \"How did the devils enter our universe from theirs? And why now? It has been peaceful for almost a hundred thousand years. What changed?\"","Arvantos turned to him.","\"Our universe shares boundaries with the other four universes. That boundary is called the Wall of Eternity.\"","The star map changed again.","A vast translucent barrier appeared around the central universe. It was not a simple wall made of stone, metal, or energy. It looked like a cosmic membrane formed from countless layers of law, space, time, fate, and origin. It separated the five universes from one another while still allowing them to exist within the same greater cosmic structure.","\"As the name suggests, the Wall of Eternity is almost eternal,\" Arvantos said. \"Its durability is worthy of that name. Under normal circumstances, it cannot be broken by armies, ordinary treasures, or even most supreme experts. It is not only a physical barrier. It is a law boundary that prevents the universes from collapsing into one another.\"","He raised his hand, and a tiny point of darkness appeared on one side of the barrier.","\"But almost impossible does not mean completely impossible.\"","Everyone stared at the point of darkness.","\"With enough power, and with the help of a treasure at the level of a Primal Treasure, even the Wall of Eternity can be pierced. Not destroyed. Not shattered. Only pierced enough to create a temporary or narrow passage.\"","Orion swallowed. \"A Primal Treasure can do that?\"","Arvantos nodded. \"A true Primal Treasure is not merely a powerful weapon. Each one was born from a source older than the current order of the five universes. They carry authority that can affect the structure of reality itself. If used properly, one of them can change the flow of a war. If used recklessly, it can destroy entire star regions.\"","He looked at the dark point on the wall.","\"If I am not wrong, the devils possess one of the five Primal Treasures. They must have spent the last hundred thousand years storing energy inside it. They waited, accumulated, prepared, and concealed their movements until that treasure finally held enough power to pierce a small hole through the Wall of Eternity.\"","His voice became heavier with every word.","\"And through that hole, the devils have invaded our universe.\""]},{"number":1994,"title":"Chapter 1994 - 500 Years of Time!","paragraphs":["\"So, what is the plan?\" Max asked at that moment, his eyes still fixed on Arvantos. \"Are we just going to let the devils invade our universe?\"","The question made the hall grow quieter.","The other geniuses also looked toward Arvantos. None of them said anything, but their expressions showed that they wanted the same answer. They had just learned that the devils had pierced the Wall of Eternity, entered their universe, and even dared to stand before the Primordials to make demands. If the situation was already that serious, then waiting, negotiating, and discussing terms sounded far too passive.","Arvantos turned toward Max.","\"The situation is not that simple,\" he said in a steady voice. \"One fortunate thing about this crisis is also the very thing the devils managed to damage. I am talking about the Wall of Eternity.\"","The star map above the hall shifted once again, and the image of the central universe reappeared. Around it, the enormous translucent barrier shimmered with countless layers of law, space, time, and origin. On one side of that barrier was a tiny dark opening, so small that it almost looked insignificant compared to the vastness of the wall.","\"The devils used one of the five Primal Treasures to pierce a hole through the Wall of Eternity,\" Arvantos continued. \"However, piercing it is not the same as breaking it. The Wall of Eternity is still standing, and because of that, it remains our greatest safeguard.\"","He raised his hand toward the tiny opening in the star map.","\"Right now, the hole is extremely small. It is barely stable enough to let a limited number of beings enter our universe. The stronger a being is, the greater the pressure they place on the opening. If someone above the current limit tries to cross, the passage may collapse, and the Wall of Eternity may crush them before they can fully enter.\"","Damian’s eyes narrowed. \"What is the current limit?\"","\"At most, beings around the Divine King Realm can pass through,\" Arvantos replied. \"Even then, they cannot pass in large numbers. From what we can tell, only a few hundred devils have entered so far. That number is dangerous, but it is not enough to launch a full invasion against the entire Divine Realm.\"","The tense atmosphere eased slightly, though no one truly relaxed.","A few hundred devils at the Divine King Realm were terrifying enough to destroy weaker star realms, but against the entire Divine Realm and the Primordial Race, that force alone would not be enough to bring about total war.","Arvantos continued, \"If the devils want to send a true army, they will need to widen the hole and make the passage stable enough for stronger existences to cross. That will not be easy. Even with a Primal Treasure, the Wall of Eternity cannot be opened quickly. Based on our current judgment, it may take them around five hundred years to create a large enough breach for a proper invasion army.\"","He sighed softly.","\"Five hundred years is not much, especially for beings at our level. But it is still time. Time to prepare. Time to gather forces. Time to strengthen the younger generation. Time to investigate their methods and search for a way to seal the breach before it grows.\"","The ten geniuses became silent after hearing this.","Five hundred years sounded like an enormous amount of time to mortals, but to cultivators in the Divine Realm, it was frighteningly short. Some elders spent longer than that in a single seclusion. Some inheritances took thousands of years to mature. For a universe that might have to prepare for a war of survival, five hundred years was only a brief pause before the storm.","Revona, who had been quiet until then, finally asked, \"What are the devils’ conditions?\"","Arvantos looked at her.","Revona continued calmly, \"From what I understood, they also do not want to start a war immediately. If they were confident in attacking right now, they would not have bothered making demands. They are looking for something else.\"","Arvantos nodded. \"Your judgment is correct.\"","His gaze moved across the group.","\"It is not easy for the devils to start a war against our universe right now. As I said, only a small group has crossed through the opening. We do not know when another group will be able to enter, and we do not know how much energy their Primal Treasure must accumulate before the passage stabilizes again. If they attack recklessly now, the few devils already inside our universe may be wiped out before reinforcements can arrive.\"","Orion frowned. \"Then why not just wipe them out?\"","\"Because doing so may start the very war we are trying to delay,\" Arvantos replied.","The hall grew quiet again.","Arvantos’s expression became colder. \"The most troublesome part is not the few hundred devils. It is the young devil you saw earlier. His name is Varok, and he is the son of Devil Emperor Abaddon.\"","The expressions of the geniuses changed.","They had already heard Arvantos describe Abaddon as one of the leaders of the Devil Race, a ruthless conqueror who would slaughter entire worlds to obtain what he wanted. If Varok was his son, then killing him would not be a simple military decision. It would become a direct provocation against one of the most dangerous beings beyond their universe.","Arvantos said, \"If we kill Varok here, Abaddon will not treat it as the loss of a small scouting force. He will treat it as humiliation and blood debt. He may abandon caution and pour everything he has into forcing the breach open, even if doing so damages his own side. A ruler like him will not allow his son to be killed in another universe without consequence.\"","Kaiden frowned. \"So both sides are restrained.\"","\"Exactly,\" Arvantos said. \"The devils cannot start a full war right away because their forces inside our universe are too limited. We cannot simply kill all of them because doing so may force Abaddon to retaliate before we are ready. In a way, neither side truly wants an immediate war.\"","Max’s eyes darkened slightly.","That kind of balance was unstable.","It was not peace.","It was only two enemies standing at the edge of a blade, each waiting for the other to make the wrong move."]},{"number":1995,"title":"Chapter 1995: Pearl of Abyss!","paragraphs":["Revona asked again, \"Then what do the devils want in exchange for delaying the war?\"","Arvantos’s expression became ugly.","\"They want permission to establish a force in the Divine Realm.\"","The hall instantly became colder.","Arvantos continued, \"They also want independent freedom to move throughout the Divine Realm, interact with other forces, and conduct their own affairs, provided they do not openly slaughter our people or destroy our territories.\"","The ten geniuses frowned almost at the same time.","That condition was far too much.","Letting devils enter the Divine Realm was already dangerous. Allowing them to create their own force and move freely among the sects, clans, empires, and hidden organizations of the Divine Realm was even worse. The devils might not need to slaughter anyone openly. They could tempt ambitious cultivators, corrupt weaker factions, manipulate internal disputes, buy information, plant spies, and slowly create chaos from within.","Max spoke in a solemn voice. \"They could corrupt our human forces in no time.\"","\"That is our concern as well,\" Arvantos said with a sigh. \"Many Divine Realm forces look noble on the surface, but greed exists everywhere. There will always be clans hungry for power, sects desperate for forbidden techniques, rulers who want to break through, and traitors willing to sell their own universe for personal gain. The devils understand this. That is why their demand is dangerous.\"","Morgana sneered. \"Then refusing sounds obvious.\"","\"It would be obvious if Varok were only an ordinary envoy,\" Arvantos said.","Max’s gaze sharpened. \"Why not imprison or seal Varok somewhere?\"","Everyone looked toward him.","Max remained calm as he continued, \"That way, Devil Emperor Abaddon would not know his son is dead, and we would still have around five hundred years to prepare for war. If Varok is the main reason we cannot act, then keeping him alive but sealed should solve the immediate problem.\"","For a moment, no one spoke.","It was a ruthless suggestion, but no one could deny that it was practical.","Arvantos looked at Max for a few seconds before shaking his head.","\"It is not that simple.\"","Max narrowed his eyes. \"Because of Abaddon?\"","\"Partly,\" Arvantos said. \"But more importantly, because of what Varok carries.\"","He raised his hand again, and the star map changed. A dark pearl appeared above the image of the devils. It looked small, but the moment its image formed, the space around it seemed to sink inward, as though even the projection of the treasure carried an aura of endless abyss.","\"Varok possesses one of the five Primal Treasures,\" Arvantos said. \"It is called the Pearl of Abyss.\"","The name caused a strange pressure to settle over the hall.","Arvantos’s voice became solemn. \"The Pearl of Abyss is not a normal treasure. It contains a power that even we do not fully understand. It can distort space, hide fate traces, open abyssal passages, protect its bearer, and release destructive power far beyond Varok’s own cultivation. If forced into a desperate situation, Varok may activate it.\"","Damian frowned. \"What would happen then?\"","\"That is exactly the problem,\" Arvantos replied. \"We do not know.\"","The answer made everyone’s expression darken.","Arvantos continued, \"A Primal Treasure is too unpredictable. Each one possesses abilities that surpass ordinary laws. If Varok activates the Pearl of Abyss in the middle of our universe, it may create another passage. It may summon something from the devil universe. It may collapse a star realm into abyssal corruption. It may even allow him to escape and inform Abaddon that we tried to trap him.\"","He looked at Max. \"So sealing him sounds good in theory, but if the Pearl of Abyss reacts before we complete the seal, the consequences may be far worse than letting him remain under observation.\"","Max remained silent.","Arvantos then explained further, \"There are five Primal Treasures in existence, at least according to what we know. We Primordials possess one. The devils possess two. One is the Pearl of Abyss in Varok’s hands, and the other remains in the devil universe, where they are using it to pierce the Wall of Eternity. The fourth is in the possession of the leader of the Angel Race. As for the fifth, its whereabouts are still unknown.\"","His gaze moved slowly across the ten geniuses.","\"You must understand what that means. The devils did not send Varok here merely as a messenger. They sent him with a Primal Treasure because they wanted him to be untouchable, or at least dangerous enough that we would hesitate before acting against him.\"","The hall became oppressively silent.","The devils were not simply making demands.","They were using Varok as bait, shield, envoy, and threat all at once.","If the Primordials killed him, Abaddon would have a reason to start war.","If they imprisoned him, the Pearl of Abyss might cause a disaster.","If they agreed to his terms, devils would gain a foothold in the Divine Realm.","If they refused outright, the devils might escalate the situation while the Wall of Eternity continued weakening.","Arvantos sighed again, and for the first time, the ten geniuses could clearly see the weight carried by the Primarchs.","\"That is why we are in a bind. We cannot trust the devils. We cannot allow them to move freely. We cannot kill Varok carelessly. We cannot ignore the hole in the Wall of Eternity. And we cannot assume five hundred years will be enough.\"","He looked at them with a solemn expression.","\"This is why we summoned all of you.\"","Max’s eyes sharpened slightly.","Arvantos continued, \"The older generation will handle negotiations, defense lines, and the Wall of Eternity. But the future war will not be decided by old strength alone. If the invasion truly expands, your generation will become the blade of this universe.\"","His voice grew deeper.","\"And before that day comes, all of you must become strong enough to survive the battlefield that is coming.\"","After hearing Arvantos’s words, the ten geniuses fell into a heavy silence.","The pressure on their shoulders seemed to increase a hundredfold in an instant."]},{"number":1996,"title":"Chapter 1996: Training Chamber!","paragraphs":["Before this, their desire to grow stronger had been personal. Some wanted to stand at the peak of the Divine Realm. Some wanted to surpass their rivals. Some wanted to prove their bloodlines, inheritances, and talents. Some simply wanted to become strong enough that no one could decide their fate for them.","But now, that desire had changed.","This was no longer only about pride, ambition, or reputation.","Their entire universe was at stake.","If the devils truly widened the hole in the Wall of Eternity, then the war that had nearly destroyed the Divine Realm and Mortal Realm hundreds of thousands of years ago might begin again. If the Angel Race or the Dragon Race moved while the devils invaded, the situation could become even worse.","The ten geniuses standing in this hall were no longer just young talents being nurtured for future glory. They were now part of the universe’s preparation for survival.","Max felt the weight of that truth more clearly than most.","He had already seen too many strange things happen around him. The Voidwalker Clan’s buried history had surfaced. The First Progenitor had spoken to him and warned him about Anover. The devils had appeared in the Divine Realm soon after that warning.","Now Arvantos was telling them that the devils possessed two Primal Treasures, that Varok carried the Pearl of Abyss, and that the Wall of Eternity might fully crack open in about five hundred years.","Five hundred years.","To others, that might sound like a long time.","To Max, it sounded like a countdown.","Arvantos looked at the faces of the ten geniuses and seemed to understand what they were feeling. A faint smile appeared on his face, though the solemnity in his eyes did not fully disappear.","\"You do not need to worry too much right now,\" he said. \"The burden of the universe will not be placed on your shoulders today. The older generation will handle the immediate negotiations, the defense lines, the monitoring of the Wall of Eternity, and the meeting with the devils. What you need to do is use the time given to you properly.\"","His gaze swept across Max, Revona, Damian, Ervin, Morgana, Kaiden, Orion, Rosaline, Rakan, Aurelian, and the others.","\"For the next week, all of you will remain inside the Primordial Ancestral Domain until the meeting with the devils ends. During this time, none of you are to leave unless I personally allow it. The Divine Realm may look calm on the surface, but once news of the devils spreads among the top forces, many things will begin moving in the dark. Some people will panic. Some will prepare. Some will scheme. Some may even try to contact the devils for their own benefit.\"","His voice became deeper.","\"You are all too important to be allowed to wander outside without protection right now.\"","Morgana raised an eyebrow slightly, but she did not argue.","Arvantos continued, \"I have great plans for all of you. The Primordial Race has resources, places, and inheritances that are normally not opened even to our own younger generation without strict qualifications. However, the situation has changed. If war is coming, then old rules must give way to survival.\"","The ten geniuses immediately became more attentive.","Arvantos then said, \"Sarvion will take you to the training chambers of the Primordial Race. Those chambers were built to stimulate Primordial bloodline potential, sharpen law comprehension, strengthen bodies, and draw out hidden abilities. Since all of you have already obtained Primordial Bloodline, you may be able to awaken abilities that are still sleeping inside you.\"","Max’s eyes shifted slightly.","Awaken abilities of the Primordial Bloodline.","His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline had already increased his base strength by ten times, brought him closer to the laws of the world, and strengthened his Pseudo Cosmic Paths. Yet he had always felt that he had not truly unlocked everything hidden inside it.","Compared to his other powers, the Primordial Bloodline felt broad and fundamental, but also strangely incomplete, as though it had given him a foundation first and was waiting for the right environment to reveal more.","A training chamber made by the Primordial Race might be exactly what he needed.","As Arvantos finished speaking, the door of the hall opened.","Sarvion entered calmly.","He looked the same as before, dignified and unreadable, with an aura that seemed restrained yet impossible to ignore. His gaze moved across the ten geniuses, stopping briefly on Max before continuing.","\"Let us go,\" Sarvion said.","Without waiting for anyone to respond, he turned and walked out of the hall.","The ten geniuses followed him.","Max walked with the others, but his thoughts remained heavy. The conversation with Arvantos kept replaying in his mind. The five first races. The Wall of Eternity. The Devil Emperor Abaddon. Varok. The Pearl of Abyss. The Primal Treasures. The possibility that their universe sat at the center of all the others because of some hidden entrance to a god-like realm.","And beneath all of that, one unfinished warning continued echoing quietly.","’Watch out for Anover...’","Max did not know where Anover fit into this.","He did not know whether it was connected to Abaddon, the devils, the Primal Treasures, or something beyond even the five universes. But he had a feeling that the warning was not separate from what was happening now.","Something that could instill fear into the first inheritor of the Dimensional Keeper Legacy wouldn’t be something weak.","Sarvion led them through the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","The path they walked was very different from the halls where they had waited earlier. Those places had been grand, but this route felt older and more secluded. The walls were no longer smooth and polished.","They were made of dark-gold stone filled with natural patterns that looked like veins, stars, and ancient law marks fused together.","Every few steps, Max saw statues of Primordial experts standing along the corridor. Some had humanoid forms. Some had half-transformed bodies. Some looked so ancient and strange that Max could not even tell whether they had once been human-shaped at all.","The deeper they went, the denser the aura became.","It was not energy alone.","It was something heavier, more primitive, and closer to origin."]},{"number":1997,"title":"Chapter 1997: A Piece of Good News!","paragraphs":["Max felt his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline stir inside him as they continued walking. It did not surge violently, but it grew warmer, as though recognizing the place they were approaching.","His laws also became more sensitive. Space, flame, lightning, soul, body, and even his Emotion Severing Path seemed to sharpen slightly under the pressure of the surrounding environment.","The others felt it too.","Orion, who had been restless earlier, grew quiet. Damian’s face became serious. Ervin looked around with intense curiosity. Revona remained calm, but her eyes were no longer as indifferent as before. Even Morgana stopped making sharp remarks as they walked deeper into the ancestral grounds.","After some time, Sarvion stopped before a massive bronze-gold gate.","The gate was so tall that it looked as though it had been built for giants. Countless ancient symbols covered its surface, and at the center of the gate was a circular mark that seemed to contain many layered worlds inside it. The moment Max looked at that mark, his Primordial Bloodline pulsed once.","Sarvion turned back to them.","\"This is one of the core training facilities of the Primordial Race,\" he said. \"Normally, even the direct disciples of the Primarchs cannot enter this place casually. The chambers inside will respond differently to each of you. Do not resist the pressure. Do not force a result. Let your bloodline, laws, body, and soul adapt naturally.\"","He paused briefly before adding, \"If your Primordial Bloodline contains dormant abilities, this place will try to awaken them. Whether you succeed or not depends on your own foundation.\"","Orion grinned again, though his expression carried tension this time. \"That sounds dangerous.\"","Sarvion looked at him calmly. \"It is.\"","Orion’s grin stiffened slightly.","Sarvion placed one hand on the gate.","The bronze-gold symbols lit up one by one.","A deep sound spread through the corridor as the massive gate slowly opened, revealing a vast space beyond it.","Max stepped inside with the others.","The moment he crossed the threshold, the world changed.","At least, that was how it felt to him.","The training room did not look like a normal chamber. From Max’s perspective, it felt more like an entire sealed realm built inside the Primordial Ancestral Domain. The ceiling was so high that it disappeared into a dim golden mist.","The floor beneath his feet was made of smooth dark stone, but countless lines of light flowed through it like molten law veins. In the distance, enormous pillars rose into the mist, and every pillar carried a different aura.","Some burned with primordial flame. Some crackled with ancient lightning. Some released crushing gravity. Some distorted space. Some gave off a soul pressure so dense that even looking at them made Max’s mind tighten.","At the center of the room stood ten circular platforms.","Each platform was surrounded by runes, and above each one floated a pale golden sphere. Those spheres pulsed slowly, like hearts beating in silence. Every pulse released waves of pressure that entered Max’s body and brushed against his Primordial Bloodline.","Max’s eyes narrowed.","The room was testing them already.","He could feel it clearly.","The pressure did not attack him directly. Instead, it passed over him layer by layer, as if measuring his bones, blood, soul, laws, and hidden powers.","His Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline reacted with a faint growl. His Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline released a soft glow. His Voidwalker bloodline remained quiet but alert. His five Divine Veins pulsed one after another. His Dimensional Keeper Legacy watched silently from the depths of his foundation.","Then his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline finally responded.","A deep, ancient warmth spread through Max’s body.","For a brief moment, Max felt as if the laws of the training room had moved closer to him. The pressure on his shoulders became heavier, but it also felt clearer.","The lines on the floor, the runes around the platforms, the pillars in the distance, and the golden spheres above them all seemed to reveal tiny details that he would not have noticed before.","’So this place is designed to draw out the bloodline’s deeper potential,’ Max thought.","Sarvion’s voice echoed through the training room.","\"Choose a platform and sit. Once the chamber activates fully, each of you will be isolated in your own training space. What you see afterward may not be what the others see. The Primordial training chambers do not train everyone in the same way.\"","Max looked toward the nearest platform.","The golden sphere above it pulsed.","For some reason, he felt it calling to him.","He walked forward and stepped onto the platform. The runes around it lit up beneath his feet, and a circle of golden light rose around him. The sounds of the others faded slightly, as if distance had suddenly stretched between them.","Max sat cross-legged at the center of the platform.","The moment he closed his eyes, the pressure around him changed.","The training room vanished from his senses.","A vast primordial space opened around him, filled with golden mist, ancient law fragments, and a power that seemed to come from the earliest age of the universe.","Max took a slow breath.","His Primordial Bloodline began to awaken further.","At the same time, in the hall they had left behind, another Primordial appeared before Arvantos.","His expression was solemn.","\"All the major forces have been informed, including the Four Sacred Clans,\" the Primordial said. \"They will gather here by tonight.\"","Arvantos nodded lightly. \"Good.\"","The Primordial continued, \"Also, only the Wall of Eternity on the side of the Devil Universe has been weakened because of the hole. The boundaries connected to the Spirit Universe, Angel Universe, and Dragon Universe show no sign of damage.\"","\"That is one piece of good news, at least,\" Arvantos said.","His expression remained grave.","The other three universes had not moved yet.","But Arvantos knew very well that once the devils began stirring the situation, the others would not remain blind forever.","After a moment, both figures vanished from the hall.","The Primordial Ancestral Domain grew quiet again.","Inside the training facility, Max sat alone within his isolated space, unaware of Arvantos’s conversation.","The golden mist around him thickened.","The dormant power inside his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline began to rise."]},{"number":1998,"title":"Chapter 1998: Forceful Awakening!","paragraphs":["The awakening of a Primordial Bloodline ability was never meant to be a quick process.","For most members of the Primordial Race, awakening a true bloodline ability required decades of slow adaptation. Some needed centuries.","A Primordial had to let the bloodline settle into the body, fuse with the soul, nourish the bones, refine the organs, and gradually change the way their laws interacted with the world. Only after the bloodline became a natural part of their existence would a hidden ability begin to surface.","But Max and the others did not have decades.","They did not even have years.","The devils had already entered their universe, the Wall of Eternity had already been pierced, Varok was walking around with the Pearl of Abyss, and the meeting between the Primordials and the devils would take place in a week.","Because of that, the Primordial Race had chosen a method that was rarely used unless the situation was urgent.","The training facility had been activated at the highest level.","Level Ten Order.","At this level, the chamber no longer guided the bloodline gently. It no longer waited for the body to adapt naturally. Instead, it flooded the cultivator with concentrated primordial source energy and forced the dormant ability within the Primordial Bloodline to awaken ahead of time.","It was a crude method.","It was dangerous.","It was not recommended even among the Primordial Race.","Although the method worked, it often left behind unstable bloodline foundations. Some Primordials suffered torn meridians. Some experienced soul backlash. Some lost control of their bloodline for years afterward. Some even suffered bloodline combustion, where the dormant power ignited violently inside their bodies and burned them from within before stabilizing.","Yet this method had been used before in ancient wars.","When time was short and survival mattered more than perfection, the Primordial Race had always been willing to take risks.","Now, the same method was being used on the ten geniuses.","Inside his isolated training space, Max sat cross-legged within the golden primordial mist.","Time passed strangely here.","The first day was silent.","The golden mist seeped into his body layer by layer, and his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline responded like a sleeping ancient beast slowly opening its eyes. The energy did not merely enter his veins. It examined them. It pressed against them. It searched for something hidden within the deepest part of his bloodline origin.","On the second day, the pressure increased.","The primordial source energy became heavier and far more aggressive. It entered Max’s blood, bones, soul, and laws at the same time, trying to force the bloodline ability to appear. His five Divine Veins pulsed one after another, helping his body stabilize the impact.","The Vein of Resilience reduced the damage caused by the pressure. The Vein of Vitality repaired the tiny cracks that appeared inside his body. The Vein of Origin anchored his foundation, preventing the primordial force from scattering through him uncontrollably.","On the third day, the first signs of bloodline combustion appeared.","Golden flames suddenly ignited inside Max’s veins.","They were not external flames.","They burned from within his blood.","A sharp heat spread through his body, and for a brief moment, Max felt as if every drop of blood inside him had turned into molten gold. His skin flushed with light, his bones released faint cracking sounds, and ancient primordial runes surfaced briefly across his arms, chest, neck, and face before sinking back into his flesh.","Max opened his eyes slightly.","’So this is the danger Sarvion mentioned.’","He had already realized that the chamber was not training him gently. It was forcing his Primordial Bloodline to reveal something that should have taken years to awaken naturally. The process was effective, but it was also brutal.","The golden flames inside his bloodline tried to burn open the hidden ability, and if his body had been weaker, his bloodline might have collapsed before the ability even appeared.","Fortunately, Max’s body was not normal.","His foundation had been strengthened too many times.","His Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline gave him a terrifying physical body and monstrous vitality. His five Divine Veins reinforced different aspects of his existence. His Dimensional Sovereign Body had already transformed the nature of his physique.","His Voidwalker inheritance had deepened his dimensional foundation. And more importantly, his Unholy Trinity Body seemed capable of containing different kinds of powers without allowing them to destroy one another.","That was the strangest part.","Inside Max, too many powers existed together.","Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline, Voidwalker bloodline, Dimensional Keeper Legacy, Divine King Punishment, Emotion Severing Path, Devouring Flames, Dimensional Sovereign Body, Dimension of Soul, and his Divine Veins should have made his body a chaotic battlefield.","But the Unholy Trinity Body acted like a terrifying vessel that could hold them all. It did not make every conflict disappear, but it prevented those powers from tearing his body apart whenever they awakened, clashed, or evolved.","Because of that, Max endured the bloodline combustion.","It hurt.","The golden fire burning inside his veins was not something he could ignore, but it did not cripple him. It burned through his blood, and his body repaired the damage just as quickly.","It surged toward his soul, and his Dimension of Soul swallowed much of the impact. It tried to disrupt his law foundation, and his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline drew the laws closer instead, turning part of the damage into nourishment.","By the fourth day, the other geniuses had already begun awakening their bloodline abilities.","Max could not see them clearly because each platform had isolated its own training space, but he could still sense several violent fluctuations through the chamber. One aura erupted with a crushing force that seemed to distort gravity.","Another released a storm of primordial lightning. Another carried a freezing pressure that slowed the movement of laws. Another burned with a pale golden radiance that made the entire chamber tremble faintly.","They were awakening faster than him.","Not because their foundations were better.","But because their Primordial Bloodlines were lower in level.","Their bloodlines were easier to force open.","The abilities sleeping inside them were powerful, but not as deeply buried as the one inside Max. The lower the level of the Primordial Bloodline, the easier it was for the Level Ten Order to tear open the sealed ability.","That was why some of the others awakened on the second day, and several more awakened on the third and fourth days.","But their success came with a price."]},{"number":1999,"title":"Chapter 1999: Primordial Flames!","paragraphs":["Max sensed bloodline combustion from several directions.","Muffled groans echoed through the isolated spaces. A wave of unstable primordial force shook the chamber. Someone’s aura spiked violently before being suppressed by the training facility. Another person’s bloodline power surged so fiercely that the surrounding runes had to descend like chains to stabilize it.","The chamber was helping them awaken their abilities.","It was also preventing them from being destroyed by those abilities.","Max’s eyes remained closed.","He did not envy them.","His awakening was slower because his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline was at the highest level. If a lower bloodline was like a sealed treasure chest, then his was more like an ancient world locked behind layers of cosmic law.","Forcing it open was not simple. The chamber had to pressure his body again and again, deepen the bloodline combustion again and again, and awaken the hidden ability from the very root of his blood.","On the fifth day, the change finally came.","The golden mist around Max suddenly stopped moving.","The primordial source energy that had been pouring into him like a violent tide became silent for one breath. Then, all of it rushed toward the space between his brows.","Max’s body trembled.","A sharp pain pierced his forehead.","It felt as if something ancient inside his skull was being carved open by fire and law.","His blood boiled.","His soul shook.","His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline erupted completely.","Golden runes spread across his body, then gathered toward his forehead. The veins at his temples glowed. His eyes turned bright gold for a moment, and the air around him burned with a heat that did not resemble ordinary flame.","Then a vertical line appeared between his brows.","At first, it looked like a thin golden mark.","Then the mark split open.","A third eye opened between Max’s brows.","The moment that middle eye appeared, the entire isolated space became still.","It was not like a normal eye. Its iris was pure gold, but inside the gold were countless tiny primordial symbols rotating in circular layers. At the very center of the eye burned a small flame, calm and sacred, as if it had existed since the earliest dawn of creation.","Max took a slow breath.","He immediately understood something.","This eye was not merely a symbol of awakening.","It was the key.","Only through this middle eye could he activate the true bloodline ability of the Primordial Bloodline. The ability was not like his Black Dragon transformation, which surged through his entire body.","It was not like the Heavenly Luminance Divine Bloodline, which released light through his bloodline source. The Primordial Bloodline ability required this eye to open, observe, command, and ignite.","A name appeared naturally in his mind.","Primordial Flames.","The moment the name surfaced, the small flame within the middle eye expanded.","Golden fire appeared in front of Max.","At first, it was only a tiny wisp.","But the instant it appeared, the entire training space trembled.","The flame did not burn like normal fire. It did not rage wildly like the Devouring Flames. It did not consume with hunger like the black flames of his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline. It was quiet, pure, and terrifyingly ancient. Wherever it floated, the surrounding laws seemed to become clearer, as though the flame was not destroying reality, but returning it to a more original state.","Max stared at it with deep eyes.","His black flames and the Primordial Flames were complete opposites.","The black flames from his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline were violent, chaotic, devouring, and destructive. They burned with the nature of collapse. They swallowed energy, corroded defenses, consumed vitality, and turned whatever they touched into fuel. They were the fire of a terrifying dragon born from chaos, a flame that existed to tear apart and devour.","The Primordial Flames were different.","They were not gentle, but they were pure.","They carried the aura of origin, refinement, and ancient creation. Instead of simply burning things away, they seemed capable of refining laws, purifying corrupted energy, strengthening bloodline power, and burning through impurities hidden inside a target’s foundation.","If the black flames represented destruction through devouring, then the Primordial Flames represented destruction through returning everything to its original truth.","One flame swallowed.","The other flame refined.","One was dark chaos.","The other was golden origin.","Max slowly raised his hand.","The Primordial Flame drifted above his palm.","The moment it touched his skin, his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline pulsed again, and the middle eye between his brows glowed brighter.","Max felt his connection to the laws deepen. The surrounding primordial energy bent toward him, and even the hidden fragments of ancient law within the training chamber seemed to respond to the flame.","’So this is the ability of the highest-level Primordial Bloodline,’ Max thought.","He understood why it had taken five days.","The others had awakened their own abilities faster, but none of their bloodline reactions had reached this level. His Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline had not given him an ordinary ability.","It had awakened Primordial Flames, a power that seemed to stand at the very core of what the Primordial Race represented.","Power close to origin.","Power close to law.","Power close to the beginning of everything.","The bloodline combustion inside him slowly settled.","Golden fire still moved through his veins, but it no longer felt like a threat. It had become part of him. His body had endured the forced awakening, and his Unholy Trinity Body had accepted the new power without rejecting the others.","The Primordial Flames now existed alongside his black flames, Divine King Punishment, Emotion Severing Path, Dimensional Keeper Legacy, and all his other powers.","Max closed the middle eye between his brows.","The golden flame vanished.","The training space grew quiet again.","But Max knew that the change was permanent.","From now on, whenever that middle eye opened, he would be able to activate the bloodline ability of his Tier 4 Primordial Bloodline.","Primordial Flames.","A flame born from origin.","A flame completely opposite to the devouring black fire of his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline."]},{"number":2000,"title":"Chapter 2000: Mysterious Chaos Tree!","paragraphs":["Max could already think of many ways to use the Primordial Flames in battle.","The moment he awakened the ability, possibilities began forming in his mind one after another. He could condense the Primordial Flames into blades, wrap them around his fists, fuse them into his sword strikes, release them as a domain, or combine them with his other laws to create even more terrifying attacks.","Since he had already spent so much time controlling the black flames from his Black Dragon Chaotic Bloodline, his understanding of flame manipulation was far beyond ordinary cultivators.","The black flames were violent and difficult to control, yet Max had learned to shape them with precision, restraint, and explosive force. Because of that experience, he felt that controlling the Primordial Flames would be much easier once he became familiar with their nature.","The Primordial Flames were different from the black flames, but fire was still fire.","The black flames devoured.","The Primordial Flames refined.","One burned with chaotic hunger, while the other burned with ancient purity. If Max could use both properly, then his control over fire would no longer be limited to simple destruction. He could devour with one flame and purify with the other.","He could destroy external defenses with black flames, then burn through hidden impurities, curses, or bloodline corruption with Primordial Flames. Against enemies like devils, that difference might become extremely important.","\"I still have one day before the meeting with the devils begins,\" Max muttered as he opened his eyes. \"I should use this time properly.\"","With that thought, he stood up and left the training chamber.","When he arrived outside, he saw that the others had already left as well. The platforms that had held the ten geniuses were now empty, and the golden spheres above them had dimmed. Faint traces of unstable bloodline aura still lingered in the air, showing how violent their forced awakenings had been.","Max could sense that several of the others had succeeded in awakening their Primordial Bloodline abilities, but their foundations were not completely stable yet. The Level Ten Order had saved time, but it had also left behind strain that would take effort to repair.","Max did not think too much about it.","Everyone had their own path.","He followed the route Sarvion had shown them earlier and soon returned to the room assigned to him within the Primordial Ancestral Domain.","The room was simple, but it carried a quiet dignity. Dark-gold walls surrounded the chamber, soft primordial light flowed through thin lines in the floor, and a faint isolation formation covered the entire space. It was not luxurious, but it was secure, which was all Max needed.","After entering the room, Max closed the door and activated the formation.","Then he directly entered the Dimension of Time.","The world around him changed.","The quiet room vanished, replaced by the vast space inside his own special dimension. Time flowed differently here, and the moment Max entered, he felt the familiar silence wrap around him.","This place had helped him train, comprehend, refine, and prepare for battles many times before. Now that he had finally stepped into the Law Manifestation Realm, many things inside him had changed, and he needed to check them properly.","He had not gotten the chance to do so earlier.","When he broke through to the Law Manifestation Realm inside the inheritance chamber of the Voidwalker Clan, the commotion had shaken the entire Five Sacred Clan domain. Not long after that, he was summoned to the Primordial Race because of the devil crisis.","There had been no peaceful moment for him to sit down and examine the changes in his foundation.","Now, he finally had time.","The first thing Max checked was the Chaos Tree.","The moment he focused on it, his eyes narrowed.","The Chaos Tree had changed far more than he expected.","Compared to how it had been during the Law Refinement Realm, it had grown to an astonishing size. Previously, it had looked like a young tree, mysterious and powerful, but still limited in scale.","Now, it was enormous. Its trunk was thick and ancient, its bark was covered in dark chaotic patterns, and countless branches stretched outward like the veins of a growing world. Different elemental branches extended in different directions, each carrying its own aura, color, and law resonance. Some branches burned with flame.","Some flickered with lightning. Some were wrapped in wind. Some carried the weight of earth. Some shimmered with water, light, darkness, space, and other powers that had taken root inside Max’s foundation.","Standing before it, Max almost felt like an ant.","The difference was too great.","\"The size of the Chaos Tree increased far too much after I entered the Law Manifestation Realm,\" Max muttered as he looked up at the towering tree. \"But what is its real benefit?\"","He already understood part of the Chaos Tree’s function.","It could grow elemental branches based on the powers he possessed. From those branches, it could produce Chaos Fruits. Those fruits could then be used to grant him Divine Abilities, or they could be given to others to form Divine Bodies.","Over the past few weeks after the tournament ended, Max had plucked many Chaos Fruits from the various elemental branches and handed them to Isabella and the others. Those fruits would be distributed to capable members with good potential within his Crown force.","That alone was already valuable.","A force that could produce people with Divine Bodies would eventually become terrifying.","However, Max did not believe that was the true limit of the Chaos Tree.","It had been born from his Unholy Trinity Body.","Something born from that kind of body should not have such a simple purpose.","\"The Chaos Tree is born from my Unholy Trinity Body,\" Max muttered while his gaze moved across its vast branches. \"But unlike the Unholy Trinity Body, which allows me to contain all kinds of powers within my body, I still do not know the real purpose of the Chaos Tree.\""]}]);
